{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T07:28:21.616Z","ordinal":12060,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a024c5-b91b-72b3-ad56-490032d022a1","turn_id":"01a02d84-67e7-7143-9c14-0a1cb505f664","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3abafaf5-6c6f-45fd-a946-80b7b106e9d4","process_id":"47035","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api --paginate repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/116/comments --jq '.[] | {id,path,line,original_line,created_at,updated_at,html_url,user:.user.login,body,in_reply_to_id,commit_id,original_commit_id}'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api --paginate repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/116/comments --jq '.[] | {id,path,line,original_line,created_at,updated_at,html_url,user:.user.login,body,in_reply_to_id,commit_id,original_commit_id}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"{\"body\":\"## Useless assignment to local variable\\n\\nThe value assigned to terminalAuditAttempted here is unused.\\n\\n---\\n\\nGeneral fix: remove assignments to local variables when the assigned value is never subsequently read, unless needed for side effects (not applicable to primitive assignment).\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eBest fix here: in \\u003ccode\\u003epackages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\\u003c/code\\u003e, remove the single redundant assignment \\u003ccode\\u003eterminalAuditAttempted = true;\\u003c/code\\u003e inside the error-handling audit-write branch. This does not change behavior because:\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003ethe only relevant guard using \\u003ccode\\u003eterminalAuditAttempted\\u003c/code\\u003e in this shown block is already evaluated before the assignment,\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003edownstream result/idempotency logic depends on \\u003ccode\\u003eterminalAuditWritten\\u003c/code\\u003e and \\u003ccode\\u003eauditId\\u003c/code\\u003e, not \\u003ccode\\u003eterminalAuditAttempted\\u003c/code\\u003e.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eNo new imports, methods, or definitions are required.\",\"commit_id\":\"8d16f12d9a673cbed04f6c20cc9a06b0e770389e\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:16Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831735495\",\"id\":3831735495,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":425,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:17Z\",\"user\":\"github-code-quality[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Polynomial regular expression used on uncontrolled data\\n\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](2) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/42)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:21Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736234\",\"id\":3831736234,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":151,\"path\":\"authfn/admin/src/superconsole.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Polynomial regular expression used on uncontrolled data\\n\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](2) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](3) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](4) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](5) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](6) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](7) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](8) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](9) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](10) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](11) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/43)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736282\",\"id\":3831736282,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":137,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/client.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Polynomial regular expression used on uncontrolled data\\n\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](2) may run slow on strings starting with 'get ' and with many repetitions of '  '.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](3) may run slow on strings starting with 'get ' and with many repetitions of '  '.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/44)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736306\",\"id\":3831736306,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":37,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/registry.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Polynomial regular expression used on uncontrolled data\\n\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](2) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '_'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](3) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '_'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](4) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '_'.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/45)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736318\",\"id\":3831736318,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":45,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/registry.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Polynomial regular expression used on uncontrolled data\\n\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](2) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](3) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/46)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736335\",\"id\":3831736335,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":78,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/registry.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Polynomial regular expression used on uncontrolled data\\n\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](2) may run slow on strings starting with 'get ' and with many repetitions of '  '.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](3) may run slow on strings starting with 'get ' and with many repetitions of '  '.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](4) may run slow on strings starting with 'get ' and with many repetitions of '  '.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](5) may run slow on strings starting with 'get ' and with many repetitions of '  '.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/47)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736351\",\"id\":3831736351,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":380,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Bad HTML filtering regexp\\n\\nThis regular expression does not match script end tags like \\u003c/script \\u003e.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/52)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736362\",\"id\":3831736362,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":38,\"path\":\"superconsole/scripts/verify-function-agnostic.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Incomplete string escaping or encoding\\n\\nThis does not escape backslash characters in the input.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/53)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736380\",\"id\":3831736380,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":95,\"path\":\"uifn/dom/src/overlay.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Prototype-polluting assignment\\n\\nThis assignment may alter Object.prototype if a malicious '__proto__' string is injected from [library input](1).\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/50)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736399\",\"id\":3831736399,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":221,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/openapi.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Prototype-polluting function\\n\\nThe property chain [segment](1) is recursively assigned to [current](2) without guarding against prototype pollution.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/49)\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736417\",\"id\":3831736417,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":87,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":84,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/resource-pages.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Information exposure through a stack trace\\n\\nThis information exposed to the user depends on [stack trace information](1).\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/48)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736436\",\"id\":3831736436,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":82,\"path\":\"uifn/svelte/tests/phase-14-ssr-hydration.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Exception text reinterpreted as HTML\\n\\n[Exception text](1) is reinterpreted as HTML without escaping meta-characters.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/51)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736451\",\"id\":3831736451,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":82,\"path\":\"uifn/svelte/tests/phase-14-ssr-hydration.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Preserve numeric-looking string document IDs**\\n\\nFor a composite target such as `orders:001`, this converts the document ID from the string `\\\"001\\\"` to the number `1`. Single-document indexing therefore targets a different ID than batch indexing, which preserves string IDs, and `remove-document` can delete numeric document `1` instead of string document `\\\"001\\\"`. Preserve the ID suffix as a string or carry explicit ID-type information in the input.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:01:33Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831751943\",\"id\":3831751943,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":56,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:01:33Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Apply the declared index-list query parameters**\\n\\nWhen an installation has many configured indexes or the console supplies search/filter/pagination input, `listIndexes` ignores the entire input and always returns every index with `nextCursor: null`. This contradicts the operation's cursor-pagination declaration and makes the resource-list search UI return unrelated entries while bypassing the declared 200-item maximum; honor `limit`, `cursor`, and the advertised query fields before building the result.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:01:33Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831751947\",\"id\":3831751947,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":110,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:01:33Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**Security:** Mutation authorization is selected from the HTTP method rather than the matched operation's safety classification. Capability validation currently allows a `GET` route whose classification is `write` or `destructive`, so that operation is dispatched without `authorizeMutation` (and therefore without provider CSRF/re-auth checks). Please either reject non-read operations on safe HTTP methods during manifest validation or authorize after matching based on `entry.operation.safety.classification`.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799619\",\"id\":3831799619,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":630,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":612,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**Security:** These ownership predicates omit `tenantId`, even though `PlugFnDomainIdentity`, connections/installations, and `ownerFor()` carry it, and PlugFn core's `connectionMatchesActor()` requires exact tenant equality. If the same user or organization ID exists in two tenants, an admin mapped to tenant A can supply a tenant-B record ID and pass these checks (notably allowing `connections.refresh(id)`). Please include tenant equality in the direct-ID connection, installation, delegated, and legacy ownership checks and add a same-owner/different-tenant test.\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799625\",\"id\":3831799625,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":68,\"path\":\"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"This does not pass the package's own typecheck: `npm run typecheck --workspace superconsole` reports that `code` is not part of SvelteKit's `Error`, followed by two errors where `+error.svelte` reads `page.error.code` and `.details`. Please declare the intended `App.Error` shape in `src/app.d.ts` (or restrict these routes to the standard error shape) so the checked package is type-safe.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799628\",\"id\":3831799628,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":5,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":5,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/routes/[...missing]/+page.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"`SuperConsoleOptions.apiBasePath` changes the only prefix accepted by the server, but every bundled UI loader/action uses this hard-coded prefix. Configuring, for example, `/internal/admin` therefore makes the server reject all UI requests with 404. Please propagate the configured base path to the client/UI (including sign-in and download links), or remove/limit the option so a supported configuration cannot break the console.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799631\",\"id\":3831799631,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":9,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":9,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=1e8a9759-bd72-4e24-bd8c-217d1bba06d6 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=7bb8304f-392d-4952-ab05-eaf35f279889 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} --\\u003e\\nP1: When the build reaches `accordion`, it asks tsup to bundle nonexistent `createAccordionController`, so the build fails before producing any public primitive entrypoints. Add the missing controller exports or map catalog entries to verified source exports before bundling.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/core/scripts/build.mjs, line 24:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen the build reaches `accordion`, it asks tsup to bundle nonexistent `createAccordionController`, so the build fails before producing any public primitive entrypoints. Add the missing controller exports or map catalog entries to verified source exports before bundling.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@\\n+        ? 'CreateHoverCardProps'\\n+        : `${primitive.name}Props`,\\n+      runtime: interactive\\n+        ? `create${primitive.name}Controller`\\n+        : `${primitive.name}Contract`,\\n+      secondaryType: interactive\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:19:44Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831870338\",\"id\":3831870338,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":47,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":24,\"path\":\"uifn/core/scripts/build.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:19:48Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=f7c442d0-9cda-425a-b716-bbb0721f56ad --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=7bb8304f-392d-4952-ab05-eaf35f279889 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} --\\u003e\\nP1: The audit endpoint returns raw `AdminAuditEvent` objects, but this loader forwards them as `AuditEventViewModel` without mapping. Audit rows therefore read undefined `occurredAt`/`actor`/`action`, render the object target as `[object Object]`, and show raw outcomes 