te will render stale/empty until an action fires. Invoke the callback with the current `state` inside `subscribe` (before adding it to the set, defensively) to match that contract.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/core/src/primitives/legacy-compat.ts, line 35:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003e`createLegacyAvatar` never emits the current state to a newly subscribed callback, so a subscriber that reads after subscribing sees nothing until a later `setLoading`/`setLoaded`/`setError` transition. Controllers in this codebase (`createUIFnController` at uifn/core/src/controller.ts:412) and Svelte-store-backed adapters deliver the initial state on subscribe, so a consumer relying on the initial 'idle' state will render stale/empty until an action fires. Invoke the callback with the current `state` inside `subscribe` (before adding it to the set, defensively) to match that contract.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@\\n+      setLoaded: () =\\u003e update('loaded'),\\n+      setError: () =\\u003e update('error'),\\n+    }),\\n+    subscribe(callback) {\\n+      subscribers.add(callback);\\n+      return () =\\u003e subscribers.delete(callback);\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    subscribe(callback) {\\n      subscribers.add(callback);\\n      callback(state);\\n      return () =\\u003e subscribers.delete(callback);\\n    },\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`8ad9b66`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/8ad9b668d13ae8354920ab8d6e4ef6f1b01eeaec)\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T03:11:11Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3834931027\",\"id\":3834931027,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":46,\"original_commit_id\":\"8d16f12d9a673cbed04f6