n [`616f549`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452)\",\"commit_id\":\"94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:36:08Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835526427\",\"id\":3835526427,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"21fbc394a2a628e7fb5933c0a418b6f0766154e4\",\"original_line\":31,\"path\":\"uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:46:46Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=cf8c911b-6d4d-47a7-9594-566d34a57d61 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=810e9353-3c10-4590-b40c-3b59af9b88bb --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When a marked input has a sensitive name such as `REDACTED` or `token`, the trace writes its value unredacted in `formValues` and `attributes.value`. Pass both DOM-captured values through the same key-aware redaction used for state and callbacks before writing the trace.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs, line 195:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a marked input has a sensitive name such as `REDACTED` or `token`, the trace writes its value unredacted in `formValues` and `attributes.value`. Pass both DOM-captured values through the same key-aware redaction used for state and callbacks before writing the trace.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -0,0 +1,384 @@\\n+    if (!(element instanceof HTMLInputElement || element instanceof HTMLSelectElement || element instanceof HTMLTextAreaElement)) continue;\\n+    const key = element.name || `${element.getAttribute(PART)}:${element.getAttribute(INSTANCE) ?? ''}`;\\n+    if (element instanceof HTMLInputElement \\u0026\\u0026 ['checkbox', 'radio'].includes(element.type)) values[key] = element.checked;\\n+    else values[key] = element.value;\\n+  }\\n+  return Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(values).sort(([left], [right]) =\\u003e left.localeCompare(right)));\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`616f549`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452)\",\"commit_id\":\"94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:36:08Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835526431\",\"id\":3835526431,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"21fbc394a2a628e7fb5933c0a418b6f0766154e4\",\"original_line\":195,\"path\":\"uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:46:50Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=0dffecbd-d021-4c49-96ec-1970b3193c7c --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=810e9353-3c10-4590-b40c-3b59af9b88bb --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When `Intl.Segmenter` is unavailable, this guard routes emoji and flag strings into a code-point fallback that still matches partial grapheme clusters. Use a grapheme-aware fallback, or conservatively reject these special-character matches when no segmenter exists.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts, line 91:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen `Intl.Segmenter` is unavailable, this guard routes emoji and flag strings into a code-point fallback that still matches partial grapheme clusters. Use a grapheme-aware fallback, or conservatively reject these special-character matches when no segmenter exists.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -86,7 +88,8 @@ export function createLocaleMatcher(locale = 'en'): LocaleMatcher {\\n     startsWith(value: string, query: string) {\\n       if (query.length === 0) return true;\\n-      if (normalize(value).startsWith(normalize(query))) return true;\\n+      if (!requiresGraphemeSegmentation(value) \\u0026\\u0026 !requiresGraphemeSegmentation(query)\\n+        \\u0026\\u0026 normalize(value).startsWith(normalize(query))) return true;\\n       const querySegments = segments(query);\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`616f549`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452)\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:36:08Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835526434\",\"id\":3835526434,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":111,\"original_commit_id\":\"21fbc394a2a628e7fb5933c0a418b6f0766154e4\",\"original_line\":91,\"path\":\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:46:44Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Supply a resource selector before exposing Records**\\n\\nWhen an operator opens the DataFn Records card in Super Console, the generated list request contains no `filter`, because this resource declares neither presentation filters nor a parent binding. Requiring `filter` here therefore makes the default Records route fail validation on every visit, leaving record browsing unusable unless the operator manually constructs a JSON query parameter; add a control/binding for `filter.resource` or stop advertising this as a standalone list.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:39:29Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835531565\",\"id\":3835531565,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":502,\"original_commit_id\":\"21fbc394a2a628e7fb5933c0a418b6f0766154e4\",\"original_line\":485,\"path\":\"datafn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:39:29Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Mark file-bound collections as non-standalone**\\n\\nOpening Versions from the FileFn module page invokes `filefn.versions.list` without the required `fileId`; Grants, Share Links, and Artifacts have the same problem. These resources omit `presentation.parent` and consequently default to `standaloneList: true`, so the console advertises cards that only return input-validation errors and cannot generate related links from a file detail page; declare their file-parent bindings and disable standalone listing.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:39:29Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835531568\",\"id\":3835531568,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"21fbc394a2a628e7fb5933c0a418b6f0766154e4\",\"original_line\":37,\"path\":\"filefn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:39:29Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Do not bind share revocation to the hash prefix**\\n\\nFor each listed share link, the generic row-action binder uses the resource identity (`tokenHashPrefix`) as this operation's `token` input and hides that target field from the form. The operator therefore cannot supply the required original plaintext token, and every displayed Revoke Share action confirms and submits the hash prefix instead, so it cannot revoke the selected link; avoid projecting this as an identity-bound row action or provide an independently editable plaintext-token input.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:39:29Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835531570\",\"id\":3835531570,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"21fbc394a2a628e7fb5933c0a418b6f0766154e4\",\"original_line\":198,\"path\":\"filefn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:39:29Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Fixed by capping sync-job scans at four pages, caching connection ownership checks, and returning a resumable cursor.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32559894115/job/96999772492) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"93079657b6d79970339f92d9a8f47a085a7364c7\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:41:30Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835534629\",\"id\":3835534629,\"in_reply_to_id\":3835446480,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"93079657b6d79970339f92d9a8f47a085a7364c7\",\"original_line\":308,\"path\":\"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:41:30Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Fixed by parsing HEAD inputs as query-bearing requests and adding resource HEAD coverage with required query input.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32559894115/job/96999772492) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:41:33Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835534741\",\"id\":3835534741,\"in_reply_to_id\":3835446486,\"line\":1269,\"original_commit_id\":\"93079657b6d79970339f92d9a8f47a085a7364c7\",\"original_line\":1197,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:41:33Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Fixed by enforcing tenant equality on direct ownership paths and deriving tenant provenance for connectionless webhook receipts from reserved metadata.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32559894115/job/96999772492) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:41:36Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835534817\",\"id\":3835534817,\"in_reply_to_id\":3831799625,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":68,\"path\":\"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:41:36Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Fixed by tracking `src/app.d.ts` with the intended `App.Error` augmentation.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32559894115/job/96999772492) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:41:39Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835534884\",\"id\":3835534884,\"in_reply_to_id\":3831799628,\"line\":5,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":5,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/routes/[...missing]/+page.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:41:39Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"[P1] Derive workflow tenant ownership from an authoritative field. `WorkflowEngine.create()` and `AdapterWorkflowStorage.create()` persist caller-provided `metadata` unchanged, and no core producer reserves or populates this key. As a result, ordinary/legacy workflows are hidden from administration, while any application path that accepts workflow metadata can forge the value used here for isolation. Add a first-class tenant owner populated from authenticated context (or verify through another authoritative relation) rather than treating generic metadata as authorization provenance.\",\"commit_id\":\"94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:43:02Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835537182\",\"id\":3835537182,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"21fbc394a2a628e7fb5933c0a418b6f0766154e4\",\"original_line\":138,\"path\":\"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:43:03Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"[P1] Validate the expected action outcome rather than any activity. The vectors declare action names and callback names but no expected post-state, callback arguments, or DOM semantics, so changing an unrelated state key or invoking a callback with the wrong payload makes `observed` true; line 380 then reports `passed`, and the Svelte test only asserts that result. Encode and compare expected state/callback effects so behaviorally incorrect adapters cannot satisfy the parity gate.\",\"commit_id\":\"94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:43:02Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835537185\",\"id\":3835537185,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"21fbc394a2a628e7fb5933c0a418b6f0766154e4\",\"original_line\":264,\"path\":\"uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:43:03Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Reject duplicate resource-template URI patterns**\\n\\nWhen two templates have different names but the same `uriTemplate`, this name-only duplicate check accepts both and advertises both from `resources/templates/list`. However, `matchResource` resolves by iterating the templates and returns the first URI match, so the later template's `read`, subscription, and completion behavior is unreachable. Reject duplicate `uriTemplate` values at registration time.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:57:05Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835561789\",\"id\":3835561789,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":196,\"original_commit_id\":\"e1062e1bc94e447305c649e89abb4588563dc475\",\"original_line\":183,\"path\":\"mcpfn/core/src/registry.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:57:05Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Encode cursor payloads as UTF-8**\\n\\nWhen any active scope identifier contains a non-Latin-1 character and a HostFn list has another page, `btoa(JSON.stringify(...))` throws `InvalidCharacterError` while constructing `nextCursor`, causing an otherwise successful list request to fail. Admin scope validation permits arbitrary nonblank Unicode strings, so encode the JSON as UTF-8 bytes before base64 encoding and reverse that transformation when decoding.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:57:05Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835561790\",\"id\":3835561790,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":738,\"original_commit_id\":\"e1062e1bc94e447305c649e89abb4588563dc475\",\"original_line\":736,\"path\":\"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:57:05Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Return usable FileFn download descriptors**\\n\\nWhen either download operation is invoked through the dispatcher, declaring `url` and `headers` as output fields causes `redactAdminOutputValue` to replace the signed URL and any required headers with `\\\"[REDACTED]\\\"`. The REST, MCP, and typed SDK responses therefore cannot be used to download the file; the artifact download declaration has the same defect. Return a provider-safe descriptor instead of redacting the fields that constitute the operation's result.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:13:59Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835590707\",\"id\":3835590707,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2\",\"original_line\":185,\"path\":\"filefn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:13:59Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Include CSRF metadata for POST read operations**\\n\\nFor a read-classified operation that uses an unsafe HTTP method, such as `apifn.specs.compare` (`POST`), `SuperConsole.handle` still calls `authorizeMutation` based on the request method, so cookie-authenticated AuthFn requests require the provider CSRF header. This classification check omits that header from OpenAPI, causing generated clients or API-console requests that follow the document to receive a CSRF 403; determine CSRF metadata from the HTTP method instead.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:13:59Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835590713\",\"id\":3835590713,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2\",\"original_line\":151,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/openapi.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:13:59Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=fa3f2f92-2cc0-4420-8be4-b0bbfc0e6b7e --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=16223a79-973e-46d4-85b7-f587ce11f5e4 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP1: When the Records page opens without a `resource` query parameter, the generic console sends no `filter.resource`, and `listRecords` rejects the request before rendering the filter. Make this list operation accept a default resource or provide required resource context before exposing it as a standalone presentation.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At datafn/admin/src/index.ts, line 139:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen the Records page opens without a `resource` query parameter, the generic console sends no `filter.resource`, and `listRecords` rejects the request before rendering the filter. Make this list operation accept a default resource or provide required resource context before exposing it as a standalone presentation.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -130,9 +132,19 @@ export const dataFnAdminResources = [\\n     sortableFields: [\\\"createdAt\\\", \\\"updatedAt\\\", \\\"name\\\"],\\n     sensitiveFields: [],\\n+    presentation: {\\n+      listOperationId: \\\"datafn.records.list\\\",\\n+      query: {\\n+        filters: [{\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`0daaba2`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5)\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:48:45Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835650689\",\"id\":3835650689,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":140,\"original_commit_id\":\"616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452\",\"original_line\":139,\"path\":\"datafn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:10:01Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=c308a9a1-dc1d-42b8-95e3-169abd6035ae --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=16223a79-973e-46d4-85b7-f587ce11f5e4 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When `Intl.Segmenter` is unavailable, valid grapheme matches inside larger labels always fail. Keep grapheme boundaries in the fallback so typeahead and substring matching can match complete graphemes without accepting partial grapheme matches.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts, line 91:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen `Intl.Segmenter` is unavailable, valid grapheme matches inside larger labels always fail. Keep grapheme boundaries in the fallback so typeahead and substring matching can match complete graphemes without accepting partial grapheme matches.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -88,6 +88,9 @@ export function createLocaleMatcher(locale = 'en'): LocaleMatcher {\\n     equals: (left: string, right: string) =\\u003e collator.compare(normalize(left), normalize(right)) === 0,\\n     startsWith(value: string, query: string) {\\n       if (query.length === 0) return true;\\n+      if (!segmenter \\u0026\\u0026 (requiresGraphemeSegmentation(value) || requiresGraphemeSegmentation(query))) {\\n+        return normalize(value) === normalize(query);\\n+      }\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`0daaba2`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5)\",\"commit_id\":\"616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:48:45Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835650690\",\"id\":3835650690,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452\",\"original_line\":91,\"path\":\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:10:02Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=7325427d-e1ab-4295-8cb6-e988a488cbd7 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=16223a79-973e-46d4-85b7-f587ce11f5e4 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When callers switch between the supported `organizationId` alias and `installationId`, or omit subordinate scope metadata, valid follow-up pages are rejected. Normalize the HostFn scope once and use that normalized value for both cursor decoding and encoding.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/admin/src/index.ts, line 705:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen callers switch between the supported `organizationId` alias and `installationId`, or omit subordinate scope metadata, valid follow-up pages are rejected. Normalize the HostFn scope once and use that normalized value for both cursor decoding and encoding.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -697,22 +699,12 @@ function pageResult(\\n-        marker: string;\\n-        offset: number;\\n-      };\\n+      const decoded = decodeAdminCursor\\u003c{ offset?: unknown }\\u003e(input.cursor, context.scope);\\n       if (\\n-        decoded.marker !== marker ||\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`0daaba2`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5)\",\"commit_id\":\"616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:48:45Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835650694\",\"id\":3835650694,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452\",\"original_line\":705,\"path\":\"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:09:59Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=c37dd8ff-3dc7-48f7-9d3b-73df0bd4e2e6 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=16223a79-973e-46d4-85b7-f587ce11f5e4 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When a setter leaves its target state unchanged but another field receives the same value, `runPhase14Actions()` marks the action observed. Restrict this fallback to `expectedStateKey` so parity traces cannot pass on an unrelated state change.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs, line 317:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a setter leaves its target state unchanged but another field receives the same value, `runPhase14Actions()` marks the action observed. Restrict this fallback to `expectedStateKey` so parity traces cannot pass on an unrelated state change.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -254,14 +291,51 @@ export async function runPhase14Actions(vector, bridge, runtime, capture) {\\n+    const semanticState = toSemanticJson(next.rawState);\\n+    const statePayloadObserved = setter \\u0026\\u0026 action.arguments.length === 1\\n+      \\u0026\\u0026 semanticState \\u0026\\u0026 !Array.isArray(semanticState) \\u0026\\u0026 typeof semanticState === 'object'\\n+      \\u0026\\u0026 changed.some((key) =\\u003e stableJson(semanticState[key]) === stableJson(action.arguments[0]));\\n+    const expectedCallbackValue = setter \\u0026\\u0026 expectedStateKey\\n+      \\u0026\\u0026 semanticState \\u0026\\u0026 !Array.isArray(semanticState) \\u0026\\u0026 typeof semanticState === 'object'\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n      \\u0026\\u0026 changed.includes(expectedStateKey)\\n      \\u0026\\u0026 stableJson(semanticState[expectedStateKey]) === stableJson(action.arguments[0]);\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`0daaba2`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5)\",\"commit_id\":\"616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:48:45Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835650697\",\"id\":3835650697,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452\",\"original_line\":317,\"path\":\"uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:09:57Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=557dff1b-a201-41bf-b143-a40e36585e17 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=16223a79-973e-46d4-85b7-f587ce11f5e4 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} --\\u003e\\nP2: When ten or more same-deadline timeouts are queued, `flush()` runs `timeout-10` before `timeout-2`, changing callback and state-transition order. Sort the numeric sequence or preserve `Map` insertion order.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs, line 66:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen ten or more same-deadline timeouts are queued, `flush()` runs `timeout-10` before `timeout-2`, changing callback and state-transition order. Sort the numeric sequence or preserve `Map` insertion order.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -45,6 +49,33 @@ export function createPhase14Scheduler() {\\n+          currentTime = Math.max(currentTime, nextDueAt);\\n+          const ready = [...timeouts.entries()]\\n+            .filter(([, entry]) =\\u003e entry.dueAt \\u003c= currentTime)\\n+            .sort(([left], [right]) =\\u003e left.localeCompare(right));\\n+          for (const [handle, entry] of ready) {\\n+            timeouts.delete(handle);\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n.sort(([left], [right]) =\\u003e Number(left.slice('timeout-'.length)) - Number(right.slice('timeout-'.length)));\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`0daaba2`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5)\",\"commit_id\":\"616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:48:45Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835650702\",\"id\":3835650702,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452\",\"original_line\":66,\"path\":\"uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:09:58Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=4ffd1760-fffc-4830-b455-219db0bd5dcc --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=16223a79-973e-46d4-85b7-f587ce11f5e4 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: When a mounted primitive schedules an interval, the new action-level `flush()` silently skips every interval callback, so checkpoints can miss interval-driven state updates while the task remains pending. Process recurring tasks over a bounded virtual-time window or explicitly fail this unsupported scheduler path.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs, line 54:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a mounted primitive schedules an interval, the new action-level `flush()` silently skips every interval callback, so checkpoints can miss interval-driven state updates while the task remains pending. Process recurring tasks over a bounded virtual-time window or explicitly fail this unsupported scheduler path.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -45,6 +49,33 @@ export function createPhase14Scheduler() {\\n     queueMicrotask(callback) { globalThis.queueMicrotask(callback); },\\n+    async flush() {\\n+      let turns = 0;\\n+      while ((frames.size \\u003e 0 || timeouts.size \\u003e 0) \\u0026\\u0026 turns \\u003c 1_000) {\\n+        turns += 1;\\n+        if (frames.size \\u003e 0) {\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`0daaba2`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5)\",\"commit_id\":\"616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:48:45Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835650705\",\"id\":3835650705,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452\",\"original_line\":54,\"path\":\"uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:09:56Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Canonicalize the installation alias before idempotency**\\n\\nWhen a retry identifies the same installation through `organizationId` instead of `installationId`, this constructs a structurally different `AdminScope` even though the package defines organization as a compatibility alias. `AdminDispatcher` includes the raw scope in its idempotency identity, so the same actor, operation, and idempotency key can acquire a second claim and execute an idempotent mutation twice; scope-bound cursors also fail across the two equivalent forms. Normalize the root to one canonical property before passing the authorized scope downstream.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:52:09Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835655943\",\"id\":3835655943,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452\",\"original_line\":153,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:52:09Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Expose nested AuthFn sessions through the Sessions resource**\\n\\nFor operators using the generic Super Console, this list operation is grouped under `users` because `moduleView` groups operations by `target.resource`, while the declared `sessions` resource contains only the revoke mutation and is therefore non-listable. The operation name also does not end in `.list`, and the Sessions resource declares no presentation override or user-parent binding, so neither the AuthFn module page nor a user detail page provides a route to browse active sessions. Target the Sessions collection and declare its user-parent/list presentation metadata.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:52:09Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835655945\",\"id\":3835655945,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452\",\"original_line\":406,\"path\":\"authfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:52:09Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"The manifest contract permits a `GET` route classified as a mutation, and Super Console explicitly sends that case through `authorizeMutation`; AuthFn then requires CSRF for cookie credentials. This method-only condition removes the provider header from that operation's OpenAPI contract, so generated cookie clients can follow the contract and still be rejected.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# CSRF projection diverges for safe-method mutations\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `packages/admin/src/openapi.ts:151` — projects the CSRF header only from the HTTP method.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1213-1215` — invokes `authorizeMutation` for non-read operations using safe methods.\\n- `authfn/core/src/index.ts:166-175` — enforces CSRF whenever cookie credentials authorize a mutation.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Project provider CSRF metadata for every operation that can reach `authorizeMutation`, including both POST reads and GET mutations.\\n- Add projection coverage for a GET operation with non-read classification.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:53:03Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835657402\",\"id\":3835657402,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452\",\"original_line\":151,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/openapi.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:53:04Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=c7eab044-1ad1-490f-95c4-6fa65ad251d2 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=7f33862e-6cc7-4ff5-931f-bb9e0b0a7209 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} --\\u003e\\nP2: When two intervals share a due time, clearing the second from the first callback still invokes the second callback. Check that the interval still exists before invoking each ready interval.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs, line 78:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen two intervals share a due time, clearing the second from the first callback still invokes the second callback. Check that the interval still exists before invoking each ready interval.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -51,28 +56,36 @@ export function createPhase14Scheduler() {\\n+            .sort(([left], [right]) =\\u003e schedulerSequence(left) - schedulerSequence(right));\\n           for (const [handle, entry] of ready) {\\n-            timeouts.delete(handle);\\n+            if (handle.startsWith('timeout-')) timeouts.delete(handle);\\n+            else pendingIntervals.delete(handle);\\n             await entry.callback();\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n            if (handle.startsWith('timeout-')) timeouts.delete(handle);\\n            else if (intervals.has(handle)) pendingIntervals.delete(handle);\\n            else continue;\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`239ba00`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba)\",\"commit_id\":\"0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:13:21Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835689712\",\"id\":3835689712,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5\",\"original_line\":79,\"path\":\"uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:28:58Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=678363e7-051d-4c9a-979f-a8d89c232fd9 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=7f33862e-6cc7-4ff5-931f-bb9e0b0a7209 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: Without `Intl.Segmenter`, this condition merges every character after a ZWJ, so `a‍b` becomes one fallback cluster and a valid prefix match for `a` is missed. Only join a following extended-pictographic code point when the preceding cluster forms an emoji ZWJ sequence.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts, line 27:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWithout `Intl.Segmenter`, this condition merges every character after a ZWJ, so `a‍b` becomes one fallback cluster and a valid prefix match for `a` is missed. Only join a following extended-pictographic code point when the preceding cluster forms an emoji ZWJ sequence.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -19,11 +19,29 @@ export function createLocaleMatcher(locale = 'en'): LocaleMatcher {\\n+    for (const codePoint of Array.from(value)) {\\n+      const previous = result.at(-1);\\n+      const continuation = /\\\\p{M}|\\\\ufe0e|\\\\ufe0f|\\\\p{Emoji_Modifier}/u.test(codePoint);\\n+      const joins = codePoint === '\\\\u200d' || previous?.endsWith('\\\\u200d');\\n+      const regionalPair = /\\\\p{Regional_Indicator}/u.test(codePoint)\\n+        \\u0026\\u0026 previous !== undefined\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n      const joins = codePoint === '\\\\u200d' || (previous?.endsWith('\\\\u200d') \\u0026\\u0026 /\\\\p{Extended_Pictographic}/u.test(previous));\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`239ba00`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba)\",\"commit_id\":\"0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:13:21Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835689721\",\"id\":3835689721,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5\",\"original_line\":27,\"path\":\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:29:00Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Make bot deletion and channel connection atomic**\\n\\nWhen `connectChannel` and `deleteBot` run concurrently, the connect path can observe the bot here, then the delete path can observe no channels and delete it, after which the connect path persists a channel for the now-missing bot. Because the store contract exposes only these separate reads and writes, even the supplied memory implementation permits an orphaned active external binding; enforce the bot-exists/channel-empty invariant atomically in the persistence layer.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:14:07Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835691127\",\"id\":3835691127,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":241,\"original_commit_id\":\"0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5\",\"original_line\":218,\"path\":\"botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:14:07Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Bind HostFn cursors to their collection and query**\\n\\nWithin one HostFn scope, every list operation encodes exactly the same `{ offset }` payload, so a cursor returned by targets can be supplied to deployments, domains, or variables, and a cursor created with one target/status filter can be reused with another. The decoder accepts it and skips that many unrelated records; include the operation plus parent/filter identity in the cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:14:07Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835691129\",\"id\":3835691129,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5\",\"original_line\":728,\"path\":\"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:14:07Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Validate the complete semantic trace shape**\\n\\nFor traces loaded from JSON rather than produced under the TypeScript type, this only checks that `environment` and `cleanup` are objects and that `result` is a string. A trace can therefore omit all required environment or cleanup fields, or use a result such as `\\\"skipped\\\"`, and still pass validation; if the golden and framework traces share the malformed shape, `runSemanticParity` can report success despite having no cleanup/environment evidence. Validate the required nested fields, value enums, and counter types before comparison.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:14:07Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835691132\",\"id\":3835691132,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5\",\"original_line\":245,\"path\":\"uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:14:07Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 21fbc39.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32564177298/job/97010256347) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"8ad9b668d13ae8354920ab8d6e4ef6f1b01eeaec\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:24:33Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835708032\",\"id\":3835708032,\"in_reply_to_id\":3835078218,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"8ad9b668d13ae8354920ab8d6e4ef6f1b01eeaec\",\"original_line\":269,\"path\":\"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:24:33Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 9307965.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32564177298/job/97010256347) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"8ad9b668d13ae8354920ab8d6e4ef6f1b01eeaec\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:24:36Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835708101\",\"id\":3835708101,\"in_reply_to_id\":3835078219,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"8ad9b668d13ae8354920ab8d6e4ef6f1b01eeaec\",\"original_line\":25,\"path\":\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:24:36Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"`ready` is snapshotted before callbacks run, so an earlier interval callback can `clearInterval()` a later ready interval, but this loop still invokes the canceled callback. I reproduced two same-deadline intervals where the first clears the second and `flush()` emits both; re-check interval liveness before invoking each entry and cover cancellation ordering so parity traces do not observe callbacks production would suppress.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:26:12Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835710808\",\"id\":3835710808,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":85,\"original_commit_id\":\"0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5\",\"original_line\":80,\"path\":\"uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:26:13Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=44d0df05-0c14-4598-be82-2f7f6eb7f22a --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=c399a9ed-1c7a-49dd-b678-501e2107db35 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: When a user continues pagination with a cursor issued by the previous HostFn version, this check rejects it because the old position contains only `offset`. Version the cursor format and provide a compatibility path for in-flight cursors so rolling deployments do not strand paginated admin pages.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/admin/src/index.ts, line 709:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a user continues pagination with a cursor issued by the previous HostFn version, this check rejects it because the old position contains only `offset`. Version the cursor format and provide a compatibility path for in-flight cursors so rolling deployments do not strand paginated admin pages.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -698,13 +698,15 @@ function pageResult(\\n-      const decoded = decodeAdminCursor\\u003c{ offset?: unknown }\\u003e(input.cursor, cursorScope);\\n+      const decoded = decodeAdminCursor\\u003c{ identity?: unknown; offset?: unknown }\\u003e(input.cursor, cursorScope);\\n       if (\\n+        decoded.identity !== identity ||\\n         typeof decoded.offset !== \\\"number\\\" ||\\n         !Number.isSafeInteger(decoded.offset) ||\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:31:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835719292\",\"id\":3835719292,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":709,\"original_commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"original_line\":709,\"path\":\"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:31:22Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=ff817218-f127-46ca-90e5-f374421973d5 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=c399a9ed-1c7a-49dd-b678-501e2107db35 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} --\\u003e\\nP2: A malformed trace can pass validation when `steps[0].kind` is a non-string object whose `toString()` returns an allowed kind. Require `typeof value === 'string'` before applying the enum check.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts, line 315:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eA malformed trace can pass validation when `steps[0].kind` is a non-string object whose `toString()` returns an allowed kind. Require `typeof value === 'string'` before applying the enum check.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -238,11 +281,103 @@ export function validateSemanticTrace(trace: unknown): readonly SemanticTraceIss\\n+  };\\n+  validateChannel('steps', {\\n+    sequence: traceNumber,\\n+    kind: (value) =\\u003e ['event', 'action', 'update', 'lifecycle'].includes(String(value)),\\n+    name: traceString,\\n+  });\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    kind: (value) =\\u003e typeof value === 'string' \\u0026\\u0026 ['event', 'action', 'update', 'lifecycle'].includes(value),\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`a422e0f`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3)\",\"commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:31:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835719295\",\"id\":3835719295,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"original_line\":315,\"path\":\"uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:48:39Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=1906f030-f94c-4b43-a53d-60632aa527a3 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=c399a9ed-1c7a-49dd-b678-501e2107db35 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: Optional trace fields are silently accepted with wrong types because the new validators omit them. Add conditional validators for every optional field so `validateSemanticTrace` fails closed instead of comparing coerced values.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts, line 313:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eOptional trace fields are silently accepted with wrong types because the new validators omit them. Add conditional validators for every optional field so `validateSemanticTrace` fails closed instead of comparing coerced values.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -238,11 +281,103 @@ export function validateSemanticTrace(trace: unknown): readonly SemanticTraceIss\\n+      if (record) nested?.(record, path);\\n+    });\\n+  };\\n+  validateChannel('steps', {\\n+    sequence: traceNumber,\\n+    kind: (value) =\\u003e ['event', 'action', 'update', 'lifecycle'].includes(String(value)),\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`a422e0f`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3)\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:31:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835719296\",\"id\":3835719296,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":331,\"original_commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"original_line\":313,\"path\":\"uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:48:38Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=3e61d8ad-a875-4aa4-8b46-d150e66d0cc5 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=c399a9ed-1c7a-49dd-b678-501e2107db35 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: Reusing an acyclic semantic-JSON object in two sibling positions incorrectly produces a schema error. Track only the active recursion path and remove objects after each branch, while keeping true cycles rejected.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts, line 242:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eReusing an acyclic semantic-JSON object in two sibling positions incorrectly produces a schema error. Track only the active recursion path and remove objects after each branch, while keeping true cycles rejected.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -226,6 +226,49 @@ function addIssue(\\n+  if (value === null || typeof value === 'string' || typeof value === 'boolean') return true;\\n+  if (typeof value === 'number') return Number.isFinite(value);\\n+  if (!value || typeof value !== 'object' || seen.has(value)) return false;\\n+  seen.add(value);\\n+  if (Array.isArray(value)) return value.every((entry) =\\u003e isSemanticJsonValue(entry, seen));\\n+  return isPlainRecord(value) \\u0026\\u0026 Object.values(value).every((entry) =\\u003e isSemanticJsonValue(entry, seen));\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`a422e0f`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3)\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:31:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835719297\",\"id\":3835719297,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":250,\"original_commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"original_line\":242,\"path\":\"uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:48:37Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 239ba00 by re-checking timer liveness before invocation and covering same-deadline cancellation.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32565032165/job/97012331150) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:32:28Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835720861\",\"id\":3835720861,\"in_reply_to_id\":3835710808,\"line\":85,\"original_commit_id\":\"0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5\",\"original_line\":80,\"path\":\"uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:32:28Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"These validators cover required members only, so malformed optional evidence such as a function in `steps[].arguments` or `parts[].parts[].tabIndex` passes validation and is then converted to `null` by `toSemanticJson()`. That lets a supposedly lossless trace be accepted after silently dropping evidence; validate every declared optional field when present and add regressions.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Optional semantic evidence bypasses validation\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts:313-341` — nested validators omit the optional fields declared by `SemanticTraceStep`, `SemanticTraceTransaction`, and `SemanticTracePart`.\\n- `uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts:201-217` — normalization rewrites invalid functions, symbols, `undefined`, bigints, Dates, and non-plain objects instead of preserving them.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Reject malformed values for every declared optional semantic-trace field when that field is present.\\n- Cover optional step, transaction, and part evidence that would otherwise be normalized lossily.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:34:26Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835723789\",\"id\":3835723789,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":331,\"original_commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"original_line\":313,\"path\":\"uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:34:27Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Preserve encoded separators in route parameter values**\\n\\nWhen a valid resource ID contains `/`, such as a BotFn ID `team/support`, the console materializes it as `team%2Fsupport`, but this nested-decoding check rejects the request before route matching. The affected schemas and services generally accept arbitrary nonempty string IDs, and collection actions can create such records, so their generated detail links and row actions become unusable; either permit encoded separators inside an already-split parameter segment or constrain all route-bound IDs accordingly.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:35:32Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835725428\",\"id\":3835725428,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"original_line\":681,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:35:32Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Bind PlugFn cursors to their collection and filters**\\n\\nWithin one scope, this cursor contains only an offset, so a cursor returned by providers can be supplied to connections, installations, workflows, or deliveries, and a cursor created under one provider/status/search filter can be reused under another. The helper accepts it and skips that many unrelated filtered records; encode the operation and normalized query identity alongside the offset and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:35:32Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835725430\",\"id\":3835725430,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"original_line\":44,\"path\":\"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:35:32Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Escape resource names in composite SearchFn targets**\\n\\nWhen a configured SearchFn resource name contains `:`, which the adapter contracts permit, a target such as `orders:v2:string:doc-1` is always split here as resource `orders`; single-document indexing and removal therefore report the valid `orders:v2` index as missing even though batch indexing and clearing can use it. The new typed ID suffix only escapes the document suffix, so the resource component also needs an unambiguous encoding or resource names must be validated as delimiter-free.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:35:32Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835725432\",\"id\":3835725432,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":111,\"original_commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"original_line\":100,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:35:32Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Reject semantically equivalent resource templates**\\n\\nWhen templates differ only in variable names, such as `https://example.test/{id}` and `https://example.test/{name}`, this literal-string comparison accepts both even though they match exactly the same URI set. `matchResource` then always selects the first registered template, making the later template's read, subscription, and completion behavior unreachable. Fresh evidence in the current code is that the new duplicate guard compares only the raw `uriTemplate` strings; compare canonicalized template patterns or otherwise reject ambiguous match languages.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:35:32Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835725434\",\"id\":3835725434,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"original_line\":187,\"path\":\"mcpfn/core/src/registry.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:35:32Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in a422e0f by validating every declared optional step, transaction, and part field.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32568555254/job/97020640348) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:51:31Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835842162\",\"id\":3835842162,\"in_reply_to_id\":3835723789,\"line\":331,\"original_commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"original_line\":313,\"path\":\"uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:51:31Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Encode resource names in composite DataFn record IDs**\\n\\nWhen a valid DataFn resource name contains `:`, such as `orders:v2`, listed records receive IDs like `orders:v2:record-1`, but `splitRecordId` interprets the resource as `orders`. Opening or mutating that listed record therefore reports the resource as missing; encode the resource component when constructing the composite ID and decode it when splitting.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:51:55Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835842745\",\"id\":3835842745,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"original_line\":232,\"path\":\"datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:51:55Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Bind BillFn cursors to their collection query**\\n\\nWhen a BillFn collection has another page, the cursor records only an offset and scope, so a cursor returned by prices can be supplied to plans or usage, and a cursor issued for one search/filter/sort can be reused after changing that query. The helper accepts it and skips the same offset in an unrelated result set; include the operation and normalized query identity in the cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:51:55Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835842746\",\"id\":3835842746,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"original_line\":86,\"path\":\"billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:51:55Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Bind SearchFn cursors to the index-list query**\\n\\nWhen the configured index list exceeds one page, changing `search`, `filter`, or `sort` while retaining a cursor still applies the old offset to the new result set because the cursor is validated only against scope. This can skip matching indexes or return an empty page even though results exist; encode the operation and normalized query identity with the offset and reject mismatched cursors.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:51:55Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835842747\",\"id\":3835842747,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"original_line\":73,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:51:55Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Deleting the object from this validator's set now correctly accepts shared acyclic values, but `toSemanticJson()` keeps completed objects in its own `seen` set and rewrites the second reference as `\\\"[circular]\\\"`. This makes the new test pass while `normalizeSemanticTrace()` still corrupts accepted trace state.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Shared acyclic trace values normalize as cycles\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts:201-217` — `toSemanticJson()` never removes an object after finishing its subtree.\\n- `uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts:238-247` — validation now intentionally accepts reused acyclic values.\\n- `uifn/adapter-kit/src/__tests__/conformance.test.ts:182-193` — the new regression asserts validation only and does not exercise normalization.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Reused acyclic JSON values must remain intact through `normalizeSemanticTrace()` while true cycles remain rejected.\\n- Extend the regression to assert the normalized state, not only an empty validator issue list.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:53:17Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835845050\",\"id\":3835845050,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":254,\"original_commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"original_line\":246,\"path\":\"uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:53:17Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=7cf387f1-d0e8-4020-bd99-35da513e2481 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=851c703b-f91e-40a3-9120-49bce4958eb2 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":6} --\\u003e\\nP2: This removal leaves the single-encoded-slash-in-literal-segment case untested. The parser now preserves a depth-0 single-encoded slash as the raw segment, so `/modules/examplefn/records%2fother` returns 404 rather than the 400 this removed case asserted; the new test only covers `%2F` inside a route parameter. Keep the literal-position case covered with an explicit 404 assertion so a future refactor that decodes segments before route matching cannot silently reintroduce the slash/path ambiguity this suite exists to fence.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts, line 359:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThis removal leaves the single-encoded-slash-in-literal-segment case untested. The parser now preserves a depth-0 single-encoded slash as the raw segment, so `/modules/examplefn/records%2fother` returns 404 rather than the 400 this removed case asserted; the new test only covers `%2F` inside a route parameter. Keep the literal-position case covered with an explicit 404 assertion so a future refactor that decodes segments before route matching cannot silently reintroduce the slash/path ambiguity this suite exists to fence.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -356,7 +356,6 @@ describe('Super Console server composition', () =\\u003e {\\n     '/api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn//records',\\n     '/api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/%252e%252e/records',\\n-    '/api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/records%2fother',\\n     '/api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/records%252fother',\\n     '/api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/records%5cother',\\n     '/api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/records%255cother',\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`593b81f`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a)\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:54:51Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835847367\",\"id\":3835847367,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":1,\"original_commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"original_line\":1,\"path\":\"superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:05:43Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=bd434ffb-3e7a-4460-9065-53e2a2e8a282 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=851c703b-f91e-40a3-9120-49bce4958eb2 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When two operators share an admin scope but map to different PlugFn users or organizations, a cursor from one owner-filtered list is accepted for the other. Its offset can then skip the second operator's first records or return an empty page; include the mapped user, organization, and tenant in the cursor identity for every owner-scoped list.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 349:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen two operators share an admin scope but map to different PlugFn users or organizations, a cursor from one owner-filtered list is accepted for the other. Its offset can then skip the second operator's first records or return an empty page; include the mapped user, organization, and tenant in the cursor identity for every owner-scoped list.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -313,7 +342,12 @@ export function createPlugFnDomainAdminService(options: PlugFnDomainAdminService\\n+        values.map(connectionView),\\n+        input,\\n+        context,\\n+        pageIdentity(\\\"plugfn.connections.list\\\", input.provider, input.status),\\n+      );\\n     },\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`593b81f`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a)\",\"commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:54:51Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835847368\",\"id\":3835847368,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"original_line\":349,\"path\":\"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:05:38Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=d7b6dc26-30aa-459a-bf01-fbdef5c09f2f --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=851c703b-f91e-40a3-9120-49bce4958eb2 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: When a registry uses an RFC 6570 `;` path-parameter template, this normalizer treats it as a simple expansion and can reject a distinct valid template as a duplicate. Recognize `;` and preserve its variable names like query operators so templates such as `docs://users/{id}` and `docs://users/{;name}` can coexist.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/core/src/registry.ts, line 45:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a registry uses an RFC 6570 `;` path-parameter template, this normalizer treats it as a simple expansion and can reject a distinct valid template as a duplicate. Recognize `;` and preserve its variable names like query operators so templates such as `docs://users/{id}` and `docs://users/{;name}` can coexist.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -37,6 +37,19 @@ interface RegisteredPrompt\\u003cTContext\\u003e {\\n+\\n+function resourceTemplatePattern(uriTemplate: string): string {\\n+  return uriTemplate.replace(/\\\\{([^{}]+)\\\\}/g, (_expression, body: string) =\\u003e {\\n+    const operator = /^[+#./?\\u0026]/.exec(body)?.[0] ?? \\\"\\\";\\n+    if (operator === \\\"?\\\" || operator === \\\"\\u0026\\\") return `{${body}}`;\\n+    const variables = body.slice(operator.length).split(\\\",\\\").map((variable, index) =\\u003e {\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    const operator = /^[+#./?\\u0026;]/.exec(body)?.[0] ?? \\\"\\\";\\n    if (operator === \\\"?\\\" || operator === \\\"\\u0026\\\" || operator === \\\";\\\") return `{${body}}`;\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`593b81f`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a)\",\"commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:54:51Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835847369\",\"id\":3835847369,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":46,\"original_commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"original_line\":46,\"path\":\"mcpfn/core/src/registry.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:05:36Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=ed24e7bd-27eb-4f23-941d-5952226d0763 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=851c703b-f91e-40a3-9120-49bce4958eb2 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":7} --\\u003e\\nP2: When an encoded separator is followed by nested encoding, this early return bypasses nested-encoding validation and leaves an ambiguously encoded value for downstream route handling. Reject nested encodings before preserving a single encoded separator, or validate the remaining segment before returning it.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts, line 686:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen an encoded separator is followed by nested encoding, this early return bypasses nested-encoding validation and leaves an ambiguously encoded value for downstream route handling. Reject nested encodings before preserving a single encoded separator, or validate the remaining segment before returning it.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -677,9 +677,13 @@ export class SuperConsole {\\n+        if (unsafeDecodedSegment || (depth \\u003e 0 \\u0026\\u0026 next.includes('/'))) {\\n           throw new SuperConsoleHttpError('The administration path contains an unsafe segment.', { status: 400, code: 'INVALID_ADMIN_PATH' });\\n         }\\n+        if (depth === 0 \\u0026\\u0026 next.includes('/')) return segment;\\n         if (next === decoded) return segment;\\n         decoded = next;\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`593b81f`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a)\",\"commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:54:51Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835847374\",\"id\":3835847374,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"original_line\":686,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:05:35Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=7f520206-3cf3-4dbc-b4f7-1a130ff72724 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=851c703b-f91e-40a3-9120-49bce4958eb2 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":7} --\\u003e\\nP3: Both new/changed asserts hardcode the cursor identity string that pageIdentity() in domain-service.ts generates, duplicating its filter-order contract. Adding or reordering a captured filter in pageIdentity (e.g., a new sync-jobs filter) silently drifts these tests, and the mismatch error will not point at the real cause. Construct the identity from the same source (export a shared helper) or generate the cursor from a real first page's nextCursor instead of hand-writing the JSON.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At plugfn/admin/src/__tests__/admin.test.ts, line 212:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eBoth new/changed asserts hardcode the cursor identity string that pageIdentity() in domain-service.ts generates, duplicating its filter-order contract. Adding or reordering a captured filter in pageIdentity (e.g., a new sync-jobs filter) silently drifts these tests, and the mismatch error will not point at the real cause. Construct the identity from the same source (export a shared helper) or generate the cursor from a real first page's nextCursor instead of hand-writing the JSON.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -206,10 +206,28 @@ describe(\\\"@plugfn/admin\\\", () =\\u003e {\\n+    await service.listSyncJobs({\\n+      limit: 100,\\n+      cursor: encodeAdminCursor(context.scope, {\\n+        identity: JSON.stringify([\\\"plugfn.sync-jobs.list\\\", null, null, null, null]),\\n+        offset: forgedOffset,\\n+      }),\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`593b81f`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a)\",\"commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:54:51Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835847375\",\"id\":3835847375,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"original_line\":212,\"path\":\"plugfn/admin/src/__tests__/admin.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:05:44Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=3d1d067b-69bd-4446-8056-3fbbbce5be6f --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=851c703b-f91e-40a3-9120-49bce4958eb2 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP3: The colon-encoded remove-document has no assertion on its effect, unlike every other mutation in this test. If removal silently missed the decoded resource, the test would still pass. Add a search assertion for resource \\\"orders:v2\\\" expecting [] after the remove.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At searchfn/admin/src/__tests__/admin.test.ts, line 185:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThe colon-encoded remove-document has no assertion on its effect, unlike every other mutation in this test. If removal silently missed the decoded resource, the test would still pass. Add a search assertion for resource \\\"orders:v2\\\" expecting [] after the remove.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -171,6 +171,20 @@ describe(\\\"@searchfn/admin\\\", () =\\u003e {\\n+    }, context);\\n+    await expect(adapters.get(\\\"environment_1\\\")!.search({ resource: \\\"orders:v2\\\", query: \\\"Versioned\\\" }))\\n+      .resolves.toEqual([\\\"doc-1\\\"]);\\n+    await colonAdapter.execute(\\\"searchfn.documents.remove-document\\\", {\\n+      id: \\\"orders%3Av2:string:doc-1\\\",\\n+    }, context);\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`593b81f`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a)\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:54:51Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835847378\",\"id\":3835847378,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":204,\"original_commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"original_line\":185,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/__tests__/admin.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:05:45Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=592811c9-d3d3-4d77-a8e6-8403eabb3d87 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=851c703b-f91e-40a3-9120-49bce4958eb2 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} --\\u003e\\nP3: The preceding separator check guarantees `resource` is non-empty, and `decodeURIComponent(resource)` cannot return an empty string; this validation branch is unreachable. Remove the redundant branch.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 111:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThe preceding separator check guarantees `resource` is non-empty, and `decodeURIComponent(resource)` cannot return an empty string; this validation branch is unreachable. Remove the redundant branch.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -102,14 +102,23 @@ function splitDocumentId(value: string): { resource: string; id: string | number\\n+  } catch (error) {\\n+    throw new AdminError(\\\"invalid_argument\\\", \\\"SearchFn resource names must be percent-encoded in document targets.\\\", { cause: error });\\n+  }\\n+  if (!decodedResource) {\\n+    throw new AdminError(\\\"invalid_argument\\\", \\\"SearchFn document target resource names must be non-empty.\\\");\\n+  }\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`593b81f`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a)\",\"commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:54:51Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835847379\",\"id\":3835847379,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"original_line\":111,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:05:46Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Synchronize the Textarea value binding on input**\\n\\nWhen a consumer uses the advertised `bind:value` API and types into this textarea, the bound variable is never updated: `value` is declared bindable and forwarded to `PrimitiveRoot`, but unlike the generated Input root, no `input` handler assigns the DOM value back to it. The parent therefore retains the initial value, and a later reactive update can overwrite what the user typed; install an input handler that updates `value` while preserving the consumer's handler.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871106\",\"id\":3835871106,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":10,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":10,\"path\":\"uifn/svelte/lib/generated/textarea/Root.svelte\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Classify malformed OpenAPI documents as invalid input**\\n\\nWhen `document` contains malformed YAML, lacks an OpenAPI version, or declares an unsupported version, `parseOpenAPI` throws a plain `Error` here. `AdminDispatcher` normalizes plain errors to `internal`, so expected client validation failures from both registration and the analogous comparison path become HTTP 500 responses instead of actionable `invalid_argument` responses; catch parse failures and translate them to an admin input error.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871110\",\"id\":3835871110,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":189,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":189,\"path\":\"apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Bind ApiFn cursors to scope and collection**\\n\\nWhen a cursor from specs, another project, or another installation is supplied to the environments list (or vice versa), this accepts it as a raw offset and silently skips that many records in the unrelated collection. Since the cursor carries neither scope nor operation identity, ordinary scope changes while retaining the URL cursor can produce empty or incomplete pages; encode and validate the active scope and collection with the offset.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871113\",\"id\":3835871113,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":154,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":154,\"path\":\"apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Bind BotFn cursors to the channel filter and scope**\\n\\nWhen a channel cursor is reused after changing `botId`, or a bots/channel cursor is reused in another collection or project, this raw numeric offset remains valid and skips records from the new result set. This makes filtered pagination return incomplete or terminal-looking pages even when matching records exist; include the operation, scope, and `botId` query identity in the cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871115\",\"id\":3835871115,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":167,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":167,\"path\":\"botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=e5c4adf4-ac55-4511-8b95-044570f04cee --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=5a311de1-61b7-4d68-8481-4dcf664e4fbd --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When callers omit a sort direction or send a descriptor without a field, the comparator uses the same effective ordering but the cursor identity changes. Build the identity from normalized effective sort descriptors so equivalent page requests can continue.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 92:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen callers omit a sort direction or send a descriptor without a field, the comparator uses the same effective ordering but the cursor identity changes. Build the identity from normalized effective sort descriptors so equivalent page requests can continue.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -83,16 +85,27 @@ function list(\\n+    operationId,\\n+    input.search?.trim().toLowerCase(),\\n+    input.filter,\\n+    input.sort ?? [],\\n+  );\\n+  const decoded = input.cursor\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    sorts.filter((descriptor) =\\u003e Boolean(descriptor.field)).map((descriptor) =\\u003e ({ field: descriptor.field, direction: descriptor.direction === \\\"desc\\\" ? \\\"desc\\\" : \\\"asc\\\" })),\\n```\",\"commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871239\",\"id\":3835871239,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":92,\"path\":\"billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=a0aefc6f-f5d8-4c86-9345-c905ad6bb840 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=5a311de1-61b7-4d68-8481-4dcf664e4fbd --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When `search` is empty or whitespace-only, filtering treats it as no search but the cursor identity treats it differently, so an equivalent next-page request is rejected. Normalize empty searches to `undefined` before computing the identity.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 90:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen `search` is empty or whitespace-only, filtering treats it as no search but the cursor identity treats it differently, so an equivalent next-page request is rejected. Normalize empty searches to `undefined` before computing the identity.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -83,16 +85,27 @@ function list(\\n-  const decoded = input.cursor ? decodeAdminCursor\\u003c{ offset?: unknown }\\u003e(input.cursor, context.scope) : { offset: 0 };\\n+  const identity = adminPageIdentity(\\n+    operationId,\\n+    input.search?.trim().toLowerCase(),\\n+    input.filter,\\n+    input.sort ?? [],\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    input.search?.trim() ? input.search.trim().toLowerCase() : undefined,\\n```\",\"commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871252\",\"id\":3835871252,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":90,\"path\":\"billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=450e93a2-581c-40f6-a6a3-6bef44f4564c --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=5a311de1-61b7-4d68-8481-4dcf664e4fbd --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: During a rolling deployment, a page cursor issued by the previous server contains only `offset`, so this check rejects the next-page request. Version the cursor schema and retain a compatibility path while old cursors drain, or explicitly handle restart semantics instead of invalidating `version: 1` tokens silently.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 85:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eDuring a rolling deployment, a page cursor issued by the previous server contains only `offset`, so this check rejects the next-page request. Version the cursor schema and retain a compatibility path while old cursors drain, or explicitly handle restart semantics instead of invalidating `version: 1` tokens silently.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -68,12 +70,21 @@ function list(\\n   if (!decoded || typeof decoded !== \\\"object\\\" || Array.isArray(decoded)) {\\n     throw new AdminError(\\\"invalid_argument\\\", \\\"The SearchFn cursor is invalid.\\\");\\n   }\\n+  if (decoded.identity !== identity) {\\n+    throw new AdminError(\\\"invalid_argument\\\", \\\"The SearchFn cursor does not belong to this index-list query.\\\");\\n+  }\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871253\",\"id\":3835871253,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":85,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":85,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:40Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=fa774002-8729-4340-86d5-dfb6dadbd47a --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=5a311de1-61b7-4d68-8481-4dcf664e4fbd --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP3: `listAdapters` uses an operation identity that is not declared or registered. Use `searchfn.adapters-backends.list` so operation-bound cursor validation remains consistent.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 186:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003e`listAdapters` uses an operation identity that is not declared or registered. Use `searchfn.adapters-backends.list` so operation-bound cursor validation remains consistent.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -175,7 +183,7 @@ export function createSearchFnDomainAdminService(\\n     async listAdapters(input, context) {\\n       const { adapterInfo } = await state(context);\\n-      return list([adapterInfo], input, context);\\n+      return list([adapterInfo], input, context, \\\"searchfn.adapters.list\\\");\\n     },\\n     async getAdapter(input, context) {\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n      return list([adapterInfo], input, context, \\\"searchfn.adapters-backends.list\\\");\\n```\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871255\",\"id\":3835871255,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":186,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":186,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:40Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=f7498236-c489-4984-96df-d2d54653cc76 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=5a311de1-61b7-4d68-8481-4dcf664e4fbd --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP3: 'does not route an encoded separator embedded in a literal segment' passes even if the server treated %2f as a real route separator: decoded or not, records%2fother matches no registered route, so the 404/OPERATION_NOT_ENABLED assertions cannot detect a routing regression. Use a path whose over-decoded form would hit a real route, e.g. /api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/resources%2frecords (would dispatch the records handler if %2f were split), and keep asserting 404 and handler not called.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts, line 382:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003e'does not route an encoded separator embedded in a literal segment' passes even if the server treated %2f as a real route separator: decoded or not, records%2fother matches no registered route, so the 404/OPERATION_NOT_ENABLED assertions cannot detect a routing regression. Use a path whose over-decoded form would hit a real route, e.g. /api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/resources%2frecords (would dispatch the records handler if %2f were split), and keep asserting 404 and handler not called.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -376,6 +377,14 @@ describe('Super Console server composition', () =\\u003e {\\n \\n+  it('does not route an encoded separator embedded in a literal segment', async () =\\u003e {\\n+    const { console, handler } = installation();\\n+    const result = await console.handle(request('/api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/records%2fother'));\\n+    expect(result.status).toBe(404);\\n+    expect(await result.json()).toMatchObject({ error: { code: 'OPERATION_NOT_ENABLED' } });\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    const result = await console.handle(request('/api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/resources%2frecords'));\\n```\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871257\",\"id\":3835871257,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":384,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":382,\"path\":\"superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:40Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=c633d0b9-3d7c-4b6c-b47b-f287eeab08e9 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=5a311de1-61b7-4d68-8481-4dcf664e4fbd --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":5} --\\u003e\\nP3: The cursor identity is produced by `stableSerialize`, which sorts object keys with `localeCompare`. That ordering depends on the process locale and ICU version, so a cursor identity computed by one server process (or before a redeploy) can fail strict equality against the same query recomputed by another process, rejecting valid cursors with \\\"does not belong to this collection query.\\\" Sort keys by UTF-16 code units (`.sort()` default or `(a,b) =\\u003e a \\u003c b ? -1 : a \\u003e b ? 1 : 0`) so identities are reproducible across processes.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/pagination.ts, line 47:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThe cursor identity is produced by `stableSerialize`, which sorts object keys with `localeCompare`. That ordering depends on the process locale and ICU version, so a cursor identity computed by one server process (or before a redeploy) can fail strict equality against the same query recomputed by another process, rejecting valid cursors with \\\"does not belong to this collection query.\\\" Sort keys by UTF-16 code units (`.sort()` default or `(a,b) =\\u003e a \\u003c b ? -1 : a \\u003e b ? 1 : 0`) so identities are reproducible across processes.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -42,6 +42,11 @@ export function decodeAdminCursor\\u003cT\\u003e(cursor: string, expectedScope: AdminScope):\\n \\n+/** Canonical identity for binding an offset cursor to one operation and query. */\\n+export function adminPageIdentity(operationId: string, ...query: unknown[]): string {\\n+  return stableSerialize([operationId, ...query.map((value) =\\u003e value ?? null)]);\\n+}\\n+\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871260\",\"id\":3835871260,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":47,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/pagination.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:40Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 593b81f by removing completed objects from the recursion set and asserting normalized shared state.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32569323032/job/97022407951) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:48Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871423\",\"id\":3835871423,\"in_reply_to_id\":3835845050,\"line\":254,\"original_commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"original_line\":246,\"path\":\"uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:48Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"The pinned SDK 1.25.2 does not recognize `;` as an operator, so both `docs://users/{id}` and the newly allowed `docs://users/{;name}` use its ordinary-variable matcher and accept `docs://users/;name=alice`. Because `matchResource()` returns the first match, handler selection now depends on registration order; keep these registrations conflicting or reject unsupported semicolon templates until matching has real RFC 6570 matrix-parameter semantics.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Semicolon templates create ambiguous resource dispatch\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `mcpfn/core/src/registry.ts:43-51` — duplicate detection now treats `;` as a supported, name-bearing operator.\\n- `mcpfn/core/src/registry.ts:212-225` — the two overlapping templates are accepted into the registry.\\n- `mcpfn/core/src/registry.ts:461-463` — resource dispatch returns the first template whose SDK matcher succeeds.\\n- `mcpfn/core/tests/protocol.test.ts:49-64` — the regression asserts only that both templates register, not which handler receives an overlapping URI.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Any two templates accepted by the registry must not match the same concrete URI under the pinned SDK's actual `UriTemplate.match()` implementation.\\n- Semicolon path-parameter syntax must either be rejected fail-closed or parsed and matched with its RFC 6570 semantics.\\n\\n## Suggested approach\\n- Under SDK 1.25.2, retain the prior collision behavior for `;` expressions and add a read regression for `docs://users/;name=alice`; alternatively, replace the matcher before recognizing `;` as a distinct operator.\\n\\n## Contract evidence\\n- SDK 1.25.2 omits `;` from `getOperator()` and compiles the resulting ordinary variable with `([^/,]+)`: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/v1.25.2/src/shared/uriTemplate.ts\\n- RFC 6570 defines `{;var}` as path-style parameter expansion: https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6570.html#section-3.2.7\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:16:36Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835880268\",\"id\":3835880268,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":46,\"path\":\"mcpfn/core/src/registry.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:16:37Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Forward undeclared native attributes to the DOM**\\n\\nWhen a consumer supplies a valid native attribute that is not in `ROOT_DOM_PROP`, such as `pattern`, `form`, `maxlength`, `inputmode`, or an anchor's `download`, this fallback classifies it as a controller input instead of a DOM prop. Because the generated component types advertise the full native element interface but the corresponding contracts do not project these undeclared inputs, the attribute disappears from the rendered element, breaking browser validation and native behavior; undeclared properties should be forwarded to `dom` rather than `inputs`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"5e968d705663c2a2f4ab0e63d3bf45948824ad9b\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:19:40Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835884895\",\"id\":3835884895,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"5e968d705663c2a2f4ab0e63d3bf45948824ad9b\",\"original_line\":135,\"path\":\"uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:19:40Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Sort HostFn records before applying offset cursors**\\n\\nWhen a durable `HostFnOperatorStore` returns the same records in a different order between requests—as database queries without an explicit ordering may—this slices the raw array by offset, so later cursor pages can duplicate or skip records even when the collection itself is unchanged. The store interface promises no ordering, and all HostFn collections share this helper; establish a deterministic tie-broken order before slicing.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"5e968d705663c2a2f4ab0e63d3bf45948824ad9b\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:19:40Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835884897\",\"id\":3835884897,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"5e968d705663c2a2f4ab0e63d3bf45948824ad9b\",\"original_line\":724,\"path\":\"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:19:40Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Clone HostFn records returned from the memory store**\\n\\nWhen a caller—or the supplied deployment executor, which receives objects obtained through these methods—mutates a returned target or deployment, the mutation changes the object held inside the memory store without calling `put*`. Changing an ID or scope is especially damaging because the map key then disagrees with the stored value; clone records on reads and lists just as this store already does on writes.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"5e968d705663c2a2f4ab0e63d3bf45948824ad9b\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:19:40Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835884899\",\"id\":3835884899,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"5e968d705663c2a2f4ab0e63d3bf45948824ad9b\",\"original_line\":139,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:19:40Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=c9db29b1-0333-4e1b-82f8-88a651137fe5 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=565efb3e-1cfe-4884-a6da-1f223d760f97 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: When a record’s `updatedAt` changes between page requests, this offset cursor no longer identifies the same page boundary, so records can be skipped or repeated. Sort by an immutable key such as `id`, or switch this cursor to a keyset containing the sort key.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/admin/src/index.ts, line 727:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a record’s `updatedAt` changes between page requests, this offset cursor no longer identifies the same page boundary, so records can be skipped or repeated. Sort by an immutable key such as `id`, or switch this cursor to a keyset containing the sort key.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -721,12 +721,19 @@ function pageResult(\\n+  const orderedItems = [...items].sort((left, right) =\\u003e {\\n+    const leftItem = left as { updatedAt?: unknown; createdAt?: unknown; id?: unknown };\\n+    const rightItem = right as { updatedAt?: unknown; createdAt?: unknown; id?: unknown };\\n+    const timestamp = String(leftItem.updatedAt ?? leftItem.createdAt ?? \\\"\\\")\\n+      .localeCompare(String(rightItem.updatedAt ?? rightItem.createdAt ?? \\\"\\\"));\\n+    return timestamp || String(leftItem.id ?? \\\"\\\").localeCompare(String(rightItem.id ?? \\\"\\\"));\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    return String(leftItem.id ?? \\\"\\\").localeCompare(String(rightItem.id ?? \\\"\\\"));\\n```\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:40:41Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835919209\",\"id\":3835919209,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":729,\"original_commit_id\":\"b2718e4ed53dd5ee5e04dac45c917bba478d3a1c\",\"original_line\":729,\"path\":\"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:40:42Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=20fe96ed-7e64-411c-a84c-55ae85627760 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=565efb3e-1cfe-4884-a6da-1f223d760f97 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} --\\u003e\\nP2: When `DateInput` or `DatePicker` receives valid controller props such as `calendar` or `messages`, this branch classifies them as DOM props because the generated `inputNames` metadata omits them. The controller is therefore created without the requested calendar or messages, so formatting and accessibility text fall back to defaults; make generated controller input metadata exhaustive before routing undeclared props to the DOM.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts, line 131:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen `DateInput` or `DatePicker` receives valid controller props such as `calendar` or `messages`, this branch classifies them as DOM props because the generated `inputNames` metadata omits them. The controller is therefore created without the requested calendar or messages, so formatting and accessibility text fall back to defaults; make generated controller input metadata exhaustive before routing undeclared props to the DOM.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -131,8 +128,7 @@ export function splitSvelteRootProps(props: AnyRecord, inputNames: readonly stri\\n     else if (declaredInputs.has(key) || /^on[A-Z]/.test(key)) inputs[key] = value;\\n-    else if (ROOT_DOM_PROP.test(key) || ROOT_EVENT_PROP.test(key)) dom[key] = value;\\n-    else inputs[key] = value;\\n+    else dom[key] = value;\\n   }\\n   return { inputs, dom, environment };\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`c6aea5c`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/c6aea5c7b1c3b023d51510b821e61b7a7f17b32f)\",\"commit_id\":\"b2718e4ed53dd5ee5e04dac45c917bba478d3a1c\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:40:42Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835919210\",\"id\":3835919210,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"b2718e4ed53dd5ee5e04dac45c917bba478d3a1c\",\"original_line\":131,\"path\":\"uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:55:49Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=545b26c9-3780-4967-8f60-c4ad37a8b621 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=565efb3e-1cfe-4884-a6da-1f223d760f97 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":6} --\\u003e\\nP2: This new assertion codifies a false-positive duplicate: `docs://users/{;name}` is rejected as a duplicate of `docs://users/{id}` only because `resourceTemplatePattern`'s operator set `[+#./?\\u0026]` omits `;`, so `{;name}` normalizes to `{v0}` like `{id}`. `;` is a valid RFC 6570 operator; sections prefixed this way match `docs://users/;name=...`, distinct from plain-segment matches. Valid template forms using `{;...}` are now rejected with a misleading \\\"Duplicate ... URI\\\" error. Add `;` to the operator set in registry.ts so `{;v0}` is kept and genuinely overlapping matrix templates still collide; if `;` templates are instead intentionally unsupported, reject them with an explicit message and code rather than a duplicate error.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/core/tests/protocol.test.ts, line 64:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThis new assertion codifies a false-positive duplicate: `docs://users/{;name}` is rejected as a duplicate of `docs://users/{id}` only because `resourceTemplatePattern`'s operator set `[+#./?\\u0026]` omits `;`, so `{;name}` normalizes to `{v0}` like `{id}`. `;` is a valid RFC 6570 operator; sections prefixed this way match `docs://users/;name=...`, distinct from plain-segment matches. Valid template forms using `{;...}` are now rejected with a misleading \\\"Duplicate ... URI\\\" error. Add `;` to the operator set in registry.ts so `{;v0}` is kept and genuinely overlapping matrix templates still collide; if `;` templates are instead intentionally unsupported, reject them with an explicit message and code rather than a duplicate error.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ describe(\\\"McpFn protocol primitives\\\", () =\\u003e {\\n       name: \\\"matrix-account\\\",\\n       read: async (uri) =\\u003e ({ contents: [{ uri: uri.toString(), text: \\\"matrix\\\" }] }),\\n-    })).not.toThrow();\\n+    })).toThrow(\\\"Duplicate MCP resource template URI: docs://users/{;name}\\\");\\n   });\\n \\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:40:42Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835919214\",\"id\":3835919214,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":64,\"original_commit_id\":\"b2718e4ed53dd5ee5e04dac45c917bba478d3a1c\",\"original_line\":64,\"path\":\"mcpfn/core/tests/protocol.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:40:42Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=daa00630-654a-4c6b-9dfd-82a4af6ed2c9 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=565efb3e-1cfe-4884-a6da-1f223d760f97 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP3: scoped() now deep-clones every element before listDeployments/listDomains/listVariables apply their targetId filter, so entries that get discarded are cloned wastefully (and listVariables transiently clones the stored secret value before stripping it). Filter by targetId first, then clone only what is returned.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts, line 122:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003escoped() now deep-clones every element before listDeployments/listDomains/listVariables apply their targetId filter, so entries that get discarded are cloned wastefully (and listVariables transiently clones the stored secret value before stripping it). Filter by targetId first, then clone only what is returned.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -117,7 +117,9 @@ function scoped\\u003cT extends { scope: HostFnScope }\\u003e(\\n-  return [...values].filter((value) =\\u003e scopeKey(value.scope) === key);\\n+  return [...values]\\n+    .filter((value) =\\u003e scopeKey(value.scope) === key)\\n+    .map((value) =\\u003e structuredClone(value));\\n }\\n \\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:40:42Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835919215\",\"id\":3835919215,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":130,\"original_commit_id\":\"b2718e4ed53dd5ee5e04dac45c917bba478d3a1c\",\"original_line\":122,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:40:42Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Preserve numeric types in composite record IDs**\\n\\nWhen a DataFn row has a numeric ID, `compositeRecordId` serializes it indistinguishably from a string ID and this parser always restores it as a string. Consequently, opening a listed numeric-ID record queries with `filters.id = \\\"42\\\"` rather than `42`, and mutation validation rejects a numeric `payload.id`; encode the ID type in the composite target and restore it when splitting.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835922082\",\"id\":3835922082,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":140,\"original_commit_id\":\"b2718e4ed53dd5ee5e04dac45c917bba478d3a1c\",\"original_line\":145,\"path\":\"datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Bind metadata cursors to their DataFn collection**\\n\\nWhen a scope has enough metadata for pagination, the cursor returned by resources, relations, indices, or capabilities contains only an offset and scope, so it can be reused in any of the other collections. The receiving operation accepts it and skips the same number of unrelated records, yielding incomplete or empty pages; include the metadata operation or collection identity in this cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835922087\",\"id\":3835922087,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":64,\"original_commit_id\":\"b2718e4ed53dd5ee5e04dac45c917bba478d3a1c\",\"original_line\":63,\"path\":\"datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Resolve queued deployments when scheduling fails**\\n\\nWhen `executor.deploy` rejects before accepting a deployment, the record has already been persisted as `queued`, and this path neither marks it failed nor removes it. The request returns an error while subsequent deployment lists continue reporting a job that will never run, so persist a terminal/unknown outcome or otherwise reconcile the record on executor failure.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835922091\",\"id\":3835922091,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":262,\"original_commit_id\":\"b2718e4ed53dd5ee5e04dac45c917bba478d3a1c\",\"original_line\":243,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in b2718e4 by rejecting the conflicting semicolon template registration.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32570683228/job/97025594358) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:47:10Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835938234\",\"id\":3835938234,\"in_reply_to_id\":3835880268,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":46,\"path\":\"mcpfn/core/src/registry.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:47:10Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Distinct accepted IDs can compare equal under `localeCompare`, for example composed `é` and decomposed `e\\\\u0301`. When timestamps tie and the backing store changes their input order between requests, offset slicing can duplicate one record and omit another, so this needs a locale-independent total tie-breaker.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# HostFn pagination lacks a total tie-breaker\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `hostfn/admin/src/index.ts:724-729` — the final comparison can return zero for distinct IDs accepted by the manifest.\\n- `hostfn/admin/src/__tests__/admin.test.ts:160-201` — the reordering regression covers only ASCII IDs whose comparisons are nonzero.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Define a strict, locale-independent total order for every accepted HostFn ID before applying an offset cursor.\\n- Cover distinct equal-collation IDs under a store that changes result order between page requests.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:49:44Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835946128\",\"id\":3835946128,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":729,\"original_commit_id\":\"b2718e4ed53dd5ee5e04dac45c917bba478d3a1c\",\"original_line\":729,\"path\":\"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:49:44Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Bind MCP cursors to the list operation**\\n\\nWhen a cursor returned by `tools/list` is supplied to `prompts/list`, `resources/list`, or `resources/templates/list`, this shared decoder accepts it as the same raw offset and skips entries in the unrelated collection; the same problem occurs when a visibility-dependent tools/resources list changes between requests. Include the list method and relevant query/context identity in the opaque cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"c6aea5c7b1c3b023d51510b821e61b7a7f17b32f\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:01:56Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835986662\",\"id\":3835986662,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"c6aea5c7b1c3b023d51510b821e61b7a7f17b32f\",\"original_line\":104,\"path\":\"mcpfn/core/src/server.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:01:56Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Expose read-classified resource actions**\\n\\nWhen a resource has a non-list/get read operation, this filter removes it from the only detail-page action projection. In the inspected manifests this makes `filefn.files.download`, `filefn.artifacts.download`, and `apifn.specs.compare` unreachable from the generic Super Console UI even though their capabilities are enabled; distinguish read actions from canonical list/detail reads rather than dropping every read-classified operation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:01:56Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835986673\",\"id\":3835986673,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":395,\"original_commit_id\":\"c6aea5c7b1c3b023d51510b821e61b7a7f17b32f\",\"original_line\":395,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:01:56Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Reject malformed token leaves before recursing**\\n\\nWhen a runtime-loaded theme contains a partial token such as `{ $type: 'color' }` without `$value`, `isDesignToken` returns false and this recursively treats the token—and then its scalar `$type` string—as token groups until the stack overflows. Consequently `assertTokenShape` never emits the advertised `UIFnTokenError` for exactly the malformed input it is meant to validate; verify that non-token nodes are plain group objects before descending.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:01:56Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835986675\",\"id\":3835986675,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":161,\"original_commit_id\":\"c6aea5c7b1c3b023d51510b821e61b7a7f17b32f\",\"original_line\":161,\"path\":\"uifn/tokens/src/schema.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:01:56Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Because this branch returns `false` without `document`, standard attributes absent from the static lists, such as `accesskey`, are omitted from SSR but added after browser prototype discovery. This makes the rendered root differ across server and browser execution and can cause hydration warnings or a late attribute change.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Native prop routing is not SSR-deterministic\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts:102-124` — server execution cannot use the browser prototype fallback.\\n- `uifn/svelte/lib/internal/PrimitiveRoot.svelte:49-55,93-95` — only `split.dom` reaches the rendered root spread.\\n- `uifn/svelte/tests/root-props.test.ts:5-23` — coverage exercises only statically allowlisted attributes.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Classify valid native root attributes identically with and without `document`.\\n- Add SSR/browser parity coverage for a standard attribute outside the current static lists, such as `accesskey`.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"c6aea5c7b1c3b023d51510b821e61b7a7f17b32f\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:05:19Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835996676\",\"id\":3835996676,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"c6aea5c7b1c3b023d51510b821e61b7a7f17b32f\",\"original_line\":109,\"path\":\"uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:05:20Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=c8b82495-11b1-4a7f-ab5e-ba68ce67659d --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=22be5463-3f8c-4e83-93ac-026ff63a485e --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When a root receives normalized `aria`, `data`, or `on` objects, this branch routes them into controller inputs and drops the corresponding DOM props. Classify these adapter keys as DOM props before the fallback.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts, line 156:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a root receives normalized `aria`, `data`, or `on` objects, this branch routes them into controller inputs and drops the corresponding DOM props. Classify these adapter keys as DOM props before the fallback.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -128,7 +153,11 @@ export function splitSvelteRootProps(props: AnyRecord, inputNames: readonly stri\\n     if (key === 'environment') environment = value as UIFnEnvironment | undefined;\\n     else if (declaredInputs.has(key) || /^on[A-Z]/.test(key)) inputs[key] = value;\\n-    else dom[key] = value;\\n+    else if (ROOT_DOM_PROP.test(key) || ROOT_EVENT_PROP.test(key)) dom[key] = value;\\n+    else {\\n+      inputs[key] = value;\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    else if (key === 'aria' || key === 'data' || key === 'on' || ROOT_DOM_PROP.test(key) || ROOT_EVENT_PROP.test(key)) dom[key] = value;\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`358c4d2`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/358c4d2bec007a1e6c8a738302df38e03a6281e4)\",\"commit_id\":\"c6aea5c7b1c3b023d51510b821e61b7a7f17b32f\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:05:26Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835996858\",\"id\":3835996858,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"c6aea5c7b1c3b023d51510b821e61b7a7f17b32f\",\"original_line\":156,\"path\":\"uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:19:38Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=29c934f3-2f72-4b36-83e3-245254b139cf --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=22be5463-3f8c-4e83-93ac-026ff63a485e --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: During SSR, standard native attributes not listed in the static regexes are dropped from the rendered root until browser hydration. Use a server-independent native-attribute set, or otherwise classify these attributes as DOM props without relying on `document`.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts, line 159:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eDuring SSR, standard native attributes not listed in the static regexes are dropped from the rendered root until browser hydration. Use a server-independent native-attribute set, or otherwise classify these attributes as DOM props without relying on `document`.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -128,7 +153,11 @@ export function splitSvelteRootProps(props: AnyRecord, inputNames: readonly stri\\n+    else if (ROOT_DOM_PROP.test(key) || ROOT_EVENT_PROP.test(key)) dom[key] = value;\\n+    else {\\n+      inputs[key] = value;\\n+      if (isUndeclaredNativeProp(key)) dom[key] = value;\\n+    }\\n   }\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`358c4d2`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/358c4d2bec007a1e6c8a738302df38e03a6281e4)\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:05:27Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835996860\",\"id\":3835996860,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":146,\"original_commit_id\":\"c6aea5c7b1c3b023d51510b821e61b7a7f17b32f\",\"original_line\":159,\"path\":\"uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:19:41Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=359c5626-9af6-4a7d-859e-8ef55aa46c22 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=8add03eb-2e54-4224-a134-d62e7a9b9b83 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: When a dynamic list recreates equivalent objects with different property order, `JSON.stringify(values)` changes the identity and rejects the next-page cursor as expired. Hash `canonicalJson(values)` so cursor validity follows JSON content rather than object key order.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/core/src/server.ts, line 102:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a dynamic list recreates equivalent objects with different property order, `JSON.stringify(values)` changes the identity and rejects the next-page cursor as expired. Hash `canonicalJson(values)` so cursor validity follows JSON content rather than object key order.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -95,12 +96,22 @@ function page\\u003cT\\u003e(\\n+  operation: \\\"tools\\\" | \\\"resources\\\" | \\\"resource-templates\\\" | \\\"prompts\\\",\\n ): { values: T[]; nextCursor?: string } {\\n+  const identity = createHash(\\\"sha256\\\")\\n+    .update(JSON.stringify(values))\\n+    .digest(\\\"base64url\\\")\\n+    .slice(0, 16);\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`9bd82d2`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/9bd82d29b653cf7bea0c3222a1474288fd873494)\",\"commit_id\":\"358c4d2bec007a1e6c8a738302df38e03a6281e4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:22:44Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836023995\",\"id\":3836023995,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"358c4d2bec007a1e6c8a738302df38e03a6281e4\",\"original_line\":102,\"path\":\"mcpfn/core/src/server.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:26:48Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=e8a8b4ae-b204-4bf3-8aa9-8fda128c1e35 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=8add03eb-2e54-4224-a134-d62e7a9b9b83 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} --\\u003e\\nP3: This changes the public cursor shape, but `mcpfn/core/README.md` still documents `mcpfn:\\u003coffset\\u003e` cursors. Update the package documentation to describe the opaque, operation/collection-bound cursor and its expiry behavior.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/core/src/server.ts, line 124:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThis changes the public cursor shape, but `mcpfn/core/README.md` still documents `mcpfn:\\u003coffset\\u003e` cursors. Update the package documentation to describe the opaque, operation/collection-bound cursor and its expiry behavior.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -109,7 +120,9 @@ function page\\u003cT\\u003e(\\n     values: selected,\\n-    ...(nextOffset \\u003c values.length ? { nextCursor: `mcpfn:${nextOffset}` } : {}),\\n+    ...(nextOffset \\u003c values.length\\n+      ? { nextCursor: `mcpfn:${operation}:${identity}:${nextOffset}` }\\n+      : {}),\\n   };\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:22:44Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836023997\",\"id\":3836023997,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":125,\"original_commit_id\":\"358c4d2bec007a1e6c8a738302df38e03a6281e4\",\"original_line\":124,\"path\":\"mcpfn/core/src/server.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:22:44Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 358c4d2 with deterministic static native-attribute classification and accesskey coverage.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32572663978/job/97030344428) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"c6aea5c7b1c3b023d51510b821e61b7a7f17b32f\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:27:49Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836032277\",\"id\":3836032277,\"in_reply_to_id\":3835996676,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"c6aea5c7b1c3b023d51510b821e61b7a7f17b32f\",\"original_line\":109,\"path\":\"uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:27:49Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"The deterministic allowlist still drops native props accepted by the public Svelte element types, including `indeterminate`, `defaultChecked`, `part`, and `popover`. The prior browser prototype path forwarded these in the client; after this change they remain controller inputs and never reach the root spread, so valid typed props silently stop affecting the DOM.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Static root-prop classification is incomplete\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts:102-143` — only names in `NATIVE_ROOT_PROPS` are mirrored to `split.dom`.\\n- `uifn/svelte/lib/generated/input/Root.svelte:7-19` — the public root type accepts Svelte input properties that are not controller inputs.\\n- `uifn/svelte/tests/root-props.test.ts:5-30` — covers newly allowlisted attributes but not typed properties omitted from the set.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Deterministically forward every supported native attribute/property accepted by the public Svelte root types during SSR and browser rendering.\\n- Add coverage for a global attribute and input-only properties such as `indeterminate` and `defaultChecked`.\\n\\n## Contract evidence\\n- Svelte `HTMLInputAttributes` includes `indeterminate`, `defaultChecked`, and `defaultchecked`: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sveltejs/svelte/svelte%405.46.4/packages/svelte/elements.d.ts\\n- `HTMLInputElement.indeterminate` is a script-set native property: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLInputElement/indeterminate\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"358c4d2bec007a1e6c8a738302df38e03a6281e4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:31:54Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836038808\",\"id\":3836038808,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"358c4d2bec007a1e6c8a738302df38e03a6281e4\",\"original_line\":105,\"path\":\"uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:31:55Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Consume the FileFn download descriptor in action results**\\n\\nWhen an operator runs either exposed FileFn download action, the response is shaped as `data.item.{url,headers}`, but this branch only looks for `data.downloadUrl`; moreover, every `ActionButton` caller leaves `openDownloadReceipt` at its default `false`. Fresh evidence in the current tree is that the read actions are now exposed and their descriptors are no longer redacted, but the UI still discards them and merely reports completion, so no download starts and provider-required headers cannot be applied.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"9bd82d29b653cf7bea0c3222a1474288fd873494\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:34:49Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836043479\",\"id\":3836043479,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"9bd82d29b653cf7bea0c3222a1474288fd873494\",\"original_line\":159,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/ActionButton.svelte\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:34:49Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Encode scope components in memory-store keys**\\n\\nWhen scope identifiers contain `/`, distinct scopes can produce the same key—for example, installation/workspace pairs `a/b` + `c` and `a` + `b/c` are indistinguishable here. Admin scope validation permits such nonblank identifiers, so the memory store can list, retrieve, overwrite, or delete another scope's HostFn records; use an unambiguous tuple serialization rather than delimiter concatenation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"9bd82d29b653cf7bea0c3222a1474288fd873494\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:34:49Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836043481\",\"id\":3836043481,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"9bd82d29b653cf7bea0c3222a1474288fd873494\",\"original_line\":112,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:34:49Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Reject credentials embedded in environment URLs**\\n\\nWhen `baseUrl` is an HTTP(S) URL such as `REDACTED`, this validation accepts it and persists `parsed.toString()`. Environment records are explicitly presented as non-secret endpoints and return `baseUrl` without redaction, so the embedded credential is exposed through list/get responses and the generic console; reject URLs with a nonempty `username` or `REDACTED` before storing them.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:34:49Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836043483\",\"id\":3836043483,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":261,\"original_commit_id\":\"9bd82d29b653cf7bea0c3222a1474288fd873494\",\"original_line\":261,\"path\":\"apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:34:49Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Decode policy IDs before dispatching updates**\\n\\nWhen a mutable policy ID requires URL encoding, such as `retention%20policy` or `team%2Fpolicy`, this passes the encoded segment directly to the configured operation as `input.id`. The operation therefore looks up the literal percent-encoded ID instead of the policy advertised by the settings service; decode the path parameter as is already done for operation IDs and module route parameters.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"a3a6f63fef417435b4161f13dda766b63a08cd5a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:59:58Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836085089\",\"id\":3836085089,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"a3a6f63fef417435b4161f13dda766b63a08cd5a\",\"original_line\":626,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:59:58Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Reject CSS syntax in theme scope selectors**\\n\\nWhen `scope` is derived from configuration or other non-constant input, the check accepts braces, semicolons, and comma-separated selectors. For example, `:root { color:red; } body` passes validation and is interpolated directly into the stylesheet, allowing injected CSS declarations rather than merely selecting a theme root; validate the scope as a single selector or reject CSS control characters before interpolation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"a3a6f63fef417435b4161f13dda766b63a08cd5a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:59:58Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836085091\",\"id\":3836085091,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"a3a6f63fef417435b4161f13dda766b63a08cd5a\",\"original_line\":58,\"path\":\"uifn/theme/src/mount.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:59:58Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in a3a6f63 with deterministic coverage for the omitted native properties.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32574128726/job/97033852165) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"358c4d2bec007a1e6c8a738302df38e03a6281e4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:04:26Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836092411\",\"id\":3836092411,\"in_reply_to_id\":3836038808,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"358c4d2bec007a1e6c8a738302df38e03a6281e4\",\"original_line\":105,\"path\":\"uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:04:26Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=b87cbc65-0790-4cc7-a0d2-37fce4ac323c --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=61344dbc-0113-40de-bbe1-05190ca20cc9 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":7} --\\u003e\\nP1: When a header-bearing receipt redirects, `fetcher` follows the redirect without revalidating its destination, which can forward provider credentials such as `x-download-key` to the redirect target. Reject redirects or validate each redirect destination before replaying receipt headers.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts, line 304:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a header-bearing receipt redirects, `fetcher` follows the redirect without revalidating its destination, which can forward provider credentials such as `x-download-key` to the redirect target. Reject redirects or validate each redirect destination before replaying receipt headers.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -269,6 +269,51 @@ export function openSafeAdminDownload(\\n+  const response = await fetcher(safeHref, {\\n+    headers,\\n+    credentials: 'omit',\\n+    redirect: 'follow',\\n+  });\\n+  if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`The download provider returned HTTP ${response.status}.`);\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    redirect: 'error',\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`e3e7054`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/e3e70545660f6090bf9fbf5e28d76d5f405c25ef)\",\"commit_id\":\"a3a6f63fef417435b4161f13dda766b63a08cd5a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:05:14Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836093856\",\"id\":3836093856,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"a3a6f63fef417435b4161f13dda766b63a08cd5a\",\"original_line\":304,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:22:34Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=edfa162d-8357-45ad-ae4b-25568f581590 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=61344dbc-0113-40de-bbe1-05190ca20cc9 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When FileFn uses proxy-backed storage instead of signed URLs, the new receipt helper rejects its `/proxy/files/...` descriptor as untrusted, so Super Console downloads fail. Route the proxy through a trusted admin download endpoint or add an explicit, function-owned allowlist for this proxy route.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts, line 283:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen FileFn uses proxy-backed storage instead of signed URLs, the new receipt helper rejects its `/proxy/files/...` descriptor as untrusted, so Super Console downloads fail. Route the proxy through a trusted admin download endpoint or add an explicit, function-owned allowlist for this proxy route.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -269,6 +269,51 @@ export function openSafeAdminDownload(\\n+  fetcher: typeof fetch = fetch\\n+): Promise\\u003cboolean\\u003e {\\n+  if (typeof window === 'undefined') return false;\\n+  const safeHref = safeAdminDownloadHref(receipt.url, {\\n+    origin: window.location.origin,\\n+    signedExternal: receipt.signedExternal ?? true,\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`e3e7054`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/e3e70545660f6090bf9fbf5e28d76d5f405c25ef)\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:05:14Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836093861\",\"id\":3836093861,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":298,\"original_commit_id\":\"a3a6f63fef417435b4161f13dda766b63a08cd5a\",\"original_line\":283,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:22:35Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=eeb28512-6d03-465c-b1c4-10c21fa7610d --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=61344dbc-0113-40de-bbe1-05190ca20cc9 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":6} --\\u003e\\nP3: The test leaves URL.createObjectURL, URL.revokeObjectURL, and HTMLAnchorElement.prototype.click mocked for the rest of the jsdom file run; nothing restores them. Restore the originals in an afterEach so later tests cannot silently depend on or break against the patched globals.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/tests/ui/admin-api.test.ts, line 184:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThe test leaves URL.createObjectURL, URL.revokeObjectURL, and HTMLAnchorElement.prototype.click mocked for the rest of the jsdom file run; nothing restores them. Restore the originals in an afterEach so later tests cannot silently depend on or break against the patched globals.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -176,6 +177,27 @@ describe('administration API boundary', () =\\u003e {\\n+    const fetcher = vi.fn\\u003ctypeof fetch\\u003e(async () =\\u003e new Response('file contents'));\\n+    const createObjectURL = vi.fn(() =\\u003e 'blob:download');\\n+    const revokeObjectURL = vi.fn();\\n+    Object.defineProperty(URL, 'createObjectURL', { configurable: true, value: createObjectURL });\\n+    Object.defineProperty(URL, 'revokeObjectURL', { configurable: true, value: revokeObjectURL });\\n+    const click = vi.spyOn(HTMLAnchorElement.prototype, 'click').mockImplementation(() =\\u003e undefined);\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`e3e7054`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/e3e70545660f6090bf9fbf5e28d76d5f405c25ef)\",\"commit_id\":\"e3e70545660f6090bf9fbf5e28d76d5f405c25ef\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:05:14Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836093863\",\"id\":3836093863,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"a3a6f63fef417435b4161f13dda766b63a08cd5a\",\"original_line\":184,\"path\":\"superconsole/tests/ui/admin-api.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:22:37Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Header-bearing downloads still cannot satisfy `FileFnAdminDownloadDescriptor` for required secret-named headers: dispatcher redaction converts `authorization` to `[REDACTED]`, and this helper omits it. Conversely, `redirect: 'follow'` forwards retained custom headers such as `x-download-key` across origin-changing redirects, so this path either drops required credentials or can disclose them to a redirect target.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Provider-header downloads are incomplete and redirect-unsafe\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `filefn/admin/src/index.ts:108` — permits arbitrary provider-required download headers.\\n- `filefn/admin/src/__tests__/admin.test.ts:238-270` — demonstrates a descriptor containing both `x-download-key` and `authorization`, with the latter masked by dispatcher redaction.\\n- `packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts:325` — applies implicit-secret redaction to external operation data.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts:291-305` — drops masked headers but follows redirects with the remaining custom headers.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Support the declared FileFn descriptor contract without exposing provider credentials to an origin-changing redirect.\\n- Add end-to-end coverage for a provider that requires a secret-named header and for redirect behavior with a custom header.\\n\\n## Suggested approach\\n- Execute header-bearing descriptors through a controlled same-origin backend that validates redirect destinations, or narrow the descriptor contract and reject redirects before sending provider headers.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"a3a6f63fef417435b4161f13dda766b63a08cd5a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:07:02Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836096732\",\"id\":3836096732,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"a3a6f63fef417435b4161f13dda766b63a08cd5a\",\"original_line\":304,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:07:03Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=76dc5b64-0a59-4f64-bd54-f80f873c489b --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=ae157349-1510-44f6-bd27-b5ce590b49e7 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":7} --\\u003e\\nP1: When `themeToCSS` output is emitted through a raw `\\u003cstyle\\u003e` HTML sink, a scope such as `\\u003c/style\\u003e\\u003cscript\\u003e...\\u003c/script\\u003e` passes this check and enables script injection. Reject `\\u003c` and `\\u003e` here, or HTML-escape the output at the sink.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/theme/src/mount.ts, line 55:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen `themeToCSS` output is emitted through a raw `\\u003cstyle\\u003e` HTML sink, a scope such as `\\u003c/style\\u003e\\u003cscript\\u003e...\\u003c/script\\u003e` passes this check and enables script injection. Reject `\\u003c` and `\\u003e` here, or HTML-escape the output at the sink.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@ export interface MountedTheme {\\n }\\n \\n-const UNSAFE_SCOPE_PATTERN = /(^|\\\\s)(html|body)\\\\s+body|html\\\\s+body|\\\\*/i;\\n+const UNSAFE_SCOPE_PATTERN = /(^|\\\\s)(html|body)\\\\s+body|html\\\\s+body|\\\\*|[{},;@]|\\\\/\\\\*|\\\\*\\\\/|[\\\\^@-\\\\^_\\\\u007f]/i;\\n \\n export function assertSafeThemeScope(scope: string): void {\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\nconst UNSAFE_SCOPE_PATTERN = /(^|\\\\s)(html|body)\\\\s+body|html\\\\s+body|\\\\*|[\\u003c\\u003e{},;@]|\\\\/\\\\*|\\\\*\\\\/|[\\\\^@-\\\\^_\\\\u007f]/i;\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`09ff931`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2)\",\"commit_id\":\"e3e70545660f6090bf9fbf5e28d76d5f405c25ef\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:25:49Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836128762\",\"id\":3836128762,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"e3e70545660f6090bf9fbf5e28d76d5f405c25ef\",\"original_line\":55,\"path\":\"uifn/theme/src/mount.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:44:59Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Include relation names in generated IDs**\\n\\nWhen a valid schema defines multiple relations with the same endpoints and type but different `relation` or `inverse` names, this function assigns them identical IDs. The relations list then supplies duplicate keyed row IDs to the Super Console, and `getRelation` always returns the first match, making the other relation unaddressable; include the relation identity fields in the generated ID.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"e3e70545660f6090bf9fbf5e28d76d5f405c25ef\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:27:17Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836131320\",\"id\":3836131320,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"e3e70545660f6090bf9fbf5e28d76d5f405c25ef\",\"original_line\":87,\"path\":\"datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:27:17Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Expose document actions as collection actions**\\n\\nWhen SearchFn is operated through the generic Super Console, `documents` has no list or get operation (`domainReadResourceIds` excludes it), but `index` and `remove-document` are projected here as ID-bound resource actions. The module page only renders collection actions, while the non-listable documents resource has no reachable detail page, so both operations are unavailable in the UI; project these action-only operations as collection actions so their `id` inputs can be entered in the action form.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:27:17Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836131324\",\"id\":3836131324,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":594,\"original_commit_id\":\"e3e70545660f6090bf9fbf5e28d76d5f405c25ef\",\"original_line\":594,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:27:17Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"`isImplicitAdminSecretKey()` is only a redaction heuristic, so it misses real provider credentials such as GCS `x-goog-encryption-key`; this descriptor reaches the admin response and the browser forwards the raw customer AES-256 key. Please use an explicit browser-safe header contract or force provider-secret receipts through a server proxy, and cover this concrete header.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Provider secrets bypass the header classifier\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `filefn/admin/src/domain-service.ts:27` — treats a name-based redaction heuristic as a complete provider-credential classifier.\\n- `packages/admin/src/audit.ts:3` — does not recognize `x-goog-encryption-key` or `x-amz-server-side-encryption-customer-key` as implicit secrets.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts:294` — forwards every accepted descriptor header from the admin response into browser Fetch.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- No provider credential may be serialized to the browser solely because its name falls outside the implicit-redaction heuristic.\\n- File and artifact downloads must fail closed or use a controlled server-side path for customer encryption keys and equivalent credentials.\\n- Add a regression using `x-goog-encryption-key`; Google documents it as the Base64-encoded customer AES-256 key: https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/encryption/customer-supplied-keys\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"e3e70545660f6090bf9fbf5e28d76d5f405c25ef\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:40:34Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836153593\",\"id\":3836153593,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"e3e70545660f6090bf9fbf5e28d76d5f405c25ef\",\"original_line\":27,\"path\":\"filefn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:40:34Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Make share-link creation replay-safe after audit failures**\\n\\nWhen `shares.createShareLink` succeeds but the required terminal audit write fails, `AdminDispatcher` returns a dependency error after the live share and its one-time plaintext token have already been created. Because this operation explicitly disables idempotency, a retry creates another share instead of recovering the first result; the first link remains active while its token is lost, and it cannot be revoked through this admin API because revocation requires that original token. Preserve the result behind an idempotency key or otherwise reconcile/revoke the created share on post-execution failure.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:48:01Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836166999\",\"id\":3836166999,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":199,\"original_commit_id\":\"09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2\",\"original_line\":199,\"path\":\"filefn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:48:01Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 09ff931 by rejecting every provider-header descriptor before it can reach the browser.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32576627004/job/97039815460) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"e3e70545660f6090bf9fbf5e28d76d5f405c25ef\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:51:27Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836173133\",\"id\":3836173133,\"in_reply_to_id\":3836153593,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"e3e70545660f6090bf9fbf5e28d76d5f405c25ef\",\"original_line\":27,\"path\":\"filefn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:51:27Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 09ff931 by narrowing admin downloads to header-free signed URLs or same-origin proxies.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32576627004/job/97039815460) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"a3a6f63fef417435b4161f13dda766b63a08cd5a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:51:30Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836173201\",\"id\":3836173201,\"in_reply_to_id\":3836096732,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"a3a6f63fef417435b4161f13dda766b63a08cd5a\",\"original_line\":304,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:51:30Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=99b73b72-467f-4fb0-94c8-d6d109053ef9 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=9c17cfe9-eced-4720-9690-e7e1d35fc8fc --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} --\\u003e\\nP1: When Super Console registers SearchFn, `remove-document` makes registry construction fail because destructive collection targets are rejected. Keep this per-document action resource-targeted.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At searchfn/admin/src/index.ts, line 214:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen Super Console registers SearchFn, `remove-document` makes registry construction fail because destructive collection targets are rejected. Keep this per-document action resource-targeted.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -211,7 +211,7 @@ export const searchFnAdminActions = [\\n     requiresConfirmation: false,\\n     idempotent: true,\\n-    target: \\\"resource\\\",\\n+    target: \\\"collection\\\",\\n   },\\n   {\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    target: \\\"resource\\\",\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`b1157c7`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943)\",\"commit_id\":\"09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:52:46Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836175572\",\"id\":3836175572,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2\",\"original_line\":214,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:08:48Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=8a782aae-9488-4c0c-97d9-09edf428e738 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=9c17cfe9-eced-4720-9690-e7e1d35fc8fc --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: Valid scoped themes using the CSS child combinator now fail validation because `\\u003e` is classified as unsafe. Reject `\\u003c` for the closing-tag injection case, but keep `\\u003e` allowed so valid selectors continue to work.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/theme/src/mount.ts, line 55:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eValid scoped themes using the CSS child combinator now fail validation because `\\u003e` is classified as unsafe. Reject `\\u003c` for the closing-tag injection case, but keep `\\u003e` allowed so valid selectors continue to work.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@ export interface MountedTheme {\\n }\\n \\n-const UNSAFE_SCOPE_PATTERN = /(^|\\\\s)(html|body)\\\\s+body|html\\\\s+body|\\\\*|[{},;@]|\\\\/\\\\*|\\\\*\\\\/|[\\\\^@-\\\\^_\\\\u007f]/i;\\n+const UNSAFE_SCOPE_PATTERN = /(^|\\\\s)(html|body)\\\\s+body|html\\\\s+body|\\\\*|[\\u003c\\u003e{},;@]|\\\\/\\\\*|\\\\*\\\\/|[\\\\^@-\\\\^_\\\\u007f]/i;\\n \\n export function assertSafeThemeScope(scope: string): void {\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\nconst UNSAFE_SCOPE_PATTERN = /(^|\\\\s)(html|body)\\\\s+body|html\\\\s+body|\\\\*|[\\u003c{},;@]|\\\\/\\\\*|\\\\*\\\\/|[\\\\^@-\\\\^_\\\\u007f]/i;\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`b1157c7`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943)\",\"commit_id\":\"09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:52:46Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836175576\",\"id\":3836175576,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2\",\"original_line\":55,\"path\":\"uifn/theme/src/mount.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:08:51Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=39a9603b-aab7-4d43-9006-4369b15941ef --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=9c17cfe9-eced-4720-9690-e7e1d35fc8fc --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: This replacement removes the UI coverage proving that header-free signed receipts still open successfully. Retain a positive header-free receipt case alongside the provider-header rejection, or the browser download flow can regress while these tests remain green.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/tests/ui/admin-api.test.ts, line 184:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThis replacement removes the UI coverage proving that header-free signed receipts still open successfully. Retain a positive header-free receipt case alongside the provider-header rejection, or the browser download flow can regress while these tests remain green.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -181,43 +181,11 @@ describe('administration API boundary', () =\\u003e {\\n-\\n-  it('fails closed when a required provider header was redacted', async () =\\u003e {\\n-    const fetcher = vi.fn\\u003ctypeof fetch\\u003e();\\n+  it('fails closed for every provider-header download receipt', async () =\\u003e {\\n     await expect(openSafeAdminDownloadReceipt({\\n       url: 'https://storage.example.test/signed-object',\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`b1157c7`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943)\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:52:46Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836175580\",\"id\":3836175580,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":184,\"original_commit_id\":\"09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2\",\"original_line\":184,\"path\":\"superconsole/tests/ui/admin-api.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:08:50Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=cf78719a-6a4b-4d8b-8c63-1ca359ed9c75 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=9c17cfe9-eced-4720-9690-e7e1d35fc8fc --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When two valid relations use different `joinTable` values without `relation` or `inverse` names, this ID collides and `getRelation` always returns the first relation. Include `joinTable` and other schema fields that distinguish a relation in the identity.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 89:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen two valid relations use different `joinTable` values without `relation` or `inverse` names, this ID collides and `getRelation` always returns the first relation. Include `joinTable` and other schema fields that distinguish a relation in the identity.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -81,10 +81,12 @@ function relationId(value: {\\n   const from = Array.isArray(value.from) ? value.from : [value.from];\\n   const to = Array.isArray(value.to) ? value.to : [value.to];\\n-  return `${from.join(\\\",\\\")}-\\u003e${to.join(\\\",\\\")}:${value.type}`;\\n+  return JSON.stringify([from, to, value.type, value.relation ?? null, value.inverse ?? null]);\\n }\\n \\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n  return JSON.stringify([from, to, value.type, value.relation ?? null, value.inverse ?? null, (value as { joinTable?: string }).joinTable ?? null]);\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`b1157c7`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943)\",\"commit_id\":\"09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:52:46Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836175582\",\"id\":3836175582,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2\",\"original_line\":89,\"path\":\"datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:08:47Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"`remove-document` is destructive, but this collection target violates the shared manifest invariant; `createAdminRegistry()` rejects SearchFn with `destructive targets must identify one resource`. Any installation that registers this adapter therefore fails during registry construction.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# SearchFn cannot register with a destructive collection target\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `searchfn/admin/src/index.ts:244` — projects a destructive single-document operation as a collection target.\\n- `packages/admin/src/validator.ts:899-906` — rejects every destructive collection target.\\n- `packages/admin/src/registry.ts:93-95` — validates each adapter manifest during registry construction.\\n- `searchfn/admin/src/index.ts:214` — the same reclassification makes single-document indexing lose its structured document ID in audit targets.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Keep single-document operations bound to their required `id` for validation and auditing.\\n- Preserve a discoverable way to invoke manually addressed document actions without misclassifying them as collection mutations.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:53:45Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836177284\",\"id\":3836177284,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2\",\"original_line\":244,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:53:46Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"This tuple still collides for distinct relations allowed by `validateSchema()`. Two `many-many` entries with the same endpoints and names but different `joinTable` values list under the same ID, so `getRelation()` can only return the first one.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Relation IDs remain non-unique\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts:80-90` — omits valid relation-defining fields such as `joinTable`, `joinColumns`, FK fields, metadata, and delete policy.\\n- `datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts:131-138` — resolves colliding IDs with `find()`, making every later match unaddressable.\\n- `datafn/admin/src/__tests__/admin.test.ts:126-150` — varies only `relation` and `inverse`, and uses the non-schema type `many-to-many` rather than `many-many`.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Generate a stable distinct ID for every relation entry accepted by DataFn schema validation.\\n- Cover two production-valid relations whose current five-field tuples are identical but whose relation definitions differ.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:53:45Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836177287\",\"id\":3836177287,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2\",\"original_line\":89,\"path\":\"datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:53:46Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=bb84f4d4-8421-4bf7-bd2b-f9920c826acc --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=de51d2b7-51be-4233-98de-40e1e764bc05 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP1: When compensation succeeds after a terminal audit failure, the dispatcher can leave a required-audit mutation with no terminal failed event or durable reconciliation marker. Persist an explicit rollback/failure audit state and reconcile that state on retry instead of completing the claim without audit metadata.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts, line 417:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen compensation succeeds after a terminal audit failure, the dispatcher can leave a required-audit mutation with no terminal failed event or durable reconciliation marker. Persist an explicit rollback/failure audit state and reconcile that state on retry instead of completing the claim without audit metadata.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -396,7 +396,40 @@ export class AdminDispatcher {\\n+              result: domainResponse,\\n+              cause: error,\\n+            });\\n+            domainCompleted = false;\\n+            domainResponse = undefined;\\n+          } catch (cause) {\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`966f314`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/966f3141aac7e6b7c3a676bf3955ef1028c79a8b)\",\"commit_id\":\"9cf9e6116cdc974d1e7b01fdc5a7ed24e54f4029\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:13:41Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836215909\",\"id\":3836215909,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"original_line\":417,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:33:35Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=82a49015-d0cd-4840-a8fa-c24ee30b1ff2 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=de51d2b7-51be-4233-98de-40e1e764bc05 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP1: When an audit sink accepts the terminal event and then loses its acknowledgement, this compensator rolls back the already-audited domain mutation. Preserve the pending stable audit claim for ambiguous errors, or compensate only after the sink definitively confirms that it did not persist the event.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts, line 411:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen an audit sink accepts the terminal event and then loses its acknowledgement, this compensator rolls back the already-audited domain mutation. Preserve the pending stable audit claim for ambiguous errors, or compensate only after the sink definitively confirms that it did not persist the event.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -396,7 +396,40 @@ export class AdminDispatcher {\\n+        const compensator = entry.adapter.compensators?.[entry.operation.id];\\n+        if (compensator) {\\n+          try {\\n+            await compensator({\\n+              input: request.input,\\n+              context: request.context,\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`966f314`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/966f3141aac7e6b7c3a676bf3955ef1028c79a8b)\",\"commit_id\":\"9cf9e6116cdc974d1e7b01fdc5a7ed24e54f4029\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:13:41Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836215913\",\"id\":3836215913,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"original_line\":411,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:33:35Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=ae4eaeb5-91cc-4b8f-94ea-7038ebd9faab --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=de51d2b7-51be-4233-98de-40e1e764bc05 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: When a FileFn service returns `accepted: true` without `item.token`, this callback throws after the share was created and leaves the share active without durable cleanup. Require `item.token` for the create-share contract and provide a durable reconciliation path for responses that still omit it.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At filefn/admin/src/index.ts, line 367:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a FileFn service returns `accepted: true` without `item.token`, this callback throws after the share was created and leaves the share active without durable cleanup. Require `item.token` for the create-share contract and provide a durable reconciliation path for responses that still omit it.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -355,6 +355,19 @@ export function createFileFnAdminAdapter(service: FileFnAdminService): AdminCapa\\n+        const shareInput = input as CreateShareAdminInput;\\n+        const shareResult = result as AdminOperationResult\\u003cFileFnAdminOperationOutputMap[\\\"filefn.share-links.create-share\\\"]\\u003e;\\n+        const token = shareResult.data.item?.token;\\n+        if (!token) throw new Error(\\\"The created FileFn share token is unavailable for compensation.\\\");\\n+        await service.revokeShareLink({ fileId: shareInput.fileId, token }, context);\\n+      },\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:13:41Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836215914\",\"id\":3836215914,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":367,\"original_commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"original_line\":367,\"path\":\"filefn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:13:41Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=74c72b48-d7a0-478d-a718-104e8dc8af96 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=de51d2b7-51be-4233-98de-40e1e764bc05 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When a caller supplies `html \\u003e body` or `html\\u003ebody`, this pattern now accepts a document-wide scope and emits a rule targeting `body`. Preserve child combinators for scoped selectors, but reject `html`/`body` global combinations explicitly instead of removing `\\u003e` from the guard.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/theme/src/mount.ts, line 55:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a caller supplies `html \\u003e body` or `html\\u003ebody`, this pattern now accepts a document-wide scope and emits a rule targeting `body`. Preserve child combinators for scoped selectors, but reject `html`/`body` global combinations explicitly instead of removing `\\u003e` from the guard.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@ export interface MountedTheme {\\n }\\n \\n-const UNSAFE_SCOPE_PATTERN = /(^|\\\\s)(html|body)\\\\s+body|html\\\\s+body|\\\\*|[\\u003c\\u003e{},;@]|\\\\/\\\\*|\\\\*\\\\/|[\\\\^@-\\\\^_\\\\u007f]/i;\\n+const UNSAFE_SCOPE_PATTERN = /(^|\\\\s)(html|body)\\\\s+body|html\\\\s+body|\\\\*|[\\u003c{},;@]|\\\\/\\\\*|\\\\*\\\\/|[\\\\^@-\\\\^_\\\\u007f]/i;\\n \\n export function assertSafeThemeScope(scope: string): void {\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\nconst UNSAFE_SCOPE_PATTERN = /(^|\\\\s)(html|body)\\\\s+body|html\\\\s+body|html\\\\s*\\u003e\\\\s*body|body\\\\s*\\u003e\\\\s*body|\\\\*|[\\u003c{},;@]|\\\\/\\\\*|\\\\*\\\\/|[\\\\^@-\\\\^_\\\\u007f]/i;\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`966f314`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/966f3141aac7e6b7c3a676bf3955ef1028c79a8b)\",\"commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:13:41Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836215915\",\"id\":3836215915,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"original_line\":55,\"path\":\"uifn/theme/src/mount.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:33:33Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=612d4e24-d6c2-4b12-94da-6f83bb135d6f --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=de51d2b7-51be-4233-98de-40e1e764bc05 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: Per the HTML spec and current Chrome/Firefox/Safari, `window.open(url, '_blank', 'noopener')` returns null because the `noopener` feature is set. The mock makes it return `{ opener: window }`, so it asserts the opposite of the real browser contract: in production `popup` is always null, `openSafeAdminDownload` returns false, `openSafeAdminDownloadReceipt` resolves false, and ActionButton.svelte throws 'The download receipt did not contain a trusted URL.' after every successful download. Model the real contract (mock `window.open` to return null) and change the implementation so a null result from a noopener open is not treated as failure; the `popup.opener = null` branch is dead code in real browsers.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/tests/ui/admin-api.test.ts, line 192:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003ePer the HTML spec and current Chrome/Firefox/Safari, `window.open(url, '_blank', 'noopener')` returns null because the `noopener` feature is set. The mock makes it return `{ opener: window }`, so it asserts the opposite of the real browser contract: in production `popup` is always null, `openSafeAdminDownload` returns false, `openSafeAdminDownloadReceipt` resolves false, and ActionButton.svelte throws 'The download receipt did not contain a trusted URL.' after every successful download. Model the real contract (mock `window.open` to return null) and change the implementation so a null result from a noopener open is not treated as failure; the `popup.opener = null` branch is dead code in real browsers.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -188,6 +188,24 @@ describe('administration API boundary', () =\\u003e {\\n   });\\n \\n+  it('opens a header-free signed download receipt', async () =\\u003e {\\n+    const popup = { opener: window } as unknown as Window;\\n+    const open = vi.spyOn(window, 'open').mockReturnValue(popup);\\n+    try {\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:13:41Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836215924\",\"id\":3836215924,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"original_line\":192,\"path\":\"superconsole/tests/ui/admin-api.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:13:41Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Canonicalize scopes before forming idempotency identities**\\n\\nWhen the same operation, actor, and idempotency key are first dispatched with `{ organizationId: \\\"tenant\\\" }` and then with `{ installationId: \\\"tenant\\\" }`, scope validation treats both forms as the same installation, but this raw scope object produces two different storage identities. The second request therefore acquires a new claim and executes the supposedly idempotent mutation again; normalize the deprecated alias to a single canonical scope representation before constructing the identity.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836216783\",\"id\":3836216783,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"original_line\":529,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Reject non-finite JSON numbers**\\n\\nWhen a direct dispatcher caller supplies, or an adapter returns, `NaN` or either infinity under a schema declaring `type: \\\"number\\\"`, `valueType` classifies it as a valid number. The dispatcher consequently accepts the value, while JSON serialization changes it to `null`, so clients receive data that no longer satisfies the declared output schema; non-finite numbers should fail validation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836216785\",\"id\":3836216785,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":95,\"original_commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"original_line\":59,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Require schema properties to be owned by the input**\\n\\nWhen an input has a custom prototype containing a required field, this `in` check accepts the inherited value even though the subsequent `Object.entries` traversal never validates it. This is reachable through the module HTTP transport because assigning a parsed `{\\\"__proto__\\\": {...}}` body changes the accumulator's prototype; the dispatcher then clones away that prototype and invokes the adapter with the required field missing instead of rejecting the request. Check required fields with `Object.hasOwn`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836216788\",\"id\":3836216788,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":257,\"original_commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"original_line\":192,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in b1157c7 by deriving relation IDs from the complete stable relation definition and covering distinct join tables.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32577802524/job/97042606435) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:15:08Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836218617\",\"id\":3836218617,\"in_reply_to_id\":3836177287,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2\",\"original_line\":89,\"path\":\"datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:15:08Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in b1157c7 by restoring resource-bound document targets and exposing manually addressed actions in the module view.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32577802524/job/97042606435) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:15:11Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836218693\",\"id\":3836218693,\"in_reply_to_id\":3836177284,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2\",\"original_line\":244,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:15:11Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"A rejected `write()` is not proof that the terminal event was absent: the sink contract explicitly allows a durable write whose acknowledgement is lost. In that case this branch revokes the share while the audit log permanently says it succeeded.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Compensation can contradict a committed audit event\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `packages/admin/src/audit.ts:48-55` — requires first-write-wins behavior after acknowledgement loss.\\n- `packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts:372-409` — marks the write complete only after acknowledgement, then compensates every rejection.\\n- `filefn/admin/src/index.ts:363-369` — revokes the successfully created share.\\n- `filefn/admin/src/__tests__/admin.test.ts:155-161` — covers only a throw before any durable write.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Preserve agreement between durable terminal audit state and the final FileFn share state when the sink commits but its acknowledgement is lost.\\n- Add a commit-then-reject regression matching the declared sink contract.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:17:17Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836222588\",\"id\":3836222588,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"original_line\":409,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:17:18Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"This mock hides the browser behavior the test needs to cover: with the `noopener` feature, `window.open()` returns `null` even when it successfully opens the tab. Production therefore reports every signed download as untrusted after opening it; model the null return and make success independent of that inaccessible handle.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Signed downloads report false failure\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `superconsole/tests/ui/admin-api.test.ts:191-204` — supplies a non-null popup for a `noopener` call.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts:259-272` — interprets the mandated null return as popup blocking.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/components/ActionButton.svelte:157-166` — turns that false result into an operation error.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- A successfully initiated `noopener` download must not be reported as an untrusted receipt.\\n- Cover the browser's null-return contract documented at https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/open#noopener.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:17:18Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836222590\",\"id\":3836222590,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":203,\"original_commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"original_line\":193,\"path\":\"superconsole/tests/ui/admin-api.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:17:18Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=3d27b3eb-4ddf-485c-8aa2-512f40f6421f --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=cdff0ac4-797a-42be-ab6d-26c4cf0f300f --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} --\\u003e\\nP1: When compensation succeeds but the rollback audit write fails, the idempotency record loses the stable terminal audit marker needed for reconciliation. Preserve the failed result together with the existing `terminalAuditId` and a pending audit state, then replay and finalize that failed terminal event instead of replacing the record without audit metadata.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts, line 433:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen compensation succeeds but the rollback audit write fails, the idempotency record loses the stable terminal audit marker needed for reconciliation. Preserve the failed result together with the existing `terminalAuditId` and a pending audit state, then replay and finalize that failed terminal event instead of replacing the record without audit metadata.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -416,6 +417,30 @@ export class AdminDispatcher {\\n+              );\\n+              terminalAuditWritten = true;\\n+              auditId = rollbackAuditId;\\n+            } catch (cause) {\\n+              dispatchError = new AdminError(\\n+                \\\"dependency_unavailable\\\",\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`9cf9e61`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/9cf9e6116cdc974d1e7b01fdc5a7ed24e54f4029)\",\"commit_id\":\"9cf9e6116cdc974d1e7b01fdc5a7ed24e54f4029\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:37:31Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836261301\",\"id\":3836261301,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"966f3141aac7e6b7c3a676bf3955ef1028c79a8b\",\"original_line\":433,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:13:10Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=351598df-ffd6-4cc0-a9ae-d7340df16079 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=cdff0ac4-797a-42be-ab6d-26c4cf0f300f --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: Valid scoped selectors containing the text `body\\u003ebody` in an attribute value or class name are now rejected. Require a selector-token boundary before `html|body` (or parse the selector) so this guard only matches actual element selectors.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/theme/src/mount.ts, line 55:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eValid scoped selectors containing the text `body\\u003ebody` in an attribute value or class name are now rejected. Require a selector-token boundary before `html|body` (or parse the selector) so this guard only matches actual element selectors.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@ export interface MountedTheme {\\n }\\n \\n-const UNSAFE_SCOPE_PATTERN = /(^|\\\\s)(html|body)\\\\s+body|html\\\\s+body|\\\\*|[\\u003c{},;@]|\\\\/\\\\*|\\\\*\\\\/|[\\\\^@-\\\\^_\\\\u007f]/i;\\n+const UNSAFE_SCOPE_PATTERN = /(^|\\\\s)(html|body)\\\\s+body|html\\\\s+body|(?:html|body)\\\\s*\\u003e\\\\s*body|\\\\*|[\\u003c{},;@]|\\\\/\\\\*|\\\\*\\\\/|[\\\\^@-\\\\^_\\\\u007f]/i;\\n \\n export function assertSafeThemeScope(scope: string): void {\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\nconst UNSAFE_SCOPE_PATTERN = /(^|\\\\s)(html|body)\\\\s+body|html\\\\s+body|(?:^|[\\\\s\\u003e])(html|body)\\\\s*\\u003e\\\\s*body|\\\\*|[\\u003c{},;@]|\\\\/\\\\*|\\\\*\\\\/|[\\\\^@-\\\\^_\\\\u007f]/i;\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`9cf9e61`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/9cf9e6116cdc974d1e7b01fdc5a7ed24e54f4029)\",\"commit_id\":\"966f3141aac7e6b7c3a676bf3955ef1028c79a8b\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:37:31Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836261305\",\"id\":3836261305,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"966f3141aac7e6b7c3a676bf3955ef1028c79a8b\",\"original_line\":55,\"path\":\"uifn/theme/src/mount.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:13:07Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=b26cf3b2-8038-4a52-ade4-c71469c5499c --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=cdff0ac4-797a-42be-ab6d-26c4cf0f300f --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: Escaped CSS identifiers bypass the new global-selector guard: `\\\\\\\\68 tml\\u003ebody` still targets `html \\u003e body`. Reject CSS escape syntax (at minimum backslashes) or validate the selector with a CSS parser before interpolating it.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/theme/src/mount.ts, line 55:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eEscaped CSS identifiers bypass the new global-selector guard: `\\\\\\\\68 tml\\u003ebody` still targets `html \\u003e body`. Reject CSS escape syntax (at minimum backslashes) or validate the selector with a CSS parser before interpolating it.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@ export interface MountedTheme {\\n }\\n \\n-const UNSAFE_SCOPE_PATTERN = /(^|\\\\s)(html|body)\\\\s+body|html\\\\s+body|\\\\*|[\\u003c{},;@]|\\\\/\\\\*|\\\\*\\\\/|[\\\\^@-\\\\^_\\\\u007f]/i;\\n+const UNSAFE_SCOPE_PATTERN = /(^|\\\\s)(html|body)\\\\s+body|html\\\\s+body|(?:html|body)\\\\s*\\u003e\\\\s*body|\\\\*|[\\u003c{},;@]|\\\\/\\\\*|\\\\*\\\\/|[\\\\^@-\\\\^_\\\\u007f]/i;\\n \\n export function assertSafeThemeScope(scope: string): void {\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\nconst UNSAFE_SCOPE_PATTERN = /(^|\\\\s)(html|body)\\\\s+body|html\\\\s+body|(?:html|body)\\\\s*\\u003e\\\\s*body|\\\\*|[\\u003c{},;@\\\\\\\\]|\\\\/\\\\*|\\\\*\\\\/|[\\\\^@-\\\\^_\\\\u007f]/i;\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`9cf9e61`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/9cf9e6116cdc974d1e7b01fdc5a7ed24e54f4029)\",\"commit_id\":\"966f3141aac7e6b7c3a676bf3955ef1028c79a8b\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:37:31Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836261313\",\"id\":3836261313,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"966f3141aac7e6b7c3a676bf3955ef1028c79a8b\",\"original_line\":55,\"path\":\"uifn/theme/src/mount.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:13:08Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 966f314 by compensating only when the sink explicitly proves the terminal event was not persisted.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32579028898/job/97045524060) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:39:33Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836265178\",\"id\":3836265178,\"in_reply_to_id\":3836222588,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"original_line\":409,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:39:33Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 966f314 by treating the `noopener` null handle as an initiated download and covering that browser contract.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32579028898/job/97045524060) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:39:36Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836265300\",\"id\":3836265300,\"in_reply_to_id\":3836222590,\"line\":203,\"original_commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"original_line\":193,\"path\":\"superconsole/tests/ui/admin-api.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:39:36Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Validate token values before interpolating CSS**\\n\\nWhen a custom runtime theme contains CSS control syntax in a string-valued token, such as a dimension value of `1px;}body{display:none`, this interpolation lets the value escape its custom-property declaration and inject arbitrary rules into the generated stylesheet. `themeToCSS` accepts `DesignTokenTheme` directly without validation, and the token validator only checks that non-number values are strings, so validate each token's CSS grammar or reject control syntax before composing the stylesheet.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:40:01Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836266338\",\"id\":3836266338,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":96,\"original_commit_id\":\"966f3141aac7e6b7c3a676bf3955ef1028c79a8b\",\"original_line\":78,\"path\":\"uifn/theme/src/mount.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:40:01Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Detect blocked download windows**\\n\\nWhen a browser blocks popups, `window.open` returns `null`, but this helper discards that result and reports success. Fresh evidence is that the receipt is now consumed, but `ActionButton` only reaches this call after awaiting the administration request, by which time strict browsers commonly no longer consider it part of the initiating click; the download can therefore remain unopened while the UI reports completion. Pre-open a window during the click or treat a null return as failure and provide a direct navigation fallback.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"966f3141aac7e6b7c3a676bf3955ef1028c79a8b\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:40:01Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836266343\",\"id\":3836266343,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"966f3141aac7e6b7c3a676bf3955ef1028c79a8b\",\"original_line\":271,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:40:01Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"This only rejects a non-finite value when the current schema declares a numeric type. Valid open schemas such as `{ type: \\\"object\\\", additionalProperties: true }` still accept nested `NaN`/`Infinity`, so the dispatcher accepts domain output that Super Console later silently serializes as `null`.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Open schemas still admit non-finite values\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `packages/admin/src/validator.ts:58,92-102` — special classification has no effect when `schema.type` is omitted.\\n- `packages/admin/src/validator.ts:199-222` — `additionalProperties: true` accepts unknown values without recursively checking JSON validity.\\n- `packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts:294-298` — treats such domain output as valid.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:58-68` — `JSON.stringify()` changes accepted non-finite values to `null`.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Reject non-finite numbers at every depth regardless of whether the surrounding valid schema is typed, open, or typeless.\\n- Cover open-object, typeless-property, and array-item cases so the test fails with the current implementation.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:42:58Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836271738\",\"id\":3836271738,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":93,\"original_commit_id\":\"966f3141aac7e6b7c3a676bf3955ef1028c79a8b\",\"original_line\":58,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:42:59Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Filter connection lists by exact tenant identity**\\n\\nWhen the identity mapper returns a tenantless identity (`tenantId` is undefined), this passes an owner with an undefined tenant to `connections.list`; PlugFn's `ConnectionStorage.listByOwner` omits the tenant predicate when that value is absent, so connections for the same user or organization in every tenant are returned and mapped without an `assertConnectionOwner` check. This leaks cross-tenant connection names, scopes, and status through the list operation even though the corresponding detail operation rejects those records; post-filter the results using the exact tenant/owner checks or make the storage query distinguish tenantless records.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:16:45Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836570650\",\"id\":3836570650,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":357,\"original_commit_id\":\"9cf9e6116cdc974d1e7b01fdc5a7ed24e54f4029\",\"original_line\":347,\"path\":\"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:16:45Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 9cf9e61 with recursive open-schema validation and focused regression coverage.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32587012001/job/97064830292) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:18:08Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836573261\",\"id\":3836573261,\"in_reply_to_id\":3836271738,\"line\":93,\"original_commit_id\":\"966f3141aac7e6b7c3a676bf3955ef1028c79a8b\",\"original_line\":58,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:18:09Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"The earlier completion has already persisted a successful result and pending `succeeded` audit shape. If this replacement `complete()` fails before persisting, or a durable store rejects replacing a completed record, the catch below swallows it and a retry reports success after the compensator rolled back the domain state.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Compensation can leave the durable success record authoritative\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts:350-356` — persists the successful domain result and pending `succeeded` terminal event before audit delivery.\\n- `packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts:540-565` — attempts the compensated-failure replacement after rollback and suppresses any storage failure.\\n- `packages/admin/src/idempotency.ts:53-55,137-142` — the contract promises repeatability for the same result, while only the in-memory implementation explicitly permits replacing a completed result.\\n- `packages/admin/src/dispatcher.test.ts:315-379` — covers failed audit acknowledgement but not before-write or after-write failure of the compensation-state completion.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Make the compensated result and failed terminal-audit shape durably authoritative before any retry can observe the stale success record, including lost acknowledgements.\\n- Define the required atomic transition for distributed stores and cover both before-write and after-write completion failures.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:19:40Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836576354\",\"id\":3836576354,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":680,\"original_commit_id\":\"9cf9e6116cdc974d1e7b01fdc5a7ed24e54f4029\",\"original_line\":542,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:19:41Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=e4d0a90a-8a2e-48b8-9fa7-873371ab35cd --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=5275fc5a-473b-448f-902e-ead0ba012162 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When a required-audit idempotent mutation loses its terminal sink acknowledgement, replay redelivers the stable event ID without the original policy metadata. Persist the metadata in the pending audit marker before `writeAudit` so reconciliation reproduces the terminal event shape.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/idempotency.ts, line 25:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a required-audit idempotent mutation loses its terminal sink acknowledgement, replay redelivers the stable event ID without the original policy metadata. Persist the metadata in the pending audit marker before `writeAudit` so reconciliation reproduces the terminal event shape.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -19,6 +19,10 @@ export interface AdminIdempotencyRecord\\u003cT = unknown\\u003e {\\n+    /** Terminal event shape to redeliver when a sink acknowledgement is lost. */\\n+    outcome?: \\\"succeeded\\\" | \\\"failed\\\";\\n+    errorCode?: string;\\n+    metadata?: Readonly\\u003cRecord\\u003cstring, unknown\\u003e\\u003e;\\n     updatedAt: string;\\n   };\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:19:51Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836576637\",\"id\":3836576637,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":25,\"original_commit_id\":\"9cf9e6116cdc974d1e7b01fdc5a7ed24e54f4029\",\"original_line\":25,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/idempotency.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:19:51Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=d51c08ff-e32a-43dc-9121-02bb60c2fac6 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=5275fc5a-473b-448f-902e-ead0ba012162 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: When policy metadata contains secret-shaped or input-derived values, compensated failures persist it unredacted in the idempotency store even though the audit copy is sanitized. Redact the metadata before storing it, or persist only the fixed compensation marker.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts, line 554:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen policy metadata contains secret-shaped or input-derived values, compensated failures persist it unredacted in the idempotency store even though the audit copy is sanitized. Redact the metadata before storing it, or persist only the fixed compensation marker.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -533,12 +537,26 @@ export class AdminDispatcher {\\n+                      auditId: stableCompensationAuditId,\\n+                      outcome: \\\"failed\\\" as const,\\n+                      errorCode: \\\"dependency_unavailable\\\",\\n+                      ...(compensationAuditMetadata ? { metadata: compensationAuditMetadata } : {}),\\n+                      updatedAt: timestamp,\\n+                    },\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`fbb3868`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fbb3868fb8eeb21421e1dc9f7a079535ab7a84a2)\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:19:51Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836576638\",\"id\":3836576638,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":691,\"original_commit_id\":\"9cf9e6116cdc974d1e7b01fdc5a7ed24e54f4029\",\"original_line\":554,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T03:21:26Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=12b4ae7d-07c6-4988-94fe-fa19f0253b17 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=ac74b095-fd12-400a-8308-fe5692b2e6b7 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP1: When a compensator throws after durable preparation, every retry returns `compensationPending` without invoking compensation again, leaving the domain side effect unresolved indefinitely. Add a durable compensation retry/reconciliation path, or persist an actionable outbox task before returning pending.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts, line 238:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a compensator throws after durable preparation, every retry returns `compensationPending` without invoking compensation again, leaving the domain side effect unresolved indefinitely. Add a durable compensation retry/reconciliation path, or persist an actionable outbox task before returning pending.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -226,6 +235,18 @@ export class AdminDispatcher {\\n         if (reservation.status === \\\"replay\\\") {\\n           const prior = outwardAdminResult(reservation.record.result, entry);\\n           const originalAuditId = reservation.record.auditId ?? prior.auditId;\\n+          if (reservation.record.compensation?.status === \\\"pending\\\") {\\n+            const { auditId: _originalReceipt, ...priorWithoutReceipt } = prior;\\n+            return {\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`73485e8`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/73485e82e24ea8b3fb883a02c63044e033b54dec)\",\"commit_id\":\"fbb3868fb8eeb21421e1dc9f7a079535ab7a84a2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T03:24:16Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837609982\",\"id\":3837609982,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"fbb3868fb8eeb21421e1dc9f7a079535ab7a84a2\",\"original_line\":238,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T05:02:13Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Reconcile attached domains when persistence fails**\\n\\nWhen the provider successfully attaches the domain but `putDomain` rejects, this operation returns an error while leaving a live domain with no corresponding store record. The failed idempotent invocation is then fenced as an error, and retrying with a new key can attach a duplicate; meanwhile the console cannot discover or detach the original domain. Persist a durable pending intent before calling the executor, or compensate the provider attachment when the final write fails.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"73485e82e24ea8b3fb883a02c63044e033b54dec\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T03:26:35Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837613144\",\"id\":3837613144,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"fbb3868fb8eeb21421e1dc9f7a079535ab7a84a2\",\"original_line\":299,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T03:26:35Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Make confirmation issuance recoverable after audit failures**\\n\\nWhen `performConfirmOperation` successfully creates a valid confirmation token but this terminal audit write fails, the endpoint returns an error and discards the only receipt while the token remains live and the audit trail contains only the attempted event. Retrying issues another token, so a transient sink failure accumulates valid, unreturned credentials without a successful issuance record; make issuance replay-safe or revoke/reconcile the issued token before returning the failure.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"fbb3868fb8eeb21421e1dc9f7a079535ab7a84a2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T03:26:35Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837613146\",\"id\":3837613146,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"fbb3868fb8eeb21421e1dc9f7a079535ab7a84a2\",\"original_line\":1062,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T03:26:35Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in fbb3868 by fencing compensation before rollback and covering ambiguous transition acknowledgements.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32615132104/job/97134492380) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T03:28:58Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837616583\",\"id\":3837616583,\"in_reply_to_id\":3836576354,\"line\":680,\"original_commit_id\":\"9cf9e6116cdc974d1e7b01fdc5a7ed24e54f4029\",\"original_line\":542,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T03:28:58Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"A pending compensation record returns unchanged on every replay. If the compensator failed after fencing, or the pending-to-completed `complete()` failed before writing, later requests can neither retry reconciliation nor deliver the pending failed audit, leaving this key permanently stranded.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Pending compensation has no convergence path\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts:238-249` — returns every pending compensation replay before audit or compensation recovery.\\n- `packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts:492-533` — a compensator failure leaves the durable record pending.\\n- `packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts:620-644` — a failed pending-to-completed transition is swallowed.\\n- `packages/admin/src/idempotency.ts:42-50,66-69` — replay returns no claim, while `complete()` requires the original claim.\\n- `packages/admin/src/dispatcher.test.ts:475-486` — asserts only that the retry remains failed, not that pending state eventually converges.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Provide a retry or reconciliation path that can durably advance pending compensation to an accurate completed or failed state and recover its terminal audit without re-running a completed compensation.\\n- Cover compensator failure and before-write completion failure through eventual terminal convergence.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"fbb3868fb8eeb21421e1dc9f7a079535ab7a84a2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T03:30:43Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837618923\",\"id\":3837618923,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"fbb3868fb8eeb21421e1dc9f7a079535ab7a84a2\",\"original_line\":238,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T03:30:44Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=39b8386d-07af-4c4b-966a-2cd3f1c53428 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=547f7f2b-689d-4798-9bbc-7218b6ecb05a --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP1: When a compensation retry successfully writes its rollback audit, this call marks the pending audit completed through `complete` instead of `finalizeAudit`. A compliant durable store can reject that transition, leaving compensation pending and causing every replay to run the compensator again; complete the compensation while the audit remains pending, then call `finalizeAudit` with the stable audit ID.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts, line 898:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a compensation retry successfully writes its rollback audit, this call marks the pending audit completed through `complete` instead of `finalizeAudit`. A compliant durable store can reject that transition, leaving compensation pending and causing every replay to run the compensator again; complete the compensation while the audit remains pending, then call `finalizeAudit` with the stable audit ID.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -715,6 +770,157 @@ export class AdminDispatcher {\\n+        ...(terminalAuditWritten ? { auditId } : {}),\\n+        audit: {\\n+          ...claimedRecord.audit,\\n+          status: terminalAuditWritten ? \\\"completed\\\" : \\\"pending\\\",\\n+          updatedAt: completedAt,\\n+        },\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`db08968`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10)\",\"commit_id\":\"73485e82e24ea8b3fb883a02c63044e033b54dec\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T05:06:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837749551\",\"id\":3837749551,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"73485e82e24ea8b3fb883a02c63044e033b54dec\",\"original_line\":898,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:03:46Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=741c8597-a9a6-4cc6-98a4-39141e680a53 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=547f7f2b-689d-4798-9bbc-7218b6ecb05a --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP1: When a replay arrives while the original request is still compensating, this pending marker can be claimed by a second reconciliation attempt. The original claim can then complete the record without resolving that reconciliation wait, so the replay hangs forever even though compensation completed; represent the initial compensation as the same acquired claim, or add an explicit in-progress state and settle/fence concurrent waiters.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/idempotency.ts, line 190:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a replay arrives while the original request is still compensating, this pending marker can be claimed by a second reconciliation attempt. The original claim can then complete the record without resolving that reconciliation wait, so the replay hangs forever even though compensation completed; represent the initial compensation as the same acquired claim, or add an explicit in-progress state and settle/fence concurrent waiters.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -152,11 +179,19 @@ export class MemoryAdminIdempotencyStore implements AdminIdempotencyStore {\\n         throw new AdminError(\\\"conflict\\\", \\\"The idempotency completion fingerprint does not match its reservation.\\\");\\n       }\\n       existing.record = structuredClone(record) as AdminIdempotencyRecord;\\n+      if (existing.reconciliation?.token === claim.token) {\\n+        const reconciliation = existing.reconciliation;\\n+        existing.reconciliation = undefined;\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`db08968`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10)\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T05:06:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837749556\",\"id\":3837749556,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":191,\"original_commit_id\":\"73485e82e24ea8b3fb883a02c63044e033b54dec\",\"original_line\":190,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/idempotency.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:03:48Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=4a76bb57-f1a8-4d40-bf1a-000e29527b9a --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=547f7f2b-689d-4798-9bbc-7218b6ecb05a --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: When `executor.attachDomain` rejects, this pre-write leaves the domain permanently `pending` because the method has no failure transition. Mark definitive failures as `failed` (or remove them) and retain `pending` only for ambiguous outcomes that require reconciliation before another attach.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts, line 300:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen `executor.attachDomain` rejects, this pre-write leaves the domain permanently `pending` because the method has no failure transition. Mark definitive failures as `failed` (or remove them) and retain `pending` only for ambiguous outcomes that require reconciliation before another attach.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -294,6 +294,10 @@ export class HostFnOperatorService {\\n+    // Persist the provider intent before the external side effect. If the\\n+    // provider succeeds but the active transition fails, operators can still\\n+    // discover and detach the pending domain instead of creating duplicates.\\n+    await this.store.putDomain(domain);\\n     await this.executor.attachDomain({ target, domain });\\n     const active = { ...domain, status: \\\"active\\\" as const };\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`db08968`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10)\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T05:06:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837749559\",\"id\":3837749559,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":350,\"original_commit_id\":\"73485e82e24ea8b3fb883a02c63044e033b54dec\",\"original_line\":300,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:03:47Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=60731e6c-6207-4e08-b9ce-a9e13d59b2ac --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=547f7f2b-689d-4798-9bbc-7218b6ecb05a --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP3: This line is ~112 characters while the surrounding paragraph wraps at ~80-95 characters, so the wrap breaks at the join and the paragraph renders unevenly in file views and diffs. Re-wrap the line at the same width as its neighbors.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/README.md, line 49:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThis line is ~112 characters while the surrounding paragraph wraps at ~80-95 characters, so the wrap breaks at the join and the paragraph renders unevenly in file views and diffs. Re-wrap the line at the same width as its neighbors.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -46,12 +46,16 @@ from its name or require a repository-wide package catalog.\\n Startup fails closed when enabled operations require infrastructure that was\\n not injected: a required audit sink, atomic idempotency store, mutation\\n-authorization, or a bound confirmation issuer/verifier. Required-audit\\n+authorization, or a bound staged confirmation issuer/activator/revoker/verifier. Required-audit\\n mutations and confirmation issuance append a sanitized `attempted` event before\\n invoking mutable state, then append a terminal outcome. Audit and domain state\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\nauthorization, or a bound staged confirmation\\nissuer/activator/revoker/verifier. Required-audit\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`db08968`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10)\",\"commit_id\":\"73485e82e24ea8b3fb883a02c63044e033b54dec\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T05:06:23Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837749560\",\"id\":3837749560,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"73485e82e24ea8b3fb883a02c63044e033b54dec\",\"original_line\":49,\"path\":\"superconsole/README.md\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:03:49Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Compare object-valued enum members structurally**\\n\\nWhen an operation schema declares an object or array in `enum`, JSON-decoded input that is structurally identical is rejected because `Object.is` compares those values by reference. `AdminJsonSchema` permits arbitrary enum values and manifest validation does not restrict them to scalars, so such a valid schema becomes unusable through REST or MCP; compare enum members using JSON structural equality instead.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"73485e82e24ea8b3fb883a02c63044e033b54dec\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T05:06:53Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837750217\",\"id\":3837750217,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"73485e82e24ea8b3fb883a02c63044e033b54dec\",\"original_line\":86,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T05:06:53Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 73485e8 with atomic compensation claims, retryable reconciliation, and convergence coverage.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32619327758/job/97144952161) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"fbb3868fb8eeb21421e1dc9f7a079535ab7a84a2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T05:07:09Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837750570\",\"id\":3837750570,\"in_reply_to_id\":3837618923,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"fbb3868fb8eeb21421e1dc9f7a079535ab7a84a2\",\"original_line\":238,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T05:07:09Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"A provider exception now leaves this domain permanently `pending`, including when the provider definitely performed no attachment. Because `detachDomain` deletes local state only after provider detachment succeeds, a provider `not found` response can make the intent undeletable while later attach attempts create new random IDs.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Pending attachment intents cannot always converge\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:300-303` — persists `pending` before the provider call but records neither a failed outcome nor a resumable attachment identity when that call throws.\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:306-313` — requires provider detachment to succeed before deleting the local intent.\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/__tests__/operator.test.ts:82-122` — covers only active-transition persistence failure after provider success.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Ensure both definite and ambiguous provider attachment failures have an idempotent recovery path that can converge local and provider state without accumulating pending records.\\n- Cover provider-call failure and cleanup when the provider has no corresponding domain.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T05:09:34Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837753920\",\"id\":3837753920,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":350,\"original_commit_id\":\"73485e82e24ea8b3fb883a02c63044e033b54dec\",\"original_line\":300,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T05:09:35Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"This persists `succeeded` before the staged token becomes verifiable. If `activate()` fails below, the endpoint revokes the token and returns 503 but emits no failed or revoked terminal event, so the durable audit trail still claims successful issuance for a token that never became usable.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Activation failure leaves a false successful issuance audit\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1067-1103` — records success before activation and handles activation failure only through revocation and an HTTP error.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/types.ts:171-194` — defines activation as the transition that makes a staged token verifiable.\\n- `superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts:741-775` — covers audit failure before activation but not activation failure after the success event.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Make the durable audit history reflect activation failure or revocation so a failed request cannot end with only a successful issuance event.\\n- Add activation-failure coverage that asserts the token remains unusable and the terminal audit is truthful.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"73485e82e24ea8b3fb883a02c63044e033b54dec\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T05:09:34Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837753923\",\"id\":3837753923,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"73485e82e24ea8b3fb883a02c63044e033b54dec\",\"original_line\":1067,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T05:09:35Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Restrict the public processing service to authorized methods**\\n\\nWhen an application exposes this newly public service through an in-process integration, callers can invoke `processing.listArtifacts(fileId, ctx)` directly even though that method explicitly ignores `ctx` and queries all artifacts for the file; only `listArtifactsForFile` calls `requireReadableFile`. Publishing the full `ProcessingService` therefore bypasses the authorization enforced by both the HTTP routes and the admin adapter, so expose an authorization-safe facade or keep the worker-level methods private.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:10:24Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837842304\",\"id\":3837842304,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":334,\"path\":\"filefn/server/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:10:24Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Resolve composed schemas before deciding an action has no fields**\\n\\nWhen a valid operation input schema declares its named properties through `allOf`, this returns no editable fields because only top-level `properties` is inspected. The generic action then either submits `{}` immediately or shows a dialog without the required controls, so operations using a schema composition accepted by the manifest validator cannot be invoked from Super Console; merge compatible `allOf` object properties and requirements before constructing the fields.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:10:24Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837842305\",\"id\":3837842305,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":40,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:10:24Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in db08968 by reusing failed/pending intents and treating provider not-found as successful cleanup.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32621923528/job/97151211375) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:10:46Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837842803\",\"id\":3837842803,\"in_reply_to_id\":3837753920,\"line\":350,\"original_commit_id\":\"73485e82e24ea8b3fb883a02c63044e033b54dec\",\"original_line\":300,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:10:46Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in db08968 by activating before success and recording activation failures as denied.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32621923528/job/97151211375) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"73485e82e24ea8b3fb883a02c63044e033b54dec\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:10:49Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837842878\",\"id\":3837842878,\"in_reply_to_id\":3837753923,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"73485e82e24ea8b3fb883a02c63044e033b54dec\",\"original_line\":1067,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:10:49Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=cb881319-a120-42d3-b828-1c0079262e06 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=1e72b8f2-90ba-48d3-9476-e3e34a0fb189 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When two attach requests for the same target and hostname overlap, both calls can observe no existing record, create different IDs, and attach twice. Add an atomic uniqueness/claim operation or serialize attachment by scope, target, and hostname before invoking the executor.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts, line 297:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen two attach requests for the same target and hostname overlap, both calls can observe no existing record, create different IDs, and attach twice. Add an atomic uniqueness/claim operation or serialize attachment by scope, target, and hostname before invoking the executor.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -285,20 +293,46 @@ export class HostFnOperatorService {\\n-      updatedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\\n-    };\\n+    const existing = (await this.store.listDomains(scope, target.id)).find(\\n+      (candidate) =\\u003e candidate.hostname === input.hostname,\\n+    );\\n+    if (existing?.status === \\\"active\\\") return existing;\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`16a31f1`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a)\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:11:46Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837844404\",\"id\":3837844404,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":326,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":297,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:34:58Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=89be188a-3d29-4074-98b4-6af5402f6185 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=1e72b8f2-90ba-48d3-9476-e3e34a0fb189 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When a JSON request uses `-0` for a numeric `const` or `enum`, this helper rejects it against `0`; use JSON numeric equality instead of `Object.is`.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/validator.ts, line 17:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a JSON request uses `-0` for a numeric `const` or `enum`, this helper rejects it against `0`; use JSON numeric equality instead of `Object.is`.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -13,6 +13,17 @@ export interface AdminValidationIssue {\\n }\\n \\n+function adminJsonValueEquals(left: unknown, right: unknown): boolean {\\n+  if (Object.is(left, right)) return true;\\n+  if (\\n+    left !== null \\u0026\\u0026 right !== null \\u0026\\u0026\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n  if (left === right) return true;\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`16a31f1`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a)\",\"commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:11:46Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837844406\",\"id\":3837844406,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":17,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:34:56Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=98b68b18-5a90-4858-af75-b4769ab246db --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=1e72b8f2-90ba-48d3-9476-e3e34a0fb189 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: When a required-audit mutation handler throws, `domainCompensated` is false but the preceding failure audit sets `auditId`; this line removes that receipt before persisting the fenced failure. Replays then cannot report `meta.originalAuditId`; strip the receipt only for the compensation/finalize-audit path.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts, line 677:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a required-audit mutation handler throws, `domainCompensated` is false but the preceding failure audit sets `auditId`; this line removes that receipt before persisting the fenced failure. Replays then cannot report `meta.originalAuditId`; strip the receipt only for the compensation/finalize-audit path.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -668,15 +674,15 @@ export class AdminDispatcher {\\n             // fenced: execution may have committed before the error surfaced.\\n             const stableCompensationAuditId = domainCompensated ? terminalAuditId : undefined;\\n             const timestamp = this.now().toISOString();\\n+            const { auditId: _failedAuditReceipt, ...persistedFailedResult } = failedResult;\\n             await this.idempotency.complete(idempotencyClaim, {\\n               identity: idempotencyIdentity,\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n            const persistedFailedResult = domainCompensated\\n              ? (({ auditId: _failedAuditReceipt, ...result }) =\\u003e result)(failedResult)\\n              : failedResult;\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`16a31f1`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a)\",\"commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:11:46Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837844410\",\"id\":3837844410,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":677,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:34:57Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=cd5bac7f-ecc4-4bdc-8192-6bc42654fed2 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=1e72b8f2-90ba-48d3-9476-e3e34a0fb189 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":7} --\\u003e\\nP3: This edit dropped the only regression coverage for the lost rollback-audit-acknowledgement branch: when `writeAudit` (outcome \\\"failed\\\") throws inside `reconcileCompensation`, the dispatcher keeps compensation=completed with audit pending and returns `reconciliationRequired:true` without an auditId until a later replay recovers it. Removing `failedAuditAttempts` and the `retry_audit` assertion leaves that documented path unexercised. Keep a variant that injects one \\\"failed\\\" outcome rejection on the retry and asserts the two-step recovery (`reconciliationRequired` → then `recoveredTerminalAudit`/`auditId`).\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/dispatcher.test.ts, line 361:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThis edit dropped the only regression coverage for the lost rollback-audit-acknowledgement branch: when `writeAudit` (outcome \\\"failed\\\") throws inside `reconcileCompensation`, the dispatcher keeps compensation=completed with audit pending and returns `reconciliationRequired:true` without an auditId until a later replay recovers it. Removing `failedAuditAttempts` and the `retry_audit` assertion leaves that documented path unexercised. Keep a variant that injects one \\\"failed\\\" outcome rejection on the retry and asserts the two-step recovery (`reconciliationRequired` → then `recoveredTerminalAudit`/`auditId`).\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -36,6 +36,53 @@ describe(\\\"AdminDispatcher\\\", () =\\u003e {\\n     expect(different).not.toBe(first);\\n   });\\n \\n+  it(\\\"settles concurrent replay waiters when the original compensation claim completes\\\", async () =\\u003e {\\n+    const store = new MemoryAdminIdempotencyStore();\\n+    const identity = {\\n+      key: \\\"concurrent-compensation\\\",\\n+      actorId: \\\"user_1\\\",\\n+      scope: context().scope,\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`16a31f1`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a)\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:11:46Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837844412\",\"id\":3837844412,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":1,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":1,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:34:55Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=04df7e3e-5692-4051-8dcf-49c107346f7d --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=1e72b8f2-90ba-48d3-9476-e3e34a0fb189 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP3: In the new activation-failure test, `expect(active).toBe(false)` is vacuous: `active` starts false and nothing can set it true (`activate` throws before any assignment), and `verify` is never called. The title's claim \\\"leaves the staged token unusable\\\" is therefore not actually exercised. Initialize `let active = true;` so the assertion verifies `revoke` genuinely deactivated the token, or assert on `verify` returning false for the staged token.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts, line 780:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eIn the new activation-failure test, `expect(active).toBe(false)` is vacuous: `active` starts false and nothing can set it true (`activate` throws before any assignment), and `verify` is never called. The title's claim \\\"leaves the staged token unusable\\\" is therefore not actually exercised. Initialize `let active = true;` so the assertion verifies `revoke` genuinely deactivated the token, or assert on `verify` returning false for the staged token.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -770,10 +770,54 @@ describe('Super Console server composition', () =\\u003e {\\n+  it('records activation failure as denied and leaves the staged token unusable', async () =\\u003e {\\n+    const capability = manifest({ destructive: true });\\n+    const outcomes: Array\\u003c{ outcome: string; errorCode?: string }\\u003e = [];\\n+    let active = false;\\n+    const revoke = vi.fn(async () =\\u003e { active = false; });\\n+    const console = createSuperConsole({\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`16a31f1`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a)\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:11:46Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837844415\",\"id\":3837844415,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":782,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":780,\"path\":\"superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:34:54Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Reusing this intent while replacing `tls` breaks the new executor contract: a retry can send the same domain ID with different configuration, so provider idempotency may preserve the old TLS setting while local state records the new one. Reject conflicting retry input or keep the original intent immutable; the active fast path above must also not silently accept a different `tls` request.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Retried domain identity can change meaning\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:90-94` — requires retries under one domain ID to be idempotent.\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:299-305` — ignores conflicting TLS for active domains and overwrites it for failed or pending domains.\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/__tests__/operator.test.ts:124-168` — retries only identical default-TLS input.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- One provider idempotency identity must never represent two different hostname/TLS requests.\\n- Conflicting retry input must fail explicitly or use a separately defined update operation.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:13:43Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837847469\",\"id\":3837847469,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":303,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:13:44Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"The token is already verifiable when this required audit write starts. If it fails and `revoke()` also rejects, lines 1112-1114 suppress that failure and return 503 with a live unaudited token; make revocation failure durable and retryable, or use sequencing that cannot leave this state.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Audit failure can strand an activated confirmation\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1067-1073` — makes the token verifiable before the success event is durable.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1102-1115` — attempts revocation after audit failure but discards revocation failure without recording reconciliation state.\\n- `superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts:741-775` — covers only successful revocation and hard-codes verification to false.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- A failed issuance response must not leave a verifiable confirmation without its required success audit.\\n- Cover simultaneous success-audit and revocation failure with a verifier that reflects actual activation state.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:13:44Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837847471\",\"id\":3837847471,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":1102,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:13:44Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"`stableSerialize` treats every object by enumerable entries, so `{ const: {} }` accepts `new Date()` even though JSON transport emits an ISO string. Restrict constants, enum members, and compared values to JSON data, or use type-aware comparison that rejects non-plain and cyclic objects.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Structural equality accepts non-JSON values\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `packages/admin/src/validator.ts:16-24` — structurally serializes arbitrary `unknown` objects.\\n- `packages/admin/src/types.ts:20-27` — permits `unknown` schema constants and enum members.\\n- `packages/admin/src/validator.test.ts:40-59` — covers plain JSON containers only.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Runtime equality must agree with the JSON value that REST and MCP transport actually emit.\\n- Add non-plain and cyclic-value coverage so invalid adapter output is rejected rather than retyped in transport.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:13:44Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837847474\",\"id\":3837847474,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":22,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:13:44Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 16a31f1 by auditing while the token is still staged and activating only afterward.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32623271995/job/97154635862) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:37:46Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837883366\",\"id\":3837883366,\"in_reply_to_id\":3837847471,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":1102,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:37:46Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 16a31f1 by restricting structural comparison to finite, acyclic JSON data.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32623271995/job/97154635862) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:37:49Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837883427\",\"id\":3837883427,\"in_reply_to_id\":3837847474,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":22,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:37:49Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 16a31f1 by preserving one TLS configuration per attachment identity.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32623271995/job/97154635862) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:37:52Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837883475\",\"id\":3837883475,\"in_reply_to_id\":3837847469,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":303,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:37:52Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=f6a06edf-39cd-4d25-acb5-7952783aa704 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=4777accd-4d7f-40ee-8add-816fdeaf04ee --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: When multiple `allOf` branches define the same property, the shallow merge drops constraints from earlier branches. Derive field presentation separately and validate against the complete property composition (or the original input schema) so the console does not dispatch values it presents as valid but the admin validator rejects.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts, line 45:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen multiple `allOf` branches define the same property, the shallow merge drops constraints from earlier branches. Derive field presentation separately and validate against the complete property composition (or the original input schema) so the console does not dispatch values it presents as valid but the admin validator rejects.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -36,9 +36,18 @@ function fieldType(schema: AdminJsonSchema): ActionFieldType {\\n+  const collectObjectShape = (candidate: AdminJsonSchema): void =\\u003e {\\n+    for (const name of candidate.required ?? []) required.add(name);\\n+    for (const [name, property] of Object.entries(candidate.properties ?? {})) {\\n+      properties[name] = properties[name] ? { ...properties[name], ...property } : property;\\n+    }\\n+    for (const branch of candidate.allOf ?? []) collectObjectShape(branch);\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:39:13Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837885494\",\"id\":3837885494,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":45,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":45,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:39:14Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=65868d1e-ab59-422a-ae0f-bcef908ac0ed --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=4777accd-4d7f-40ee-8add-816fdeaf04ee --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When `uniqueItems` contains unsupported object values, `keys.includes(undefined)` bypasses uniqueness validation, and the open item schema accepts those values. Reject unsupported JSON values here (or emit a validation issue) rather than silently skipping `uniqueItems`.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/validator.ts, line 221:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen `uniqueItems` contains unsupported object values, `keys.includes(undefined)` bypasses uniqueness validation, and the open item schema accepts those values. Reject unsupported JSON values here (or emit a validation issue) rather than silently skipping `uniqueItems`.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -179,8 +217,8 @@ export function validateAdminValue(\\n-      const keys = value.map(stableSerialize);\\n-      if (new Set(keys).size !== keys.length)\\n+      const keys = value.map((item) =\\u003e comparableJsonValue(item));\\n+      if (!keys.includes(undefined) \\u0026\\u0026 new Set(keys).size !== keys.length)\\n         issues.push({\\n           path,\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n      if (keys.includes(undefined)) {\\n        issues.push({\\n          path,\\n          message: \\\"must contain only JSON values\\\",\\n          keyword: \\\"type\\\",\\n        });\\n      } else if (new Set(keys).size !== keys.length)\\n```\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:39:14Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837885495\",\"id\":3837885495,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":221,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":221,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:39:14Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=244a7b3d-8a40-4461-a334-0f82c44b3458 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=4777accd-4d7f-40ee-8add-816fdeaf04ee --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} --\\u003e\\nP2: When distinct JSON property names compare equal under locale collation, this sort makes structural equality depend on property insertion order. Use a deterministic code-unit key comparator instead of `localeCompare`.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/validator.ts, line 37:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen distinct JSON property names compare equal under locale collation, this sort makes structural equality depend on property insertion order. Use a deterministic code-unit key comparator instead of `localeCompare`.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -14,14 +14,38 @@ export interface AdminValidationIssue {\\n+  seen.add(value);\\n+  const entries = isArray\\n+    ? Array.from(value, (item, index) =\\u003e [String(index), item] as const)\\n+    : Object.entries(value as Record\\u003cstring, unknown\\u003e).sort(([leftKey], [rightKey]) =\\u003e leftKey.localeCompare(rightKey));\\n+  const serialized: string[] = [];\\n+  for (const [key, item] of entries) {\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:39:14Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837885501\",\"id\":3837885501,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":37,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":37,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:39:14Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Reconcile variable records after provider deletion**\\n\\nWhen the provider deletion succeeds but `store.deleteVariable` rejects, the stale variable record remains while this request returns an error. Retrying with the same idempotency key replays that error, and retrying with a new key can still never remove the record when the provider reports that the already-deleted variable is not found, because this path does not tolerate provider-not-found as `detachDomain` does. Treat an already-absent provider variable as success or persist a deletion intent so the store record can be reconciled.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:40:38Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837887588\",\"id\":3837887588,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":414,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":414,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:40:38Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"This map coalesces requests only within one `HostFnOperatorService` instance. Two instances sharing a durable store can both observe no hostname, generate different domain IDs, and call the provider because the store contract has no atomic reservation.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Attachment identity is not serialized across service instances\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:214-217` — keeps in-flight identities in an instance-local map.\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:52-74` — exposes separate list and put operations but no atomic hostname reservation.\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:324-350` — performs a read, generates a random ID, then writes the intent.\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/__tests__/operator.test.ts:176-199` — exercises two calls through only one service instance.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Concurrent attachment requests sharing a durable store must converge on one domain ID and one immutable hostname/TLS identity across service instances.\\n\\n## Suggested approach\\n- Add an atomic reserve-or-read operation to the store contract, or require an equivalent unique scope/target/hostname constraint that returns the winning intent.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:41:30Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837889099\",\"id\":3837889099,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":301,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":301,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:41:31Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"`localeCompare()` can return zero for distinct keys such as composed `é` and decomposed `e\\\\u0301`, so stable sort preserves their insertion order. Equivalent objects containing both keys can therefore produce different comparison strings and fail `const`, `enum`, or `uniqueItems`; use a locale-independent code-unit ordering.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:41:30Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837889101\",\"id\":3837889101,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":37,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":37,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:41:31Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"After this durable `succeeded` event, the process can stop before `activate()`, leaving an unusable staged token with a successful terminal audit. The documented reconciliation handles attempts without terminal events, so this inverse state needs a durable activation/reconciliation path rather than an unrecoverable success window.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Confirmation success can precede durable activation\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1067-1089` — persists success before attempting activation.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/types.ts:171-186` — defines staged tokens as unusable until activation.\\n- `superconsole/README.md:149-166` — requires durable injected infrastructure but describes reconciliation only for missing terminal events.\\n- `superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts:741-823` — covers in-process audit and activation failures, not interruption between the two steps.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- A durable success event must imply an active token, or durable state must identify and reconcile success-audited tokens whose activation has not completed.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:41:30Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837889103\",\"id\":3837889103,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":1067,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":1067,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:41:31Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Shallow-merging the same property across `allOf` branches overwrites earlier nested `properties` and `required` constraints. For example, branches requiring `payload.a` and `payload.b` leave only the latter schema here, so the form accepts input that the dispatcher rejects against the original schema.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Overlapping allOf property schemas lose constraints\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts:42-49` — flattens `allOf` with object spread rather than preserving intersection semantics.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts:87-132` — validates the flattened property schema instead of the original combined schema.\\n- `superconsole/tests/ui/action-form.test.ts:45-63` — covers only disjoint properties across branches.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Editable fields may be discovered across branches, but validation must retain every constraint applied to a repeated property by the full `allOf` schema.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:41:30Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837889106\",\"id\":3837889106,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":45,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":45,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:41:31Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":3,"nanos":609789792},"formatted_output":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 142829)\nTotal output lines: 336\n\n{\"body\":\"## Useless assignment to local variable\\n\\nThe value assigned to terminalAuditAttempted here is unused.\\n\\n---\\n\\nGeneral fix: remove assignments to local variables when the assigned value is never subsequently read, unless needed for side effects (not applicable to primitive assignment).\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eBest fix here: in \\u003ccode\\u003epackages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\\u003c/code\\u003e, remove the single redundant assignment \\u003ccode\\u003eterminalAuditAttempted = true;\\u003c/code\\u003e inside the error-handling audit-write branch. This does not change behavior because:\\u003c/p\\u003e\\n\\u003cul\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003ethe only relevant guard using \\u003ccode\\u003eterminalAuditAttempted\\u003c/code\\u003e in this shown block is already evaluated before the assignment,\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003cli\\u003edownstream result/idempotency logic depends on \\u003ccode\\u003eterminalAuditWritten\\u003c/code\\u003e and \\u003ccode\\u003eauditId\\u003c/code\\u003e, not \\u003ccode\\u003eterminalAuditAttempted\\u003c/code\\u003e.\\u003c/li\\u003e\\n\\u003c/ul\\u003e\\n\\u003cp\\u003eNo new imports, methods, or definitions are required.\",\"commit_id\":\"8d16f12d9a673cbed04f6c20cc9a06b0e770389e\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:16Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831735495\",\"id\":3831735495,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":425,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:17Z\",\"user\":\"github-code-quality[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Polynomial regular expression used on uncontrolled data\\n\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](2) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/42)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:21Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736234\",\"id\":3831736234,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":151,\"path\":\"authfn/admin/src/superconsole.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Polynomial regular expression used on uncontrolled data\\n\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](2) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](3) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](4) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](5) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](6) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](7) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](8) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](9) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](10) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](11) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/43)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736282\",\"id\":3831736282,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":137,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/client.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Polynomial regular expression used on uncontrolled data\\n\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](2) may run slow on strings starting with 'get ' and with many repetitions of '  '.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](3) may run slow on strings starting with 'get ' and with many repetitions of '  '.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/44)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736306\",\"id\":3831736306,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":37,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/registry.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Polynomial regular expression used on uncontrolled data\\n\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](2) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '_'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](3) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '_'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](4) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '_'.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/45)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736318\",\"id\":3831736318,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":45,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/registry.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Polynomial regular expression used on uncontrolled data\\n\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](2) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](3) may run slow on strings with many repetitions of '/'.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/46)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736335\",\"id\":3831736335,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":78,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/registry.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Polynomial regular expression used on uncontrolled data\\n\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](2) may run slow on strings starting with 'get ' and with many repetitions of '  '.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](3) may run slow on strings starting with 'get ' and with many repetitions of '  '.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](4) may run slow on strings starting with 'get ' and with many repetitions of '  '.\\nThis [regular expression](1) that depends on [library input](5) may run slow on strings starting with 'get ' and with many repetitions of '  '.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/47)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736351\",\"id\":3831736351,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":380,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Bad HTML filtering regexp\\n\\nThis regular expression does not match script end tags like \\u003c/script \\u003e.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/52)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736362\",\"id\":3831736362,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":38,\"path\":\"superconsole/scripts/verify-function-agnostic.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Incomplete string escaping or encoding\\n\\nThis does not escape backslash characters in the input.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/53)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736380\",\"id\":3831736380,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":95,\"path\":\"uifn/dom/src/overlay.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Prototype-polluting assignment\\n\\nThis assignment may alter Object.prototype if a malicious '__proto__' string is injected from [library input](1).\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/50)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736399\",\"id\":3831736399,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":221,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/openapi.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Prototype-polluting function\\n\\nThe property chain [segment](1) is recursively assigned to [current](2) without guarding against prototype pollution.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/49)\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736417\",\"id\":3831736417,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":87,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":84,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/resource-pages.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Information exposure through a stack trace\\n\\nThis information exposed to the user depends on [stack trace information](1).\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/48)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736436\",\"id\":3831736436,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":82,\"path\":\"uifn/svelte/tests/phase-14-ssr-hydration.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Exception text reinterpreted as HTML\\n\\n[Exception text](1) is reinterpreted as HTML without escaping meta-characters.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/51)\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736451\",\"id\":3831736451,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":82,\"path\":\"uifn/svelte/tests/phase-14-ssr-hydration.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Preserve numeric-looking string document IDs**\\n\\nFor a composite target such as `orders:001`, this converts the document ID from the string `\\\"001\\\"` to the number `1`. Single-document indexing therefore targets a different ID than batch indexing, which preserves string IDs, and `remove-document` can delete numeric document `1` instead of string document `\\\"001\\\"`. Preserve the ID suffix as a string or carry explicit ID-type information in the input.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:01:33Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831751943\",\"id\":3831751943,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":56,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:01:33Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Apply the declared index-list query parameters**\\n\\nWhen an installation has many configured indexes or the console supplies search/filter/pagination input, `listIndexes` ignores the entire input and always returns every index with `nextCursor: null`. This contradicts the operation's cursor-pagination declaration and makes the resource-list search UI return unrelated entries while bypassing the declared 200-item maximum; honor `limit`, `cursor`, and the advertised query fields before building the result.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:01:33Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831751947\",\"id\":3831751947,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":110,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:01:33Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**Security:** Mutation authorization is selected from the HTTP method rather than the matched operation's safety classification. Capability validation currently allows a `GET` route whose classification is `write` or `destructive`, so that operation is dispatched without `authorizeMutation` (and therefore without provider CSRF/re-auth checks). Please either reject non-read operations on safe HTTP methods during manifest validation or authorize after matching based on `entry.operation.safety.classification`.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799619\",\"id\":3831799619,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":630,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":612,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**Security:** These ownership predicates omit `tenantId`, even though `PlugFnDomainIdentity`, connections/installations, and `ownerFor()` carry it, and PlugFn core's `connectionMatchesActor()` requires exact tenant equality. If the same user or organization ID exists in two tenants, an admin mapped to tenant A can supply a tenant-B record ID and pass these checks (notably allowing `connections.refresh(id)`). Please include tenant equality in the direct-ID connection, installation, delegated, and legacy ownership checks and add a same-owner/different-tenant test.\",\"commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799625\",\"id\":3831799625,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":68,\"path\":\"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"This does not pass the package's own typecheck: `npm run typecheck --workspace superconsole` reports that `code` is not part of SvelteKit's `Error`, followed by two errors where `+error.svelte` reads `page.error.code` and `.details`. Please declare the intended `App.Error` shape in `src/app.d.ts` (or restrict these routes to the standard error shape) so the checked package is type-safe.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799628\",\"id\":3831799628,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":5,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":5,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/routes/[...missing]/+page.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"`SuperConsoleOptions.apiBasePath` changes the only prefix accepted by the server, but every bundled UI loader/action uses this hard-coded prefix. Configuring, for example, `/internal/admin` therefore makes the server reject all UI requests with 404. Please propagate the configured base path to the client/UI (including sign-in and download links), or remove/limit the option so a supported configuration cannot break the console.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799631\",\"id\":3831799631,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":9,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":9,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=1e8a9759-bd72-4e24-bd8c-217d1bba06d6 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=7bb8304f-392d-4952-ab05-eaf35f279889 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} --\\u003e\\nP1: When the build reaches `accordion`, it asks tsup to bundle nonexistent `createAccordionController`, so the build fails before producing any public primitive entrypoints. Add the missing controller exports or map catalog entries to verified source exports before bundling.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/core/scripts/build.mjs, line 24:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen the build reaches `accordion`, it asks tsup to bundle nonexistent `createAccordionController`, so the build fails before producing any public primitive entrypoints. Add the missing controller exports or map catalog entries to verified source exports before bundling.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@\\n+        ? 'CreateHoverCardProps'\\n+        : `${primitive.name}Props`,\\n+      runtime: interactive\\n+        ? `create${primitive.name}Controller`\\n+        : `${primitive.name}Contract`,\\n+      secondaryType: interactive\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:19:44Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831870338\",\"id\":3831870338,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":47,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":24,\"path\":\"uifn/core/scripts/build.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:19:48Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=f7c442d0-9cda-425a-b716-bbb0721f56ad --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=7bb8304f-392d-4952-ab05-eaf35f279889 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} --\\u003e\\nP1: The audit endpoint returns raw `AdminAuditEvent` objects, but this loader forwards them as `AuditEventViewModel` without mapping. Audit rows therefore read undefined `occurredAt`/`actor`/`action`, render the object target as `[object Object]`, and show raw outcomes as `Unknown`; map each event to t…132829 tokens truncated…or use a separately defined update operation.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:13:43Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837847469\",\"id\":3837847469,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":303,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:13:44Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"The token is already verifiable when this required audit write starts. If it fails and `revoke()` also rejects, lines 1112-1114 suppress that failure and return 503 with a live unaudited token; make revocation failure durable and retryable, or use sequencing that cannot leave this state.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Audit failure can strand an activated confirmation\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1067-1073` — makes the token verifiable before the success event is durable.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1102-1115` — attempts revocation after audit failure but discards revocation failure without recording reconciliation state.\\n- `superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts:741-775` — covers only successful revocation and hard-codes verification to false.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- A failed issuance response must not leave a verifiable confirmation without its required success audit.\\n- Cover simultaneous success-audit and revocation failure with a verifier that reflects actual activation state.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:13:44Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837847471\",\"id\":3837847471,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":1102,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:13:44Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"`stableSerialize` treats every object by enumerable entries, so `{ const: {} }` accepts `new Date()` even though JSON transport emits an ISO string. Restrict constants, enum members, and compared values to JSON data, or use type-aware comparison that rejects non-plain and cyclic objects.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Structural equality accepts non-JSON values\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `packages/admin/src/validator.ts:16-24` — structurally serializes arbitrary `unknown` objects.\\n- `packages/admin/src/types.ts:20-27` — permits `unknown` schema constants and enum members.\\n- `packages/admin/src/validator.test.ts:40-59` — covers plain JSON containers only.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Runtime equality must agree with the JSON value that REST and MCP transport actually emit.\\n- Add non-plain and cyclic-value coverage so invalid adapter output is rejected rather than retyped in transport.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:13:44Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837847474\",\"id\":3837847474,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":22,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:13:44Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 16a31f1 by auditing while the token is still staged and activating only afterward.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32623271995/job/97154635862) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:37:46Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837883366\",\"id\":3837883366,\"in_reply_to_id\":3837847471,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":1102,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:37:46Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 16a31f1 by restricting structural comparison to finite, acyclic JSON data.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32623271995/job/97154635862) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:37:49Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837883427\",\"id\":3837883427,\"in_reply_to_id\":3837847474,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":22,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:37:49Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 16a31f1 by preserving one TLS configuration per attachment identity.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32623271995/job/97154635862) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:37:52Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837883475\",\"id\":3837883475,\"in_reply_to_id\":3837847469,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":303,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:37:52Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=f6a06edf-39cd-4d25-acb5-7952783aa704 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=4777accd-4d7f-40ee-8add-816fdeaf04ee --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: When multiple `allOf` branches define the same property, the shallow merge drops constraints from earlier branches. Derive field presentation separately and validate against the complete property composition (or the original input schema) so the console does not dispatch values it presents as valid but the admin validator rejects.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts, line 45:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen multiple `allOf` branches define the same property, the shallow merge drops constraints from earlier branches. Derive field presentation separately and validate against the complete property composition (or the original input schema) so the console does not dispatch values it presents as valid but the admin validator rejects.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -36,9 +36,18 @@ function fieldType(schema: AdminJsonSchema): ActionFieldType {\\n+  const collectObjectShape = (candidate: AdminJsonSchema): void =\\u003e {\\n+    for (const name of candidate.required ?? []) required.add(name);\\n+    for (const [name, property] of Object.entries(candidate.properties ?? {})) {\\n+      properties[name] = properties[name] ? { ...properties[name], ...property } : property;\\n+    }\\n+    for (const branch of candidate.allOf ?? []) collectObjectShape(branch);\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:39:13Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837885494\",\"id\":3837885494,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":45,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":45,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:39:14Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=65868d1e-ab59-422a-ae0f-bcef908ac0ed --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=4777accd-4d7f-40ee-8add-816fdeaf04ee --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When `uniqueItems` contains unsupported object values, `keys.includes(undefined)` bypasses uniqueness validation, and the open item schema accepts those values. Reject unsupported JSON values here (or emit a validation issue) rather than silently skipping `uniqueItems`.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/validator.ts, line 221:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen `uniqueItems` contains unsupported object values, `keys.includes(undefined)` bypasses uniqueness validation, and the open item schema accepts those values. Reject unsupported JSON values here (or emit a validation issue) rather than silently skipping `uniqueItems`.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -179,8 +217,8 @@ export function validateAdminValue(\\n-      const keys = value.map(stableSerialize);\\n-      if (new Set(keys).size !== keys.length)\\n+      const keys = value.map((item) =\\u003e comparableJsonValue(item));\\n+      if (!keys.includes(undefined) \\u0026\\u0026 new Set(keys).size !== keys.length)\\n         issues.push({\\n           path,\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n      if (keys.includes(undefined)) {\\n        issues.push({\\n          path,\\n          message: \\\"must contain only JSON values\\\",\\n          keyword: \\\"type\\\",\\n        });\\n      } else if (new Set(keys).size !== keys.length)\\n```\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:39:14Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837885495\",\"id\":3837885495,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":221,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":221,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:39:14Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=244a7b3d-8a40-4461-a334-0f82c44b3458 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=4777accd-4d7f-40ee-8add-816fdeaf04ee --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} --\\u003e\\nP2: When distinct JSON property names compare equal under locale collation, this sort makes structural equality depend on property insertion order. Use a deterministic code-unit key comparator instead of `localeCompare`.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/validator.ts, line 37:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen distinct JSON property names compare equal under locale collation, this sort makes structural equality depend on property insertion order. Use a deterministic code-unit key comparator instead of `localeCompare`.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -14,14 +14,38 @@ export interface AdminValidationIssue {\\n+  seen.add(value);\\n+  const entries = isArray\\n+    ? Array.from(value, (item, index) =\\u003e [String(index), item] as const)\\n+    : Object.entries(value as Record\\u003cstring, unknown\\u003e).sort(([leftKey], [rightKey]) =\\u003e leftKey.localeCompare(rightKey));\\n+  const serialized: string[] = [];\\n+  for (const [key, item] of entries) {\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:39:14Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837885501\",\"id\":3837885501,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":37,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":37,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:39:14Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Reconcile variable records after provider deletion**\\n\\nWhen the provider deletion succeeds but `store.deleteVariable` rejects, the stale variable record remains while this request returns an error. Retrying with the same idempotency key replays that error, and retrying with a new key can still never remove the record when the provider reports that the already-deleted variable is not found, because this path does not tolerate provider-not-found as `detachDomain` does. Treat an already-absent provider variable as success or persist a deletion intent so the store record can be reconciled.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:40:38Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837887588\",\"id\":3837887588,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":414,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":414,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:40:38Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"This map coalesces requests only within one `HostFnOperatorService` instance. Two instances sharing a durable store can both observe no hostname, generate different domain IDs, and call the provider because the store contract has no atomic reservation.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Attachment identity is not serialized across service instances\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:214-217` — keeps in-flight identities in an instance-local map.\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:52-74` — exposes separate list and put operations but no atomic hostname reservation.\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:324-350` — performs a read, generates a random ID, then writes the intent.\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/__tests__/operator.test.ts:176-199` — exercises two calls through only one service instance.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Concurrent attachment requests sharing a durable store must converge on one domain ID and one immutable hostname/TLS identity across service instances.\\n\\n## Suggested approach\\n- Add an atomic reserve-or-read operation to the store contract, or require an equivalent unique scope/target/hostname constraint that returns the winning intent.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:41:30Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837889099\",\"id\":3837889099,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":301,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":301,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:41:31Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"`localeCompare()` can return zero for distinct keys such as composed `é` and decomposed `e\\\\u0301`, so stable sort preserves their insertion order. Equivalent objects containing both keys can therefore produce different comparison strings and fail `const`, `enum`, or `uniqueItems`; use a locale-independent code-unit ordering.\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:41:30Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837889101\",\"id\":3837889101,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":37,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":37,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:41:31Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"After this durable `succeeded` event, the process can stop before `activate()`, leaving an unusable staged token with a successful terminal audit. The documented reconciliation handles attempts without terminal events, so this inverse state needs a durable activation/reconciliation path rather than an unrecoverable success window.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Confirmation success can precede durable activation\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1067-1089` — persists success before attempting activation.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/types.ts:171-186` — defines staged tokens as unusable until activation.\\n- `superconsole/README.md:149-166` — requires durable injected infrastructure but describes reconciliation only for missing terminal events.\\n- `superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts:741-823` — covers in-process audit and activation failures, not interruption between the two steps.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- A durable success event must imply an active token, or durable state must identify and reconcile success-audited tokens whose activation has not completed.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:41:30Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837889103\",\"id\":3837889103,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":1067,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":1067,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:41:31Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Shallow-merging the same property across `allOf` branches overwrites earlier nested `properties` and `required` constraints. For example, branches requiring `payload.a` and `payload.b` leave only the latter schema here, so the form accepts input that the dispatcher rejects against the original schema.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Overlapping allOf property schemas lose constraints\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts:42-49` — flattens `allOf` with object spread rather than preserving intersection semantics.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts:87-132` — validates the flattened property schema instead of the original combined schema.\\n- `superconsole/tests/ui/action-form.test.ts:45-63` — covers only disjoint properties across branches.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Editable fields may be discovered across branches, but validation must retain every constraint applied to a repeated property by the full `allOf` schema.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:41:30Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837889106\",\"id\":3837889106,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":45,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":45,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:41:31Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n"},"started_at_ms":1787470098005,"completed_at_ms":1787470101615}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T07:28:22.992Z","ordinal":12061,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a024c5-b91b-72b3-ad56-490032d022a1","turn_id":"01a02d84-67e7-7143-9c14-0a1cb505f664","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-17c69851-37a1-47e7-8e88-04e0091c03b5","process_id":"62665","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api graphql --paginate -f query='query($endCursor: String) { repository(owner: \"21nCo\", name: \"super-functions\") { pullRequest(number: 116) { reviewThreads(first: 100, after: $endCursor) { nodes { isResolved path comments(first: 20) { nodes { body author { login } createdAt outdated url diffHunk originalLine line } } } pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor } } } } }' --jq '.data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[] | select(.isResolved == false)'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other gh api graphql --paginate -f query='query($endCursor: String) { repository(owner: \"21nCo\", name: \"super-functions\") { pullRequest(number: 116) { reviewThreads(first: 100, after: $endCursor) { nodes { isResolved path comments(first: 20) { nodes { body author { login } createdAt outdated url diffHunk originalLine line } } } pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor } } } } }' --jq '.data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[] | select(.isResolved == false)'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"{\"comments\":{\"nodes\":[{\"author\":{\"login\":\"github-advanced-security\"},\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Prototype-polluting function\\n\\nThe property chain [segment](1) is recursively assigned to [current](2) without guarding against prototype pollution.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/49)\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"diffHunk\":\"@@ -0,0 +1,307 @@\\n+import { ADMIN_API_PREFIX, fetchAdmin, materializeAdminActionHref, scopedConsoleHref, withAdminScope, type AdminFetch } from './admin-api';\\n+import {\\n+  inferAdminResourceColumns,\\n+  inferAdminResourceFields,\\n+  inferAdminResourceStatus,\\n+  inferAdminResourceTitle,\\n+  isAdminRecord,\\n+  moduleById,\\n+  normalizeAdminResourceRows,\\n+  readAdminPresentationField,\\n+  type AdminErrorViewModel,\\n+  type AdminResourceViewModel,\\n+  type RegistryViewModel,\\n+  type ResourceDetailViewModel,\\n+  type ResourceListViewModel,\\n+} from './view-models';\\n+\\n+interface ResourceRouteInput {\\n+  fetcher: AdminFetch;\\n+  url: URL;\\n+  registry: RegistryViewModel;\\n+  moduleId: string;\\n+  resourceId: string;\\n+  sourceModuleId?: string;\\n+}\\n+\\n+function resourceForRoute(\\n+  resources: AdminResourceViewModel[] | undefined,\\n+  resourceId: string,\\n+  sourceModuleId?: string\\n+): AdminResourceViewModel | undefined {\\n+  return resources?.find((candidate) =\\u003e {\\n+    const canonicalId = candidate.resourceId ?? candidate.id;\\n+    if (sourceModuleId) {\\n+      return candidate.sourceModuleId?.toLowerCase() === sourceModuleId.toLowerCase()\\n+        \\u0026\\u0026 canonicalId.toLowerCase() === resourceId.toLowerCase();\\n+    }\\n+    return candidate.id.toLowerCase() === resourceId.toLowerCase()\\n+      || (!candidate.foldedIntoModuleId \\u0026\\u0026 canonicalId.toLowerCase() === resourceId.toLowerCase());\\n+  });\\n+}\\n+\\n+function unavailable(resourceId: string, moduleId: string): AdminErrorViewModel {\\n+  return {\\n+    status: 404,\\n+    code: 'RESOURCE_NOT_ENABLED',\\n+    message: `${resourceId} is not an enabled ${moduleId} administration resource.`,\\n+  };\\n+}\\n+\\n+function parseQueryValue(raw: string, schema: AdminResourceViewModel['listInputSchema']): unknown {\\n+  const types = schema?.type ? (Array.isArray(schema.type) ? schema.type : [schema.type]) : [];\\n+  if (types.includes('null') \\u0026\\u0026 raw === 'null') return null;\\n+  if (types.includes('integer') || types.includes('number')) {\\n+    const parsed = Number(raw);\\n+    return Number.isFinite(parsed) ? parsed : raw;\\n+  }\\n+  if (types.includes('boolean')) return raw === 'true' ? true : raw === 'false' ? false : raw;\\n+  if (types.includes('object') || types.includes('array')) {\\n+    try { return JSON.parse(raw); } catch { return raw; }\\n+  }\\n+  return raw;\\n+}\\n+\\n+function inputSchemaAtPath(\\n+  schema: AdminResourceViewModel['listInputSchema'],\\n+  path: string,\\n+): AdminResourceViewModel['listInputSchema'] {\\n+  let current = schema;\\n+  for (const segment of path.split('.')) {\\n+    if (!current) return undefined;\\n+    const types = current.type ? (Array.isArray(current.type) ? current.type : [current.type]) : [];\\n+    if (!types.includes('object')) return undefined;\\n+    current = current.properties?.[segment];\\n+  }\\n+  return current;\\n+}\\n+\\n+function setInputPath(target: Record\\u003cstring, unknown\\u003e, path: string, value: unknown): void {\\n+  const segments = path.split('.');\\n+  let current = target;\\n+  segments.forEach((segment, index) =\\u003e {\\n+    if (index === segments.length - 1) {\\n+      current[segment] = value;\",\"line\":87,\"originalLine\":84,\"outdated\":false,\"url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736417\"}]},\"isResolved\":false,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/resource-pages.ts\"}\n{\"comments\":{\"nodes\":[{\"author\":{\"login\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\"},\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Preserve numeric-looking string document IDs**\\n\\nFor a composite target such as `orders:001`, this converts the document ID from the string `\\\"001\\\"` to the number `1`. Single-document indexing therefore targets a different ID than batch indexing, which preserves string IDs, and `remove-document` can delete numeric document `1` instead of string document `\\\"001\\\"`. Preserve the ID suffix as a string or carry explicit ID-type information in the input.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-21T16:01:33Z\",\"diffHunk\":\"@@ -0,0 +1,169 @@\\n+import type { SearchAdapter, SearchDocument } from \\\"@searchfn/adapter-contracts\\\";\\n+import {\\n+  AdminError,\\n+  type AdminOperationContext,\\n+  type AdminOperationResult,\\n+} from \\\"@superfunctions/admin\\\";\\n+import type {\\n+  SearchFnAdminRecord,\\n+  SearchFnAdminService,\\n+  SearchFnItemOutput,\\n+  SearchFnListOutput,\\n+  SearchFnMutationOutput,\\n+} from \\\"./types.js\\\";\\n+\\n+type JsonRecord = Record\\u003cstring, unknown\\u003e;\\n+\\n+export interface SearchFnDomainAdminServiceOptions {\\n+  /** Must resolve an adapter already isolated to the active scope and optional namespace/region. */\\n+  adapter(context: AdminOperationContext): SearchAdapter | Promise\\u003cSearchAdapter\\u003e;\\n+  /** Returns the configured index names visible inside the same isolated adapter. */\\n+  resources(context: AdminOperationContext): readonly string[] | Promise\\u003creadonly string[]\\u003e;\\n+}\\n+\\n+function object(value: unknown, name: string): JsonRecord {\\n+  if (!value || typeof value !== \\\"object\\\" || Array.isArray(value)) {\\n+    throw new AdminError(\\\"invalid_argument\\\", `${name} must be an object.`);\\n+  }\\n+  return value as JsonRecord;\\n+}\\n+\\n+function string(value: unknown, name: string): string {\\n+  if (typeof value !== \\\"string\\\" || value.length === 0) {\\n+    throw new AdminError(\\\"invalid_argument\\\", `${name} must be a non-empty string.`);\\n+  }\\n+  return value;\\n+}\\n+\\n+function item(value: object): AdminOperationResult\\u003cSearchFnItemOutput\\u003e {\\n+  return { ok: true, data: { item: { ...value } } };\\n+}\\n+\\n+function list(values: object[]): AdminOperationResult\\u003cSearchFnListOutput\\u003e {\\n+  return { ok: true, data: { items: values.map((value) =\\u003e ({ ...value })), nextCursor: null } };\\n+}\\n+\\n+function accepted(value: JsonRecord): AdminOperationResult\\u003cSearchFnMutationOutput\\u003e {\\n+  return { ok: true, data: { accepted: true, ...value } };\\n+}\\n+\\n+function splitDocumentId(value: string): { resource: string; id: string | number } {\\n+  const separator = value.indexOf(\\\":\\\");\\n+  if (separator \\u003c= 0 || separator === value.length - 1) {\\n+    throw new AdminError(\\\"invalid_argument\\\", \\\"SearchFn document targets use the form resource:id.\\\");\\n+  }\\n+  const id = value.slice(separator + 1);\\n+  return { resource: value.slice(0, separator), id: /^\\\\d+$/.test(id) ? Number(id) : id };\",\"line\":null,\"originalLine\":56,\"outdated\":true,\"url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831751943\"}]},\"isResolved\":false,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\"}\n{\"comments\":{\"nodes\":[{\"author\":{\"login\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector\"},\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Apply the declared index-list query parameters**\\n\\nWhen an installation has many configured indexes or the console supplies search/filter/pagination input, `listIndexes` ignores the entire input and always returns every index with `nextCursor: null`. This contradicts the operation's cursor-pagination declaration and makes the resource-list search UI return unrelated entries while bypassing the declared 200-item maximum; honor `limit`, `cursor`, and the advertised query fields before building the result.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-21T16:01:33Z\",\"diffHunk\":\"@@ -0,0 +1,169 @@\\n+import type { SearchAdapter, SearchDocument } from \\\"@searchfn/adapter-contracts\\\";\\n+import {\\n+  AdminError,\\n+  type AdminOperationContext,\\n+  type AdminOperationResult,\\n+} from \\\"@superfunctions/admin\\\";\\n+import type {\\n+  SearchFnAdminRecord,\\n+  SearchFnAdminService,\\n+  SearchFnItemOutput,\\n+  SearchFnListOutput,\\n+  SearchFnMutationOutput,\\n+} from \\\"./types.js\\\";\\n+\\n+type JsonRecord = Record\\u003cstring, unknown\\u003e;\\n+\\n+export interface SearchFnDomainAdminServiceOptions {\\n+  /** Must resolve an adapter already isolated to the active scope and optional namespace/region. */\\n+  adapter(context: AdminOperationContext): SearchAdapter | Promise\\u003cSearchAdapter\\u003e;\\n+  /** Returns the configured index names visible inside the same isolated adapter. */\\n+  resources(context: AdminOperationContext): readonly string[] | Promise\\u003creadonly string[]\\u003e;\\n+}\\n+\\n+function object(value: unknown, name: string): JsonRecord {\\n+  if (!value || typeof value !== \\\"object\\\" || Array.isArray(value)) {\\n+    throw new AdminError(\\\"invalid_argument\\\", `${name} must be an object.`);\\n+  }\\n+  return value as JsonRecord;\\n+}\\n+\\n+function string(value: unknown, name: string): string {\\n+  if (typeof value !== \\\"string\\\" || value.length === 0) {\\n+    throw new AdminError(\\\"invalid_argument\\\", `${name} must be a non-empty string.`);\\n+  }\\n+  return value;\\n+}\\n+\\n+function item(value: object): AdminOperationResult\\u003cSearchFnItemOutput\\u003e {\\n+  return { ok: true, data: { item: { ...value } } };\\n+}\\n+\\n+function list(values: object[]): AdminOperationResult\\u003cSearchFnListOutput\\u003e {\\n+  return { ok: true, data: { items: values.map((value) =\\u003e ({ ...value })), nextCursor: null } };\\n+}\\n+\\n+function accepted(value: JsonRecord): AdminOperationResult\\u003cSearchFnMutationOutput\\u003e {\\n+  return { ok: true, data: { accepted: true, ...value } };\\n+}\\n+\\n+function splitDocumentId(value: string): { resource: string; id: string | number } {\\n+  const separator = value.indexOf(\\\":\\\");\\n+  if (separator \\u003c= 0 || separator === value.length - 1) {\\n+    throw new AdminError(\\\"invalid_argument\\\", \\\"SearchFn document targets use the form resource:id.\\\");\\n+  }\\n+  const id = value.slice(separator + 1);\\n+  return { resource: value.slice(0, separator), id: /^\\\\d+$/.test(id) ? Number(id) : id };\\n+}\\n+\\n+function documents(value: unknown): SearchDocument[] {\\n+  if (!Array.isArray(value) || value.length === 0) {\\n+    throw new AdminError(\\\"invalid_argument\\\", \\\"payload.documents must be a non-empty array.\\\");\\n+  }\\n+  return value.map((entry, index) =\\u003e {\\n+    const document = object(entry, `payload.documents[${index}]`);\\n+    const id = document.id;\\n+    if (typeof id !== \\\"string\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 typeof id !== \\\"number\\\") {\\n+      throw new AdminError(\\\"invalid_argument\\\", `payload.documents[${index}].id must be a string or number.`);\\n+    }\\n+    const fields = object(document.fields, `payload.documents[${index}].fields`);\\n+    if (Object.values(fields).some((field) =\\u003e typeof field !== \\\"string\\\")) {\\n+      throw new AdminError(\\\"invalid_argument\\\", `payload.documents[${index}].fields values must be strings.`);\\n+    }\\n+    return { id, fields: fields as Record\\u003cstring, string\\u003e };\\n+  });\\n+}\\n+\\n+/** Delegates to the configured SearchAdapter; no raw backend or cross-scope query is constructed here. */\\n+export function createSearchFnDomainAdminService(\\n+  options: SearchFnDomainAdminServiceOptions,\\n+): SearchFnAdminService {\\n+  const state = async (context: AdminOperationContext) =\\u003e {\\n+    const adapter = await options.adapter(context);\\n+    const resources = [...await options.resources(context)];\\n+    return {\\n+      adapter,\\n+      resources,\\n+      adapterInfo: {\\n+        id: adapter.name,\\n+        name: adapter.name,\\n+        status: \\\"available\\\",\\n+        capabilities: adapter.capabilities ?? {},\\n+      } satisfies SearchFnAdminRecord,\\n+      indexInfo: resources.map((resource) =\\u003e ({ id: resource, name: resource, status: \\\"available\\\" })),\\n+    };\\n+  };\\n+\\n+  return {\\n+    async listAdapters(_input, context) {\\n+      const { adapterInfo } = await state(context);\\n+      return list([adapterInfo]);\\n+    },\\n+    async getAdapter(input, context) {\\n+      const { adapter, adapterInfo } = await state(context);\\n+      if (string(input.id, \\\"id\\\") !== adapter.name) {\\n+        throw new AdminError(\\\"not_found\\\", \\\"SearchFn adapter was not found in the active scope.\\\");\\n+      }\\n+      return item(adapterInfo);\\n+    },\\n+    async listIndexes(_input, context) {\\n+      return list((await state(context)).indexInfo);\",\"line\":null,\"originalLine\":110,\"outdated\":true,\"url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831751947\"}]},\"isResolved\":false,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\"}\n{\"comments\":{\"nodes\":[{\"author\":{\"login\":\"cubic-dev-ai\"},\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=1e8a9759-bd72-4e24-bd8c-217d1bba06d6 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=7bb8304f-392d-4952-ab05-eaf35f279889 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} --\\u003e\\nP1: When the build reaches `accordion`, it asks tsup to bundle nonexistent `createAccordionController`, so the build fails before producing any public primitive entrypoints. Add the missing controller exports or map catalog entries to verified source exports before bundling.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/core/scripts/build.mjs, line 24:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen the build reaches `accordion`, it asks tsup to bundle nonexistent `createAccordionController`, so the build fails before producing any public primitive entrypoints. Add the missing controller exports or map catalog entries to verified source exports before bundling.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -0,0 +1,8