 (unresolved issues)</summary>\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\n\\\\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n<file name=\\\\\\\"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\\\\\\\">\\\\n\\\\n<violation number=\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\" location=\\\\\\\"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts:45\\\\\\\">\\\\nP2: When multiple `allOf` branches define the same property, the shallow merge drops constraints from earlier branches. Derive field presentation separately and validate against the complete property composition (or the original input schema) so the console does not dispatch values it presents as valid but the admin validator rejects.</violation>\\\\n</file>\\\\n\\\\n<file name=\\\\\\\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\\\\\\\">\\\\n\\\\n<violation number=\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\" location=\\\\\\\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts:37\\\\\\\">\\\\nP2: When distinct JSON property names compare equal under locale collation, this sort makes structural equality depend on property insertion order. Use a deterministic code-unit key comparator instead of `localeCompare`.</violation>\\\\n\\\\n<violation number=\\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\" location=\\\\\\\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts:221\\\\\\\">\\\\nP2: When `uniqueItems` contains unsupported object values, `keys.includes(undefined)` bypasses uniqueness validation, and the open item schema accepts those values. Reject unsupported JSON values here (or emit a validation issue) rather than silently skipping `uniqueItems`.</violation>\\\\n</file>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n</details>\\\\n\\\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/116/ai_pr_review_1787466863082_f6fbac11-740c-4c3d-85d2-00e52e1dea83?returnTo=http