{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T07:33:37.253Z","ordinal":12176,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0d3207775ece027d016a8aa24d730887d0ab809354a4f33f08","status":"completed","call_id":"call_Idd2o9s8LNQB6d2okBlD6B5v","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/superconsole/README.md\\n@@\\n-Confirmation services must return an unusable staged token from `issue`.\\n-Super Console writes the succeeded audit while the token is still staged, then\\n-activates it. Activation failures are recorded as denied events and trigger an\\n-idempotent `revoke`; audit failures therefore cannot leave a live unaudited token.\\n+Confirmation services must return an unusable staged token from `issue` and\\n+durably bind it to the supplied terminal audit ID in `prepareActivation`.\\n+Super Console then writes that exact succeeded audit and activates the token.\\n+Providers must reconcile prepared records after interruption: activate when the\\n+bound success audit exists, otherwise revoke or expire them. Activation failures\\n+are recorded as denied events and trigger an idempotent `revoke`; audit failures\\n+therefore cannot leave a live unaudited token, while a post-audit interruption\\n+remains durably identifiable and recoverable.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02d84-67e7-7143-9c14-0a1cb505f664","create_time":1787470409.171525}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T07:33:37.268Z","ordinal":12177,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a024c5-b91b-72b3-ad56-490032d022a1","turn_id":"01a02d84-67e7-7143-9c14-0a1cb505f664","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-754fe8af-aedc-4eb9-ad23-68e1411c6847","changes":{"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/superconsole/README.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -54,6 +54,10 @@\n \n-Confirmation services must return an unusable staged token from `issue`.\n-Super Console writes the succeeded audit while the token is still staged, then\n-activates it. Activation failures are recorded as denied events and trigger an\n-idempotent `revoke`; audit failures therefore cannot leave a live unaudited token.\n+Confirmation services must return an unusable staged token from `issue` and\n+durably bind it to the supplied terminal audit ID in `prepareActivation`.\n+Super Console then writes that exact succeeded audit and activates the token.\n+Providers must reconcile prepared records after interruption: activate when the\n+bound success audit exists, otherwise revoke or expire them. Activation failures\n+are recorded as denied events and trigger an idempotent `revoke`; audit failures\n+therefore cannot leave a live unaudited token, while a post-audit interruption\n+remains durably identifiable and recoverable.\n \n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/superconsole/README.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1787470417268,"completed_at_ms":1787470417268}}
