ce\\\":10} --\\u003e\\nP2: For integer-like property names, `Object.fromEntries`/`JSON.stringify` undo the code-unit sort, so `canonicalJson` is not actually canonical in the ordering promised by `compareCodeUnits`. Serialize sorted entries directly or use a representation that prevents integer-key reordering.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/core/src/canonical.ts, line 15:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eFor integer-like property names, `Object.fromEntries`/`JSON.stringify` undo the code-unit sort, so `canonicalJson` is not actually canonical in the ordering promised by `compareCodeUnits`. Serialize sorted entries directly or use a representation that prevents integer-key reordering.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@\\n+    return Object.fromEntries(\\n+      Object.entries(value as Record\\u003cstring, unknown\\u003e)\\n+        .filter(([, entry]) =\\u003e entry !== undefined)\\n+        .sort(([left], [right]) =\\u003e compareCodeUnits(left, right))\\n+        .map(([key, entry]) =\\u003e [key, canonicalize(entry)]),\\n+    );\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`8d16f12`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/8d16f12d9a673cbed04f6c20cc9a06b0e770389e)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:20:59Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831878612\",\"id\":3831878612,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":21,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":15,\"path\":\"mcpfn/core/src/canonical.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T02:52:47Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 8d16f12 by rejecting non-default API base paths at construction.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32547360654/job/96968142055) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T02:53:46Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3834896880\",\"id\":3834896880,\"in_reply_to_id\":3831799631,\"line\":9,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":9,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T02:53:46Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 8d16f12 by authorizing safe-method operations from their matched safety classification.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32547360654/job/96968142055) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T02:53:55Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3834897177\",\"id\":3834897177,\"in_reply_to_id\":3831799619,\"line\":631,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":612,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T02:53:55Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Rounding to the nearest step and then clamping can still produce an unaligned endpoint: `{ min: 0, max: 10, step: 4 }` rounds to `12` and clamps back to `10`. Consequently `End` returns a value the same range's step contract cannot produce.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Range endpoint remains off-step after overshoot\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `uifn/core/src/algorithms/range.ts:39-40` — clamp converts an overshooting aligned value into an unaligned maximum.\\n- `uifn/core/src/algorithms/range.ts:63` — `End` delegates to this path.\\n- `uifn/core/src/__tests__/phase-06-algorithms.test.ts:113` — the `step: 3` case rounds down and misses the overshoot case.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Keyboard endpoints and normalized values must follow one consistent step-alignment policy for non-divisible ranges.\\n- Cover a range such as `{ min: 0, max: 10, step: 4 }` where nearest-step rounding overshoots.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T02:58:51Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3834909065\",\"id\":3834909065,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":53,\"original_commit_id\":\"8d16f12d9a673cbed04f6c20cc9a06b0e770389e\",\"original_line\":40,\"path\":\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/range.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T02:58:52Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=4bb93148-4ee5-4901-9212-e34211f9a3af --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=e23e6324-2c6c-4e6a-843e-4e4bd3612e24 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} --\\u003e\\nP2: For valid finite ranges near `Number.MAX_VALUE`, the decimal shift can overflow and make `alignRangeValue` return `NaN` instead of a bounded value. Check the shifted number for finiteness and fall back without scaling when it overflows.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/core/src/algorithms/range.ts, line 18:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eFor valid finite ranges near `Number.MAX_VALUE`, the decimal shift can overflow and make `alignRangeValue` return `NaN` instead of a bounded value. Check the shifted number for finiteness and fall back without scaling when it overflows.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -8,8 +8,16 @@ export interface RangeDefinition {\\n+\\n+function roundRangeValue(value: number, precision: number): number {\\n+  const [coefficient, exponentText = '0'] = String(value).split('e');\\n+  const shifted = Math.round(Number(`${coefficient}e${Number(exponentText) + precision}`));\\n+  const [rounded, roundedExponent = '0'] = String(shifted).split('e');\\n+  return Number(`${rounded}e${Number(roundedExponent) - precision}`);\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n  const shiftedValue = Number(`${coefficient}e${Number(exponentText) + precision}`);\\n  if (!Number.isFinite(shiftedValue)) return value;\\n  const shifted = Math.round(shiftedValue);\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`8ad9b66`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/8ad9b668d13ae8354920ab8d6e4ef6f1b01eeaec)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T03:11:10Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3834931001\",\"id\":3834931001,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":18,\"original_commit_id\":\"8d16f12d9a673cbed04f6c20cc9a06b0e770389e\",\"original_line\":18,\"path\":\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/range.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T04:17:03Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=43728912-4ab4-431b-a5b2-3c85221ab368 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=e23e6324-2c6c-4e6a-843e-4e4bd3612e24 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When a registered manifest uses `constructor`, `prototype`, or `__proto__` in a query path, this guard throws before the request can produce an admin error view. Reject reserved path segments during manifest validation, or catch this construction error in `loadResourceList` so the resource page does not fail unexpectedly.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/src/lib/components/resource-pages.ts, line 81:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a registered manifest uses `constructor`, `prototype`, or `__proto__` in a query path, this guard throws before the request can produce an admin error view. Reject reserved path segments during manifest validation, or catch this construction error in `loadResourceList` so the resource page does not fail unexpectedly.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -78,14 +78,17 @@ function inputSchemaAtPath(\\n \\n function setInputPath(target: Record\\u003cstring, unknown\\u003e, path: string, value: unknown): void {\\n   const segments = path.split('.');\\n+  if (segments.some((segment) =\\u003e segment === '__proto__' || segment === 'prototype' || segment === 'constructor')) {\\n+    throw new Error('Administration input paths cannot address object prototype properties.');\\n+  }\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`21fbc39`](https://github.com/21nCo/s