\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T03:11:11Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3834931014\",\"id\":3834931014,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":15,\"original_commit_id\":\"8d16f12d9a673cbed04f6c20cc9a06b0e770389e\",\"original_line\":13,\"path\":\"uifn/core/scripts/build.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T03:11:12Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=7f4cb88a-a8c4-4182-9da6-4649f3a956a9 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=e23e6324-2c6c-4e6a-843e-4e4bd3612e24 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: The catch block drops the error entirely: ssrFixStacktrace(cause) is now a no-op whose result is unused, and the cause is neither sent to the client nor logged. When a request fails, the test just sees 'Internal Server Error' (HTTP 500) with no record of the underlying error, forcing a reproduce to debug. Log the cause server-side before ending the response.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/svelte/tests/phase-14-ssr-hydration.mjs, line 83:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThe catch block drops the error entirely: ssrFixStacktrace(cause) is now a no-op whose result is unused, and the cause is neither sent to the client nor logged. When a request fails, the test just sees 'Internal Server Error' (HTTP 500) with no record of the underlying error, forcing a reproduce to debug. Log the cause server-side before ending the response.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -79,7 +79,8 @@ const server = createHttpServer(async (request, response) =\\u003e {\\n     response.statusCode = 500;\\n-    response.end(cause instanceof Error ? cause.stack : String(cause));\\n+    response.setHeader('content-type', 'text/plain; charset=utf-8');\\n+    response.end('Internal Server Error');\\n   }\\n });\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`8ad9b66`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/8ad9b668d13ae8354920ab8d6e4ef6f1b01eeaec)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T03:11:11Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3834931015\",\"id\":3834931015,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":84,\"original_commit_id\":\"8d16f12d9a673cbed04f6c20cc9a06b0e770389e\",\"original_line\":83,\"path\":\"uifn/svelte/tests/phase-14-ssr-hydration.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T04:16:59Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=1dd40970-7313-474a-b2b6-01bef11be5d0 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=e23e6324-2c6c-4e6a-843e-4e4bd3612e24 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":5} --\\u003e\\nP2: `createLegacyAvatar` never emits the current state to a newly subscribed callback, so a subscriber that reads after subscribing sees nothing until a later `setLoading`/`setLoaded`/`setError` transition. Controllers in this codebase (`createUIFnController` at uifn/core/src/controller.ts:412) and Svelte-store-backed adapters deliver the initial state on subscribe, so a consumer relying on the initial 'idle' state will render stale/empty until an action fires. Invoke the callback with the current `state` inside `subscribe` (before adding it to the set, defensively) to match that contract.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/core/src/primitives/legacy-compat.ts, line 35:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003e`createLegacyAvatar` never emits the current state to a newly subscribed callback, so a subscriber that reads after subscribing sees nothing until a later `setLoading`/`setLoaded`/`setError` transition. Controllers in this codebase (`createUIFnController` at uifn/core/src/controller.ts:412) and Svelte-store-backed adapters deliver the initial state on subscribe, so a consumer relying on the initial 'idle' state will render stale/empty until an action fires. Invoke the callback with the current `state` inside `subscribe` (before adding it to the set, defensively) to match that contract.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@\\n+      setLoaded: () =\\u003e update('loaded'),\\n+      setError: () =\\u003e update('error'),\\n+    }),\\n+    subscribe(callback) {\\n+      subscribers.add(callback);\\n+      return () =\\u003e subscribers.delete(callback);\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    subscribe(callback) {\\n      subscribers.add(callback);\\n      callback(state);\\n      return () =\\u003e subscribers.delete(callback);\\n    },\\n```\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`8ad9b66`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/8ad9b668d13ae8354920ab8d6e4ef6f1b01eeaec)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T03:11:11Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3834931027\",\"id\":3834931027,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":46,\"original_commit_id\":\"8d16f12d9a673cbed04f6c20cc9a06b0e770389e\",\"original_line\":38,\"path\":\"uifn/core/src/primitives/legacy-compat.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T04:16:55Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=53368711-c4f6-4ddd-a894-4fa095bceaac --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=e23e6324-2c6c-4e6a-843e-4e4bd3612e24 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":5} --\\u003e\\nP3: This service issues and accepts plain offset cursors that are not signed or authenticated; `decodeAdminCursor`'s own contract requires production providers to issue opaque, signed cursor positions. Any operator in scope can forge or alter an offset. This is only a data-exposure/page-skip risk (scope is still validated), but it diverges from the documented guidance to use signed cursors for production admin surfaces.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 71:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThis service issues and accepts plain offset cursors that are not signed or authenticated; `decodeAdminCursor`'s own contract requires production providers to issue opaque, signed cursor positions. Any operator in scope can forge or alter an offset. This is only a data-exposure/page-skip risk (scope is still validated), but it diverges from the documented guidance to use signed cursors for production admin surfaces.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -39,21 +43,63 @@ function item(value: object): AdminOperationResult\\u003cSearchFnItemOutput\\u003e {\\n+    }\\n+    return String(left.id ?? \\\"\\\").localeCompare(String(right.id ?? \\\"\\\"));\\n+  });\\n+  const decoded = input.cursor\\n+    ? decodeAdminCursor\\u003c{ offset?: unknown }\\u003e(input.cursor, context.scope)\\n+    : { offset: 0 };\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T03:11:11Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3834931032\",\"id\":3834931032,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":79,\"original_commit_id\":\"8d16f12d9a673cbed04f6c20cc9a06b0e770389e\",\"original_line\":71,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T03:11:12Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 8ad9b66 by capping the aligned step index before calculating the endpoint.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32551236919/job/96978227728) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T04:24:08Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835074704\",\"id\":3835074704,\"in_reply_to_id\":3834909065,\"line\":53,\"original_commit_id\":\"8d16f12d9a673cbed04f6c20cc9a06b0e770389e\",\"original_line\":40,\"path\":\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/range.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T04:24:08Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"These newly applied filters and sorts operate on arbitrary keys, but the manifest advertises `status`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, and `name` for catalog records that do not contain those fields. A console-generated `status` filter therefore drops every valid product, plan, or price, while advertised sorts silently collapse to the `id` fallback.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# BillFn list controls do not match their manifest\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts:67-78` — evaluates every requested field against the returned record without reconciling the capability contract.\\n- `billfn/admin/src/index.ts:56-92` — advertises product, plan, and price fields absent from their domain records.\\n- `billfn/admin/src/__tests__/admin.test.ts:148-156` — tests `productKey` and `id`, not the controls exposed by the manifest.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Every advertised filter and sort field must exist with the documented semantics on its resource records.\\n- Cover manifest-generated filtering and sorting for the domain-backed catalog resources.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T04:26:08Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835078214\",\"id\":3835078214,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":82,\"original_commit_id\":\"8ad9b668d13ae8354920ab8d6e4ef6f1b01eeaec\",\"original_line\":68,\"path\":\"billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T04:26:09Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=d37f08b0-fdf9-47e7-a2ba-9175b691b67a --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=e132b4ff-cab0-498f-ac59-f8230337c676 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When the manifest advertises catalog fields absent from the records, this generic filter drops every record for a non-`undefined` value and the sorter falls back to `id`. Align the manifest with the record shape or map those fields before applying the controls.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 68:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen the manifest advertises catalog fields absent from the records, this generic filter drops every record for a non-`undefined` value and the sorter falls back to `id`. Align the manifest with the record shape or map those fields before applying the controls.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -51,8 +54,35 @@ function asJson(value: object): JsonRecord {\\n+    records = records.filter((value) =\\u003e JSON.stringify(value).toLowerCase().includes(query));\\n+  }\\n+  if (input.filter) {\\n+    records = records.filter((value) =\\u003e Object.entries(input.filter!).every(([key, expected]) =\\u003e Object.is(value[key], expected)));\\n+  }\\n+  const sorts = input.sort ?? [];\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T04:32:38Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835088601\",\"id\":3835088601,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":82,\"original_commit_id\":\"8ad9b668d13ae8354920ab8d6e4ef6f1b01eeaec\",\"original_line\":68,\"path\":\"billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T04:32:38Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in e1f368a.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32555839931/job/96989690073) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T06:06:30Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835345164\",\"id\":3835345164,\"in_reply_to_id\":3835078214,\"line\":82,\"original_commit_id\":\"8ad9b668d13ae8354920ab8d6e4ef6f1b01eeaec\",\"original_line\":68,\"path\":\"billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T06:06:30Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Offset paging is now delegated to storage, but the query orders only by non-unique `createdAt`. Jobs created in the same timestamp can change relative order between page requests, so operators can skip or repeat jobs.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Sync-job pages lack a total order\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `plugfn/core/src/storage/adapters/database.ts:665-667` — applies offset under a `createdAt`-only order.\\n- `plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts:279-286` — builds cursors from that offset.\\n- `plugfn/admin/src/__tests__/admin.test.ts:162-181` — uses unique timestamps and does not exercise tied rows.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Use a deterministic total ordering shared by the storage query and cursor semantics.\\n- Cover pagination across jobs with identical `createdAt` values.\\n\\n## Suggested approach\\n- Add a unique secondary order key such as `id`, or use a keyset cursor over the complete ordering tuple.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T06:09:00Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835350203\",\"id\":3835350203,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":667,\"original_commit_id\":\"e1f368ac354ce6fec024eca61b2c723c9f4d04ab\",\"original_line\":667,\"path\":\"plugfn/core/src/storage/adapters/database.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T06:09:01Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=df717917-3f8e-4754-9c91-29f62a494553 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=c3096435-6aa1-4235-8388-39d72d0f9ba1 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP3: The test named \\\"filters sync-job lists by tenant as well as owner\\\" never exercises the owner filter: both created jobs belong to userId \\\"user_1\\\" and differ only in tenantId, and the setup identity maps to user_1. The test only proves tenant filtering, so the \\\"as well as owner\\\" claim overstates coverage and would not catch a regression that drops the ownerId filter from listSyncJobs. Add a job owned by a different userId/ownerId and assert it is excluded, or rename the test to reflect that only tenant filtering is covered.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At plugfn/admin/src/__tests__/admin.test.ts, line 184:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThe test named \\\"filters sync-job lists by tenant as well as owner\\\" never exercises the owner filter: both created jobs belong to userId \\\"user_1\\\" and differ only in tenantId, and the setup identity maps to user_1. The test only proves tenant filtering, so the \\\"as well as owner\\\" claim overstates coverage and would not catch a regression that drops the ownerId filter from listSyncJobs. Add a job owned by a different userId/ownerId and assert it is excluded, or rename the test to reflect that only tenant filtering is covered.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -168,6 +174,26 @@ describe(\\\"@plugfn/admin\\\", () =\\u003e {\\n+    expect(listJobs).toHaveBeenLastCalledWith(expect.any(Object), 101, forgedOffset);\\n+  });\\n+\\n+  it(\\\"filters sync-job lists by tenant as well as owner\\\", async () =\\u003e {\\n+    const { adapter, runtime } = setup();\\n+    const owned = await runtime.runtime.sync.createJob({\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`9307965`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/93079657b6d79970339f92d9a8f47a085a7364c7)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T06:09:40Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835351194\",\"id\":3835351194,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":281,\"original_commit_id\":\"e1f368ac354ce6fec024eca61b2c723c9f4d04ab\",\"original_line\":184,\"path\":\"plugfn/admin/src/__tests__/admin.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T06:51:42Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 9307965 by adding `id` as the deterministic secondary sort key and covering the storage query.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32557933930/job/96994981904) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T06:53:14Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835442052\",\"id\":3835442052,\"in_reply_to_id\":3835350203,\"line\":667,\"original_commit_id\":\"e1f368ac354ce6fec024eca61b2c723c9f4d04ab\",\"original_line\":667,\"path\":\"plugfn/core/src/storage/adapters/database.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T06:53:14Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"`HEAD` is normalized for registry matching here, but `operationInput()` still branches on the original method and treats `HEAD` as body-bearing. A valid GET route with required query input, such as DataFn records, loses its query parameters and returns a validation error instead of GET-equivalent status and headers.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# HEAD route normalization does not reach input extraction\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1197-1217` — matches the GET entry but passes the original HEAD request into input extraction.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:489-507` — parses query parameters only for GET and DELETE.\\n- `datafn/admin/src/index.ts:473-486` — the records GET route requires a query-supplied `filter` object.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Resource HEAD requests must parse the same path and query input as their corresponding GET request before suppressing the response body.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T06:54:58Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835446486\",\"id\":3835446486,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":1297,\"original_commit_id\":\"93079657b6d79970339f92d9a8f47a085a7364c7\",\"original_line\":1197,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T06:54:59Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=cecd96d5-fea9-47e6-9ef9-343acdb10224 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=293bf4ea-051a-4cb6-a17e-41f23ab3583f --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: HEAD requests are now routed to GET read operations (via routeMethod), but operationInput only treats request.method === 'GET' (or 'DELETE') as a query-parameter request. For a HEAD request it falls into the else branch and reads the empty body, so all query parameters are dropped and a HEAD to an operation that requires query params, or that should filter by them, dispatches with an empty input (returning 400 instead of 200, or executing unfiltered). Normalize HEAD in operationInput (e.g. treat 'HEAD' like 'GET') so HEAD mirrors GET.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts, line 1197:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eHEAD requests are now routed to GET read operations (via routeMethod), but operationInput only treats request.method === 'GET' (or 'DELETE') as a query-parameter request. For a HEAD request it falls into the else branch and reads the empty body, so all query parameters are dropped and a HEAD to an operation that requires query params, or that should filter by them, dispatches with an empty input (returning 400 instead of 200, or executing unfiltered). Normalize HEAD in operationInput (e.g. treat 'HEAD' like 'GET') so HEAD mirrors GET.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -1194,9 +1194,10 @@ export class SuperConsole {\\n       ? `${this.registry.apiBasePath}/modules/${encodeURIComponent(moduleId)}/resources/${rest.join('/')}`\\n       : undefined;\\n-    let entry = this.registry.matchRoute(request.method, matchedPath);\\n+    const routeMethod = request.method === 'HEAD' ? 'GET' : request.method;\\n+    let entry = this.registry.matchRoute(routeMethod, matchedPath);\\n     if (!entry \\u0026\\u0026 resourceAliasPath) {\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`21fbc39`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/21fbc394a2a628e7fb5933c0a418b6f0766154e4)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:07:58Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835481670\",\"id\":3835481670,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":1297,\"original_commit_id\":\"e3800bea453a3e7e5f3db105e18501b25cc850db\",\"original_line\":1197,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:34:09Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=0dffecbd-d021-4c49-96ec-1970b3193c7c --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=810e9353-3c10-4590-b40c-3b59af9b88bb --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When `Intl.Segmenter` is unavailable, this guard routes emoji and flag strings into a code-point fallback that still matches partial grapheme clusters. Use a grapheme-aware fallback, or conservatively reject these special-character matches when no segmenter exists.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts, line 91:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen `Intl.Segmenter` is unavailable, this guard routes emoji and flag strings into a code-point fallback that still matches partial grapheme clusters. Use a grapheme-aware fallback, or conservatively reject these special-character matches when no segmenter exists.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -86,7 +88,8 @@ export function createLocaleMatcher(locale = 'en'): LocaleMatcher {\\n     startsWith(value: string, query: string) {\\n       if (query.length === 0) return true;\\n-      if (normalize(value).startsWith(normalize(query))) return true;\\n+      if (!requiresGraphemeSegmentation(value) \\u0026\\u0026 !requiresGraphemeSegmentation(query)\\n+        \\u0026\\u0026 normalize(value).startsWith(normalize(query))) return true;\\n       const querySegments = segments(query);\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`616f549`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:36:08Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835526434\",\"id\":3835526434,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":111,\"original_commit_id\":\"21fbc394a2a628e7fb5933c0a418b6f0766154e4\",\"original_line\":91,\"path\":\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:46:44Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Supply a resource selector before exposing Records**\\n\\nWhen an operator opens the DataFn Records card in Super Console, the generated list request contains no `filter`, because this resource declares neither presentation filters nor a parent binding. Requiring `filter` here therefore makes the default Records route fail validation on every visit, leaving record browsing unusable unless the operator manually constructs a JSON query parameter; add a control/binding for `filter.resource` or stop advertising this as a standalone list.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:39:29Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835531565\",\"id\":3835531565,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":502,\"original_commit_id\":\"21fbc394a2a628e7fb5933c0a418b6f0766154e4\",\"original_line\":485,\"path\":\"datafn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:39:29Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Fixed by parsing HEAD inputs as query-bearing requests and adding resource HEAD coverage with required query input.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32559894115/job/96999772492) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:41:33Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835534741\",\"id\":3835534741,\"in_reply_to_id\":3835446486,\"line\":1297,\"original_commit_id\":\"93079657b6d79970339f92d9a8f47a085a7364c7\",\"original_line\":1197,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:41:33Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Fixed by tracking `src/app.d.ts` with the intended `App.Error` augmentation.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32559894115/job/96999772492) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:41:39Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835534884\",\"id\":3835534884,\"in_reply_to_id\":3831799628,\"line\":5,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":5,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/routes/[...missing]/+page.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:41:39Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Reject duplicate resource-template URI patterns**\\n\\nWhen two templates have different names but the same `uriTemplate`, this name-only duplicate check accepts both and advertises both from `resources/templates/list`. However, `matchResource` resolves by iterating the templates and returns the first URI match, so the later template's `read`, subscription, and completion behavior is unreachable. Reject duplicate `uriTemplate` values at registration time.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:57:05Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835561789\",\"id\":3835561789,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":196,\"original_commit_id\":\"e1062e1bc94e447305c649e89abb4588563dc475\",\"original_line\":183,\"path\":\"mcpfn/core/src/registry.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:57:05Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Encode cursor payloads as UTF-8**\\n\\nWhen any active scope identifier contains a non-Latin-1 character and a HostFn list has another page, `btoa(JSON.stringify(...))` throws `InvalidCharacterError` while constructing `nextCursor`, causing an otherwise successful list request to fail. Admin scope validation permits arbitrary nonblank Unicode strings, so encode the JSON as UTF-8 bytes before base64 encoding and reverse that transformation when decoding.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:57:05Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835561790\",\"id\":3835561790,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":738,\"original_commit_id\":\"e1062e1bc94e447305c649e89abb4588563dc475\",\"original_line\":736,\"path\":\"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T07:57:05Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=fa3f2f92-2cc0-4420-8be4-b0bbfc0e6b7e --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=16223a79-973e-46d4-85b7-f587ce11f5e4 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP1: When the Records page opens without a `resource` query parameter, the generic console sends no `filter.resource`, and `listRecords` rejects the request before rendering the filter. Make this list operation accept a default resource or provide required resource context before exposing it as a standalone presentation.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At datafn/admin/src/index.ts, line 139:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen the Records page opens without a `resource` query parameter, the generic console sends no `filter.resource`, and `listRecords` rejects the request before rendering the filter. Make this list operation accept a default resource or provide required resource context before exposing it as a standalone presentation.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -130,9 +132,19 @@ export const dataFnAdminResources = [\\n     sortableFields: [\\\"createdAt\\\", \\\"updatedAt\\\", \\\"name\\\"],\\n     sensitiveFields: [],\\n+    presentation: {\\n+      listOperationId: \\\"datafn.records.list\\\",\\n+      query: {\\n+        filters: [{\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`0daaba2`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T08:48:45Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835650689\",\"id\":3835650689,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":140,\"original_commit_id\":\"616f549ea9b97cefe5af650bace4b343d1d62452\",\"original_line\":139,\"path\":\"datafn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:10:01Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Make bot deletion and channel connection atomic**\\n\\nWhen `connectChannel` and `deleteBot` run concurrently, the connect path can observe the bot here, then the delete path can observe no channels and delete it, after which the connect path persists a channel for the now-missing bot. Because the store contract exposes only these separate reads and writes, even the supplied memory implementation permits an orphaned active external binding; enforce the bot-exists/channel-empty invariant atomically in the persistence layer.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:14:07Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835691127\",\"id\":3835691127,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":241,\"original_commit_id\":\"0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5\",\"original_line\":218,\"path\":\"botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:14:07Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"`ready` is snapshotted before callbacks run, so an earlier interval callback can `clearInterval()` a later ready interval, but this loop still invokes the canceled callback. I reproduced two same-deadline intervals where the first clears the second and `flush()` emits both; re-check interval liveness before invoking each entry and cover cancellation ordering so parity traces do not observe callbacks production would suppress.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:26:12Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835710808\",\"id\":3835710808,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":85,\"original_commit_id\":\"0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5\",\"original_line\":80,\"path\":\"uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:26:13Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=44d0df05-0c14-4598-be82-2f7f6eb7f22a --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=c399a9ed-1c7a-49dd-b678-501e2107db35 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: When a user continues pagination with a cursor issued by the previous HostFn version, this check rejects it because the old position contains only `offset`. Version the cursor format and provide a compatibility path for in-flight cursors so rolling deployments do not strand paginated admin pages.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/admin/src/index.ts, line 709:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a user continues pagination with a cursor issued by the previous HostFn version, this check rejects it because the old position contains only `offset`. Version the cursor format and provide a compatibility path for in-flight cursors so rolling deployments do not strand paginated admin pages.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -698,13 +698,15 @@ function pageResult(\\n-      const decoded = decodeAdminCursor\\u003c{ offset?: unknown }\\u003e(input.cursor, cursorScope);\\n+      const decoded = decodeAdminCursor\\u003c{ identity?: unknown; offset?: unknown }\\u003e(input.cursor, cursorScope);\\n       if (\\n+        decoded.identity !== identity ||\\n         typeof decoded.offset !== \\\"number\\\" ||\\n         !Number.isSafeInteger(decoded.offset) ||\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:31:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835719292\",\"id\":3835719292,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":709,\"original_commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"original_line\":709,\"path\":\"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:31:22Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=1906f030-f94c-4b43-a53d-60632aa527a3 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=c399a9ed-1c7a-49dd-b678-501e2107db35 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: Optional trace fields are silently accepted with wrong types because the new validators omit them. Add conditional validators for every optional field so `validateSemanticTrace` fails closed instead of comparing coerced values.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts, line 313:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eOptional trace fields are silently accepted with wrong types because the new validators omit them. Add conditional validators for every optional field so `validateSemanticTrace` fails closed instead of comparing coerced values.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -238,11 +281,103 @@ export function validateSemanticTrace(trace: unknown): readonly SemanticTraceIss\\n+      if (record) nested?.(record, path);\\n+    });\\n+  };\\n+  validateChannel('steps', {\\n+    sequence: traceNumber,\\n+    kind: (value) =\\u003e ['event', 'action', 'update', 'lifecycle'].includes(String(value)),\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`a422e0f`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:31:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835719296\",\"id\":3835719296,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":331,\"original_commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"original_line\":313,\"path\":\"uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:48:38Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=3e61d8ad-a875-4aa4-8b46-d150e66d0cc5 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=c399a9ed-1c7a-49dd-b678-501e2107db35 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: Reusing an acyclic semantic-JSON object in two sibling positions incorrectly produces a schema error. Track only the active recursion path and remove objects after each branch, while keeping true cycles rejected.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts, line 242:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eReusing an acyclic semantic-JSON object in two sibling positions incorrectly produces a schema error. Track only the active recursion path and remove objects after each branch, while keeping true cycles rejected.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -226,6 +226,49 @@ function addIssue(\\n+  if (value === null || typeof value === 'string' || typeof value === 'boolean') return true;\\n+  if (typeof value === 'number') return Number.isFinite(value);\\n+  if (!value || typeof value !== 'object' || seen.has(value)) return false;\\n+  seen.add(value);\\n+  if (Array.isArray(value)) return value.every((entry) =\\u003e isSemanticJsonValue(entry, seen));\\n+  return isPlainRecord(value) \\u0026\\u0026 Object.values(value).every((entry) =\\u003e isSemanticJsonValue(entry, seen));\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`a422e0f`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:31:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835719297\",\"id\":3835719297,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":250,\"original_commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"original_line\":242,\"path\":\"uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:48:37Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 239ba00 by re-checking timer liveness before invocation and covering same-deadline cancellation.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32565032165/job/97012331150) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:32:28Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835720861\",\"id\":3835720861,\"in_reply_to_id\":3835710808,\"line\":85,\"original_commit_id\":\"0daaba2290b1745967ebbd250707fdf57b1405b5\",\"original_line\":80,\"path\":\"uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:32:28Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"These validators cover required members only, so malformed optional evidence such as a function in `steps[].arguments` or `parts[].parts[].tabIndex` passes validation and is then converted to `null` by `toSemanticJson()`. That lets a supposedly lossless trace be accepted after silently dropping evidence; validate every declared optional field when present and add regressions.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Optional semantic evidence bypasses validation\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts:313-341` — nested validators omit the optional fields declared by `SemanticTraceStep`, `SemanticTraceTransaction`, and `SemanticTracePart`.\\n- `uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts:201-217` — normalization rewrites invalid functions, symbols, `undefined`, bigints, Dates, and non-plain objects instead of preserving them.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Reject malformed values for every declared optional semantic-trace field when that field is present.\\n- Cover optional step, transaction, and part evidence that would otherwise be normalized lossily.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:34:26Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835723789\",\"id\":3835723789,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":331,\"original_commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"original_line\":313,\"path\":\"uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:34:27Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Escape resource names in composite SearchFn targets**\\n\\nWhen a configured SearchFn resource name contains `:`, which the adapter contracts permit, a target such as `orders:v2:string:doc-1` is always split here as resource `orders`; single-document indexing and removal therefore report the valid `orders:v2` index as missing even though batch indexing and clearing can use it. The new typed ID suffix only escapes the document suffix, so the resource component also needs an unambiguous encoding or resource names must be validated as delimiter-free.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:35:32Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835725432\",\"id\":3835725432,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":111,\"original_commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"original_line\":100,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T09:35:32Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in a422e0f by validating every declared optional step, transaction, and part field.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32568555254/job/97020640348) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:51:31Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835842162\",\"id\":3835842162,\"in_reply_to_id\":3835723789,\"line\":331,\"original_commit_id\":\"239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba\",\"original_line\":313,\"path\":\"uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:51:31Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Deleting the object from this validator's set now correctly accepts shared acyclic values, but `toSemanticJson()` keeps completed objects in its own `seen` set and rewrites the second reference as `\\\"[circular]\\\"`. This makes the new test pass while `normalizeSemanticTrace()` still corrupts accepted trace state.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Shared acyclic trace values normalize as cycles\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts:201-217` — `toSemanticJson()` never removes an object after finishing its subtree.\\n- `uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts:238-247` — validation now intentionally accepts reused acyclic values.\\n- `uifn/adapter-kit/src/__tests__/conformance.test.ts:182-193` — the new regression asserts validation only and does not exercise normalization.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Reused acyclic JSON values must remain intact through `normalizeSemanticTrace()` while true cycles remain rejected.\\n- Extend the regression to assert the normalized state, not only an empty validator issue list.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:53:17Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835845050\",\"id\":3835845050,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":254,\"original_commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"original_line\":246,\"path\":\"uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:53:17Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=7cf387f1-d0e8-4020-bd99-35da513e2481 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=851c703b-f91e-40a3-9120-49bce4958eb2 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":6} --\\u003e\\nP2: This removal leaves the single-encoded-slash-in-literal-segment case untested. The parser now preserves a depth-0 single-encoded slash as the raw segment, so `/modules/examplefn/records%2fother` returns 404 rather than the 400 this removed case asserted; the new test only covers `%2F` inside a route parameter. Keep the literal-position case covered with an explicit 404 assertion so a future refactor that decodes segments before route matching cannot silently reintroduce the slash/path ambiguity this suite exists to fence.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts, line 359:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThis removal leaves the single-encoded-slash-in-literal-segment case untested. The parser now preserves a depth-0 single-encoded slash as the raw segment, so `/modules/examplefn/records%2fother` returns 404 rather than the 400 this removed case asserted; the new test only covers `%2F` inside a route parameter. Keep the literal-position case covered with an explicit 404 assertion so a future refactor that decodes segments before route matching cannot silently reintroduce the slash/path ambiguity this suite exists to fence.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -356,7 +356,6 @@ describe('Super Console server composition', () =\\u003e {\\n     '/api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn//records',\\n     '/api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/%252e%252e/records',\\n-    '/api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/records%2fother',\\n     '/api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/records%252fother',\\n     '/api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/records%5cother',\\n     '/api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/records%255cother',\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`593b81f`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:54:51Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835847367\",\"id\":3835847367,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":1,\"original_commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"original_line\":1,\"path\":\"superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:05:43Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=3d1d067b-69bd-4446-8056-3fbbbce5be6f --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=851c703b-f91e-40a3-9120-49bce4958eb2 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP3: The colon-encoded remove-document has no assertion on its effect, unlike every other mutation in this test. If removal silently missed the decoded resource, the test would still pass. Add a search assertion for resource \\\"orders:v2\\\" expecting [] after the remove.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At searchfn/admin/src/__tests__/admin.test.ts, line 185:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThe colon-encoded remove-document has no assertion on its effect, unlike every other mutation in this test. If removal silently missed the decoded resource, the test would still pass. Add a search assertion for resource \\\"orders:v2\\\" expecting [] after the remove.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -171,6 +171,20 @@ describe(\\\"@searchfn/admin\\\", () =\\u003e {\\n+    }, context);\\n+    await expect(adapters.get(\\\"environment_1\\\")!.search({ resource: \\\"orders:v2\\\", query: \\\"Versioned\\\" }))\\n+      .resolves.toEqual([\\\"doc-1\\\"]);\\n+    await colonAdapter.execute(\\\"searchfn.documents.remove-document\\\", {\\n+      id: \\\"orders%3Av2:string:doc-1\\\",\\n+    }, context);\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`593b81f`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T10:54:51Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835847378\",\"id\":3835847378,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":204,\"original_commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"original_line\":185,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/__tests__/admin.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:05:45Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Synchronize the Textarea value binding on input**\\n\\nWhen a consumer uses the advertised `bind:value` API and types into this textarea, the bound variable is never updated: `value` is declared bindable and forwarded to `PrimitiveRoot`, but unlike the generated Input root, no `input` handler assigns the DOM value back to it. The parent therefore retains the initial value, and a later reactive update can overwrite what the user typed; install an input handler that updates `value` while preserving the consumer's handler.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871106\",\"id\":3835871106,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":10,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":10,\"path\":\"uifn/svelte/lib/generated/textarea/Root.svelte\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Classify malformed OpenAPI documents as invalid input**\\n\\nWhen `document` contains malformed YAML, lacks an OpenAPI version, or declares an unsupported version, `parseOpenAPI` throws a plain `Error` here. `AdminDispatcher` normalizes plain errors to `internal`, so expected client validation failures from both registration and the analogous comparison path become HTTP 500 responses instead of actionable `invalid_argument` responses; catch parse failures and translate them to an admin input error.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871110\",\"id\":3835871110,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":189,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":189,\"path\":\"apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Bind ApiFn cursors to scope and collection**\\n\\nWhen a cursor from specs, another project, or another installation is supplied to the environments list (or vice versa), this accepts it as a raw offset and silently skips that many records in the unrelated collection. Since the cursor carries neither scope nor operation identity, ordinary scope changes while retaining the URL cursor can produce empty or incomplete pages; encode and validate the active scope and collection with the offset.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871113\",\"id\":3835871113,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":154,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":154,\"path\":\"apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Bind BotFn cursors to the channel filter and scope**\\n\\nWhen a channel cursor is reused after changing `botId`, or a bots/channel cursor is reused in another collection or project, this raw numeric offset remains valid and skips records from the new result set. This makes filtered pagination return incomplete or terminal-looking pages even when matching records exist; include the operation, scope, and `botId` query identity in the cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871115\",\"id\":3835871115,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":167,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":167,\"path\":\"botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=450e93a2-581c-40f6-a6a3-6bef44f4564c --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=5a311de1-61b7-4d68-8481-4dcf664e4fbd --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: During a rolling deployment, a page cursor issued by the previous server contains only `offset`, so this check rejects the next-page request. Version the cursor schema and retain a compatibility path while old cursors drain, or explicitly handle restart semantics instead of invalidating `version: 1` tokens silently.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 85:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eDuring a rolling deployment, a page cursor issued by the previous server contains only `offset`, so this check rejects the next-page request. Version the cursor schema and retain a compatibility path while old cursors drain, or explicitly handle restart semantics instead of invalidating `version: 1` tokens silently.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -68,12 +70,21 @@ function list(\\n   if (!decoded || typeof decoded !== \\\"object\\\" || Array.isArray(decoded)) {\\n     throw new AdminError(\\\"invalid_argument\\\", \\\"The SearchFn cursor is invalid.\\\");\\n   }\\n+  if (decoded.identity !== identity) {\\n+    throw new AdminError(\\\"invalid_argument\\\", \\\"The SearchFn cursor does not belong to this index-list query.\\\");\\n+  }\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871253\",\"id\":3835871253,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":85,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":85,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:40Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=fa774002-8729-4340-86d5-dfb6dadbd47a --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=5a311de1-61b7-4d68-8481-4dcf664e4fbd --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP3: `listAdapters` uses an operation identity that is not declared or registered. Use `searchfn.adapters-backends.list` so operation-bound cursor validation remains consistent.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 186:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003e`listAdapters` uses an operation identity that is not declared or registered. Use `searchfn.adapters-backends.list` so operation-bound cursor validation remains consistent.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -175,7 +183,7 @@ export function createSearchFnDomainAdminService(\\n     async listAdapters(input, context) {\\n       const { adapterInfo } = await state(context);\\n-      return list([adapterInfo], input, context);\\n+      return list([adapterInfo], input, context, \\\"searchfn.adapters.list\\\");\\n     },\\n     async getAdapter(input, context) {\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n      return list([adapterInfo], input, context, \\\"searchfn.adapters-backends.list\\\");\\n```\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871255\",\"id\":3835871255,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":186,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":186,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:40Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=f7498236-c489-4984-96df-d2d54653cc76 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=5a311de1-61b7-4d68-8481-4dcf664e4fbd --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP3: 'does not route an encoded separator embedded in a literal segment' passes even if the server treated %2f as a real route separator: decoded or not, records%2fother matches no registered route, so the 404/OPERATION_NOT_ENABLED assertions cannot detect a routing regression. Use a path whose over-decoded form would hit a real route, e.g. /api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/resources%2frecords (would dispatch the records handler if %2f were split), and keep asserting 404 and handler not called.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts, line 382:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003e'does not route an encoded separator embedded in a literal segment' passes even if the server treated %2f as a real route separator: decoded or not, records%2fother matches no registered route, so the 404/OPERATION_NOT_ENABLED assertions cannot detect a routing regression. Use a path whose over-decoded form would hit a real route, e.g. /api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/resources%2frecords (would dispatch the records handler if %2f were split), and keep asserting 404 and handler not called.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -376,6 +377,14 @@ describe('Super Console server composition', () =\\u003e {\\n \\n+  it('does not route an encoded separator embedded in a literal segment', async () =\\u003e {\\n+    const { console, handler } = installation();\\n+    const result = await console.handle(request('/api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/records%2fother'));\\n+    expect(result.status).toBe(404);\\n+    expect(await result.json()).toMatchObject({ error: { code: 'OPERATION_NOT_ENABLED' } });\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    const result = await console.handle(request('/api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/resources%2frecords'));\\n```\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871257\",\"id\":3835871257,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":385,\"original_commit_id\":\"593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a\",\"original_line\":382,\"path\":\"superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:40Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 593b81f by removing completed objects from the recursion set and asserting normalized shared state.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32569323032/job/97022407951) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:48Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871423\",\"id\":3835871423,\"in_reply_to_id\":3835845050,\"line\":254,\"original_commit_id\":\"a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3\",\"original_line\":246,\"path\":\"uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:10:48Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=c9db29b1-0333-4e1b-82f8-88a651137fe5 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=565efb3e-1cfe-4884-a6da-1f223d760f97 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: When a record’s `updatedAt` changes between page requests, this offset cursor no longer identifies the same page boundary, so records can be skipped or repeated. Sort by an immutable key such as `id`, or switch this cursor to a keyset containing the sort key.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/admin/src/index.ts, line 727:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a record’s `updatedAt` changes between page requests, this offset cursor no longer identifies the same page boundary, so records can be skipped or repeated. Sort by an immutable key such as `id`, or switch this cursor to a keyset containing the sort key.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -721,12 +721,19 @@ function pageResult(\\n+  const orderedItems = [...items].sort((left, right) =\\u003e {\\n+    const leftItem = left as { updatedAt?: unknown; createdAt?: unknown; id?: unknown };\\n+    const rightItem = right as { updatedAt?: unknown; createdAt?: unknown; id?: unknown };\\n+    const timestamp = String(leftItem.updatedAt ?? leftItem.createdAt ?? \\\"\\\")\\n+      .localeCompare(String(rightItem.updatedAt ?? rightItem.createdAt ?? \\\"\\\"));\\n+    return timestamp || String(leftItem.id ?? \\\"\\\").localeCompare(String(rightItem.id ?? \\\"\\\"));\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    return String(leftItem.id ?? \\\"\\\").localeCompare(String(rightItem.id ?? \\\"\\\"));\\n```\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:40:41Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835919209\",\"id\":3835919209,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":729,\"original_commit_id\":\"b2718e4ed53dd5ee5e04dac45c917bba478d3a1c\",\"original_line\":729,\"path\":\"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:40:42Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=545b26c9-3780-4967-8f60-c4ad37a8b621 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=565efb3e-1cfe-4884-a6da-1f223d760f97 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":6} --\\u003e\\nP2: This new assertion codifies a false-positive duplicate: `docs://users/{;name}` is rejected as a duplicate of `docs://users/{id}` only because `resourceTemplatePattern`'s operator set `[+#./?\\u0026]` omits `;`, so `{;name}` normalizes to `{v0}` like `{id}`. `;` is a valid RFC 6570 operator; sections prefixed this way match `docs://users/;name=...`, distinct from plain-segment matches. Valid template forms using `{;...}` are now rejected with a misleading \\\"Duplicate ... URI\\\" error. Add `;` to the operator set in registry.ts so `{;v0}` is kept and genuinely overlapping matrix templates still collide; if `;` templates are instead intentionally unsupported, reject them with an explicit message and code rather than a duplicate error.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/core/tests/protocol.test.ts, line 64:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThis new assertion codifies a false-positive duplicate: `docs://users/{;name}` is rejected as a duplicate of `docs://users/{id}` only because `resourceTemplatePattern`'s operator set `[+#./?\\u0026]` omits `;`, so `{;name}` normalizes to `{v0}` like `{id}`. `;` is a valid RFC 6570 operator; sections prefixed this way match `docs://users/;name=...`, distinct from plain-segment matches. Valid template forms using `{;...}` are now rejected with a misleading \\\"Duplicate ... URI\\\" error. Add `;` to the operator set in registry.ts so `{;v0}` is kept and genuinely overlapping matrix templates still collide; if `;` templates are instead intentionally unsupported, reject them with an explicit message and code rather than a duplicate error.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ describe(\\\"McpFn protocol primitives\\\", () =\\u003e {\\n       name: \\\"matrix-account\\\",\\n       read: async (uri) =\\u003e ({ contents: [{ uri: uri.toString(), text: \\\"matrix\\\" }] }),\\n-    })).not.toThrow();\\n+    })).toThrow(\\\"Duplicate MCP resource template URI: docs://users/{;name}\\\");\\n   });\\n \\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:40:42Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835919214\",\"id\":3835919214,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":64,\"original_commit_id\":\"b2718e4ed53dd5ee5e04dac45c917bba478d3a1c\",\"original_line\":64,\"path\":\"mcpfn/core/tests/protocol.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:40:42Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=daa00630-654a-4c6b-9dfd-82a4af6ed2c9 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=565efb3e-1cfe-4884-a6da-1f223d760f97 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP3: scoped() now deep-clones every element before listDeployments/listDomains/listVariables apply their targetId filter, so entries that get discarded are cloned wastefully (and listVariables transiently clones the stored secret value before stripping it). Filter by targetId first, then clone only what is returned.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts, line 122:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003escoped() now deep-clones every element before listDeployments/listDomains/listVariables apply their targetId filter, so entries that get discarded are cloned wastefully (and listVariables transiently clones the stored secret value before stripping it). Filter by targetId first, then clone only what is returned.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -117,7 +117,9 @@ function scoped\\u003cT extends { scope: HostFnScope }\\u003e(\\n-  return [...values].filter((value) =\\u003e scopeKey(value.scope) === key);\\n+  return [...values]\\n+    .filter((value) =\\u003e scopeKey(value.scope) === key)\\n+    .map((value) =\\u003e structuredClone(value));\\n }\\n \\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:40:42Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835919215\",\"id\":3835919215,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":137,\"original_commit_id\":\"b2718e4ed53dd5ee5e04dac45c917bba478d3a1c\",\"original_line\":122,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:40:42Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Preserve numeric types in composite record IDs**\\n\\nWhen a DataFn row has a numeric ID, `compositeRecordId` serializes it indistinguishably from a string ID and this parser always restores it as a string. Consequently, opening a listed numeric-ID record queries with `filters.id = \\\"42\\\"` rather than `42`, and mutation validation rejects a numeric `payload.id`; encode the ID type in the composite target and restore it when splitting.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835922082\",\"id\":3835922082,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":140,\"original_commit_id\":\"b2718e4ed53dd5ee5e04dac45c917bba478d3a1c\",\"original_line\":145,\"path\":\"datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Bind metadata cursors to their DataFn collection**\\n\\nWhen a scope has enough metadata for pagination, the cursor returned by resources, relations, indices, or capabilities contains only an offset and scope, so it can be reused in any of the other collections. The receiving operation accepts it and skips the same number of unrelated records, yielding incomplete or empty pages; include the metadata operation or collection identity in this cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835922087\",\"id\":3835922087,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":64,\"original_commit_id\":\"b2718e4ed53dd5ee5e04dac45c917bba478d3a1c\",\"original_line\":63,\"path\":\"datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Resolve queued deployments when scheduling fails**\\n\\nWhen `executor.deploy` rejects before accepting a deployment, the record has already been persisted as `queued`, and this path neither marks it failed nor removes it. The request returns an error while subsequent deployment lists continue reporting a job that will never run, so persist a terminal/unknown outcome or otherwise reconcile the record on executor failure.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835922091\",\"id\":3835922091,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":302,\"original_commit_id\":\"b2718e4ed53dd5ee5e04dac45c917bba478d3a1c\",\"original_line\":243,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Distinct accepted IDs can compare equal under `localeCompare`, for example composed `é` and decomposed `e\\\\u0301`. When timestamps tie and the backing store changes their input order between requests, offset slicing can duplicate one record and omit another, so this needs a locale-independent total tie-breaker.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# HostFn pagination lacks a total tie-breaker\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `hostfn/admin/src/index.ts:724-729` — the final comparison can return zero for distinct IDs accepted by the manifest.\\n- `hostfn/admin/src/__tests__/admin.test.ts:160-201` — the reordering regression covers only ASCII IDs whose comparisons are nonzero.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Define a strict, locale-independent total order for every accepted HostFn ID before applying an offset cursor.\\n- Cover distinct equal-collation IDs under a store that changes result order between page requests.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:49:44Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835946128\",\"id\":3835946128,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":729,\"original_commit_id\":\"b2718e4ed53dd5ee5e04dac45c917bba478d3a1c\",\"original_line\":729,\"path\":\"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T11:49:44Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Expose read-classified resource actions**\\n\\nWhen a resource has a non-list/get read operation, this filter removes it from the only detail-page action projection. In the inspected manifests this makes `filefn.files.download`, `filefn.artifacts.download`, and `apifn.specs.compare` unreachable from the generic Super Console UI even though their capabilities are enabled; distinguish read actions from canonical list/detail reads rather than dropping every read-classified operation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:01:56Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835986673\",\"id\":3835986673,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":395,\"original_commit_id\":\"c6aea5c7b1c3b023d51510b821e61b7a7f17b32f\",\"original_line\":395,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:01:56Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Reject malformed token leaves before recursing**\\n\\nWhen a runtime-loaded theme contains a partial token such as `{ $type: 'color' }` without `$value`, `isDesignToken` returns false and this recursively treats the token—and then its scalar `$type` string—as token groups until the stack overflows. Consequently `assertTokenShape` never emits the advertised `UIFnTokenError` for exactly the malformed input it is meant to validate; verify that non-token nodes are plain group objects before descending.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:01:56Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835986675\",\"id\":3835986675,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":161,\"original_commit_id\":\"c6aea5c7b1c3b023d51510b821e61b7a7f17b32f\",\"original_line\":161,\"path\":\"uifn/tokens/src/schema.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:01:56Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=29c934f3-2f72-4b36-83e3-245254b139cf --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=22be5463-3f8c-4e83-93ac-026ff63a485e --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: During SSR, standard native attributes not listed in the static regexes are dropped from the rendered root until browser hydration. Use a server-independent native-attribute set, or otherwise classify these attributes as DOM props without relying on `document`.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts, line 159:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eDuring SSR, standard native attributes not listed in the static regexes are dropped from the rendered root until browser hydration. Use a server-independent native-attribute set, or otherwise classify these attributes as DOM props without relying on `document`.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -128,7 +153,11 @@ export function splitSvelteRootProps(props: AnyRecord, inputNames: readonly stri\\n+    else if (ROOT_DOM_PROP.test(key) || ROOT_EVENT_PROP.test(key)) dom[key] = value;\\n+    else {\\n+      inputs[key] = value;\\n+      if (isUndeclaredNativeProp(key)) dom[key] = value;\\n+    }\\n   }\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`358c4d2`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/358c4d2bec007a1e6c8a738302df38e03a6281e4)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:05:27Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835996860\",\"id\":3835996860,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":146,\"original_commit_id\":\"c6aea5c7b1c3b023d51510b821e61b7a7f17b32f\",\"original_line\":159,\"path\":\"uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:19:41Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=e8a8b4ae-b204-4bf3-8aa9-8fda128c1e35 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=8add03eb-2e54-4224-a134-d62e7a9b9b83 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} --\\u003e\\nP3: This changes the public cursor shape, but `mcpfn/core/README.md` still documents `mcpfn:\\u003coffset\\u003e` cursors. Update the package documentation to describe the opaque, operation/collection-bound cursor and its expiry behavior.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/core/src/server.ts, line 124:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThis changes the public cursor shape, but `mcpfn/core/README.md` still documents `mcpfn:\\u003coffset\\u003e` cursors. Update the package documentation to describe the opaque, operation/collection-bound cursor and its expiry behavior.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -109,7 +120,9 @@ function page\\u003cT\\u003e(\\n     values: selected,\\n-    ...(nextOffset \\u003c values.length ? { nextCursor: `mcpfn:${nextOffset}` } : {}),\\n+    ...(nextOffset \\u003c values.length\\n+      ? { nextCursor: `mcpfn:${operation}:${identity}:${nextOffset}` }\\n+      : {}),\\n   };\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:22:44Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836023997\",\"id\":3836023997,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":125,\"original_commit_id\":\"358c4d2bec007a1e6c8a738302df38e03a6281e4\",\"original_line\":124,\"path\":\"mcpfn/core/src/server.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:22:44Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Reject credentials embedded in environment URLs**\\n\\nWhen `baseUrl` is an HTTP(S) URL such as `REDACTED`, this validation accepts it and persists `parsed.toString()`. Environment records are explicitly presented as non-secret endpoints and return `baseUrl` without redaction, so the embedded credential is exposed through list/get responses and the generic console; reject URLs with a nonempty `username` or `REDACTED` before storing them.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:34:49Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836043483\",\"id\":3836043483,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":261,\"original_commit_id\":\"9bd82d29b653cf7bea0c3222a1474288fd873494\",\"original_line\":261,\"path\":\"apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T12:34:49Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=edfa162d-8357-45ad-ae4b-25568f581590 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=61344dbc-0113-40de-bbe1-05190ca20cc9 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When FileFn uses proxy-backed storage instead of signed URLs, the new receipt helper rejects its `/proxy/files/...` descriptor as untrusted, so Super Console downloads fail. Route the proxy through a trusted admin download endpoint or add an explicit, function-owned allowlist for this proxy route.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts, line 283:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen FileFn uses proxy-backed storage instead of signed URLs, the new receipt helper rejects its `/proxy/files/...` descriptor as untrusted, so Super Console downloads fail. Route the proxy through a trusted admin download endpoint or add an explicit, function-owned allowlist for this proxy route.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -269,6 +269,51 @@ export function openSafeAdminDownload(\\n+  fetcher: typeof fetch = fetch\\n+): Promise\\u003cboolean\\u003e {\\n+  if (typeof window === 'undefined') return false;\\n+  const safeHref = safeAdminDownloadHref(receipt.url, {\\n+    origin: window.location.origin,\\n+    signedExternal: receipt.signedExternal ?? true,\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`e3e7054`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/e3e70545660f6090bf9fbf5e28d76d5f405c25ef)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:05:14Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836093861\",\"id\":3836093861,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":298,\"original_commit_id\":\"a3a6f63fef417435b4161f13dda766b63a08cd5a\",\"original_line\":283,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:22:35Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Expose document actions as collection actions**\\n\\nWhen SearchFn is operated through the generic Super Console, `documents` has no list or get operation (`domainReadResourceIds` excludes it), but `index` and `remove-document` are projected here as ID-bound resource actions. The module page only renders collection actions, while the non-listable documents resource has no reachable detail page, so both operations are unavailable in the UI; project these action-only operations as collection actions so their `id` inputs can be entered in the action form.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:27:17Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836131324\",\"id\":3836131324,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":594,\"original_commit_id\":\"e3e70545660f6090bf9fbf5e28d76d5f405c25ef\",\"original_line\":594,\"path\":\"searchfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:27:17Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Make share-link creation replay-safe after audit failures**\\n\\nWhen `shares.createShareLink` succeeds but the required terminal audit write fails, `AdminDispatcher` returns a dependency error after the live share and its one-time plaintext token have already been created. Because this operation explicitly disables idempotency, a retry creates another share instead of recovering the first result; the first link remains active while its token is lost, and it cannot be revoked through this admin API because revocation requires that original token. Preserve the result behind an idempotency key or otherwise reconcile/revoke the created share on post-execution failure.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:48:01Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836166999\",\"id\":3836166999,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":199,\"original_commit_id\":\"09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2\",\"original_line\":199,\"path\":\"filefn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:48:01Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=39a9603b-aab7-4d43-9006-4369b15941ef --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=9c17cfe9-eced-4720-9690-e7e1d35fc8fc --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: This replacement removes the UI coverage proving that header-free signed receipts still open successfully. Retain a positive header-free receipt case alongside the provider-header rejection, or the browser download flow can regress while these tests remain green.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/tests/ui/admin-api.test.ts, line 184:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThis replacement removes the UI coverage proving that header-free signed receipts still open successfully. Retain a positive header-free receipt case alongside the provider-header rejection, or the browser download flow can regress while these tests remain green.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -181,43 +181,11 @@ describe('administration API boundary', () =\\u003e {\\n-\\n-  it('fails closed when a required provider header was redacted', async () =\\u003e {\\n-    const fetcher = vi.fn\\u003ctypeof fetch\\u003e();\\n+  it('fails closed for every provider-header download receipt', async () =\\u003e {\\n     await expect(openSafeAdminDownloadReceipt({\\n       url: 'https://storage.example.test/signed-object',\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`b1157c7`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T13:52:46Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836175580\",\"id\":3836175580,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":184,\"original_commit_id\":\"09ff9316cb763313a0501724121358137704f6f2\",\"original_line\":184,\"path\":\"superconsole/tests/ui/admin-api.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:08:50Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=ae4eaeb5-91cc-4b8f-94ea-7038ebd9faab --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=de51d2b7-51be-4233-98de-40e1e764bc05 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: When a FileFn service returns `accepted: true` without `item.token`, this callback throws after the share was created and leaves the share active without durable cleanup. Require `item.token` for the create-share contract and provide a durable reconciliation path for responses that still omit it.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At filefn/admin/src/index.ts, line 367:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a FileFn service returns `accepted: true` without `item.token`, this callback throws after the share was created and leaves the share active without durable cleanup. Require `item.token` for the create-share contract and provide a durable reconciliation path for responses that still omit it.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -355,6 +355,19 @@ export function createFileFnAdminAdapter(service: FileFnAdminService): AdminCapa\\n+        const shareInput = input as CreateShareAdminInput;\\n+        const shareResult = result as AdminOperationResult\\u003cFileFnAdminOperationOutputMap[\\\"filefn.share-links.create-share\\\"]\\u003e;\\n+        const token = shareResult.data.item?.token;\\n+        if (!token) throw new Error(\\\"The created FileFn share token is unavailable for compensation.\\\");\\n+        await service.revokeShareLink({ fileId: shareInput.fileId, token }, context);\\n+      },\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:13:41Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836215914\",\"id\":3836215914,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":367,\"original_commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"original_line\":367,\"path\":\"filefn/admin/src/index.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:13:41Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Reject non-finite JSON numbers**\\n\\nWhen a direct dispatcher caller supplies, or an adapter returns, `NaN` or either infinity under a schema declaring `type: \\\"number\\\"`, `valueType` classifies it as a valid number. The dispatcher consequently accepts the value, while JSON serialization changes it to `null`, so clients receive data that no longer satisfies the declared output schema; non-finite numbers should fail validation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836216785\",\"id\":3836216785,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":97,\"original_commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"original_line\":59,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Require schema properties to be owned by the input**\\n\\nWhen an input has a custom prototype containing a required field, this `in` check accepts the inherited value even though the subsequent `Object.entries` traversal never validates it. This is reachable through the module HTTP transport because assigning a parsed `{\\\"__proto__\\\": {...}}` body changes the accumulator's prototype; the dispatcher then clones away that prototype and invokes the adapter with the required field missing instead of rejecting the request. Check required fields with `Object.hasOwn`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836216788\",\"id\":3836216788,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":266,\"original_commit_id\":\"b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943\",\"original_line\":192,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Validate token values before interpolating CSS**\\n\\nWhen a custom runtime theme contains CSS control syntax in a string-valued token, such as a dimension value of `1px;}body{display:none`, this interpolation lets the value escape its custom-property declaration and inject arbitrary rules into the generated stylesheet. `themeToCSS` accepts `DesignTokenTheme` directly without validation, and the token validator only checks that non-number values are strings, so validate each token's CSS grammar or reject control syntax before composing the stylesheet.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:40:01Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836266338\",\"id\":3836266338,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":96,\"original_commit_id\":\"966f3141aac7e6b7c3a676bf3955ef1028c79a8b\",\"original_line\":78,\"path\":\"uifn/theme/src/mount.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:40:01Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"This only rejects a non-finite value when the current schema declares a numeric type. Valid open schemas such as `{ type: \\\"object\\\", additionalProperties: true }` still accept nested `NaN`/`Infinity`, so the dispatcher accepts domain output that Super Console later silently serializes as `null`.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Open schemas still admit non-finite values\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `packages/admin/src/validator.ts:58,92-102` — special classification has no effect when `schema.type` is omitted.\\n- `packages/admin/src/validator.ts:199-222` — `additionalProperties: true` accepts unknown values without recursively checking JSON validity.\\n- `packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts:294-298` — treats such domain output as valid.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:58-68` — `JSON.stringify()` changes accepted non-finite values to `null`.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Reject non-finite numbers at every depth regardless of whether the surrounding valid schema is typed, open, or typeless.\\n- Cover open-object, typeless-property, and array-item cases so the test fails with the current implementation.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:42:58Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836271738\",\"id\":3836271738,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":95,\"original_commit_id\":\"966f3141aac7e6b7c3a676bf3955ef1028c79a8b\",\"original_line\":58,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T14:42:59Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Filter connection lists by exact tenant identity**\\n\\nWhen the identity mapper returns a tenantless identity (`tenantId` is undefined), this passes an owner with an undefined tenant to `connections.list`; PlugFn's `ConnectionStorage.listByOwner` omits the tenant predicate when that value is absent, so connections for the same user or organization in every tenant are returned and mapped without an `assertConnectionOwner` check. This leaks cross-tenant connection names, scopes, and status through the list operation even though the corresponding detail operation rejects those records; post-filter the results using the exact tenant/owner checks or make the storage query distinguish tenantless records.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:16:45Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836570650\",\"id\":3836570650,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":357,\"original_commit_id\":\"9cf9e6116cdc974d1e7b01fdc5a7ed24e54f4029\",\"original_line\":347,\"path\":\"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:16:45Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in 9cf9e61 with recursive open-schema validation and focused regression coverage.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32587012001/job/97064830292) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:18:08Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836573261\",\"id\":3836573261,\"in_reply_to_id\":3836271738,\"line\":95,\"original_commit_id\":\"966f3141aac7e6b7c3a676bf3955ef1028c79a8b\",\"original_line\":58,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:18:09Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"The earlier completion has already persisted a successful result and pending `succeeded` audit shape. If this replacement `complete()` fails before persisting, or a durable store rejects replacing a completed record, the catch below swallows it and a retry reports success after the compensator rolled back the domain state.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Compensation can leave the durable success record authoritative\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts:350-356` — persists the successful domain result and pending `succeeded` terminal event before audit delivery.\\n- `packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts:540-565` — attempts the compensated-failure replacement after rollback and suppresses any storage failure.\\n- `packages/admin/src/idempotency.ts:53-55,137-142` — the contract promises repeatability for the same result, while only the in-memory implementation explicitly permits replacing a completed result.\\n- `packages/admin/src/dispatcher.test.ts:315-379` — covers failed audit acknowledgement but not before-write or after-write failure of the compensation-state completion.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Make the compensated result and failed terminal-audit shape durably authoritative before any retry can observe the stale success record, including lost acknowledgements.\\n- Define the required atomic transition for distributed stores and cover both before-write and after-write completion failures.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:19:40Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836576354\",\"id\":3836576354,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":680,\"original_commit_id\":\"9cf9e6116cdc974d1e7b01fdc5a7ed24e54f4029\",\"original_line\":542,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:19:41Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=e4d0a90a-8a2e-48b8-9fa7-873371ab35cd --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=5275fc5a-473b-448f-902e-ead0ba012162 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When a required-audit idempotent mutation loses its terminal sink acknowledgement, replay redelivers the stable event ID without the original policy metadata. Persist the metadata in the pending audit marker before `writeAudit` so reconciliation reproduces the terminal event shape.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/idempotency.ts, line 25:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a required-audit idempotent mutation loses its terminal sink acknowledgement, replay redelivers the stable event ID without the original policy metadata. Persist the metadata in the pending audit marker before `writeAudit` so reconciliation reproduces the terminal event shape.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -19,6 +19,10 @@ export interface AdminIdempotencyRecord\\u003cT = unknown\\u003e {\\n+    /** Terminal event shape to redeliver when a sink acknowledgement is lost. */\\n+    outcome?: \\\"succeeded\\\" | \\\"failed\\\";\\n+    errorCode?: string;\\n+    metadata?: Readonly\\u003cRecord\\u003cstring, unknown\\u003e\\u003e;\\n     updatedAt: string;\\n   };\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:19:51Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836576637\",\"id\":3836576637,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":25,\"original_commit_id\":\"9cf9e6116cdc974d1e7b01fdc5a7ed24e54f4029\",\"original_line\":25,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/idempotency.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:19:51Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=d51c08ff-e32a-43dc-9121-02bb60c2fac6 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=5275fc5a-473b-448f-902e-ead0ba012162 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP2: When policy metadata contains secret-shaped or input-derived values, compensated failures persist it unredacted in the idempotency store even though the audit copy is sanitized. Redact the metadata before storing it, or persist only the fixed compensation marker.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts, line 554:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen policy metadata contains secret-shaped or input-derived values, compensated failures persist it unredacted in the idempotency store even though the audit copy is sanitized. Redact the metadata before storing it, or persist only the fixed compensation marker.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -533,12 +537,26 @@ export class AdminDispatcher {\\n+                      auditId: stableCompensationAuditId,\\n+                      outcome: \\\"failed\\\" as const,\\n+                      errorCode: \\\"dependency_unavailable\\\",\\n+                      ...(compensationAuditMetadata ? { metadata: compensationAuditMetadata } : {}),\\n+                      updatedAt: timestamp,\\n+                    },\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`fbb3868`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/fbb3868fb8eeb21421e1dc9f7a079535ab7a84a2)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-22T17:19:51Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836576638\",\"id\":3836576638,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":691,\"original_commit_id\":\"9cf9e6116cdc974d1e7b01fdc5a7ed24e54f4029\",\"original_line\":554,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T03:21:26Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in fbb3868 by fencing compensation before rollback and covering ambiguous transition acknowledgements.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32615132104/job/97134492380) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T03:28:58Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837616583\",\"id\":3837616583,\"in_reply_to_id\":3836576354,\"line\":680,\"original_commit_id\":\"9cf9e6116cdc974d1e7b01fdc5a7ed24e54f4029\",\"original_line\":542,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T03:28:58Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=741c8597-a9a6-4cc6-98a4-39141e680a53 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=547f7f2b-689d-4798-9bbc-7218b6ecb05a --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP1: When a replay arrives while the original request is still compensating, this pending marker can be claimed by a second reconciliation attempt. The original claim can then complete the record without resolving that reconciliation wait, so the replay hangs forever even though compensation completed; represent the initial compensation as the same acquired claim, or add an explicit in-progress state and settle/fence concurrent waiters.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/idempotency.ts, line 190:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen a replay arrives while the original request is still compensating, this pending marker can be claimed by a second reconciliation attempt. The original claim can then complete the record without resolving that reconciliation wait, so the replay hangs forever even though compensation completed; represent the initial compensation as the same acquired claim, or add an explicit in-progress state and settle/fence concurrent waiters.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -152,11 +179,19 @@ export class MemoryAdminIdempotencyStore implements AdminIdempotencyStore {\\n         throw new AdminError(\\\"conflict\\\", \\\"The idempotency completion fingerprint does not match its reservation.\\\");\\n       }\\n       existing.record = structuredClone(record) as AdminIdempotencyRecord;\\n+      if (existing.reconciliation?.token === claim.token) {\\n+        const reconciliation = existing.reconciliation;\\n+        existing.reconciliation = undefined;\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`db08968`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T05:06:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837749556\",\"id\":3837749556,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":191,\"original_commit_id\":\"73485e82e24ea8b3fb883a02c63044e033b54dec\",\"original_line\":190,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/idempotency.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:03:48Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=cd5bac7f-ecc4-4bdc-8192-6bc42654fed2 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=1e72b8f2-90ba-48d3-9476-e3e34a0fb189 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":7} --\\u003e\\nP3: This edit dropped the only regression coverage for the lost rollback-audit-acknowledgement branch: when `writeAudit` (outcome \\\"failed\\\") throws inside `reconcileCompensation`, the dispatcher keeps compensation=completed with audit pending and returns `reconciliationRequired:true` without an auditId until a later replay recovers it. Removing `failedAuditAttempts` and the `retry_audit` assertion leaves that documented path unexercised. Keep a variant that injects one \\\"failed\\\" outcome rejection on the retry and asserts the two-step recovery (`reconciliationRequired` → then `recoveredTerminalAudit`/`auditId`).\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/dispatcher.test.ts, line 361:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eThis edit dropped the only regression coverage for the lost rollback-audit-acknowledgement branch: when `writeAudit` (outcome \\\"failed\\\") throws inside `reconcileCompensation`, the dispatcher keeps compensation=completed with audit pending and returns `reconciliationRequired:true` without an auditId until a later replay recovers it. Removing `failedAuditAttempts` and the `retry_audit` assertion leaves that documented path unexercised. Keep a variant that injects one \\\"failed\\\" outcome rejection on the retry and asserts the two-step recovery (`reconciliationRequired` → then `recoveredTerminalAudit`/`auditId`).\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -36,6 +36,53 @@ describe(\\\"AdminDispatcher\\\", () =\\u003e {\\n     expect(different).not.toBe(first);\\n   });\\n \\n+  it(\\\"settles concurrent replay waiters when the original compensation claim completes\\\", async () =\\u003e {\\n+    const store = new MemoryAdminIdempotencyStore();\\n+    const identity = {\\n+      key: \\\"concurrent-compensation\\\",\\n+      actorId: \\\"user_1\\\",\\n+      scope: context().scope,\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`16a31f1`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:11:46Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837844412\",\"id\":3837844412,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":1,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":1,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:34:55Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=04df7e3e-5692-4051-8dcf-49c107346f7d --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=1e72b8f2-90ba-48d3-9476-e3e34a0fb189 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} --\\u003e\\nP3: In the new activation-failure test, `expect(active).toBe(false)` is vacuous: `active` starts false and nothing can set it true (`activate` throws before any assignment), and `verify` is never called. The title's claim \\\"leaves the staged token unusable\\\" is therefore not actually exercised. Initialize `let active = true;` so the assertion verifies `revoke` genuinely deactivated the token, or assert on `verify` returning false for the staged token.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts, line 780:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eIn the new activation-failure test, `expect(active).toBe(false)` is vacuous: `active` starts false and nothing can set it true (`activate` throws before any assignment), and `verify` is never called. The title's claim \\\"leaves the staged token unusable\\\" is therefore not actually exercised. Initialize `let active = true;` so the assertion verifies `revoke` genuinely deactivated the token, or assert on `verify` returning false for the staged token.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -770,10 +770,54 @@ describe('Super Console server composition', () =\\u003e {\\n+  it('records activation failure as denied and leaves the staged token unusable', async () =\\u003e {\\n+    const capability = manifest({ destructive: true });\\n+    const outcomes: Array\\u003c{ outcome: string; errorCode?: string }\\u003e = [];\\n+    let active = false;\\n+    const revoke = vi.fn(async () =\\u003e { active = false; });\\n+    const console = createSuperConsole({\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`16a31f1`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:11:46Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837844415\",\"id\":3837844415,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":786,\"original_commit_id\":\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\",\"original_line\":780,\"path\":\"superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:34:54Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"This map coalesces requests only within one `HostFnOperatorService` instance. Two instances sharing a durable store can both observe no hostname, generate different domain IDs, and call the provider because the store contract has no atomic reservation.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Attachment identity is not serialized across service instances\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:214-217` — keeps in-flight identities in an instance-local map.\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:52-74` — exposes separate list and put operations but no atomic hostname reservation.\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:324-350` — performs a read, generates a random ID, then writes the intent.\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/__tests__/operator.test.ts:176-199` — exercises two calls through only one service instance.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Concurrent attachment requests sharing a durable store must converge on one domain ID and one immutable hostname/TLS identity across service instances.\\n\\n## Suggested approach\\n- Add an atomic reserve-or-read operation to the store contract, or require an equivalent unique scope/target/hostname constraint that returns the winning intent.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:41:30Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837889099\",\"id\":3837889099,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":341,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":301,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T06:41:31Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=58d3a9fb-3175-48fc-8d56-910cdffff4fc --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=82794d43-c58d-4735-82d0-b67349fc5014 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP1: When an attachment lease expires while its provider call is still unwinding, another worker can reclaim the same domain ID. The stale worker’s unconditional status write can then overwrite the newer result and clear its lease, leaving provider state and admin state inconsistent. Fence both status transitions with `claimToken` using a conditional store update.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts, line 400:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen an attachment lease expires while its provider call is still unwinding, another worker can reclaim the same domain ID. The stale worker’s unconditional status write can then overwrite the newer result and clear its lease, leaving provider state and admin state inconsistent. Fence both status transitions with `claimToken` using a conditional store update.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -362,10 +388,24 @@ export class HostFnOperatorService {\\n     const active = { ...domain, status: \\\"active\\\" as const };\\n-    await this.store.putDomain(active);\\n+    try {\\n+      await this.store.putDomain(active);\\n+    } catch (error) {\\n+      try {\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:41:30Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837985680\",\"id\":3837985680,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":400,\"original_commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"original_line\":400,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:41:30Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=cfaeb841-19ba-4b16-ac26-771595fa5e78 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=82794d43-c58d-4735-82d0-b67349fc5014 --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} --\\u003e\\nP2: When `prepareActivation` fails and the denied audit write also fails, this await escapes and the endpoint returns a generic 500 instead of the retryable 503 used for other confirmation audit failures. Wrap this denied-audit write and return `AUDIT_UNAVAILABLE` when it cannot be persisted.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts, line 1089:\\n\\n\\u003ccomment\\u003eWhen `prepareActivation` fails and the denied audit write also fails, this await escapes and the endpoint returns a generic 500 instead of the retryable 503 used for other confirmation audit failures. Wrap this denied-audit write and return `AUDIT_UNAVAILABLE` when it cannot be persisted.\\u003c/comment\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cfile context\\u003e\\n@@ -1063,8 +1064,33 @@ export class SuperConsole {\\n+      } catch {\\n+        // The token remains staged and unusable when activation preparation fails.\\n+      }\\n+      await this.auditConfirmation(entry, operationId, immutable.input, immutable.state.context, 'denied', started, 'CONFIRMATION_ACTIVATION_PREPARE_FAILED');\\n+      throw new SuperConsoleHttpError('The confirmation token could not be prepared for activation.', { status: 503, code: 'CONFIRMATION_ACTIVATION_FAILED', details: { retryable: true } });\\n+    }\\n\\u003c/file context\\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n```suggestion\\n      try {\\n        await this.auditConfirmation(entry, operationId, immutable.input, immutable.state.context, 'denied', started, 'CONFIRMATION_ACTIVATION_PREPARE_FAILED');\\n      } catch {\\n        throw new SuperConsoleHttpError('The confirmation activation preparation failure could not be audited.', { status: 503, code: 'AUDIT_UNAVAILABLE', details: { retryable: true } });\\n      }\\n```\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:41:30Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837985685\",\"id\":3837985685,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":1089,\"original_commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"original_line\":1089,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:41:30Z\",\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Reject non-plain objects as JSON values**\\n\\nWhen an in-process dispatcher caller supplies a `Date`, `Map`, or other class instance under `type: \\\"object\\\"`, this branch accepts it as a valid JSON object because it never checks the prototype. The immutable snapshot preserves such instances, and output redaction converts them through `Object.entries`—for example, a valid-looking `Date` response becomes `{}`—so adapters can receive or return values that change shape at transport time; require arrays or plain/null-prototype objects throughout JSON validation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991044\",\"id\":3837991044,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":262,\"original_commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"original_line\":262,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Compare action enum objects structurally**\\n\\nWhen an action field declares an object or array in `enum` or `const`, the form parses the operator's JSON into a new object and these `Object.is` checks always reject it by reference, even when it is structurally identical to the declared value. The administration validator permits these JSON-valued members, so such operations pass manifest validation but cannot be submitted through the generic action UI; use the same structural JSON equality semantics as the runtime validator.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991047\",\"id\":3837991047,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":105,\"original_commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"original_line\":105,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**\\u003csub\\u003e\\u003csub\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\u003c/sub\\u003e\\u003c/sub\\u003e  Reconcile variables when metadata persistence fails**\\n\\nWhen `executor.setVariable` succeeds for a new variable but this store write rejects, the provider retains the live secret while the operator returns an error and has no record through which to list or delete it. A retry is not guaranteed safe because `setVariable` has no idempotency contract; persist a durable intent before the provider call or compensate/reconcile the provider variable if final persistence fails.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991049\",\"id\":3837991049,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":444,\"original_commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"original_line\":444,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in afb902d with an atomic store-level attachment claim.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32626073314/job/97161527435) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:50:19Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838002194\",\"id\":3838002194,\"in_reply_to_id\":3837889099,\"line\":341,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":301,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:50:19Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in afb902d with durable pre-audit activation preparation and reconciliation guidance.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32626073314/job/97161527435) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:50:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838002559\",\"id\":3838002559,\"in_reply_to_id\":3837889103,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":1067,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:50:22Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in afb902d with locale-independent code-unit key ordering.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32626073314/job/97161527435) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:50:25Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838002742\",\"id\":3838002742,\"in_reply_to_id\":3837889101,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":37,\"path\":\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:50:25Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"Addressed in afb902d by retaining repeated property schemas as an intersection.\\n\\n\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\u003e\\n\\u003csup\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32626073314/job/97161527435) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\u003c/sup\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:50:28Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838002878\",\"id\":3838002878,\"in_reply_to_id\":3837889106,\"line\":null,\"original_commit_id\":\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\",\"original_line\":45,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:50:28Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"The lease is explicitly reclaimable, but terminal writes still use unfenced `putDomain`. After a durable store expires and reassigns a claim, the older worker can finish later and overwrite the newer claimant's `active` or `failed` state; require claim-token-guarded terminal transitions or an equivalent compare-and-set.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Reclaimed attachment leases do not fence stale workers\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:66-73` — returns a claim token but exposes terminal domain persistence without it.\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:381-400` — both failed and active transitions call unfenced `putDomain`.\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/__tests__/operator.test.ts:211-236` — covers a still-held claim, not expiry/reclamation followed by stale completion.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Only the current attachment claimant may persist a terminal state or clear its claim.\\n- Cover an expired/reclaimed lease where the older provider call settles after the newer worker.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:54:06Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838010601\",\"id\":3838010601,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":73,\"original_commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"original_line\":73,\"path\":\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:54:07Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"This rule can reactivate a confirmation that Super Console has already denied: if `activate()` fails and `revoke()` also fails, the earlier bound success audit remains, so reconciliation follows this branch despite the later denied audit and 503 response. Make durable cancellation or denial take precedence over the prepared success before returning the failure.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\u003csummary\\u003eTechnical details\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Confirmation reconciliation can override a denied outcome\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `superconsole/README.md:55-62` — directs reconciliation to activate whenever the bound success audit exists.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1108-1142` — records denial and returns 503 after activation failure, but suppresses revocation failure.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/types.ts:179-204` — defines durable preparation and revocation without a durable denied/cancelled precedence signal.\\n- `superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts:783-828` — covers only successful revocation after activation failure.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Once issuance returns an activation failure and records denial, provider reconciliation must not later make that staged token verifiable.\\n- Cover simultaneous activation and revocation failure followed by reconciliation.\\n````\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:54:06Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838010605\",\"id\":3838010605,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":59,\"original_commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"original_line\":59,\"path\":\"superconsole/README.md\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T07:54:07Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":5,"nanos":762920583},"formatted_output":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 46170)\nTotal output lines: 113\n\n{\"body\":\"## CodeQL / Prototype-polluting function\\n\\nThe property chain [segment](1) is recursively assigned to [current](2) without guarding against prototype pollution.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/49)\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736417\",\"id\":3831736417,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":87,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":84,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/resource-pages.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\"user\":\"github-advanced-security[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"**Security:** Mutation authorization is selected from the HTTP method rather than the matched operation's safety classification. Capability validation currently allows a `GET` route whose classification is `write` or `destructive`, so that operation is dispatched without `authorizeMutation` (and therefore without provider CSRF/re-auth checks). Please either reject non-read operations on safe HTTP methods during manifest validation or authorize after matching based on `entry.operation.safety.classification`.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799619\",\"id\":3831799619,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":631,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":612,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"This does not pass the package's own typecheck: `npm run typecheck --workspace superconsole` reports that `code` is not part of SvelteKit's `Error`, followed by two errors where `+error.svelte` reads `page.error.code` and `.details`. Please declare the intended `App.Error` shape in `src/app.d.ts` (or restrict these routes to the standard error shape) so the checked package is type-safe.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799628\",\"id\":3831799628,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":5,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":5,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/routes/[...missing]/+page.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"`SuperConsoleOptions.apiBasePath` changes the only prefix accepted by the server, but every bundled UI loader/action uses this hard-coded prefix. Configuring, for example, `/internal/admin` therefore makes the server reject all UI requests with 404. Please propagate the configured base path to the client/UI (including sign-in and download links), or remove/limit the option so a supported configuration cannot break the console.\",\"commit_id\":\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799631\",\"id\":3831799631,\"in_reply_to_id\":null,\"line\":9,\"original_commit_id\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\",\"original_line\":9,\"path\":\"superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z\",\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- cubic:v=