\\\n+{:else if data.spec}\\\\n\\\\u003c/file context\\\\u003e\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003c/details\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\n```suggestion\\\\n{:else if data.loadError?.status === 401}\\\\n  \\\\u003cStatePanel kind=\\\\\\\"forbidden\\\\\\\" title=\\\\\\\"Authentication required\\\\\\\" message=\\\\\\\"Sign in through the configured operator-auth provider to access administration.\\\\\\\" actionHref=\\\\\\\"/sign-in\\\\\\\" actionLabel=\\\\\\\"Sign in\\\\\\\" /\\\\u003e\\\\n{:else if data.loadError}\\\\n```\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2026-08-21T16:19:47Z\\\",\\\"line\\\":25,\\\"originalLine\\\":23,\\\"outdated\\\":false,\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831870652\\\"}],\\\"isResolved\\\":false,\\\"path\\\":\\\"superconsole/src/routes/api/+page.svelte\\\"}\\n{\\\"comments\\\":[{\\\"author\\\":{\\\"login\\\":\\\"cubic-dev-ai\\\"},\\\"body\\\":\\\"\\\\u003c!-- cubic:v=50f4d3c8-24c4-41cf-8d77-d05a7d6cb60c --\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=7bb8304f-392d-4952-ab05-eaf35f279889 --\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\":10} --\\\\u003e\\\\nP2: For integer-like property names, `Object.fromEntries`/`JSON.stringify` undo the code-unit sort, so `canonicalJson` is not actually canonical in the ordering promised by `compareCodeUnits`. Serialize sorted entries directly or use a representation that prevents integer-key reordering.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003cdetails\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\u003csummary\\\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\\\u003c/summary\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/core/src/canonical.ts, line 15:\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003ccomment\\\\u003eFor integer-like property names, `Object.fromEntries`/`JSON.stringify` undo the code-unit sort, so `canonicalJson` is not actually canonical in the ordering promised by `compareCodeUnits`. Serialize sorted entries directly or use a representation that prevents integer-key reordering.\\\\u003c/comment\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003cfile context\\\\u003e\\\\n@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@\\\\n+    return Object.fromEntries(\\\\n+      Object.entries(value as Record\\\\u003cstring, unknown\\\\u003e)\\\\n+        .filter(([, entry]) =\\\\u003e entry !== undefined)\\\\n+        .sort(([left], [right]) =\\\\u003e compareCodeUnits(left, right))\\\\n+        .map(([key, entry]) =\\\\u003e [key,…74975 tokens truncated…r called. The title's claim \\\\\\\"leaves the staged token unusable\\\\\\\" is therefore not actually exercised. Initialize `let active = true;` so the assertion verifies `revoke` genuinely deactivated the token, or assert on `verify` returning false for the staged token.\\\\u003c/comment\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003cfile context\\\\u003e\\\\n@@ -770,10 +770,54 @@ describe('Super Console server composition', () =\\\\u003e {\\\\n+  it('records activation failure as denied and leaves the staged token unusable', async () =\\\\u003e {\\\\n+    const capability = manifest({ destructive: true });\\\\n+    const outcomes: Array\\\\u003c{ outcome: string; errorCode?: string }\\\\u003e = [];\\\\n+    let active = false;\\\\n+    const revoke = vi.fn(async () =\\\\u003e { active = false; });\\\\n+    const console = createSuperConsole({\\\\n\\\\u003c/file context\\\\u003e\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003c/details\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\n✅ Addressed in [`16a31f1`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a)\\\",\\\"commit_id\\\":\\\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\\\",\\\"created_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T06:11:46Z\\\",\\\"html_url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837844415\\\",\\\"id\\\":3837844415,\\\"in_reply_to_id\\\":null,\\\"line\\\":786,\\\"original_commit_id\\\":\\\"db08968eb1621803789348ff189f09fb66b42b10\\\",\\\"original_line\\\":780,\\\"path\\\":\\\"superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts\\\",\\\"updated_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T06:34:54Z\\\",\\\"user\\\":\\\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\\\"}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"This map coalesces requests only within one `HostFnOperatorService` instance. Two instances sharing a durable store can both observe no hostname, generate different domain IDs, and call the provider because the store contract has no atomic reservation.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003cdetails\\\\u003e\\\\u003csummary\\\\u003eTechnical details\\\\u003c/summary\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\n````markdown\\\\n# Attachment identity is not serialized across service instances\\\\n\\\\n## Affected sites\\\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:214-217` — keeps in-flight identities in an instance-local map.\\\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:52-74` — exposes separate list and put operations but no atomic hostname reservation.\\\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:324-350` — performs a read, generates a random ID, then writes the intent.\\\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/__tests__/operator.test.ts:176-199` — exercises two calls through only one service instance.\\\\n\\\\n## Required outcome\\\\n- Concurrent attachment requests sharing a durable store must converge on one domain ID and one immutable hostname/TLS identity across service instances.\\\\n\\\\n## Suggested approach\\\\n- Add an atomic reserve-or-read operation to the store contract, or require an equivalent unique scope/target/hostname constraint that returns the winning intent.\\\\n````\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003c/details\\\\u003e\\\",\\\"commit_id\\\":\\\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\\\",\\\"created_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T06:41:30Z\\\",\\\"html_url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837889099\\\",\\\"id\\\":3837889099,\\\"in_reply_to_id\\\":null,\\\"line\\\":341,\\\"original_commit_id\\\":\\\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\\\",\\\"original_line\\\":301,\\\"path\\\":\\\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\\\",\\\"updated_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T06:41:31Z\\\",\\\"user\\\":\\\"pullfrog[bot]\\\"}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"\\\\u003c!-- cubic:v=58d3a9fb-3175-48fc-8d56-910cdffff4fc --\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=82794d43-c58d-4735-82d0-b67349fc5014 --\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\":9} --\\\\u003e\\\\nP1: When an attachment lease expires while its provider call is still unwinding, another worker can reclaim the same domain ID. The stale worker’s unconditional status write can then overwrite the newer result and clear its lease, leaving provider state and admin state inconsistent. Fence both status transitions with `claimToken` using a conditional store update.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003cdetails\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\u003csummary\\\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\\\u003c/summary\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts, line 400:\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003ccomment\\\\u003eWhen an attachment lease expires while its provider call is still unwinding, another worker can reclaim the same domain ID. The stale worker’s unconditional status write can then overwrite the newer result and clear its lease, leaving provider state and admin state inconsistent. Fence both status transitions with `claimToken` using a conditional store update.\\\\u003c/comment\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003cfile context\\\\u003e\\\\n@@ -362,10 +388,24 @@ export class HostFnOperatorService {\\\\n     const active = { ...domain, status: \\\\\\\"active\\\\\\\" as const };\\\\n-    await this.store.putDomain(active);\\\\n+    try {\\\\n+      await this.store.putDomain(active);\\\\n+    } catch (error) {\\\\n+      try {\\\\n\\\\u003c/file context\\\\u003e\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003c/details\\\\u003e\\\",\\\"commit_id\\\":\\\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\\\",\\\"created_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:41:30Z\\\",\\\"html_url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837985680\\\",\\\"id\\\":3837985680,\\\"in_reply_to_id\\\":null,\\\"line\\\":400,\\\"original_commit_id\\\":\\\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\\\",\\\"original_line\\\":400,\\\"path\\\":\\\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\\\",\\\"updated_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:41:30Z\\\",\\\"user\\\":\\\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\\\"}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"\\\\u003c!-- cubic:v=cfaeb841-19ba-4b16-ac26-771595fa5e78 --\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\u003c!-- cubic:review-run=82794d43-c58d-4735-82d0-b67349fc5014 --\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\u003c!-- metadata:{\\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\":9} --\\\\u003e\\\\nP2: When `prepareActivation` fails and the denied audit write also fails, this await escapes and the endpoint returns a generic 500 instead of the retryable 503 used for other confirmation audit failures. Wrap this denied-audit write and return `AUDIT_UNAVAILABLE` when it cannot be persisted.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003cdetails\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\u003csummary\\\\u003ePrompt for AI agents\\\\u003c/summary\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts, line 1089:\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003ccomment\\\\u003eWhen `prepareActivation` fails and the denied audit write also fails, this await escapes and the endpoint returns a generic 500 instead of the retryable 503 used for other confirmation audit failures. Wrap this denied-audit write and return `AUDIT_UNAVAILABLE` when it cannot be persisted.\\\\u003c/comment\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003cfile context\\\\u003e\\\\n@@ -1063,8 +1064,33 @@ export class SuperConsole {\\\\n+      } catch {\\\\n+        // The token remains staged and unusable when activation preparation fails.\\\\n+      }\\\\n+      await this.auditConfirmation(entry, operationId, immutable.input, immutable.state.context, 'denied', started, 'CONFIRMATION_ACTIVATION_PREPARE_FAILED');\\\\n+      throw new SuperConsoleHttpError('The confirmation token could not be prepared for activation.', { status: 503, code: 'CONFIRMATION_ACTIVATION_FAILED', details: { retryable: true } });\\\\n+    }\\\\n\\\\u003c/file context\\\\u003e\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003c/details\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\n```suggestion\\\\n      try {\\\\n        await this.auditConfirmation(entry, operationId, immutable.input, immutable.state.context, 'denied', started, 'CONFIRMATION_ACTIVATION_PREPARE_FAILED');\\\\n      } catch {\\\\n        throw new SuperConsoleHttpError('The confirmation activation preparation failure could not be audited.', { status: 503, code: 'AUDIT_UNAVAILABLE', details: { retryable: true } });\\\\n      }\\\\n```\\\",\\\"commit_id\\\":\\\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\\\",\\\"created_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:41:30Z\\\",\\\"html_url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837985685\\\",\\\"id\\\":3837985685,\\\"in_reply_to_id\\\":null,\\\"line\\\":1089,\\\"original_commit_id\\\":\\\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\\\",\\\"original_line\\\":1089,\\\"path\\\":\\\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\\\",\\\"updated_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:41:30Z\\\",\\\"user\\\":\\\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\\\"}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"**\\\\u003csub\\\\u003e\\\\u003csub\\\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\\\u003c/sub\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/sub\\\\u003e  Reject non-plain objects as JSON values**\\\\n\\\\nWhen an in-process dispatcher caller supplies a `Date`, `Map`, or other class instance under `type: \\\\\\\"object\\\\\\\"`, this branch accepts it as a valid JSON object because it never checks the prototype. The immutable snapshot preserves such instances, and output redaction converts them through `Object.entries`—for example, a valid-looking `Date` response becomes `{}`—so adapters can receive or return values that change shape at transport time; require arrays or plain/null-prototype objects throughout JSON validation.\\\\n\\\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\\\",\\\"commit_id\\\":\\\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\\\",\\\"created_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\\\",\\\"html_url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991044\\\",\\\"id\\\":3837991044,\\\"in_reply_to_id\\\":null,\\\"line\\\":262,\\\"original_commit_id\\\":\\\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\\\",\\\"original_line\\\":262,\\\"path\\\":\\\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\\\",\\\"updated_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\\\",\\\"user\\\":\\\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\\\"}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"**\\\\u003csub\\\\u003e\\\\u003csub\\\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\\\u003c/sub\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/sub\\\\u003e  Compare action enum objects structurally**\\\\n\\\\nWhen an action field declares an object or array in `enum` or `const`, the form parses the operator's JSON into a new object and these `Object.is` checks always reject it by reference, even when it is structurally identical to the declared value. The administration validator permits these JSON-valued members, so such operations pass manifest validation but cannot be submitted through the generic action UI; use the same structural JSON equality semantics as the runtime validator.\\\\n\\\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\\\",\\\"commit_id\\\":\\\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\\\",\\\"created_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\\\",\\\"html_url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991047\\\",\\\"id\\\":3837991047,\\\"in_reply_to_id\\\":null,\\\"line\\\":105,\\\"original_commit_id\\\":\\\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\\\",\\\"original_line\\\":105,\\\"path\\\":\\\"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\\\",\\\"updated_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\\\",\\\"user\\\":\\\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\\\"}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"**\\\\u003csub\\\\u003e\\\\u003csub\\\\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\\\\u003c/sub\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/sub\\\\u003e  Reconcile variables when metadata persistence fails**\\\\n\\\\nWhen `executor.setVariable` succeeds for a new variable but this store write rejects, the provider retains the live secret while the operator returns an error and has no record through which to list or delete it. A retry is not guaranteed safe because `setVariable` has no idempotency contract; persist a durable intent before the provider call or compensate/reconcile the provider variable if final persistence fails.\\\\n\\\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\\\",\\\"commit_id\\\":\\\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\\\",\\\"created_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\\\",\\\"html_url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991049\\\",\\\"id\\\":3837991049,\\\"in_reply_to_id\\\":null,\\\"line\\\":444,\\\"original_commit_id\\\":\\\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\\\",\\\"original_line\\\":444,\\\"path\\\":\\\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\\\",\\\"updated_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\\\",\\\"user\\\":\\\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\\\"}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"Addressed in afb902d with an atomic store-level attachment claim.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\u003csup\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cpicture\\\\u003e\\\\u003csource media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cimg src=\\\\\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\\\\\" width=\\\\\\\"9px\\\\\\\" height=\\\\\\\"9px\\\\\\\" style=\\\\\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\\\\\" alt=\\\\\\\"Pullfrog\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/picture\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u0026nbsp;\\\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32626073314/job/97161527435) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\\\u003c/sup\\\\u003e\\\",\\\"commit_id\\\":\\\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\\\",\\\"created_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:50:19Z\\\",\\\"html_url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838002194\\\",\\\"id\\\":3838002194,\\\"in_reply_to_id\\\":3837889099,\\\"line\\\":341,\\\"original_commit_id\\\":\\\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\\\",\\\"original_line\\\":301,\\\"path\\\":\\\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\\\",\\\"updated_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:50:19Z\\\",\\\"user\\\":\\\"pullfrog[bot]\\\"}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"Addressed in afb902d with durable pre-audit activation preparation and reconciliation guidance.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\u003csup\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cpicture\\\\u003e\\\\u003csource media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cimg src=\\\\\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\\\\\" width=\\\\\\\"9px\\\\\\\" height=\\\\\\\"9px\\\\\\\" style=\\\\\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\\\\\" alt=\\\\\\\"Pullfrog\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/picture\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u0026nbsp;\\\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32626073314/job/97161527435) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\\\u003c/sup\\\\u003e\\\",\\\"commit_id\\\":\\\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\\\",\\\"created_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:50:22Z\\\",\\\"html_url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838002559\\\",\\\"id\\\":3838002559,\\\"in_reply_to_id\\\":3837889103,\\\"line\\\":null,\\\"original_commit_id\\\":\\\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\\\",\\\"original_line\\\":1067,\\\"path\\\":\\\"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\\\",\\\"updated_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:50:22Z\\\",\\\"user\\\":\\\"pullfrog[bot]\\\"}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"Addressed in afb902d with locale-independent code-unit key ordering.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\u003csup\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cpicture\\\\u003e\\\\u003csource media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cimg src=\\\\\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\\\\\" width=\\\\\\\"9px\\\\\\\" height=\\\\\\\"9px\\\\\\\" style=\\\\\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\\\\\" alt=\\\\\\\"Pullfrog\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/picture\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u0026nbsp;\\\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32626073314/job/97161527435) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\\\u003c/sup\\\\u003e\\\",\\\"commit_id\\\":\\\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\\\",\\\"created_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:50:25Z\\\",\\\"html_url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838002742\\\",\\\"id\\\":3838002742,\\\"in_reply_to_id\\\":3837889101,\\\"line\\\":null,\\\"original_commit_id\\\":\\\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\\\",\\\"original_line\\\":37,\\\"path\\\":\\\"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\\\",\\\"updated_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:50:25Z\\\",\\\"user\\\":\\\"pullfrog[bot]\\\"}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"Addressed in afb902d by retaining repeated property schemas as an intersection.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003c!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ --\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\u003csup\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cpicture\\\\u003e\\\\u003csource media=\\\\\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\\\\\" srcset=\\\\\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003cimg src=\\\\\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\\\\\" width=\\\\\\\"9px\\\\\\\" height=\\\\\\\"9px\\\\\\\" style=\\\\\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\\\\\" alt=\\\\\\\"Pullfrog\\\\\\\"\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/picture\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u0026nbsp;\\\\u0026nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32626073314/job/97161527435) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)\\\\u003c/sup\\\\u003e\\\",\\\"commit_id\\\":\\\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\\\",\\\"created_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:50:28Z\\\",\\\"html_url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838002878\\\",\\\"id\\\":3838002878,\\\"in_reply_to_id\\\":3837889106,\\\"line\\\":null,\\\"original_commit_id\\\":\\\"16a31f15e61f1ab95930f35bab2999aa40e9901a\\\",\\\"original_line\\\":45,\\\"path\\\":\\\"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\\\",\\\"updated_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:50:28Z\\\",\\\"user\\\":\\\"pullfrog[bot]\\\"}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"The lease is explicitly reclaimable, but terminal writes still use unfenced `putDomain`. After a durable store expires and reassigns a claim, the older worker can finish later and overwrite the newer claimant's `active` or `failed` state; require claim-token-guarded terminal transitions or an equivalent compare-and-set.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003cdetails\\\\u003e\\\\u003csummary\\\\u003eTechnical details\\\\u003c/summary\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\n````markdown\\\\n# Reclaimed attachment leases do not fence stale workers\\\\n\\\\n## Affected sites\\\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:66-73` — returns a claim token but exposes terminal domain persistence without it.\\\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:381-400` — both failed and active transitions call unfenced `putDomain`.\\\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/__tests__/operator.test.ts:211-236` — covers a still-held claim, not expiry/reclamation followed by stale completion.\\\\n\\\\n## Required outcome\\\\n- Only the current attachment claimant may persist a terminal state or clear its claim.\\\\n- Cover an expired/reclaimed lease where the older provider call settles after the newer worker.\\\\n````\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003c/details\\\\u003e\\\",\\\"commit_id\\\":\\\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\\\",\\\"created_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:54:06Z\\\",\\\"html_url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838010601\\\",\\\"id\\\":3838010601,\\\"in_reply_to_id\\\":null,\\\"line\\\":73,\\\"original_commit_id\\\":\\\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\\\",\\\"original_line\\\":73,\\\"path\\\":\\\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\\\",\\\"updated_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:54:07Z\\\",\\\"user\\\":\\\"pullfrog[bot]\\\"}\\n{\\\"body\\\":\\\"This rule can reactivate a confirmation that Super Console has already denied: if `activate()` fails and `revoke()` also fails, the earlier bound success audit remains, so reconciliation follows this branch despite the later denied audit and 503 response. Make durable cancellation or denial take precedence over the prepared success before returning the failure.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003cdetails\\\\u003e\\\\u003csummary\\\\u003eTechnical details\\\\u003c/summary\\\\u003e\\\\n\\\\n````markdown\\\\n# Confirmation reconciliation can override a denied outcome\\\\n\\\\n## Affected sites\\\\n- `superconsole/README.md:55-62` — directs reconciliation to activate whenever the bound success audit exists.\\\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1108-1142` — records denial and returns 503 after activation failure, but suppresses revocation failure.\\\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/types.ts:179-204` — defines durable preparation and revocation without a durable denied/cancelled precedence signal.\\\\n- `superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts:783-828` — covers only successful revocation after activation failure.\\\\n\\\\n## Required outcome\\\\n- Once issuance returns an activation failure and records denial, provider reconciliation must not later make that staged token verifiable.\\\\n- Cover simultaneous activation and revocation failure followed by reconciliation.\\\\n````\\\\n\\\\n\\\\u003c/details\\\\u003e\\\",\\\"commit_id\\\":\\\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\\\",\\\"created_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:54:06Z\\\",\\\"html_url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838010605\\\",\\\"id\\\":3838010605,\\\"in_reply_to_id\\\":null,\\\"line\\\":59,\\\"original_commit_id\\\":\\\"afb902dad102723f1e79c3c3cc51075aa88524dc\\\",\\\"original_line\\\":59,\\\"path\\\":\\\"superconsole/README.md\\\",\\\"updated_at\\\":\\\"2026-08-23T07:54:07Z\\\",\\\"user\\\":\\\"pullfrog[bot]\\\"}\\n\"}]"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02dda-f2ef-7f43-9257-ff0e7824b8c6","create_time":1787475786.391265}}}
