{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T09:03:17.471Z","ordinal":12369,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a02ddc-25df-7332-a6ef-28f580e2b2d1","call_id":"call_7GuCyVl8MspVPrB3qjCVMdDh","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\n  \"inlineCount\": 11,\n  \"inline\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 3837985680,\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n      \"line\": 400,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T07:41:30Z\",\n      \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837985680\",\n      \"title\": \"P1: When an attachment lease expires while its provider call is still unwinding, another worker can reclaim the same domain ID. The stale worker’s unconditional status write can then overwrite the newer result and clear its lease, leaving provider state and admin state inconsistent. Fence both status transitions with `claimToken` using a conditional store update.\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=58d3a9fb-3175-48fc-8d56-910cdffff4fc -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=82794d43-c58d-4735-82d0-b67349fc5014 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP1: When an attachment lease expires while its provider call is still unwinding, another worker can reclaim the same domain ID. The stale worker’s unconditional status write can then overwrite the newer result and clear its lease, leaving provider state and admin state inconsistent. Fence both status transitions with `claimToken` using a conditional store update.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts, line 400:\\n\\n<comment>When an attachment lease expires while its provider call is still unwinding, another worker can reclaim the same domain ID. The stale worker’s unconditional status write can then overwrite the newer result and clear its lease, leaving provider state and admin state inconsistent. Fence both status transitions with `claimToken` using a conditional store update.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -362,10 +388,24 @@ export class HostFnOperatorService {\\n     const active = { ...domain, status: \\\"active\\\" as const };\\n-    await this.store.putDomain(active);\\n+    try {\\n+      await this.store.putDomain(active);\\n+    } catch (error) {\\n+      try {\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 3837985685,\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\n      \"line\": 1089,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T07:41:30Z\",\n      \"user\": \"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837985685\",\n      \"title\": \"P2: When `prepareActivation` fails and the denied audit write also fails, this await escapes and the endpoint returns a generic 500 instead of the retryable 503 used for other confirmation audit failures. Wrap this denied-audit write and return `AUDIT_UNAVAILABLE` when it cannot be persisted.\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=cfaeb841-19ba-4b16-ac26-771595fa5e78 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=82794d43-c58d-4735-82d0-b67349fc5014 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: When `prepareActivation` fails and the denied audit write also fails, this await escapes and the endpoint returns a generic 500 instead of the retryable 503 used for other confirmation audit failures. Wrap this denied-audit write and return `AUDIT_UNAVAILABLE` when it cannot be persisted.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts, line 1089:\\n\\n<comment>When `prepareActivation` fails and the denied audit write also fails, this await escapes and the endpoint returns a generic 500 instead of the retryable 503 used for other confirmation audit failures. Wrap this denied-audit write and return `AUDIT_UNAVAILABLE` when it cannot be persisted.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -1063,8 +1064,33 @@ export class SuperConsole {\\n+      } catch {\\n+        // The token remains staged and unusable when activation preparation fails.\\n+      }\\n+      await this.auditConfirmation(entry, operationId, immutable.input, immutable.state.context, 'denied', started, 'CONFIRMATION_ACTIVATION_PREPARE_FAILED');\\n+      throw new SuperConsoleHttpError('The confirmation token could not be prepared for activation.', { status: 503, code: 'CONFIRMATION_ACTIVATION_FAILED', details: { retryable: true } });\\n+    }\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n      try {\\n        await this.auditConfirmation(entry, operationId, immutable.input, immutable.state.context, 'denied', started, 'CONFIRMATION_ACTIVATION_PREPARE_FAILED');\\n      } catch {\\n        throw new SuperConsoleHttpError('The confirmation activation preparation failure could not be audited.', { status: 503, code: 'AUDIT_UNAVAILABLE', details: { retryable: true } });\\n      }\\n```\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 3837991044,\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n      \"line\": 262,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n      \"user\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991044\",\n      \"title\": \"**  ![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)    Reject non-plain objects as JSON values**\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject non-plain objects as JSON values**\\n\\nWhen an in-process dispatcher caller supplies a `Date`, `Map`, or other class instance under `type: \\\"object\\\"`, this branch accepts it as a valid JSON object because it never checks the prototype. The immutable snapshot preserves such instances, and output redaction converts them through `Object.entries`—for example, a valid-looking `Date` response becomes `{}`—so adapters can receive or return values that change shape at transport time; require arrays or plain/null-prototype objects throughout JSON validation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 3837991047,\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\",\n      \"line\": 105,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n      \"user\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991047\",\n      \"title\": \"**  ![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)    Compare action enum objects structurally**\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Compare action enum objects structurally**\\n\\nWhen an action field declares an object or array in `enum` or `const`, the form parses the operator's JSON into a new object and these `Object.is` checks always reject it by reference, even when it is structurally identical to the declared value. The administration validator permits these JSON-valued members, so such operations pass manifest validation but cannot be submitted through the generic action UI; use the same structural JSON equality semantics as the runtime validator.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 3837991049,\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n      \"line\": 444,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n      \"user\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991049\",\n      \"title\": \"**  ![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)    Reconcile variables when metadata persistence fails**\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile variables when metadata persistence fails**\\n\\nWhen `executor.setVariable` succeeds for a new variable but this store write rejects, the provider retains the live secret while the operator returns an error and has no record through which to list or delete it. A retry is not guaranteed safe because `setVariable` has no idempotency contract; persist a durable intent before the provider call or compensate/reconcile the provider variable if final persistence fails.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 3838002194,\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n      \"line\": 341,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T07:50:19Z\",\n      \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838002194\",\n      \"title\": \"Addressed in afb902d with an atomic store-level attachment claim.\",\n      \"body\": \"Addressed in afb902d with an atomic store-level attachment claim.\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32626073314/job/97161527435) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 3838002559,\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T07:50:22Z\",\n      \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838002559\",\n      \"title\": \"Addressed in afb902d with durable pre-audit activation preparation and reconciliation guidance.\",\n      \"body\": \"Addressed in afb902d with durable pre-audit activation preparation and reconciliation guidance.\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32626073314/job/97161527435) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 3838002742,\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T07:50:25Z\",\n      \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838002742\",\n      \"title\": \"Addressed in afb902d with locale-independent code-unit key ordering.\",\n      \"body\": \"Addressed in afb902d with locale-independent code-unit key ordering.\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32626073314/job/97161527435) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 3838002878,\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T07:50:28Z\",\n      \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838002878\",\n      \"title\": \"Addressed in afb902d by retaining repeated property schemas as an intersection.\",\n      \"body\": \"Addressed in afb902d by retaining repeated property schemas as an intersection.\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32626073314/job/97161527435) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 3838010601,\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n      \"line\": 73,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T07:54:06Z\",\n      \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838010601\",\n      \"title\": \"The lease is explicitly reclaimable, but terminal writes still use unfenced `putDomain`. After a durable store expires and reassigns a claim, the older worker can finish later and overwrite the newer claimant's `active` or `failed` state; require claim-token-guarded terminal transitions or an equivalent compare-and-set.\",\n      \"body\": \"The lease is explicitly reclaimable, but terminal writes still use unfenced `putDomain`. After a durable store expires and reassigns a claim, the older worker can finish later and overwrite the newer claimant's `active` or `failed` state; require claim-token-guarded terminal transitions or an equivalent compare-and-set.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Reclaimed attachment leases do not fence stale workers\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:66-73` — returns a claim token but exposes terminal domain persistence without it.\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:381-400` — both failed and active transitions call unfenced `putDomain`.\\n- `hostfn/cli/src/__tests__/operator.test.ts:211-236` — covers a still-held claim, not expiry/reclamation followed by stale completion.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Only the current attachment claimant may persist a terminal state or clear its claim.\\n- Cover an expired/reclaimed lease where the older provider call settles after the newer worker.\\n````\\n\\n</details>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 3838010605,\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/README.md\",\n      \"line\": 59,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T07:54:06Z\",\n      \"user\": \"pullfrog[bot]\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838010605\",\n      \"title\": \"This rule can reactivate a confirmation that Super Console has already denied: if `activate()` fails and `revoke()` also fails, the earlier bound success audit remains, so reconciliation follows this branch despite the later denied audit and 503 response. Make durable cancellation or denial take precedence over the prepared success before returning the failure.\",\n      \"body\": \"This rule can reactivate a confirmation that Super Console has already denied: if `activate()` fails and `revoke()` also fails, the earlier bound success audit remains, so reconciliation follows this branch despite the later denied audit and 503 response. Make durable cancellation or denial take precedence over the prepared success before returning the failure.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Confirmation reconciliation can override a denied outcome\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `superconsole/README.md:55-62` — directs reconciliation to activate whenever the bound success audit exists.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1108-1142` — records denial and returns 503 after activation failure, but suppresses revocation failure.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/types.ts:179-204` — defines durable preparation and revocation without a durable denied/cancelled precedence signal.\\n- `superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts:783-828` — covers only successful revocation after activation failure.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Once issuance returns an activation failure and records denial, provider reconciliation must not later make that staged token verifiable.\\n- Cover simultaneous activation and revocation failure followed by reconciliation.\\n````\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pr\": {\n    \"parseError\": true,\n    \"chars\": 119809,\n    \"tail\": \"ELOG.md`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/README.md`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/lib/conformance/svelte-conformance.ts`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/lib/hooks/copy-to-clipboard.ts`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/lib/hooks/index.ts`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/lib/hooks/media-query.ts`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/lib/index.ts`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/lib/internal/PrimitivePart.svelte`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/lib/internal/PrimitiveRoot.svelte`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/lib/internal/index.ts`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/lib/internal/props.ts`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/package.json`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/tests/fixtures/AccordionHarness.svelte`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/tests/fixtures/AllRootsHarness.svelte`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/tests/fixtures/LifecycleHarness.svelte`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/tests/fixtures/MenubarHarness.svelte`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/tests/fixtures/Phase14AccordionSsrHarness.svelte`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/tests/fixtures/Phase14PublicTreeHarness.svelte`\\\\n\\\\u003e * `uifn/svelte/tests/fixtures/Phase14PublicTreeSsrHarness.svelte`\\\\n