9:\\n\\n<comment>This diff introduces a second copy of the route method/path parser. validator.ts `operationRoutePath` now implements the identical manual whitespace-splitting loop with the same verb allowlist, and two other consumers still parse routes differently with a regex (`routeMatches` in registry.ts line 234 and `route()` in openapi.ts line 71, both `trim().split(/\\\\s+/, 1)[0]`). Four places now derive `method`/`path` from a string route with three distinct implementations that must stay in sync; a future change to one (e.g. method normalization or path handling) can silently diverge the registry route, validation, matching, and OpenAPI generation. Extract the split-and-validate logic into a single shared helper in this package and use it from `routeOf`, `operationRoutePath`, `routeMatches`, and `route`.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -34,15 +34,42 @@ function dependenciesOf(manifest: AdminCapabilityManifest): string[] {\\n-    return { method: match[1]!.toUpperCase(), path: match[2]! };\\n+    const route = operation.route.trim();\\n+    let boundary = 0;\\n+    while (boundary < route.length && !/\\\\s/.test(route[boundary]!)) boundary += 1;\\n+    const method = route.slice(0, boundary).toUpperCase();\\n+    const path = route.slice(boundary).trimStart();\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bWPDg\",\n      \"path\": \"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T04:20:36Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T04:20:36Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835067767\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Filter provider installations by tenant**\\n\\nWhen two tenants use the same user or organization owner ID, this query filters only by `ownerKind` and `ownerId`, even though provider-installation records and the mapped identity both carry `tenantId`. The runtime storage applies exactly the supplied filters, so the list can expose another tenant's provider, scopes, status, and timestamps; include `mapped.tenantId` in the storage filter or apply the same tenant/owner predicate used by `assertInstallationOwner`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bWPDh\",\n      \"path\": \"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T04:20:36Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T04:20:36Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835067768\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Exclude cross-tenant sync jobs from list results**\\n\\nIn a multi-tenant deployment where owner IDs overlap, `listJobs` returns every job matching that owner without verifying the tenant of each job's `connectionId`. Unlike `getSyncJob`, which calls `ownedConnection` and rejects a connection from another tenant, this list path immediately projects all matches, exposing foreign job status, counters, and error text; tenant-scope the query or validate each job through its connection before returning it.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bWSjJ\",\n      \"path\": \"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T04:32:38Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T04:32:38Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835088595\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=c01d9859-f4a1-4ad6-babd-3dd90bcbb46c -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e132b4ff-cab0-498f-ac59-f8230337c676 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: When a document uses an allowed numeric ID such as `1.5`, `remove-document` sends only `\\\"1.5\\\"`, so `MemoryAdapter` leaves the numeric document searchable. Alias every finite number whose canonical string matches the target, or reject unsupported numeric IDs during indexing.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 105:\\n\\n<comment>When a document uses an allowed numeric ID such as `1.5`, `remove-document` sends only `\\\"1.5\\\"`, so `MemoryAdapter` leaves the numeric document searchable. Alias every finite number whose canonical string matches the target, or reject unsupported numeric IDs during indexing.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -98,8 +98,13 @@ function splitDocumentId(value: string): { resource: string; id: string } {\\n+}\\n+\\n+function documentRemovalIds(id: string): Array<string | number> {\\n+  if (!/^-?(?:0|[1-9]\\\\d*)$/.test(id)) return [id];\\n+  const numericId = Number(id);\\n+  return Number.isSafeInteger(numericId) ? [id, numericId] : [id];\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n  const numericId = Number(id);\\n  return Number.isFinite(numericId) && String(numericId) === id ? [id, numericId] : [id];\\n```\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bWSjP\",\n      \"path\": \"billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 82,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T04:32:38Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T04:32:38Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835088601\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=d37f08b0-fdf9-47e7-a2ba-9175b691b67a -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e132b4ff-cab0-498f-ac59-f8230337c676 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: When the manifest advertises catalog fields absent from the records, this generic filter drops every record for a non-`undefined` value and the sorter falls back to `id`. Align the manifest with the record shape or map those fields before applying the controls.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 68:\\n\\n<comment>When the manifest advertises catalog fields absent from the records, this generic filter drops every record for a non-`undefined` value and the sorter falls back to `id`. Align the manifest with the record shape or map those fields before applying the controls.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -51,8 +54,35 @@ function asJson(value: object): JsonRecord {\\n+    records = records.filter((value) => JSON.stringify(value).toLowerCase().includes(query));\\n+  }\\n+  if (input.filter) {\\n+    records = records.filter((value) => Object.entries(input.filter!).every(([key, expected]) => Object.is(value[key], expected)));\\n+  }\\n+  const sorts = input.sort ?? [];\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bW61H\",\n      \"path\": \"datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T06:05:22Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T06:05:23Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835342080\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Prefix listed DataFn record IDs with their resource**\\n\\nWhen the DataFn record list returns a normal domain row such as `{ id: \\\"task-1\\\" }`, this forwards the raw ID even though `getRecord` and `mutate` require the composite target `tasks:task-1`. The Super Console derives detail links and row-action inputs from each returned `id`, so opening or mutating any listed record produces an invalid composite-ID error. Project each row with the selected resource prefix while preserving the underlying domain ID as needed.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bW61J\",\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T06:05:22Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T06:05:23Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835342084\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Route resource HEAD requests through their GET operation**\\n\\nFor `HEAD` on a module resource list or detail route, the registry lookup uses `HEAD`, but every read operation is registered as `GET`; the subsequent method check therefore returns 405. This conflicts with the module OPTIONS response, which advertises HEAD, and unlike the module root and shell endpoints this path never strips a GET response body. Match HEAD against the corresponding GET operation and return it through `headAware`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bW8S7\",\n      \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T06:09:40Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T06:09:40Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835351187\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=b2dd4bca-b048-433a-ae26-2a170bf678ca -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=c3096435-6aa1-4235-8388-39d72d0f9ba1 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":6} -->\\nP2: For values with no exact normalized substring match, the new collation fallback segments the whole value and, for each starting grapheme, tries up to queryLength±8 slice lengths with an array slice+join+`collator.compare` per attempt. This is an O(n) segmentation plus O(n·span) comparison scan per call — a regression from the previous single regex pass. I measured ~48–93ms to reject a single 50k-char non-matching value. Consider bounding the scan (e.g. limit value segments examined or bail out after a cap) so filtering large lists stays within the old single-pass cost when there is no match.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts, line 56:\\n\\n<comment>For values with no exact normalized substring match, the new collation fallback segments the whole value and, for each starting grapheme, tries up to queryLength±8 slice lengths with an array slice+join+`collator.compare` per attempt. This is an O(n) segmentation plus O(n·span) comparison scan per call — a regression from the previous single regex pass. I measured ~48–93ms to reject a single 50k-char non-matching value. Consider bounding the scan (e.g. limit value segments examined or bail out after a cap) so filtering large lists stays within the old single-pass cost when there is no match.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -10,22 +10,53 @@ export interface LocaleMatcher {\\n+      if (queryLength > MAX_COLLATION_QUERY_SEGMENTS) return false;\\n+      const valueSegments = segments(value);\\n+      const queryInitial = initial(query);\\n+      for (let start = 0; start < valueSegments.length; start += 1) {\\n+        if (matchesAt(valueSegments, query, queryLength, queryInitial, start)) return true;\\n+      }\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXL9I\",\n      \"path\": \"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T06:54:29Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T06:54:29Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835445394\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Tenant-scope workflow ownership checks**\\n\\nWhen separate tenants map to the same `userId`, this predicate treats either tenant's workflow as owned because it ignores `mapped.tenantId`; `listWorkflows` likewise filters storage only by `userId`. Consequently the new admin surface can expose foreign workflow metadata and allows `getWorkflowStats`, enable, disable, or delete operations against the other tenant's workflow. Persist and validate a tenant identifier for workflows, or reject workflows whose tenant cannot be established.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXL9M\",\n      \"path\": \"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T06:54:29Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T06:54:29Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835445399\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject tenant-unverifiable webhook receipts**\\n\\nFor a legacy receipt without `connectionId`, this fallback authorizes solely by `ownerKind` and `ownerId`, even though the active identity is tenant-scoped and the receipt carries no tenant field. If user or organization IDs overlap across tenants, knowing a foreign receipt ID lets an operator read its receipt metadata and list its delivery status and errors. Require a tenant-verifiable connection or other tenant-bound provenance instead of accepting the legacy owner match.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXaG9\",\n      \"path\": \"datafn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 502,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T07:39:29Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T07:39:29Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835531565\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Supply a resource selector before exposing Records**\\n\\nWhen an operator opens the DataFn Records card in Super Console, the generated list request contains no `filter`, because this resource declares neither presentation filters nor a parent binding. Requiring `filter` here therefore makes the default Records route fail validation on every visit, leaving record browsing unusable unless the operator manually constructs a JSON query parameter; add a control/binding for `filter.resource` or stop advertising this as a standalone list.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXaG-\",\n      \"path\": \"filefn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T07:39:29Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T07:39:29Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835531568\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Mark file-bound collections as non-standalone**\\n\\nOpening Versions from the FileFn module page invokes `filefn.versions.list` without the required `fileId`; Grants, Share Links, and Artifacts have the same problem. These resources omit `presentation.parent` and consequently default to `standaloneList: true`, so the console advertises cards that only return input-validation errors and cannot generate related links from a file detail page; declare their file-parent bindings and disable standalone listing.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXaHA\",\n      \"path\": \"filefn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T07:39:29Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T07:39:29Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835531570\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Do not bind share revocation to the hash prefix**\\n\\nFor each listed share link, the generic row-action binder uses the resource identity (`tokenHashPrefix`) as this operation's `token` input and hides that target field from the form. The operator therefore cannot supply the required original plaintext token, and every displayed Revoke Share action confirms and submits the hash prefix instead, so it cannot revoke the selected link; avoid projecting this as an identity-bound row action or provide an independently editable plaintext-token input.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXbFH\",\n      \"path\": \"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T07:43:02Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T07:43:03Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835537182\",\n          \"body\": \"[P1] Derive workflow tenant ownership from an authoritative field. `WorkflowEngine.create()` and `AdapterWorkflowStorage.create()` persist caller-provided `metadata` unchanged, and no core producer reserves or populates this key. As a result, ordinary/legacy workflows are hidden from administration, while any application path that accepts workflow metadata can forge the value used here for isolation. Add a first-class tenant owner populated from authenticated context (or verify through another authoritative relation) rather than treating generic metadata as authorization provenance.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXbFK\",\n      \"path\": \"uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T07:43:02Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T07:43:03Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835537185\",\n          \"body\": \"[P1] Validate the expected action outcome rather than any activity. The vectors declare action names and callback names but no expected post-state, callback arguments, or DOM semantics, so changing an unrelated state key or invoking a callback with the wrong payload makes `observed` true; line 380 then reports `passed`, and the Svelte test only asserts that result. Encode and compare expected state/callback effects so behaviorally incorrect adapters cannot satisfy the parity gate.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXfQZ\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/core/src/registry.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 196,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T07:57:05Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T07:57:05Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835561789\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject duplicate resource-template URI patterns**\\n\\nWhen two templates have different names but the same `uriTemplate`, this name-only duplicate check accepts both and advertises both from `resources/templates/list`. However, `matchResource` resolves by iterating the templates and returns the first URI match, so the later template's `read`, subscription, and completion behavior is unreachable. Reject duplicate `uriTemplate` values at registration time.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXfQa\",\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 738,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T07:57:05Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T07:57:05Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835561790\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Encode cursor payloads as UTF-8**\\n\\nWhen any active scope identifier contains a non-Latin-1 character and a HostFn list has another page, `btoa(JSON.stringify(...))` throws `InvalidCharacterError` while constructing `nextCursor`, causing an otherwise successful list request to fail. Admin scope validation permits arbitrary nonblank Unicode strings, so encode the JSON as UTF-8 bytes before base64 encoding and reverse that transformation when decoding.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXkIS\",\n      \"path\": \"filefn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T08:13:59Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T08:13:59Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835590707\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Return usable FileFn download descriptors**\\n\\nWhen either download operation is invoked through the dispatcher, declaring `url` and `headers` as output fields causes `redactAdminOutputValue` to replace the signed URL and any required headers with `\\\"[REDACTED]\\\"`. The REST, MCP, and typed SDK responses therefore cannot be used to download the file; the artifact download declaration has the same defect. Return a provider-safe descriptor instead of redacting the fields that constitute the operation's result.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXkIX\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/openapi.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T08:13:59Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T08:13:59Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835590713\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Include CSRF metadata for POST read operations**\\n\\nFor a read-classified operation that uses an unsafe HTTP method, such as `apifn.specs.compare` (`POST`), `SuperConsole.handle` still calls `authorizeMutation` based on the request method, so cookie-authenticated AuthFn requests require the provider CSRF header. This classification check omits that header from OpenAPI, causing generated clients or API-console requests that follow the document to receive a CSRF 403; determine CSRF metadata from the HTTP method instead.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXvKo\",\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T08:52:09Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T08:52:09Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835655943\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Canonicalize the installation alias before idempotency**\\n\\nWhen a retry identifies the same installation through `organizationId` instead of `installationId`, this constructs a structurally different `AdminScope` even though the package defines organization as a compatibility alias. `AdminDispatcher` includes the raw scope in its idempotency identity, so the same actor, operation, and idempotency key can acquire a second claim and execute an idempotent mutation twice; scope-bound cursors also fail across the two equivalent forms. Normalize the root to one canonical property before passing the authorized scope downstream.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXvKq\",\n      \"path\": \"authfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T08:52:09Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T08:52:09Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835655945\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Expose nested AuthFn sessions through the Sessions resource**\\n\\nFor operators using the generic Super Console, this list operation is grouped under `users` because `moduleView` groups operations by `target.resource`, while the declared `sessions` resource contains only the revoke mutation and is therefore non-listable. The operation name also does not end in `.list`, and the Sessions resource declares no presentation override or user-parent binding, so neither the AuthFn module page nor a user detail page provides a route to browse active sessions. Target the Sessions collection and declare its user-parent/list presentation metadata.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXvb-\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/openapi.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T08:53:03Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T08:53:04Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835657402\",\n          \"body\": \"The manifest contract permits a `GET` route classified as a mutation, and Super Console explicitly sends that case through `authorizeMutation`; AuthFn then requires CSRF for cookie credentials. This method-only condition removes the provider header from that operation's OpenAPI contract, so generated cookie clients can follow the contract and still be rejected.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# CSRF projection diverges for safe-method mutations\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `packages/admin/src/openapi.ts:151` — projects the CSRF header only from the HTTP method.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1213-1215` — invokes `authorizeMutation` for non-read operations using safe methods.\\n- `authfn/core/src/index.ts:166-175` — enforces CSRF whenever cookie credentials authorize a mutation.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Project provider CSRF metadata for every operation that can reach `authorizeMutation`, including both POST reads and GET mutations.\\n- Add projection coverage for a GET operation with non-read classification.\\n````\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bX1GN\",\n      \"path\": \"botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 241,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:14:07Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:14:07Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835691127\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Make bot deletion and channel connection atomic**\\n\\nWhen `connectChannel` and `deleteBot` run concurrently, the connect path can observe the bot here, then the delete path can observe no channels and delete it, after which the connect path persists a channel for the now-missing bot. Because the store contract exposes only these separate reads and writes, even the supplied memory implementation permits an orphaned active external binding; enforce the bot-exists/channel-empty invariant atomically in the persistence layer.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bX1GP\",\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:14:07Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:14:07Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835691129\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind HostFn cursors to their collection and query**\\n\\nWithin one HostFn scope, every list operation encodes exactly the same `{ offset }` payload, so a cursor returned by targets can be supplied to deployments, domains, or variables, and a cursor created with one target/status filter can be reused with another. The decoder accepts it and skips that many unrelated records; include the operation plus parent/filter identity in the cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bX1GR\",\n      \"path\": \"uifn/adapter-kit/src/conformance.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:14:07Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:14:07Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835691132\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Validate the complete semantic trace shape**\\n\\nFor traces loaded from JSON rather than produced under the TypeScript type, this only checks that `environment` and `cleanup` are objects and that `result` is a string. A trace can therefore omit all required environment or cleanup fields, or use a result such as `\\\"skipped\\\"`, and still pass validation; if the golden and framework traces share the malformed shape, `runSemanticParity` can report success despite having no cleanup/environment evidence. Validate the required nested fields, value enums, and counter types before comparison.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bX52F\",\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 709,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:31:22Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:31:22Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835719292\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=44d0df05-0c14-4598-be82-2f7f6eb7f22a -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=c399a9ed-1c7a-49dd-b678-501e2107db35 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP2: When a user continues pagination with a cursor issued by the previous HostFn version, this check rejects it because the old position contains only `offset`. Version the cursor format and provide a compatibility path for in-flight cursors so rolling deployments do not strand paginated admin pages.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/admin/src/index.ts, line 709:\\n\\n<comment>When a user continues pagination with a cursor issued by the previous HostFn version, this check rejects it because the old position contains only `offset`. Version the cursor format and provide a compatibility path for in-flight cursors so rolling deployments do not strand paginated admin pages.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -698,13 +698,15 @@ function pageResult(\\n-      const decoded = decodeAdminCursor<{ offset?: unknown }>(input.cursor, cursorScope);\\n+      const decoded = decodeAdminCursor<{ identity?: unknown; offset?: unknown }>(input.cursor, cursorScope);\\n       if (\\n+        decoded.identity !== identity ||\\n         typeof decoded.offset !== \\\"number\\\" ||\\n         !Number.isSafeInteger(decoded.offset) ||\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bX636\",\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:35:32Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:35:32Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835725428\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve encoded separators in route parameter values**\\n\\nWhen a valid resource ID contains `/`, such as a BotFn ID `team/support`, the console materializes it as `team%2Fsupport`, but this nested-decoding check rejects the request before route matching. The affected schemas and services generally accept arbitrary nonempty string IDs, and collection actions can create such records, so their generated detail links and row actions become unusable; either permit encoded separators inside an already-split parameter segment or constrain all route-bound IDs accordingly.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bX638\",\n      \"path\": \"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:35:32Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:35:32Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835725430\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind PlugFn cursors to their collection and filters**\\n\\nWithin one scope, this cursor contains only an offset, so a cursor returned by providers can be supplied to connections, installations, workflows, or deliveries, and a cursor created under one provider/status/search filter can be reused under another. The helper accepts it and skips that many unrelated filtered records; encode the operation and normalized query identity alongside the offset and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bX639\",\n      \"path\": \"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 111,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:35:32Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:35:32Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835725432\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Escape resource names in composite SearchFn targets**\\n\\nWhen a configured SearchFn resource name contains `:`, which the adapter contracts permit, a target such as `orders:v2:string:doc-1` is always split here as resource `orders`; single-document indexing and removal therefore report the valid `orders:v2` index as missing even though batch indexing and clearing can use it. The new typed ID suffix only escapes the document suffix, so the resource component also needs an unambiguous encoding or resource names must be validated as delimiter-free.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bX63-\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/core/src/registry.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:35:32Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:35:32Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835725434\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject semantically equivalent resource templates**\\n\\nWhen templates differ only in variable names, such as `https://example.test/{id}` and `https://example.test/{name}`, this literal-string comparison accepts both even though they match exactly the same URI set. `matchResource` then always selects the first registered template, making the later template's read, subscription, and completion behavior unreachable. Fresh evidence in the current code is that the new duplicate guard compares only the raw `uriTemplate` strings; compare canonicalized template patterns or otherwise reject ambiguous match languages.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYPB4\",\n      \"path\": \"datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T10:51:55Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T10:51:55Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835842745\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Encode resource names in composite DataFn record IDs**\\n\\nWhen a valid DataFn resource name contains `:`, such as `orders:v2`, listed records receive IDs like `orders:v2:record-1`, but `splitRecordId` interprets the resource as `orders`. Opening or mutating that listed record therefore reports the resource as missing; encode the resource component when constructing the composite ID and decode it when splitting.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYPB5\",\n      \"path\": \"billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T10:51:55Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T10:51:55Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835842746\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind BillFn cursors to their collection query**\\n\\nWhen a BillFn collection has another page, the cursor records only an offset and scope, so a cursor returned by prices can be supplied to plans or usage, and a cursor issued for one search/filter/sort can be reused after changing that query. The helper accepts it and skips the same offset in an unrelated result set; include the operation and normalized query identity in the cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYPB6\",\n      \"path\": \"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T10:51:55Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T10:51:55Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835842747\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind SearchFn cursors to the index-list query**\\n\\nWhen the configured index list exceeds one page, changing `search`, `filter`, or `sort` while retaining a cursor still applies the old offset to the new result set because the cursor is validated only against scope. This can skip matching indexes or return an empty page even though results exist; encode the operation and normalized query identity with the offset and reject mismatched cursors.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYT3-\",\n      \"path\": \"uifn/svelte/lib/generated/textarea/Root.svelte\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 10,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871106\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Synchronize the Textarea value binding on input**\\n\\nWhen a consumer uses the advertised `bind:value` API and types into this textarea, the bound variable is never updated: `value` is declared bindable and forwarded to `PrimitiveRoot`, but unlike the generated Input root, no `input` handler assigns the DOM value back to it. The parent therefore retains the initial value, and a later reactive update can overwrite what the user typed; install an input handler that updates `value` while preserving the consumer's handler.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYT4B\",\n      \"path\": \"apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 189,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871110\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Classify malformed OpenAPI documents as invalid input**\\n\\nWhen `document` contains malformed YAML, lacks an OpenAPI version, or declares an unsupported version, `parseOpenAPI` throws a plain `Error` here. `AdminDispatcher` normalizes plain errors to `internal`, so expected client validation failures from both registration and the analogous comparison path become HTTP 500 responses instead of actionable `invalid_argument` responses; catch parse failures and translate them to an admin input error.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYT4E\",\n      \"path\": \"apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 154,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871113\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind ApiFn cursors to scope and collection**\\n\\nWhen a cursor from specs, another project, or another installation is supplied to the environments list (or vice versa), this accepts it as a raw offset and silently skips that many records in the unrelated collection. Since the cursor carries neither scope nor operation identity, ordinary scope changes while retaining the URL cursor can produce empty or incomplete pages; encode and validate the active scope and collection with the offset.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYT4G\",\n      \"path\": \"botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 167,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871115\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind BotFn cursors to the channel filter and scope**\\n\\nWhen a channel cursor is reused after changing `botId`, or a bots/channel cursor is reused in another collection or project, this raw numeric offset remains valid and skips records from the new result set. This makes filtered pagination return incomplete or terminal-looking pages even when matching records exist; include the operation, scope, and `botId` query identity in the cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYT5Y\",\n      \"path\": \"billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871239\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=e5c4adf4-ac55-4511-8b95-044570f04cee -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=5a311de1-61b7-4d68-8481-4dcf664e4fbd -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: When callers omit a sort direction or send a descriptor without a field, the comparator uses the same effective ordering but the cursor identity changes. Build the identity from normalized effective sort descriptors so equivalent page requests can continue.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 92:\\n\\n<comment>When callers omit a sort direction or send a descriptor without a field, the comparator uses the same effective ordering but the cursor identity changes. Build the identity from normalized effective sort descriptors so equivalent page requests can continue.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -83,16 +85,27 @@ function list(\\n+    operationId,\\n+    input.search?.trim().toLowerCase(),\\n+    input.filter,\\n+    input.sort ?? [],\\n+  );\\n+  const decoded = input.cursor\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    sorts.filter((descriptor) => Boolean(descriptor.field)).map((descriptor) => ({ field: descriptor.field, direction: descriptor.direction === \\\"desc\\\" ? \\\"desc\\\" : \\\"asc\\\" })),\\n```\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYT5k\",\n      \"path\": \"billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871252\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=a0aefc6f-f5d8-4c86-9345-c905ad6bb840 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=5a311de1-61b7-4d68-8481-4dcf664e4fbd -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: When `search` is empty or whitespace-only, filtering treats it as no search but the cursor identity treats it differently, so an equivalent next-page request is rejected. Normalize empty searches to `undefined` before computing the identity.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 90:\\n\\n<comment>When `search` is empty or whitespace-only, filtering treats it as no search but the cursor identity treats it differently, so an equivalent next-page request is rejected. Normalize empty searches to `undefined` before computing the identity.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -83,16 +85,27 @@ function list(\\n-  const decoded = input.cursor ? decodeAdminCursor<{ offset?: unknown }>(input.cursor, context.scope) : { offset: 0 };\\n+  const identity = adminPageIdentity(\\n+    operationId,\\n+    input.search?.trim().toLowerCase(),\\n+    input.filter,\\n+    input.sort ?? [],\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    input.search?.trim() ? input.search.trim().toLowerCase() : undefined,\\n```\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYT5l\",\n      \"path\": \"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 85,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:40Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871253\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=450e93a2-581c-40f6-a6a3-6bef44f4564c -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=5a311de1-61b7-4d68-8481-4dcf664e4fbd -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP2: During a rolling deployment, a page cursor issued by the previous server contains only `offset`, so this check rejects the next-page request. Version the cursor schema and retain a compatibility path while old cursors drain, or explicitly handle restart semantics instead of invalidating `version: 1` tokens silently.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 85:\\n\\n<comment>During a rolling deployment, a page cursor issued by the previous server contains only `offset`, so this check rejects the next-page request. Version the cursor schema and retain a compatibility path while old cursors drain, or explicitly handle restart semantics instead of invalidating `version: 1` tokens silently.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -68,12 +70,21 @@ function list(\\n   if (!decoded || typeof decoded !== \\\"object\\\" || Array.isArray(decoded)) {\\n     throw new AdminError(\\\"invalid_argument\\\", \\\"The SearchFn cursor is invalid.\\\");\\n   }\\n+  if (decoded.identity !== identity) {\\n+    throw new AdminError(\\\"invalid_argument\\\", \\\"The SearchFn cursor does not belong to this index-list query.\\\");\\n+  }\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYT5m\",\n      \"path\": \"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 186,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:40Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871255\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=fa774002-8729-4340-86d5-dfb6dadbd47a -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=5a311de1-61b7-4d68-8481-4dcf664e4fbd -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP3: `listAdapters` uses an operation identity that is not declared or registered. Use `searchfn.adapters-backends.list` so operation-bound cursor validation remains consistent.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 186:\\n\\n<comment>`listAdapters` uses an operation identity that is not declared or registered. Use `searchfn.adapters-backends.list` so operation-bound cursor validation remains consistent.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -175,7 +183,7 @@ export function createSearchFnDomainAdminService(\\n     async listAdapters(input, context) {\\n       const { adapterInfo } = await state(context);\\n-      return list([adapterInfo], input, context);\\n+      return list([adapterInfo], input, context, \\\"searchfn.adapters.list\\\");\\n     },\\n     async getAdapter(input, context) {\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n      return list([adapterInfo], input, context, \\\"searchfn.adapters-backends.list\\\");\\n```\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYT5n\",\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 386,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:40Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871257\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=f7498236-c489-4984-96df-d2d54653cc76 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=5a311de1-61b7-4d68-8481-4dcf664e4fbd -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP3: 'does not route an encoded separator embedded in a literal segment' passes even if the server treated %2f as a real route separator: decoded or not, records%2fother matches no registered route, so the 404/OPERATION_NOT_ENABLED assertions cannot detect a routing regression. Use a path whose over-decoded form would hit a real route, e.g. /api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/resources%2frecords (would dispatch the records handler if %2f were split), and keep asserting 404 and handler not called.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts, line 382:\\n\\n<comment>'does not route an encoded separator embedded in a literal segment' passes even if the server treated %2f as a real route separator: decoded or not, records%2fother matches no registered route, so the 404/OPERATION_NOT_ENABLED assertions cannot detect a routing regression. Use a path whose over-decoded form would hit a real route, e.g. /api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/resources%2frecords (would dispatch the records handler if %2f were split), and keep asserting 404 and handler not called.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -376,6 +377,14 @@ describe('Super Console server composition', () => {\\n \\n+  it('does not route an encoded separator embedded in a literal segment', async () => {\\n+    const { console, handler } = installation();\\n+    const result = await console.handle(request('/api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/records%2fother'));\\n+    expect(result.status).toBe(404);\\n+    expect(await result.json()).toMatchObject({ error: { code: 'OPERATION_NOT_ENABLED' } });\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    const result = await console.handle(request('/api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/resources%2frecords'));\\n```\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYT5q\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/pagination.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:40Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835871260\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=c633d0b9-3d7c-4b6c-b47b-f287eeab08e9 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=5a311de1-61b7-4d68-8481-4dcf664e4fbd -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":5} -->\\nP3: The cursor identity is produced by `stableSerialize`, which sorts object keys with `localeCompare`. That ordering depends on the process locale and ICU version, so a cursor identity computed by one server process (or before a redeploy) can fail strict equality against the same query recomputed by another process, rejecting valid cursors with \\\"does not belong to this collection query.\\\" Sort keys by UTF-16 code units (`.sort()` default or `(a,b) => a < b ? -1 : a > b ? 1 : 0`) so identities are reproducible across processes.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/pagination.ts, line 47:\\n\\n<comment>The cursor identity is produced by `stableSerialize`, which sorts object keys with `localeCompare`. That ordering depends on the process locale and ICU version, so a cursor identity computed by one server process (or before a redeploy) can fail strict equality against the same query recomputed by another process, rejecting valid cursors with \\\"does not belong to this collection query.\\\" Sort keys by UTF-16 code units (`.sort()` default or `(a,b) => a < b ? -1 : a > b ? 1 : 0`) so identities are reproducible across processes.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -42,6 +42,11 @@ export function decodeAdminCursor<T>(cursor: string, expectedScope: AdminScope):\\n \\n+/** Canonical identity for binding an offset cursor to one operation and query. */\\n+export function adminPageIdentity(operationId: string, ...query: unknown[]): string {\\n+  return stableSerialize([operationId, ...query.map((value) => value ?? null)]);\\n+}\\n+\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYWOB\",\n      \"path\": \"uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:19:40Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:19:40Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835884895\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Forward undeclared native attributes to the DOM**\\n\\nWhen a consumer supplies a valid native attribute that is not in `ROOT_DOM_PROP`, such as `pattern`, `form`, `maxlength`, `inputmode`, or an anchor's `download`, this fallback classifies it as a controller input instead of a DOM prop. Because the generated component types advertise the full native element interface but the corresponding contracts do not project these undeclared inputs, the attribute disappears from the rendered element, breaking browser validation and native behavior; undeclared properties should be forwarded to `dom` rather than `inputs`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYWOE\",\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:19:40Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:19:40Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835884897\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Sort HostFn records before applying offset cursors**\\n\\nWhen a durable `HostFnOperatorStore` returns the same records in a different order between requests—as database queries without an explicit ordering may—this slices the raw array by offset, so later cursor pages can duplicate or skip records even when the collection itself is unchanged. The store interface promises no ordering, and all HostFn collections share this helper; establish a deterministic tie-broken order before slicing.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYWOG\",\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:19:40Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:19:40Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835884899\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Clone HostFn records returned from the memory store**\\n\\nWhen a caller—or the supplied deployment executor, which receives objects obtained through these methods—mutates a returned target or deployment, the mutation changes the object held inside the memory store without calling `put*`. Changing an ID or scope is especially damaging because the map key then disagrees with the stored value; clone records on reads and lists just as this store already does on writes.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYb9K\",\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 729,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:40:41Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:40:42Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835919209\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=c9db29b1-0333-4e1b-82f8-88a651137fe5 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=565efb3e-1cfe-4884-a6da-1f223d760f97 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP2: When a record’s `updatedAt` changes between page requests, this offset cursor no longer identifies the same page boundary, so records can be skipped or repeated. Sort by an immutable key such as `id`, or switch this cursor to a keyset containing the sort key.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/admin/src/index.ts, line 727:\\n\\n<comment>When a record’s `updatedAt` changes between page requests, this offset cursor no longer identifies the same page boundary, so records can be skipped or repeated. Sort by an immutable key such as `id`, or switch this cursor to a keyset containing the sort key.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -721,12 +721,19 @@ function pageResult(\\n+  const orderedItems = [...items].sort((left, right) => {\\n+    const leftItem = left as { updatedAt?: unknown; createdAt?: unknown; id?: unknown };\\n+    const rightItem = right as { updatedAt?: unknown; createdAt?: unknown; id?: unknown };\\n+    const timestamp = String(leftItem.updatedAt ?? leftItem.createdAt ?? \\\"\\\")\\n+      .localeCompare(String(rightItem.updatedAt ?? rightItem.createdAt ?? \\\"\\\"));\\n+    return timestamp || String(leftItem.id ?? \\\"\\\").localeCompare(String(rightItem.id ?? \\\"\\\"));\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    return String(leftItem.id ?? \\\"\\\").localeCompare(String(rightItem.id ?? \\\"\\\"));\\n```\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYb9M\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/core/tests/protocol.test.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 64,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:40:42Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:40:42Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835919214\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=545b26c9-3780-4967-8f60-c4ad37a8b621 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=565efb3e-1cfe-4884-a6da-1f223d760f97 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":6} -->\\nP2: This new assertion codifies a false-positive duplicate: `docs://users/{;name}` is rejected as a duplicate of `docs://users/{id}` only because `resourceTemplatePattern`'s operator set `[+#./?&]` omits `;`, so `{;name}` normalizes to `{v0}` like `{id}`. `;` is a valid RFC 6570 operator; sections prefixed this way match `docs://users/;name=...`, distinct from plain-segment matches. Valid template forms using `{;...}` are now rejected with a misleading \\\"Duplicate ... URI\\\" error. Add `;` to the operator set in registry.ts so `{;v0}` is kept and genuinely overlapping matrix templates still collide; if `;` templates are instead intentionally unsupported, reject them with an explicit message and code rather than a duplicate error.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/core/tests/protocol.test.ts, line 64:\\n\\n<comment>This new assertion codifies a false-positive duplicate: `docs://users/{;name}` is rejected as a duplicate of `docs://users/{id}` only because `resourceTemplatePattern`'s operator set `[+#./?&]` omits `;`, so `{;name}` normalizes to `{v0}` like `{id}`. `;` is a valid RFC 6570 operator; sections prefixed this way match `docs://users/;name=...`, distinct from plain-segment matches. Valid template forms using `{;...}` are now rejected with a misleading \\\"Duplicate ... URI\\\" error. Add `;` to the operator set in registry.ts so `{;v0}` is kept and genuinely overlapping matrix templates still collide; if `;` templates are instead intentionally unsupported, reject them with an explicit message and code rather than a duplicate error.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ describe(\\\"McpFn protocol primitives\\\", () => {\\n       name: \\\"matrix-account\\\",\\n       read: async (uri) => ({ contents: [{ uri: uri.toString(), text: \\\"matrix\\\" }] }),\\n-    })).not.toThrow();\\n+    })).toThrow(\\\"Duplicate MCP resource template URI: docs://users/{;name}\\\");\\n   });\\n \\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYb9N\",\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 139,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:40:42Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:40:42Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835919215\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=daa00630-654a-4c6b-9dfd-82a4af6ed2c9 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=565efb3e-1cfe-4884-a6da-1f223d760f97 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP3: scoped() now deep-clones every element before listDeployments/listDomains/listVariables apply their targetId filter, so entries that get discarded are cloned wastefully (and listVariables transiently clones the stored secret value before stripping it). Filter by targetId first, then clone only what is returned.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts, line 122:\\n\\n<comment>scoped() now deep-clones every element before listDeployments/listDomains/listVariables apply their targetId filter, so entries that get discarded are cloned wastefully (and listVariables transiently clones the stored secret value before stripping it). Filter by targetId first, then clone only what is returned.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -117,7 +117,9 @@ function scoped<T extends { scope: HostFnScope }>(\\n-  return [...values].filter((value) => scopeKey(value.scope) === key);\\n+  return [...values]\\n+    .filter((value) => scopeKey(value.scope) === key)\\n+    .map((value) => structuredClone(value));\\n }\\n \\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYca_\",\n      \"path\": \"datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 140,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835922082\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve numeric types in composite record IDs**\\n\\nWhen a DataFn row has a numeric ID, `compositeRecordId` serializes it indistinguishably from a string ID and this parser always restores it as a string. Consequently, opening a listed numeric-ID record queries with `filters.id = \\\"42\\\"` rather than `42`, and mutation validation rejects a numeric `payload.id`; encode the ID type in the composite target and restore it when splitting.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYcbC\",\n      \"path\": \"datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 64,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835922087\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind metadata cursors to their DataFn collection**\\n\\nWhen a scope has enough metadata for pagination, the cursor returned by resources, relations, indices, or capabilities contains only an offset and scope, so it can be reused in any of the other collections. The receiving operation accepts it and skips the same number of unrelated records, yielding incomplete or empty pages; include the metadata operation or collection identity in this cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYcbF\",\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 311,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835922091\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Resolve queued deployments when scheduling fails**\\n\\nWhen `executor.deploy` rejects before accepting a deployment, the record has already been persisted as `queued`, and this path neither marks it failed nor removes it. The request returns an error while subsequent deployment lists continue reporting a job that will never run, so persist a terminal/unknown outcome or otherwise reconcile the record on executor failure.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYgUY\",\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 729,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:49:44Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:49:44Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835946128\",\n          \"body\": \"Distinct accepted IDs can compare equal under `localeCompare`, for example composed `é` and decomposed `e\\\\u0301`. When timestamps tie and the backing store changes their input order between requests, offset slicing can duplicate one record and omit another, so this needs a locale-independent total tie-breaker.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# HostFn pagination lacks a total tie-breaker\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `hostfn/admin/src/index.ts:724-729` — the final comparison can return zero for distinct IDs accepted by the manifest.\\n- `hostfn/admin/src/__tests__/admin.test.ts:160-201` — the reordering regression covers only ASCII IDs whose comparisons are nonzero.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Define a strict, locale-independent total order for every accepted HostFn ID before applying an offset cursor.\\n- Cover distinct equal-collation IDs under a store that changes result order between page requests.\\n````\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYmrU\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/core/src/server.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:01:56Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:01:56Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835986662\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind MCP cursors to the list operation**\\n\\nWhen a cursor returned by `tools/list` is supplied to `prompts/list`, `resources/list`, or `resources/templates/list`, this shared decoder accepts it as the same raw offset and skips entries in the unrelated collection; the same problem occurs when a visibility-dependent tools/resources list changes between requests. Include the list method and relevant query/context identity in the opaque cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYmrb\",\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 395,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:01:56Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:01:56Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835986673\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Expose read-classified resource actions**\\n\\nWhen a resource has a non-list/get read operation, this filter removes it from the only detail-page action projection. In the inspected manifests this makes `filefn.files.download`, `filefn.artifacts.download`, and `apifn.specs.compare` unreachable from the generic Super Console UI even though their capabilities are enabled; distinguish read actions from canonical list/detail reads rather than dropping every read-classified operation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYmrd\",\n      \"path\": \"uifn/tokens/src/schema.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 161,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:01:56Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:01:56Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835986675\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject malformed token leaves before recursing**\\n\\nWhen a runtime-loaded theme contains a partial token such as `{ $type: 'color' }` without `$value`, `isDesignToken` returns false and this recursively treats the token—and then its scalar `$type` string—as token groups until the stack overflows. Consequently `assertTokenShape` never emits the advertised `UIFnTokenError` for exactly the malformed input it is meant to validate; verify that non-token nodes are plain group objects before descending.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYs2s\",\n      \"path\": \"mcpfn/core/src/server.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 125,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:22:44Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:22:44Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836023997\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=e8a8b4ae-b204-4bf3-8aa9-8fda128c1e35 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=8add03eb-2e54-4224-a134-d62e7a9b9b83 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} -->\\nP3: This changes the public cursor shape, but `mcpfn/core/README.md` still documents `mcpfn:<offset>` cursors. Update the package documentation to describe the opaque, operation/collection-bound cursor and its expiry behavior.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At mcpfn/core/src/server.ts, line 124:\\n\\n<comment>This changes the public cursor shape, but `mcpfn/core/README.md` still documents `mcpfn:<offset>` cursors. Update the package documentation to describe the opaque, operation/collection-bound cursor and its expiry behavior.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -109,7 +120,9 @@ function page<T>(\\n     values: selected,\\n-    ...(nextOffset < values.length ? { nextCursor: `mcpfn:${nextOffset}` } : {}),\\n+    ...(nextOffset < values.length\\n+      ? { nextCursor: `mcpfn:${operation}:${identity}:${nextOffset}` }\\n+      : {}),\\n   };\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYwNl\",\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/components/ActionButton.svelte\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:34:49Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:34:49Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836043479\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Consume the FileFn download descriptor in action results**\\n\\nWhen an operator runs either exposed FileFn download action, the response is shaped as `data.item.{url,headers}`, but this branch only looks for `data.downloadUrl`; moreover, every `ActionButton` caller leaves `openDownloadReceipt` at its default `false`. Fresh evidence in the current tree is that the read actions are now exposed and their descriptors are no longer redacted, but the UI still discards them and merely reports completion, so no download starts and provider-required headers cannot be applied.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYwNm\",\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:34:49Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:34:49Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836043481\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Encode scope components in memory-store keys**\\n\\nWhen scope identifiers contain `/`, distinct scopes can produce the same key—for example, installation/workspace pairs `a/b` + `c` and `a` + `b/c` are indistinguishable here. Admin scope validation permits such nonblank identifiers, so the memory store can list, retrieve, overwrite, or delete another scope's HostFn records; use an unambiguous tuple serialization rather than delimiter concatenation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYwNo\",\n      \"path\": \"apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 261,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:34:49Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:34:49Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836043483\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject credentials embedded in environment URLs**\\n\\nWhen `baseUrl` is an HTTP(S) URL such as `REDACTED`, this validation accepts it and persists `parsed.toString()`. Environment records are explicitly presented as non-secret endpoints and return `baseUrl` without redaction, so the embedded credential is exposed through list/get responses and the generic console; reject URLs with a nonempty `username` or `REDACTED` before storing them.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bY3RV\",\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:59:58Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:59:58Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836085089\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Decode policy IDs before dispatching updates**\\n\\nWhen a mutable policy ID requires URL encoding, such as `retention%20policy` or `team%2Fpolicy`, this passes the encoded segment directly to the configured operation as `input.id`. The operation therefore looks up the literal percent-encoded ID instead of the policy advertised by the settings service; decode the path parameter as is already done for operation IDs and module route parameters.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bY3RX\",\n      \"path\": \"uifn/theme/src/mount.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:59:58Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:59:58Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836085091\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject CSS syntax in theme scope selectors**\\n\\nWhen `scope` is derived from configuration or other non-constant input, the check accepts braces, semicolons, and comma-separated selectors. For example, `:root { color:red; } body` passes validation and is interpolated directly into the stylesheet, allowing injected CSS declarations rather than merely selecting a theme root; validate the scope as a single selector or reject CSS control characters before interpolation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bY_MR\",\n      \"path\": \"datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T13:27:17Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T13:27:17Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836131320\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Include relation names in generated IDs**\\n\\nWhen a valid schema defines multiple relations with the same endpoints and type but different `relation` or `inverse` names, this function assigns them identical IDs. The relations list then supplies duplicate keyed row IDs to the Super Console, and `getRelation` always returns the first match, making the other relation unaddressable; include the relation identity fields in the generated ID.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bY_MU\",\n      \"path\": \"searchfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 594,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T13:27:17Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T13:27:17Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836131324\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Expose document actions as collection actions**\\n\\nWhen SearchFn is operated through the generic Super Console, `documents` has no list or get operation (`domainReadResourceIds` excludes it), but `index` and `remove-document` are projected here as ID-bound resource actions. The module page only renders collection actions, while the non-listable documents resource has no reachable detail page, so both operations are unavailable in the UI; project these action-only operations as collection actions so their `id` inputs can be entered in the action form.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bZFMh\",\n      \"path\": \"filefn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 199,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T13:48:01Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T13:48:01Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836166999\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Make share-link creation replay-safe after audit failures**\\n\\nWhen `shares.createShareLink` succeeds but the required terminal audit write fails, `AdminDispatcher` returns a dependency error after the live share and its one-time plaintext token have already been created. Because this operation explicitly disables idempotency, a retry creates another share instead of recovering the first result; the first link remains active while its token is lost, and it cannot be revoked through this admin API because revocation requires that original token. Preserve the result behind an idempotency key or otherwise reconcile/revoke the created share on post-execution failure.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bZNZ3\",\n      \"path\": \"filefn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 367,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:13:41Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:13:41Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836215914\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=ae4eaeb5-91cc-4b8f-94ea-7038ebd9faab -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=de51d2b7-51be-4233-98de-40e1e764bc05 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP2: When a FileFn service returns `accepted: true` without `item.token`, this callback throws after the share was created and leaves the share active without durable cleanup. Require `item.token` for the create-share contract and provide a durable reconciliation path for responses that still omit it.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At filefn/admin/src/index.ts, line 367:\\n\\n<comment>When a FileFn service returns `accepted: true` without `item.token`, this callback throws after the share was created and leaves the share active without durable cleanup. Require `item.token` for the create-share contract and provide a durable reconciliation path for responses that still omit it.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -355,6 +355,19 @@ export function createFileFnAdminAdapter(service: FileFnAdminService): AdminCapa\\n+        const shareInput = input as CreateShareAdminInput;\\n+        const shareResult = result as AdminOperationResult<FileFnAdminOperationOutputMap[\\\"filefn.share-links.create-share\\\"]>;\\n+        const token = shareResult.data.item?.token;\\n+        if (!token) throw new Error(\\\"The created FileFn share token is unavailable for compensation.\\\");\\n+        await service.revokeShareLink({ fileId: shareInput.fileId, token }, context);\\n+      },\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bZNZ8\",\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/tests/ui/admin-api.test.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:13:41Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:13:41Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836215924\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=612d4e24-d6c2-4b12-94da-6f83bb135d6f -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=de51d2b7-51be-4233-98de-40e1e764bc05 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP2: Per the HTML spec and current Chrome/Firefox/Safari, `window.open(url, '_blank', 'noopener')` returns null because the `noopener` feature is set. The mock makes it return `{ opener: window }`, so it asserts the opposite of the real browser contract: in production `popup` is always null, `openSafeAdminDownload` returns false, `openSafeAdminDownloadReceipt` resolves false, and ActionButton.svelte throws 'The download receipt did not contain a trusted URL.' after every successful download. Model the real contract (mock `window.open` to return null) and change the implementation so a null result from a noopener open is not treated as failure; the `popup.opener = null` branch is dead code in real browsers.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/tests/ui/admin-api.test.ts, line 192:\\n\\n<comment>Per the HTML spec and current Chrome/Firefox/Safari, `window.open(url, '_blank', 'noopener')` returns null because the `noopener` feature is set. The mock makes it return `{ opener: window }`, so it asserts the opposite of the real browser contract: in production `popup` is always null, `openSafeAdminDownload` returns false, `openSafeAdminDownloadReceipt` resolves false, and ActionButton.svelte throws 'The download receipt did not contain a trusted URL.' after every successful download. Model the real contract (mock `window.open` to return null) and change the implementation so a null result from a noopener open is not treated as failure; the `popup.opener = null` branch is dead code in real browsers.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -188,6 +188,24 @@ describe('administration API boundary', () => {\\n   });\\n \\n+  it('opens a header-free signed download receipt', async () => {\\n+    const popup = { opener: window } as unknown as Window;\\n+    const open = vi.spyOn(window, 'open').mockReturnValue(popup);\\n+    try {\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bZNjX\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836216783\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Canonicalize scopes before forming idempotency identities**\\n\\nWhen the same operation, actor, and idempotency key are first dispatched with `{ organizationId: \\\"tenant\\\" }` and then with `{ installationId: \\\"tenant\\\" }`, scope validation treats both forms as the same installation, but this raw scope object produces two different storage identities. The second request therefore acquires a new claim and executes the supposedly idempotent mutation again; normalize the deprecated alias to a single canonical scope representation before constructing the identity.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bZNjY\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 97,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836216785\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject non-finite JSON numbers**\\n\\nWhen a direct dispatcher caller supplies, or an adapter returns, `NaN` or either infinity under a schema declaring `type: \\\"number\\\"`, `valueType` classifies it as a valid number. The dispatcher consequently accepts the value, while JSON serialization changes it to `null`, so clients receive data that no longer satisfies the declared output schema; non-finite numbers should fail validation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bZNjZ\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 272,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836216788\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Require schema properties to be owned by the input**\\n\\nWhen an input has a custom prototype containing a required field, this `in` check accepts the inherited value even though the subsequent `Object.entries` traversal never validates it. This is reachable through the module HTTP transport because assigning a parsed `{\\\"__proto__\\\": {...}}` body changes the accumulator's prototype; the dispatcher then clones away that prototype and invokes the adapter with the required field missing instead of rejecting the request. Check required fields with `Object.hasOwn`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bZV7R\",\n      \"path\": \"uifn/theme/src/mount.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 96,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:40:01Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:40:01Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836266338\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Validate token values before interpolating CSS**\\n\\nWhen a custom runtime theme contains CSS control syntax in a string-valued token, such as a dimension value of `1px;}body{display:none`, this interpolation lets the value escape its custom-property declaration and inject arbitrary rules into the generated stylesheet. `themeToCSS` accepts `DesignTokenTheme` directly without validation, and the token validator only checks that non-number values are strings, so validate each token's CSS grammar or reject control syntax before composing the stylesheet.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bZV7U\",\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:40:01Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:40:01Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836266343\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Detect blocked download windows**\\n\\nWhen a browser blocks popups, `window.open` returns `null`, but this helper discards that result and reports success. Fresh evidence is that the receipt is now consumed, but `ActionButton` only reaches this call after awaiting the administration request, by which time strict browsers commonly no longer consider it part of the initiating click; the download can therefore remain unopened while the UI reports completion. Pre-open a window during the click or treat a null return as failure and provide a direct navigation fallback.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6baJcm\",\n      \"path\": \"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 357,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T17:16:45Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T17:16:45Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836570650\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Filter connection lists by exact tenant identity**\\n\\nWhen the identity mapper returns a tenantless identity (`tenantId` is undefined), this passes an owner with an undefined tenant to `connections.list`; PlugFn's `ConnectionStorage.listByOwner` omits the tenant predicate when that value is absent, so connections for the same user or organization in every tenant are returned and mapped without an `assertConnectionOwner` check. This leaks cross-tenant connection names, scopes, and status through the list operation even though the corresponding detail operation rejects those records; post-filter the results using the exact tenant/owner checks or make the storage query distinguish tenantless records.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6baKc5\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/idempotency.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 25,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T17:19:51Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-22T17:19:51Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836576637\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=e4d0a90a-8a2e-48b8-9fa7-873371ab35cd -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=5275fc5a-473b-448f-902e-ead0ba012162 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: When a required-audit idempotent mutation loses its terminal sink acknowledgement, replay redelivers the stable event ID without the original policy metadata. Persist the metadata in the pending audit marker before `writeAudit` so reconciliation reproduces the terminal event shape.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/idempotency.ts, line 25:\\n\\n<comment>When a required-audit idempotent mutation loses its terminal sink acknowledgement, replay redelivers the stable event ID without the original policy metadata. Persist the metadata in the pending audit marker before `writeAudit` so reconciliation reproduces the terminal event shape.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -19,6 +19,10 @@ export interface AdminIdempotencyRecord<T = unknown> {\\n+    /** Terminal event shape to redeliver when a sink acknowledgement is lost. */\\n+    outcome?: \\\"succeeded\\\" | \\\"failed\\\";\\n+    errorCode?: string;\\n+    metadata?: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>>;\\n     updatedAt: string;\\n   };\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bc5vd\",\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T03:26:35Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-23T03:26:35Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837613144\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile attached domains when persistence fails**\\n\\nWhen the provider successfully attaches the domain but `putDomain` rejects, this operation returns an error while leaving a live domain with no corresponding store record. The failed idempotent invocation is then fenced as an error, and retrying with a new key can attach a duplicate; meanwhile the console cannot discover or detach the original domain. Persist a durable pending intent before calling the executor, or compensate the provider attachment when the final write fails.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bc5vf\",\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T03:26:35Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-23T03:26:35Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837613146\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Make confirmation issuance recoverable after audit failures**\\n\\nWhen `performConfirmOperation` successfully creates a valid confirmation token but this terminal audit write fails, the endpoint returns an error and discards the only receipt while the token remains live and the audit trail contains only the attempted event. Retrying issues another token, so a transient sink failure accumulates valid, unreturned credentials without a successful issuance record; make issuance replay-safe or revoke/reconcile the issued token before returning the failure.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdRKH\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T05:06:53Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-23T05:06:53Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837750217\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Compare object-valued enum members structurally**\\n\\nWhen an operation schema declares an object or array in `enum`, JSON-decoded input that is structurally identical is rejected because `Object.is` compares those values by reference. `AdminJsonSchema` permits arbitrary enum values and manifest validation does not restrict them to scalars, so such a valid schema becomes unusable through REST or MCP; compare enum members using JSON structural equality instead.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdgrD\",\n      \"path\": \"filefn/server/src/index.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T06:10:24Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-23T06:10:24Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837842304\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restrict the public processing service to authorized methods**\\n\\nWhen an application exposes this newly public service through an in-process integration, callers can invoke `processing.listArtifacts(fileId, ctx)` directly even though that method explicitly ignores `ctx` and queries all artifacts for the file; only `listArtifactsForFile` calls `requireReadableFile`. Publishing the full `ProcessingService` therefore bypasses the authorization enforced by both the HTTP routes and the admin adapter, so expose an authorization-safe facade or keep the worker-level methods private.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdgrE\",\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T06:10:24Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-23T06:10:24Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837842305\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Resolve composed schemas before deciding an action has no fields**\\n\\nWhen a valid operation input schema declares its named properties through `allOf`, this returns no editable fields because only top-level `properties` is inspected. The generic action then either submits `{}` immediately or shows a dialog without the required controls, so operations using a schema composition accepted by the manifest validator cannot be invoked from Super Console; merge compatible `allOf` object properties and requirements before constructing the fields.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdoWJ\",\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T06:40:38Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-23T06:40:38Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837887588\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile variable records after provider deletion**\\n\\nWhen the provider deletion succeeds but `store.deleteVariable` rejects, the stale variable record remains while this request returns an error. Retrying with the same idempotency key replays that error, and retrying with a new key can still never remove the record when the provider reports that the already-deleted variable is not found, because this path does not tolerate provider-not-found as `detachDomain` does. Treat an already-absent provider variable as success or persist a deletion intent so the store record can be reconciled.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_i\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 268,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991044\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject non-plain objects as JSON values**\\n\\nWhen an in-process dispatcher caller supplies a `Date`, `Map`, or other class instance under `type: \\\"object\\\"`, this branch accepts it as a valid JSON object because it never checks the prototype. The immutable snapshot preserves such instances, and output redaction converts them through `Object.entries`—for example, a valid-looking `Date` response becomes `{}`—so adapters can receive or return values that change shape at transport time; require arrays or plain/null-prototype objects throughout JSON validation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_l\",\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991047\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Compare action enum objects structurally**\\n\\nWhen an action field declares an object or array in `enum` or `const`, the form parses the operator's JSON into a new object and these `Object.is` checks always reject it by reference, even when it is structurally identical to the declared value. The administration validator permits these JSON-valued members, so such operations pass manifest validation but cannot be submitted through the generic action UI; use the same structural JSON equality semantics as the runtime validator.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_n\",\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 461,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991049\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile variables when metadata persistence fails**\\n\\nWhen `executor.setVariable` succeeds for a new variable but this store write rejects, the provider retains the live secret while the operator returns an error and has no record through which to list or delete it. A retry is not guaranteed safe because `setVariable` has no idempotency contract; persist a durable intent before the provider call or compensate/reconcile the provider variable if final persistence fails.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd9cQ\",\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/README.md\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:54:06Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:54:07Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838010605\",\n          \"body\": \"This rule can reactivate a confirmation that Super Console has already denied: if `activate()` fails and `revoke()` also fails, the earlier bound success audit remains, so reconciliation follows this branch despite the later denied audit and 503 response. Make durable cancellation or denial take precedence over the prepared success before returning the failure.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Confirmation reconciliation can override a denied outcome\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `superconsole/README.md:55-62` — directs reconciliation to activate whenever the bound success audit exists.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1108-1142` — records denial and returns 503 after activation failure, but suppresses revocation failure.\\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/types.ts:179-204` — defines durable preparation and revocation without a durable denied/cancelled precedence signal.\\n- `superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts:783-828` — covers only successful revocation after activation failure.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Once issuance returns an activation failure and records denial, provider reconciliation must not later make that staged token verifiable.\\n- Cover simultaneous activation and revocation failure followed by reconciliation.\\n````\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beVvV\",\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 230,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:16:56Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:16:56Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838155807\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=aee689c8-aa40-4c1e-90bd-f3790b287173 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=2c758959-78c0-46f1-bcb1-33373d5c1906 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP1: When a pending domain is detached while attachment is in flight, the unchanged claim remains valid after deletion and this completion recreates the domain. Revoke the claim atomically with deletion and require the claimed record to still exist before persisting the terminal state.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts, line 230:\\n\\n<comment>When a pending domain is detached while attachment is in flight, the unchanged claim remains valid after deletion and this completion recreates the domain. Revoke the claim atomically with deletion and require the claimed record to still exist before persisting the terminal state.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -222,6 +224,13 @@ export class MemoryHostFnOperatorStore implements HostFnOperatorStore {\\n+  async completeDomainAttachment(domain: HostFnDomain, claimToken: string) {\\n+    const key = this.key(domain.scope, domain.id);\\n+    if (this.domainAttachmentClaims.get(key) !== claimToken) return false;\\n+    this.domains.set(key, structuredClone(domain));\\n+    this.domainAttachmentClaims.delete(key);\\n+    return true;\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beVvX\",\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 826,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:16:56Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:16:56Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838155809\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=4657c4fd-9b79-4e88-b603-7ef700cbbd32 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=2c758959-78c0-46f1-bcb1-33373d5c1906 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP3: The deny-path assertion uses `expect.any(String)` for `denialAuditId`, so nothing verifies that the auditId passed to `cancelActivation` matches the id of the 'denied' audit event actually written. That link is the integrity point of the new cancelActivation contract, and the preceding test in this file already validates the identical linkage for the success path (deriving `successAuditId` from `audit.events.find(...)?.id` and asserting `prepareActivation`/`activate` receive it). Capture the denied event's id in the audit mock and assert `cancelActivation` receives exactly that id, e.g. `expect(cancelActivation).toHaveBeenCalledWith(expect.objectContaining({ token: 'staged-token', auditId: expect.any(String), denialAuditId: deniedEventId }))`.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts, line 826:\\n\\n<comment>The deny-path assertion uses `expect.any(String)` for `denialAuditId`, so nothing verifies that the auditId passed to `cancelActivation` matches the id of the 'denied' audit event actually written. That link is the integrity point of the new cancelActivation contract, and the preceding test in this file already validates the identical linkage for the success path (deriving `successAuditId` from `audit.events.find(...)?.id` and asserting `prepareActivation`/`activate` receive it). Capture the denied event's id in the audit mock and assert `cancelActivation` receives exactly that id, e.g. `expect(cancelActivation).toHaveBeenCalledWith(expect.objectContaining({ token: 'staged-token', auditId: expect.any(String), denialAuditId: deniedEventId }))`.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -818,7 +822,12 @@ describe('Super Console server composition', () => {\\n     expect(response.status).toBe(503);\\n-    expect(await verify({} as never)).toBe(false);\\n+    expect(await verify()).toBe(false);\\n+    expect(cancelActivation).toHaveBeenCalledWith(expect.objectContaining({\\n+      token: 'staged-token',\\n+      auditId: expect.any(String),\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIN\",\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 395,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158128\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Expose create and upsert operations before a record exists**\\n\\nWhen an ID-targeted operation can create a new record, this classifies it exclusively as a detail-page action, while module-level actions accept only collection targets or resources with no list/detail route. Consequently operations such as `botfn.bots.upsert`, `botfn.channels.connect`, `apifn.specs.register`, and `apifn.environments.upsert` are only reachable after navigating to an existing record whose ID is then prebound; an empty collection has no console path for creating its first record. Project these creation/upsert operations as collection actions while leaving their ID fields editable.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIQ\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 131,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158131\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject non-JSON primitive leaves in open schemas**\\n\\nWhen an adapter returns a `bigint` under a type-less or `additionalProperties: true` child schema, validation accepts it because only object prototypes and non-finite numbers are rejected. Fresh evidence after the plain-object fix is that the new guards still omit `bigint`, `symbol`, `function`, and `undefined`; the open entity schemas used by DataFn, BillFn, and SearchFn therefore allow values that cannot be represented by the REST/MCP envelopes, with a `bigint` causing the subsequent `JSON.stringify` to throw instead of producing the validated result. Reject every primitive type outside the JSON value set even when the schema omits `type`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIS\",\n      \"path\": \"botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 154,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158133\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind BotFn cursors to their collection query**\\n\\nWhen a channels cursor issued for `botId=A` is reused with `botId=B`, or a cursor from the bots list is supplied to the channels list, this shared parser accepts the raw offset and slices the unrelated result set from that position. The same cursor can also be reused in another authorized scope, yielding skipped or empty pages there; encode the operation, scope, and channel filter identity into the cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIT\",\n      \"path\": \"apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 160,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158134\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind ApiFn cursors to their resource and scope**\\n\\nWhen the offset returned by `listSpecs` is supplied to `listEnvironments`, or reused after switching to another authorized scope, this parser accepts it unchanged and skips that many unrelated records. Because the helper emits only a decimal offset for both collections, clients cannot distinguish these invalid cursor uses; include the operation and active scope in an opaque cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"snapshot_dir=/tmp/pr116-review-round.D4x5iZ\n{\n  \"number\": 116,\n  \"state\": \"OPEN\",\n  \"headRefName\": \"SFNS-2\",\n  \"headRefOid\": \"2011d9c67048f2e1eb7221edaca7d6d36568a019\",\n  \"baseRefName\": \"dev\",\n  \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:20:42Z\",\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116\",\n  \"reviews\": 123,\n  \"issueComments\": 7\n}\n{\n  \"unresolvedCount\": 141,\n  \"threads\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bNtar\",\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/components/resource-pages.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 87,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"github-advanced-security\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-21T15:59:22Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-21T15:59:23Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831736417\",\n          \"body\": \"## CodeQL / Prototype-polluting function\\n\\nThe property chain [segment](1) is recursively assigned to [current](2) without guarding against prototype pollution.\\n\\n[Show more details](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/security/code-scanning/49)\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bNv6J\",\n      \"path\": \"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-21T16:01:33Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-21T16:01:33Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831751943\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve numeric-looking string document IDs**\\n\\nFor a composite target such as `orders:001`, this converts the document ID from the string `\\\"001\\\"` to the number `1`. Single-document indexing therefore targets a different ID than batch indexing, which preserves string IDs, and `remove-document` can delete numeric document `1` instead of string document `\\\"001\\\"`. Preserve the ID suffix as a string or carry explicit ID-type information in the input.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bNv6M\",\n      \"path\": \"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"isOutdated\": true,\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-21T16:01:33Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-21T16:01:33Z\",\n          \"outdated\": true,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831751947\",\n          \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Apply the declared index-list query parameters**\\n\\nWhen an installation has many configured indexes or the console supplies search/filter/pagination input, `listIndexes` ignores the entire input and always returns every index with `nextCursor: null`. This contradicts the operation's cursor-pagination declaration and makes the resource-list search UI return unrelated entries while bypassing the declared 200-item maximum; honor `limit`, `cursor`, and the advertised query fields before building the result.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bODiX\",\n      \"path\": \"uifn/core/scripts/build.mjs\",\n      \"isOutdated\": false,\n      \"line\": 47,\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-21T16:19:44Z\",\n          \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-21T16:19:48Z\",\n          \"outdated\": false,\n          \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831870338\",\n          \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=1e8a9759-bd72-4e24-bd8c-217d1bba06d6 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=7bb8304f-392d-4952-ab05-eaf35f279889 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} -->\\nP1: When the build reaches `accordion`, it asks tsup to bundle nonexistent `createAccordionController`, so the build fails before producing any public primitive entrypoints. Add the missing c