ant cannot be established. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXL9M | plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts:199 | outdated=true\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-22T06:54:29Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835445399\n  **<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject tenant-unverifiable webhook receipts** For a legacy receipt without `connectionId`, this fallback authorizes solely by `ownerKind` and `ownerId`, even though the active identity is tenant-scoped and the receipt carries no tenant field. If user or organization IDs overlap across tenants, knowing a foreign receipt ID lets an operator read its receipt metadata and list its delivery status and errors. Require a tenant-verifiable connection or other tenant-bound provenance instead of accepting the legacy owner match. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXaG9 | datafn/admin/src/index.ts:502 | outdated=false\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-22T07:39:29Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835531565\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Supply a resource selector before exposing Records** When an operator opens the DataFn Records card in Super Console, the generated list request contains no `filter`, because this resource declares neither presentation filters nor a parent binding. Requiring `filter` here therefore makes the default Records route fail validation on every visit, leaving record browsing unusable unless the operator manually constructs a JSON query parameter; add a control/binding for `filter.resource` or stop advertising this as a standalone list. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXaG- | filefn/admin/src/index.ts:37 | outdated=true\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-22T07:39:29Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835531568\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Mark file-bound collections as non-standalone** Opening Versions from the FileFn module page invokes `filefn.versions.list` without the required `fileId`; Grants, Share Links, and Artifacts have the same problem. These resources omit `presentation.parent` and consequently default to `standaloneList: true`, so the console advertises cards that only return input-validation errors and cannot generate related links from a file detail page; declare their file-parent bindings and disable standalone listing. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXaHA | filefn/admin/src/index.ts:198 | outdated=true\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-22T07:39:29Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835531570\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Do not bind share revocation to the hash prefix** For each listed share link, the generic row-action binder uses the resource identity (`tokenHashPrefix`) as this operation's `token` input and hides that target field from the form. The operator therefore cannot supply the required original plaintext token, and every displayed Revoke Share action confirms and submits the hash prefix instead, so it cannot revoke the selected link; avoid projecting this as an identity-bound row action or provide an independently editable plaintext-token input. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXbFH | plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts:138 | outdated=true\n  [pullfrog 2026-08-22T07:43:02Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835537182\n  [P1] Derive workflow tenant ownership from an authoritative field. `WorkflowEngine.create()` and `AdapterWorkflowStorage.create()` persist caller-provided `metadata` unchanged, and no core producer reserves or populates this key. As a result, ordinary/legacy workflows are hidden from administration, while any application path that accepts workflow metadata can forge the value used here for isolation. Add a first-class tenant owner populated from authenticated context (or verify through another authoritative relation) rather than treating generic metadata as authorization provenance.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXbFK | uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs:264 | outdated=true\n  [pullfrog 2026-08-22T07:43:02Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835537185\n  [P1] Validate the expected action outcome rather than any activity. The vectors declare action names and callback names but no expected post-state, callback arguments, or DOM semantics, so changing an unrelated state key or invoking a callback with the wrong payload makes `observed` true; line 380 then reports `passed`, and the Svelte test only asserts that result. Encode and compare expected state/callback effects so behaviorally incorrect adapters cannot satisfy the parity gate.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXfQZ | mcpfn/core/src/registry.ts:196 | outdated=false\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-22T07:57:05Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835561789\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject duplicate resource-template URI patterns** When two templates have different names but the same `uriTemplate`, this name-only duplicate check accepts both and advertises both from `resources/templates/list`. However, `matchResource` resolves by iterating the templates and returns the first URI match, so the later template's `read`, subscription, and completion behavior is unreachable. Reject duplicate `uriTemplate` values at registration time. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXfQa | hostfn/admin/src/index.ts:738 | outdated=false\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-22T07:57:05Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#disc