ion has many configured indexes or the console supplies search/filter/pagination input, `listIndexes` ignores the entire input and always returns every index with `nextCursor: null`. This contradicts the operation's cursor-pagination declaration and makes the resource-list search UI return unrelated entries while bypassing the declared 200-item maximum; honor `limit`, `cursor`, and the advertised query fields before building the result. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bODiX | uifn/core/scripts/build.mjs:47 | outdated=false\n  [cubic-dev-ai 2026-08-21T16:19:44Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831870338\n  <!-- cubic:v=1e8a9759-bd72-4e24-bd8c-217d1bba06d6 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=7bb8304f-392d-4952-ab05-eaf35f279889 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":10} --> P1: When the build reaches `accordion`, it asks tsup to bundle nonexistent `createAccordionController`, so the build fails before producing any public primitive entrypoints. Add the missing controller exports or map catalog entries to verified source exports before bundling. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/core/scripts/build.mjs, line 24: <comment>When the build reaches `accordion`, it asks tsup to bundle nonexistent `createAccordionController`, so the build fails before producing any public primitive entrypoints. Add the missing controller exports or map catalog entries to verified source exports before bundling.</comment> <file context> @@ -0,0 +1,89 @@ +        ? 'CreateHoverCardProps' +        : `${primitive.name}Props`, +      runtime: interactive +        ? `create${primitive.name}Controller` +        : `${primitive.name}Contract`, +      secondaryType: interactive </file context> ``` </details>\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bODib | superconsole/src/routes/audit/+page.ts:12 | outdated=true\n  [cubic-dev-ai 2026-08-21T16:19:44Z outdated=tr