g `nextCursor`, causing an otherwise successful list request to fail. Admin scope validation permits arbitrary nonblank Unicode strings, so encode the JSON as UTF-8 bytes before base64 encoding and reverse that transformation when decoding. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXkIS | filefn/admin/src/index.ts:185 | outdated=true\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-22T08:13:59Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835590707\n  **<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Return usable FileFn download descriptors** When either download operation is invoked through the dispatcher, declaring `url` and `headers` as output fields causes `redactAdminOutputValue` to replace the signed URL and any required headers with `\"[REDACTED]\"`. The REST, MCP, and typed SDK responses therefore cannot be used to download the file; the artifact download declaration has the same defect. Return a provider-safe descriptor instead of redacting the fields that constitute the operation's result. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXkIX | packages/admin/src/openapi.ts:151 | outdated=true\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-22T08:13:59Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835590713\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Include CSRF metadata for POST read operations** For a read-classified operation that uses an unsafe HTTP method, such as `apifn.specs.compare` (`POST`), `SuperConsole.handle` still calls `authorizeMutation` based on the request method, so cookie-authenticated AuthFn requests require the provider CSRF header. This classification check omits that header from OpenAPI, causing generated clients or API-console requests that follow the document to receive a CSRF 403; determine CSRF metadata from the HTTP method instead. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXvK