ed=true\n  [pullfrog 2026-08-22T08:53:03Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835657402\n  The manifest contract permits a `GET` route classified as a mutation, and Super Console explicitly sends that case through `authorizeMutation`; AuthFn then requires CSRF for cookie credentials. This method-only condition removes the provider header from that operation's OpenAPI contract, so generated cookie clients can follow the contract and still be rejected. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # CSRF projection diverges for safe-method mutations ## Affected sites - `packages/admin/src/openapi.ts:151` — projects the CSRF header only from the HTTP method. - `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1213-1215` — invokes `authorizeMutation` for non-read operations using safe methods. - `authfn/core/src/index.ts:166-175` — enforces CSRF whenever cookie credentials authorize a mutation. ## Required outcome - Project provider CSRF metadata for every operation that can reach `authorizeMutation`, including both POST reads and GET mutations. - Add projection coverage for a GET operation with non-read classification. ```` </details>\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bX1GN | botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts:241 | outdated=false\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-22T09:14:07Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835691127\n  **<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Make bot deletion and channel connection atomic** When `connectChannel` and `deleteBot` run concurrently, the connect path can observe the bot here, then the delete path can observe no channels and delete it, after which the connect path persists a channel for the now-missing bot. Because the store contract exposes only these separate reads and writes, even the supplied memory implementation permits an orphaned active external binding; enforce the bot-exists/channel-empty in