e request returns an error while subsequent deployment lists continue reporting a job that will never run, so persist a terminal/unknown outcome or otherwise reconcile the record on executor failure. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYgUY | hostfn/admin/src/index.ts:729 | outdated=false\n  [pullfrog 2026-08-22T11:49:44Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835946128\n  Distinct accepted IDs can compare equal under `localeCompare`, for example composed `é` and decomposed `e\\u0301`. When timestamps tie and the backing store changes their input order between requests, offset slicing can duplicate one record and omit another, so this needs a locale-independent total tie-breaker. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # HostFn pagination lacks a total tie-breaker ## Affected sites - `hostfn/admin/src/index.ts:724-729` — the final comparison can return zero for distinct IDs accepted by the manifest. - `hostfn/admin/src/__tests__/admin.test.ts:160-201` — the reordering regression covers only ASCII IDs whose comparisons are nonzero. ## Required outcome - Define a strict, locale-independent total order for every accepted HostFn ID before applying an offset cursor. - Cover distinct equal-collation IDs under a store that changes result order between page requests. ```` </details>\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYmrU | mcpfn/core/src/server.ts:104 | outdated=true\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-22T12:01:56Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835986662\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind MCP cursors to the list operation** When a cursor returned by `tools/list` is supplied to `prompts/list`, `resources/list`, or `resources/templates/list`, this shared decoder accepts it as the same raw offset and skips entries in the unrelated collection; the same problem occurs when a visibility-dependent tools/re