rovider successfully attaches the domain but `putDomain` rejects, this operation returns an error while leaving a live domain with no corresponding store record. The failed idempotent invocation is then fenced as an error, and retrying with a new key can attach a duplicate; meanwhile the console cannot discover or detach the original domain. Persist a durable pending intent before calling the executor, or compensate the provider attachment when the final write fails. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bc5vf | superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1062 | outdated=true\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T03:26:35Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837613146\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Make confirmation issuance recoverable after audit failures** When `performConfirmOperation` successfully creates a valid confirmation token but this terminal audit write fails, the endpoint returns an error and discards the only receipt while the token remains live and the audit trail contains only the attempted event. Retrying issues another token, so a transient sink failure accumulates valid, unreturned credentials without a successful issuance record; make issuance replay-safe or revoke/reconcile the issued token before returning the failure. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdRKH | packages/admin/src/validator.ts:86 | outdated=true\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T05:06:53Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837750217\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Compare object-valued enum members structurally** When an operation schema declares an object or array in `enum`, JSON-decoded input that is structurally identical is rejected because `Object.is` compares those values by reference. `AdminJsonSchema` permits arbitrary enum values a