React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdoWJ | hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:414 | outdated=true\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T06:40:38Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837887588\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile variable records after provider deletion** When the provider deletion succeeds but `store.deleteVariable` rejects, the stale variable record remains while this request returns an error. Retrying with the same idempotency key replays that error, and retrying with a new key can still never remove the record when the provider reports that the already-deleted variable is not found, because this path does not tolerate provider-not-found as `detachDomain` does. Treat an already-absent provider variable as success or persist a deletion intent so the store record can be reconciled. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_i | packages/admin/src/validator.ts:268 | outdated=false\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T07:44:38Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991044\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject non-plain objects as JSON values** When an in-process dispatcher caller supplies a `Date`, `Map`, or other class instance under `type: \"object\"`, this branch accepts it as a valid JSON object because it never checks the prototype. The immutable snapshot preserves such instances, and output redaction converts them through `Object.entries`—for example, a valid-looking `Date` response becomes `{}`—so adapters can receive or return values that change shape at transport time; require arrays or plain/null-prototype objects throughout JSON validation. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_l | superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts:105 | outdated=true\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T07:44:38Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991047\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Compare action enum objects structurally** When an action field declares an object or array in `enum` or `const`, the form parses the operator's JSON into a new object and these `Object.is` checks always reject it by reference, even when it is structurally identical to the declared value. The administration validator permits these JSON-valued members, so such operations pass manifest validation but cannot be submitted through the generic action UI; use the same structural JSON equality semantics as the runtime validator. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_n | hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:461 | outdated=false\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T07:44:38Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991049\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile variables when metadata persistence fails** When `executor.setVariable` succeeds for a new variable but this store write rejects, the provider retains the live secret while the operator returns an error and has no record through which to list or delete it. A retry is not guaranteed safe because `setVariable` has no idempotency contract; persist a durable intent before the provider call or compensate/reconcile the provider variable if final persistence fails. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd9cQ | superconsole/README.md:59 | outdated=true\n  [pullfrog 2026-08-23T07:54:06Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838010605\n  This rule can reactivate a confirmation that Super Console has already denied: if `activate()` fails and `revoke()` also fails, the earlier bound success audit remains, so reconciliation follows this branch despite the later denied audit and 503 response. Make durable cancellation or denial take precedence over the prepared success before returning the failure. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Confirmation reconciliation can override a denied outcome ## Affected sites - `superconsole/README.md:55-62` — directs reconciliation to activate whenever the bound success audit exists. - `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1108-1142` — records denial and returns 503 after activation failure, but suppresses revocation failure. - `superconsole/src/lib/server/types.ts:179-204` — defines durable preparation and revocation without a durable denied/cancelled precedence signal. - `superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts:783-828` — covers only successful revocation after activation failure. ## Required outcome - Once issuance returns an activation failure and records denial, provider reconciliation must not later make that staged token verifiable. - Cov\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beVvV | hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:230 | outdated=false\n  [cubic-dev-ai 2026-08-23T09:16:56Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838155807\n  <!-- cubic:v=aee689c8-aa40-4c1e-90bd-f3790b287173 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=2c758959-78c0-46f1-bcb1-33373d5c1906 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} --> P1: When a pending domain is detached while attachment is in flight, the unchanged claim remains valid after deletion and this completion recreates the domain. Revoke the claim atomically with deletion and require the claimed record to still exist before persisting the terminal state. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts, line 230: <comment>When a pending domain is detached while attachment is in flight, the unchanged claim remains valid after deletion and this completion recreates the domain. Revoke the claim atomically with deletion and require the claimed re