l/116#discussion_r3838158128\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Expose create and upsert operations before a record exists** When an ID-targeted operation can create a new record, this classifies it exclusively as a detail-page action, while module-level actions accept only collection targets or resources with no list/detail route. Consequently operations such as `botfn.bots.upsert`, `botfn.channels.connect`, `apifn.specs.register`, and `apifn.environments.upsert` are only reachable after navigating to an existing record whose ID is then prebound; an empty collection has no console path for creating its first record. Project these creation/upsert operations as collection actions while leaving their ID fields editable. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIQ | packages/admin/src/validator.ts:131 | outdated=false\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T09:18:13Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158131\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject non-JSON primitive leaves in open schemas** When an adapter returns a `bigint` under a type-less or `additionalProperties: true` child schema, validation accepts it because only object prototypes and non-finite numbers are rejected. Fresh evidence after the plain-object fix is that the new guards still omit `bigint`, `symbol`, `function`, and `undefined`; the open entity schemas used by DataFn, BillFn, and SearchFn therefore allow values that cannot be represented by the REST/MCP envelopes, with a `bigint` causing the subsequent `JSON.stringify` to throw instead of producing the validated result. Reject every primitive type outside the JSON value set even when the schema omits `type`. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIS | botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts:154 | outdated=false\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T09:18:13Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158133\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind BotFn cursors to their collection query** When a channels cursor issued for `botId=A` is reused with `botId=B`, or a cursor from the bots list is supplied to the channels list, this shared parser accepts the raw offset and slices the unrelated result set from that position. The same cursor can also be reused in another authorized scope, yielding skipped or empty pages there; encode the operation, scope, and channel filter identity into the cursor and reject mismatches. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIT | apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts:160 | outdated=false\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T09:18:13Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158134\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind ApiFn cursors to their resource and scope** When the offset returned by `listSpecs` is supplied to `listEnvironments`, or reused after switching to another authorized scope, this parser accepts it unchanged and skips that many unrelated records. Because the helper emits only a decimal offset for both collections, clients cannot distinguish these invalid cursor uses; include the operation and active scope in an opaque cursor and reject mismatches. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10792},"formatted_output":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 40714)\nTotal output lines: 844\n\n{\n  \"number\": 116,\n  \"state\": \"OPEN\",\n  \"headRefName\": \"SFNS-2\",\n  \"headRefOid\": \"2011d9c67048f2e1eb7221edaca7d6d36568a019\",\n  \"baseRefName\": \"dev\",\n  \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:20:42Z\",\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116\",\n  \"reviews\": 123,\n  \"issueComments\": 7\n}\n{\n  \"unresolvedCount\": 141