d the root cause and fix it. At uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts, line 18: <comment>When collation-equivalent text uses combining marks or expansions, `startsWith` and `includes` slice by code-point count and compare the wrong window. Match over collation-element boundaries or candidate string boundaries instead of using `normalizedQuery.length`.</comment> <file context> @@ -0,0 +…30714 tokens truncated…-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836266338\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Validate token values before interpolating CSS** When a custom runtime theme contains CSS control syntax in a string-valued token, such as a dimension value of `1px;}body{display:none`, this interpolation lets the value escape its custom-property declaration and inject arbitrary rules into the generated stylesheet. `themeToCSS` accepts `DesignTokenTheme` directly without validation, and the token validator only checks that non-number values are strings, so validate each token's CSS grammar or reject control syntax before composing the stylesheet. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bZV7U | superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts:271 | outdated=true\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-22T14:40:01Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836266343\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Detect blocked download windows** When a browser blocks popups, `window.open` returns `null`, but this helper discards that result and reports success. Fresh evidence is that the receipt is now consumed, but `ActionButton` only reaches this call after awaiting the administration request, by which time strict browsers commonly no longer consider it part of the initiating click; the download can therefore remain unopened while the UI reports completion. Pre-open a window during the click or treat a null return as failure and provide a direct navigation fallback. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6baJcm | plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts:357 | outdated=false\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-22T17:16:45Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836570650\n  **<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Filter connection lists by exact tenant identity** When the identity mapper returns a tenantless identity (`tenantId` is undefined), this passes an owner with an undefined tenant to `connections.list`; PlugFn's `ConnectionStorage.listByOwner` omits the tenant predicate when that value is absent, so connections for the same user or organization in every tenant are returned and mapped without an `assertConnectionOwner` check. This leaks cross-tenant connection names, scopes, and status through the list operation even though the corresponding detail operation rejects those records; post-filter the results using the exact tenant/owner checks or make the storage query distinguish tenantless records. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6baKc5 | packages/admin/src/idempotency.ts:25 | outdated=false\n  [cubic-dev-ai 2026-08-22T17:19:51Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836576637\n  <!-- cubic:v=e4d0a90a-8a2e-48b8-9fa7-873371ab35cd --> <!-- cubic:review-run=5275fc5a-473b-448f-902e-ead0ba012162 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} --> P2: When a required-audit idempotent mutation loses its terminal sink acknowledgement, replay redelivers the stable event ID without the original policy metadata. Persist the metadata in the pending audit marker before `writeAudit` so reconciliation reproduces the terminal event shape. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/idempotency.ts, line 25: <comment>When a required-audit idempotent mutation loses its terminal sink acknowledgement, replay redelivers the stable event ID without the original policy metadata. Persist the metadata in the pending audit marker before `writeAudit` so reconciliation reproduces the terminal event shape.</comment> <file context> @@ -19,6 +19,10 @@ export interface AdminIdempotencyRecord<T = unknown> { +    /** Terminal event shape to redeliver when a sink acknowledgement is lost. */ +    outcome?: \"succeeded\" | \"failed\"; +    errorCode?: string; +    metadata?: Readonly<Record<string, un\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bc5vd | hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:299 | outdated=true\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T03:26:35Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837613144\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile attached domains when persistence fails** When the provider successfully attaches the domain but `putDomain` rejects, this operation returns an error while leaving a live domain with no corresponding store record. The failed idempotent invocation is then fenced as an error, and retrying with a new key can attach a duplicate; meanwhile the console cannot discover or detach the original domain. Persist a durable pending intent before calling the executor, or compensate the provider attachment when the final write fails. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bc5vf | superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1062 | outdated=true\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T03:26:35Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837613146\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Make confirmation issuance recoverable after audit failures** When `performConfirmOperation` successfully creates a valid confirmation token but this terminal audit write fails, the endpoint returns an error and discards the only receipt while the token remains live and the audit trail contains only the attempted event. Retrying issues another token, so a transient sink failure accumulates valid, unreturned credentials without a successful issuance record; make issuance replay-safe or revoke/reconcile the issued token before returning the failure. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdRKH | packages/admin/src/validator.ts:86 | outdated=true\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T05:06:53Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837750217\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Compare object-valued enum members structurally** When an operation schema declares an object or array in `enum`, JSON-decoded input that is structurally identical is rejected because `Object.is` compares those values by reference. `AdminJsonSchema` permits arbitrary enum values and manifest validation does not restrict them to scalars, so such a valid schema becomes unusable through REST or MCP; compare enum members using JSON structural equality instead. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdgrD | filefn/server/src/index.ts:334 | outdated=true\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T06:10:24Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837842304\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restrict the public processing service to authorized methods** When an application exposes this newly public service through an in-process integration, callers can invoke `processing.listArtifacts(fileId, ctx)` directly even though that method explicitly ignores `ctx` and queries all artifacts for the file; only `listArtifactsForFile` calls `requireReadableFile`. Publishing the full `ProcessingService` therefore bypasses the authorization enforced by both the HTTP routes and the admin adapter, so expose an authorization-safe facade or keep the worker-level methods private. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdgrE | superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts:40 | outdated=true\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T06:10:24Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837842305\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Resolve composed schemas before deciding an action has no fields** When a valid operation input schema declares its named properties through `allOf`, this returns no editable fields because only top-level `properties` is inspected. The generic action then either submits `{}` immediately or shows a dialog without the required controls, so operations using a schema composition accepted by the manifest validator cannot be invoked from Super Console; merge compatible `allOf` object properties and requirements before constructing the fields. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdoWJ | hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:414 | outdated=true\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T06:40:38Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837887588\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile variable records after provider deletion** When the provider deletion succeeds but `store.deleteVariable` rejects, the stale variable record remains while this request returns an error. Retrying with the same idempotency key replays that error, and retrying with a new key can still never remove the record when the provider reports that the already-deleted variable is not found, because this path does not tolerate provider-not-found as `detachDomain` does. Treat an already-absent provider variable as success or persist a deletion intent so the store record can be reconciled. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_i | packages/admin/src/validator.ts:268 | outdated=false\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T07:44:38Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991044\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject non-plain objects as JSON values** When an in-process dispatcher caller supplies a `Date`, `Map`, or other class instance under `type: \"object\"`, this branch accepts it as a valid JSON object because it never checks the prototype. The immutable snapshot preserves such instances, and output redaction converts them through `Object.entries`—for example, a valid-looking `Date` response becomes `{}`—so adapters can receive or return values that change shape at transport time; require arrays or plain/null-prototype objects throughout JSON validation. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_l | superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts:105 | outdated=true\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T07:44:38Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991047\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Compare action enum objects structurally** When an action field declares an object or array in `enum` or `const`, the form parses the operator's JSON into a new object and these `Object.is` checks always reject it by reference, even when it is structurally identical to the declared value. The administration validator permits these JSON-valued members, so such operations pass manifest validation but cannot be submitted through the generic action UI; use the same structural JSON equality semantics as the runtime validator. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_n | hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:461 | outdated=false\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T07:44:38Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991049\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile variables when metadata persistence fails** When `executor.setVariable` succeeds for a new variable but this store write rejects, the provider retains the live secret while the operator returns an error and has no record through which to list or delete it. A retry is not guaranteed safe because `setVariable` has no idempotency contract; persist a durable intent before the provider call or compensate/reconcile the provider variable if final persistence fails. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd9cQ | superconsole/README.md:59 | outdated=true\n  [pullfrog 2026-08-23T07:54:06Z outdated=true] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838010605\n  This rule can reactivate a confirmation that Super Console has already denied: if `activate()` fails and `revoke()` also fails, the earlier bound success audit remains, so reconciliation follows this branch despite the later denied audit and 503 response. Make durable cancellation or denial take precedence over the prepared success before returning the failure. <details><summary>Technical details</summary> ````markdown # Confirmation reconciliation can override a denied outcome ## Affected sites - `superconsole/README.md:55-62` — directs reconciliation to activate whenever the bound success audit exists. - `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1108-1142` — records denial and returns 503 after activation failure, but suppresses revocation failure. - `superconsole/src/lib/server/types.ts:179-204` — defines durable preparation and revocation without a durable denied/cancelled precedence signal. - `superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts:783-828` — covers only successful revocation after activation failure. ## Required outcome - Once issuance returns an activation failure and records denial, provider reconciliation must not later make that staged token verifiable. - Cov\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beVvV | hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:230 | outdated=false\n  [cubic-dev-ai 2026-08-23T09:16:56Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838155807\n  <!-- cubic:v=aee689c8-aa40-4c1e-90bd-f3790b287173 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=2c758959-78c0-46f1-bcb1-33373d5c1906 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} --> P1: When a pending domain is detached while attachment is in flight, the unchanged claim remains valid after deletion and this completion recreates the domain. Revoke the claim atomically with deletion and require the claimed record to still exist before persisting the terminal state. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts, line 230: <comment>When a pending domain is detached while attachment is in flight, the unchanged claim remains valid after deletion and this completion recreates the domain. Revoke the claim atomically with deletion and require the claimed record to still exist before persisting the terminal state.</comment> <file context> @@ -222,6 +224,13 @@ export class MemoryHostFnOperatorStore implements HostFnOperatorStore { +  async completeDomainAttachment(domain: HostFnDomain, claimToken: string) { +    const key = this.key(domain.scope, domain.id); +    if (this.domainAttachmentClaims.get(key) !=\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beVvX | superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts:826 | outdated=false\n  [cubic-dev-ai 2026-08-23T09:16:56Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838155809\n  <!-- cubic:v=4657c4fd-9b79-4e88-b603-7ef700cbbd32 --> <!-- cubic:review-run=2c758959-78c0-46f1-bcb1-33373d5c1906 --> <!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} --> P3: The deny-path assertion uses `expect.any(String)` for `denialAuditId`, so nothing verifies that the auditId passed to `cancelActivation` matches the id of the 'denied' audit event actually written. That link is the integrity point of the new cancelActivation contract, and the preceding test in this file already validates the identical linkage for the success path (deriving `successAuditId` from `audit.events.find(...)?.id` and asserting `prepareActivation`/`activate` receive it). Capture the denied event's id in the audit mock and assert `cancelActivation` receives exactly that id, e.g. `expect(cancelActivation).toHaveBeenCalledWith(expect.objectContaining({ token: 'staged-token', auditId: expect.any(String), denialAuditId: deniedEventId }))`. <details> <summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary> ```text Check if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts, line 826: <comment>The deny-path assertion uses `expect.any(String)` for `denialAuditId`, so nothing ver\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIN | superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:395 | outdated=false\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T09:18:13Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158128\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Expose create and upsert operations before a record exists** When an ID-targeted operation can create a new record, this classifies it exclusively as a detail-page action, while module-level actions accept only collection targets or resources with no list/detail route. Consequently operations such as `botfn.bots.upsert`, `botfn.channels.connect`, `apifn.specs.register`, and `apifn.environments.upsert` are only reachable after navigating to an existing record whose ID is then prebound; an empty collection has no console path for creating its first record. Project these creation/upsert operations as collection actions while leaving their ID fields editable. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIQ | packages/admin/src/validator.ts:131 | outdated=false\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T09:18:13Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158131\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject non-JSON primitive leaves in open schemas** When an adapter returns a `bigint` under a type-less or `additionalProperties: true` child schema, validation accepts it because only object prototypes and non-finite numbers are rejected. Fresh evidence after the plain-object fix is that the new guards still omit `bigint`, `symbol`, `function`, and `undefined`; the open entity schemas used by DataFn, BillFn, and SearchFn therefore allow values that cannot be represented by the REST/MCP envelopes, with a `bigint` causing the subsequent `JSON.stringify` to throw instead of producing the validated result. Reject every primitive type outside the JSON value set even when the schema omits `type`. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIS | botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts:154 | outdated=false\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T09:18:13Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158133\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind BotFn cursors to their collection query** When a channels cursor issued for `botId=A` is reused with `botId=B`, or a cursor from the bots list is supplied to the channels list, this shared parser accepts the raw offset and slices the unrelated result set from that position. The same cursor can also be reused in another authorized scope, yielding skipped or empty pages there; encode the operation, scope, and channel filter identity into the cursor and reject mismatches. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIT | apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts:160 | outdated=false\n  [chatgpt-codex-connector 2026-08-23T09:18:13Z outdated=false] https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158134\n  **<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind ApiFn cursors to their resource and scope** When the offset returned by `listSpecs` is supplied to `listEnvironments`, or reused after switching to another authorized scope, this parser accepts it unchanged and skips that many unrelated records. Because the helper emits only a decimal offset for both collections, clients cannot distinguish these invalid cursor uses; include the operation and active scope in an opaque cursor and reject mismatches. Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n"},"started_at_ms":1787481231128,"completed_at_ms":1787481231128}}
