prototypes and non-finite numbers are rejected. Fresh evidence after the plain-object fix is that the new guards still omit `bigint`, `symbol`, `function`, and `undefined`; the open entity schemas used by DataFn, BillFn, and SearchFn therefore allow values that cannot be represented by the REST/MCP envelopes, with a `bigint` causing the subsequent `JSON.stringify` to throw instead of producing the validated result. Reject every primitive type outside the JSON value set even when the schema omits `type`.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n---\n2026-08-23T09:18:13Z | chatgpt-codex-connector | botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts:154 | threadOutdated=false commentOutdated=false\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158133\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind BotFn cursors to their collection query**\n\nWhen a channels cursor issued for `botId=A` is reused with `botId=B`, or a cursor from the bots list is supplied to the channels list, this shared parser accepts the raw offset and slices the unrelated result set from that position. The same cursor can also be reused in another authorized scope, yielding skipped or empty pages there; encode the operation, scope, and channel filter identity into the cursor and reject mismatches.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n---\n2026-08-23T09:18:13Z | chatgpt-codex-connector | apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts:160 | threadOutdated=false commentOutdated=false\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158134\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind ApiFn cursors to their resource and scope**\n\nWhen the offset returned by `listSpecs` is supplied to `listEnvironments`, or reused after switching to another authorized scope, this parser accepts it unchanged and skips that many unrelated records. Because the helper emits only a decimal offset for both collections, clients cannot distinguish these invalid cursor uses; include the operation and active scope in an opaque cursor and reject mismatches.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n---\nREVIEWS SINCE 2026-08-23T09:00Z\n2026-08-23T09:16:55Z | cubic-dev-ai | COMMENTED | commit=2011d9c67048f2e1eb7221edaca7d6d36568a019\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:start -->\n**2 issues found across 11 files (changes from recent commits).**\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)</summary>\n\n```text\n\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\n\n\n<file name=\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:230\">\nP1: When a pending domain is detached while attachment is in flight, the unchanged claim remains valid after deletion and this completion recreates the domain. Revoke the claim atomically with deletion and require the claimed record to still exist before persisting the terminal state.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts:826\">\nP3: The deny-path assertion uses `expect.any(String)` for `denialAuditId`, so nothing verifies that the auditId passed to `cancelActivation` matches the id of the 'denied' audit event actually written. That link is the integrity point of the new cancelActivation contract, and the preceding test in this file already validates the identical linkage for the success path (deriving `successAuditId` from `audit.events.find(...)?.id` and asserting `prepareActivation`/`activate` receive it). Capture the denied event's id in the audit mock and assert `cancelActivation` receives exactly that id, e.g. `expect(cancelActivation).toHaveBeenCalledWith(expect.objectContaining({ token: 'staged-token', auditId: expect.any(String), denialAuditId: deniedEventId }))`.</violation>\n</file>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/116/ai_pr_review_1787476249983_6db6cb5f-63dc-48ac-93fe-bec5918d238e?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F116)</sub>\n\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787476249983_6db6cb5f-63dc-48ac-93fe-bec5918d238e:2011d9c67048f2e1eb7221edaca7d6d36568a019:2c758959-78c0-46f1-bcb1-33373d5c1906 -->\n---\n2026-08-23T09:18:00Z | pullfrog | COMMENTED | commit=2011d9c67048f2e1eb7221edaca7d6d36568a019\n\n---\n2026-08-23T09:18:13Z | chatgpt-codex-connector | COMMENTED | commit=2011d9c67048f2e1eb7221edaca7d6d36568a019\n\n### 💡 Codex Review\n\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\n\n**Reviewed commit:** `2011d9c670`\n    \n\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\n<br/>\n\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\n- Open a pull request for review\n- Mark a draft as ready\n- Comment \"@codex review\".\n\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\n\n\n\n\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \"@codex address that feedback\".\n            \n</details>\n---\n2026-08-23T09:20:42Z | pullfrog | COMMENTED | commit=2011d9c67048f2e1eb7221edaca7d6d36568a019\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> The latest commit resolves the stale HostFn worker race, but the existing confirmation thread remains open: if durable cancellation and revocation both fail, reconciliation can later activate a token after issuance returned 503.\n\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `afb902d`:\n\n- **Fenced HostFn completion** — required the active claim token for terminal domain-attachment writes and added stale-worker race coverage.\n- **Preserved attachment recovery** — persisted variable-deletion intent before provider mutation so ambiguous writes remain reconcilable.\n- **Tightened structural validation** — rejected non-plain JSON objects through open schemas and reused structural `const` and `enum` comparison in action forms.\n- **Added confirmation cancellation** — introduced durable activation cancellation and used it before recording activation failures, while leaving the both-fences-fail path unresolved in the existing thread.\n\n<!--\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 2011d9c;\nif commits have landed on SFNS-2 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\n\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\n- Files reviewed: 1801\n- Commits reviewed: 31\n- Base: dev (72aabce)\n- Head: SFNS-2 (2011d9c)\n- Reviewed commits:\n  - 2011d9c — fix: address latest PR review findings\n- Prior pullfrog review: afb902d (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#pullrequestreview-5001934873)\n-->\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [Fix it ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/116?action=fix&review_id=5002073302) ｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32630281896/job/97171914338) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n---\nISSUE COMMENTS SINCE 2026-08-23T09:00Z\n2026-08-23T09:13:44Z | sonarqubecloud\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#issuecomment-5385242013\n## [![Quality Gate Failed](https