s not infer a function\\n+from its name or require a repository-wide package catalog.\\n+\\n+Startup fails closed when enabled operations require infrastructure that was\\n+not injected: a required audit sink, atomic idempotency store, mutation\\n+authorization, or a bound staged confirmation\\n+issuer/activator/revoker/verifier. Required-audit mutations and confirmation\\n+issuance append a sanitized `attempted` event before invoking mutable state,\\n+then append a terminal outcome. Audit and domain state remain separate systems,\\n+so deployments must monitor and reconcile attempts without terminal events.\\n+\\n+Confirmation services must return an unusable staged token from `issue` and\\n+durably bind it to the supplied terminal audit ID in `prepareActivation`.\\n+Super Console then writes that exact succeeded audit and activates the token.\\n+Providers must reconcile prepared records after interruption: activate when the\\n+bound success audit exists, otherwise revoke or expire them. Activation failures\",\n      \"originalLine\": 59,\n      \"line\": null\n    }\n  ]\n}\nLATEST RAW INLINE COMMENTS\n2026-08-23T09:16:56Z | cubic-dev-ai[bot] | hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:230 | in_reply_to=\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838155807\n<!-- cubic:v=aee689c8-aa40-4c1e-90bd-f3790b287173 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=2c758959-78c0-46f1-bcb1-33373d5c1906 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP1: When a pending domain is detached while attachment is in flight, the unchanged claim remains valid after deletion and this completion recreates the domain. Revoke the claim atomically with deletion and require the claimed record to still exist before persisting the terminal state.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts, line 230:\n\n<comment>When a pending domain is detached while attachment is in flight, the unchanged claim remains valid after deletion and this completion recreates the domain. Revoke the claim atomically with deletion and require the claimed record to still exist before persisting the terminal state.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -222,6 +224,13 @@ export class MemoryHostFnOperatorStore implements HostFnOperatorStore {\n+  async completeDomainAttachment(domain: HostFnDomain, claimToken: string) {\n+    const key = this.key(domain.scope, domain.id);\n+    if (this.domainAttachmentClaims.get(key) !== claimToken) return false;\n+    this.domains.set(key, structuredClone(domain));\n+    this.domainAttachmentClaims.delete(key);\n+    return true;\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n---\n2026-08-23T09:16:56Z | cubic-dev-ai[bot] | superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts:826 | in_reply_to=\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838155809\n<!-- cubic:v=4657c4fd-9b79-4e88-b603-7ef700cbbd32 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=2c758959-78c0-46f1-bcb1-33373d5c1906 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP3: The deny-path assertion uses `expect.any(String)` for `denialAuditId`, so nothing verifies that the auditId passed to `cancelActivation` matches the id of the 'denied' audit event actually written. That link is the integrity point of the new cancelActivation contract, and the preceding test in this file already validates the identical linkage for the success path (deriving `successAuditId` from `audit.events.find(...)?.id` and asserting `prepareActivation`/`activate` receive it). Capture the denied event's id in the audit mock and assert `cancelActivation` receives exactly that id, e.g. `expect(cancelActivation).toHaveBeenCalledWith(expect.objectContaining({ token: 'staged-token', auditId: expect.any(String), denialAuditId: deniedEventId }))`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts, line 826:\n\n<comment>The deny-path assertion uses `expect.any(String)` for `denialAuditId`, so nothing verifies that the auditId passed to `cancelActivation` matches the id of the 'denied' audit event actually written. That link is the integrity point of the new cancelActivation contract, and the preceding test in this file already validates the identical linkage for the success path (deriving `successAuditId` from `audit.events.find(...)?.id` and asserting `prepareActivation`/`activate` receive it). Capture the denied event's id in the audit mock and assert `cancelActivation` receives exactly that id, e.g. `expect(cancelActivation).toHaveBeenCalledWith(expect.objectContaining({ token: 'staged-token', auditId: expect.any(String), denialAuditId: deniedEventId }))`.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -818,7 +822,12 @@ describe('Super Console server composition', () => {\n     expect(response.status).toBe(503);\n-    expect(await verify({} as never)).toBe(false);\n+    expect(await verify()).toBe(false);\n+    expect(cancelActivation).toHaveBeenCalledWith(expect.objectContaining({\n+      token: 'staged-token',\n+      auditId: expect.any(String),\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n---\n2026-08-23T09:18:00Z | pullfrog[bot] | hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:75 | in_reply_to=3838010601\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838157741\nAddressed in 2011d9c with claim-token-guarded terminal transitions and stale-worker coverage.\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32630281896/job/97171914338) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n---\n2026-08-23T09:18:13Z | chatgpt-codex-connector[bot] | superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:395 | in_reply_to=\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158128\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Expose create and upsert operations before a record exists**\n\nWhen an ID-targeted operation can create a new record, this classifies it exclusively as a detail-page action, while module-level actions accept only collection targets or resources with no list/detail route. Consequently operations such as `botfn.bots.upsert`, `botfn.channels.connect`, `apifn.specs.register`, and `apifn.environments.upsert` are only reachable after navigating to an existing record whose ID is then prebound; an empty collection has no console path for creating its first record. Project these creation/upsert operations as collection actions while leaving their ID fields editable.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n---\n2026-08-23T09:18:13Z | chatgpt-codex-connector[bot] | packages/admin/src/validator.ts:131 | in_reply_to=\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158131\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject non-JSON primitive leaves in open schemas**\n\nWhen an adapter returns a `bigint` under a type-less or `additionalProperties: true` child schema, validation accepts it because only object prototypes and non-finite numbers are rejected. Fresh evidence after the plain-object fix is that the new guards still omit `bigint`, `symbol`, `function`, and `undefined`; the open entity schemas used by DataFn, BillFn, and SearchFn therefore allow values that cannot be represented by the REST/MCP envelopes, with a `bigint` causing the subsequent `JSON.stringify` to throw instead of producing the validated result. Reject every primitive type outside the JSON value set even when the schema omits `type`.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n---\n2026-08-23T09:18:13Z | chatgpt-codex-connector[bot] | botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts:154 | in_reply_to=\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158133\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind BotFn cursors to their collection query**\n\nWhen a channels cursor issued for `botId=A` is reused with `botId=B`, or a cursor from the bots list is supplied to the channels list, this shared parser accepts the raw offset and slices the unrelated result set from that position. The same cursor can also be reused in another authorized scope, yielding skipped or empty pages there; encode the operation, scope, and channel filter identity into the cursor and reject mismatches.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n---\n2026-08-23T09:18:13Z | chatgpt-codex-connector[bot] | apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts:160 | in_reply_to=\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158134\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind ApiFn cursors to their resource and scope**\n\nWhen the offset returned by `listSpecs` is supplied to `listEnvironments`, or reused after switching to another authorized scope, this parser accepts it unchanged and skips that many unrelated records. Because the helper emits only a decimal offset for both collections, clients cannot distinguish these invalid cursor uses; include the operation and active scope in an opaque cursor and reject mismatches.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n---\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02e2d-cfe6-7e21-8f45-566081da5b6e","create_time":1787481263.091555}}}
