d=21nCo_super-functions&pullRequest=116) (required ≥ A)  \n  \n<!-- sqra:qg_revision=8c15ce1a9b985076ecd6eab7b84ae3e98b7b4173090cad0293e9595b85e00b5f -->\n<!-- sqra-placement-anchor -->\n[See analysis details on SonarQube Cloud](https://sonarcloud.io/dashboard?id=21nCo_super-functions&pullRequest=116)\n\n##   \n![](https://sonarsource.github.io/sonarcloud-github-static-resources/v2/common/light_bulb-16px.png '') Catch issues before they fail your Quality Gate with our IDE extension ![](https://sonarsource.github.io/sonarcloud-github-static-resources/v2/common/sonarlint-16px.png '') [SonarQube for IDE](https://www.sonarsource.com/products/sonarlint/features/connected-mode/?referrer=pull-request)\n\n\n---\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"UNRESOLVED COMMENTS SINCE 2026-08-23T10:35Z\n2026-08-23T10:47:40Z | chatgpt-codex-connector | datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts:64 | threadOutdated=false commentOutdated=false\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838310501\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind DataFn metadata cursors to their collection**\n\nWhen a schema has more than one page of metadata, a cursor returned by `datafn.resources.list` can be reused with `datafn.relations.list`, `datafn.indices.list`, or `datafn.capabilities.list` in the same scope, because the cursor carries only an offset. The unrelated collection is then sliced from that offset, silently skipping its initial entries; include the operation or collection identity in these cursors and reject mismatches.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n---\n2026-08-23T10:47:40Z | chatgpt-codex-connector | uifn/theme/src/mount.ts:87 | threadOutdated=false commentOutdated=false\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838310502\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Resolve token references before emitting CSS variables**\n\nWhen a valid runtime theme uses a typed reference such as `{color.surface.canvas}` with the required fallback metadata, validation resolves it only for checking, but this code flattens the original theme and emits the brace expression literally. The resulting custom property is unusable when consumed as a color or dimension, so mounted referenced tokens do not apply; emit values from `resolveTokenReferences(theme).theme` (or translate references to valid CSS `var()` expressions).\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n---\n2026-08-23T10:51:21Z | cubic-dev-ai | hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:411 | threadOutdated=false commentOutdated=false\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838317267\n<!-- cubic:v=e5362967-c544-40cf-ab2e-75288589b805 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=dda4da8d-6525-4c72-8e78-c026f961de0e -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP1: After the attachment intent is deleted, a non-404 failure from `compensateDeletedDomain()` is swallowed while the method rethrows only the original attach error. Retain a durable reconciliation intent or persist this compensation failure; otherwise an ambiguous provider attach can leave an orphaned domain with no record to retry.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts, line 411:\n\n<comment>After the attachment intent is deleted, a non-404 failure from `compensateDeletedDomain()` is swallowed while the method rethrows only the original attach error. Retain a durable reconciliation intent or persist this compensation failure; otherwise an ambiguous provider attach can leave an orphaned domain with no record to retry.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -399,6 +408,7 @@ export class HostFnOperatorService {\n         if (!completed) {\n           const current = await currentDomain();\n           if (current) return current;\n+          await compensateDeletedDomain();\n         }\n       } catch {\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n---\n2026-08-23T10:51:21Z | cubic-dev-ai | apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts:184 | threadOutdated=false commentOutdated=false\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838317268\n<!-- cubic:v=29faa622-94a8-4300-bcd7-95e6bbd0ab5e -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=dda4da8d-6525-4c72-8e78-c026f961de0e -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP2: When a cursor has a null or missing position, `position.offset` throws before the invalid-offset checks run, turning malformed client input into an internal error. Validate that `position` is a non-array object before reading `offset`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts, line 184:\n\n<comment>When a cursor has a null or missing position, `position.offset` throws before the invalid-offset checks run, turning malformed client input into an internal error. Validate that `position` is a non-array object before reading `offset`.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -153,16 +160,43 @@ function specView(record: ApiFnSpecRecord): ApiFnSpecView {\n+  const position = input.cursor === undefined\n+    ? { offset: 0, resource }\n+    : decodeAdminCursor<{ offset: number; resource: ApiFnCursorResource }>(input.cursor, cursorScope(scope));\n+  const offset = position.offset;\n   if (!Number.isSafeInteger(offset) || offset < 0) {\n     throw new AdminError(\"invalid_argument\", \"ApiFn cursor is invalid.\");\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\n  if (!position || typeof position !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(position)) {\n    throw new AdminError(\"invalid_argument\", \"ApiFn cursor is invalid.\");\n  }\n  const offset = position.offset;\n```\n---\n2026-08-23T10:51:21Z | cubic-dev-ai | botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts:186 | threadOutdated=false commentOutdated=false\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838317270\n<!-- cubic:v=9c42b7be-f7ac-4850-8457-0f1fe92b8aef -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=dda4da8d-6525-4c72-8e78-c026f961de0e -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP2: When a scope-matching cursor decodes to `null` or omits `position`, `position.offset` throws before validation, so malformed cursors return an internal error instead of `invalid_argument`. Validate the decoded position is an object before reading `offset`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts, line 186:\n\n<comment>When a scope-matching cursor decodes to `null` or omits `position`, `position.offset` throws before validation, so malformed cursors return an internal error instead of `invalid_argument`. Validate the decoded position is an object before reading `offset`.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -145,19 +152,54 @@ function requireScope(context: AdminOperationContext): BotFnOperatorScope {\n-  const offset = input.cursor === undefined ? 0 : Number(input.cursor);\n+  const position = input.cursor === undefined\n+    ? { offset: 0, query }\n+    : decodeAdminCursor<{ offset: number; query: BotFnCursorQuery }>(input.cursor, cursorScope(scope));\n+  const offset = position.offset;\n   if (!Number.isSafeInteger(offset) || offset < 0) {\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n---\n2026-08-23T10:51:58Z | pullfrog | apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts:184 | threadOutdated=false commentOutdated=false\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838318435\nA scope-valid cursor envelope can omit or null `position`, and `decodeAdminCursor()` returns that value unchecked, so this dereference throws `TypeError` instead of the declared `invalid_argument`. Validate the decoded position before reading it in both ApiFn and BotFn, and cover malformed-position envelopes.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Structurally malformed cursors escape as runtime errors\n\n## Affected sites\n- `apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts:184` — dereferences an unchecked decoded position.\n- `botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts:187` — repeats the same unchecked dereference.\n- `packages/admin/src/pagination.ts:33-39` — validates only cursor version and scope before returning `payload.position`.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Every syntactically decodable cursor with a missing, null, or otherwise malformed position must fail with `AdminError` code `invalid_argument` in both adapters.\n\n## Suggested approach\n- Validate the position as an object and validate its fields before dereferencing, either in each typed consumer or through a shared decoder validation hook.\n````\n\n</details>\n---\n2026-08-23T10:51:58Z | pullfrog | hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:429 | threadOutdated=false commentOutdated=false\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838318438\nIf this compensating detach fails transiently, the pending domain and claim have already been deleted, so a successful provider attachment is left with no durable reconciliation record. Preserve a durable intent or otherwise make compensation retryable until provider detachment is confirmed.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Deleted in-flight attachments can become untracked provider state\n\n## Affected sites\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:390-395` — compensation rethrows non-not-found provider failures without recording retry state.\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:425-438` — releases the claim and propagates compensation failure after the local domain is already absent.\n- `hostfn/cli/src/__tests__/operator.test.ts:289-315` — covers only successful compensating detach.\n\n## Required outcome\n- A provider attachment that completes after local deletion must either be confirmed detached or remain represented by durable, retryable reconciliation state.\n- Add coverage for a transient failure of the compensating detach.\n````\n\n</details>\n---\n2026-08-23T10:51:58Z | pullfrog | superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1156 | threadOutdated=false commentOutdated=false\nhttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838318443\n`activate()` rejection is documented to leave the token unusable, but this returns the ordinary successful receipt after cancellation and revocation also fail; the new test even keeps `verify()` false. Do not return an indistinguishable activated credential unless the contract and response explicitly represent pending reconciliation and callers can handle it.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Activation rejection returns an unusable credential as success\n\n## Affected sites\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/types.ts:198-206` — promises that rejected activation leaves the token unusable.\n- `superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts:1098-1156` — writes the success audit, observes activation rejection, then returns 201 without cancellation, revocation, or a denial audit.\n- `superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts:906-923` — asserts the successful receipt while `verify()` remains false and only attempted/succeeded audits exist.\n\n## Required outcome\n- A successful issuance response must identify a currently usable credential, or explicitly expose a pending/reconciliation state with a supported client contract.\n- Audit state and HTTP outcome must truthfully reflect the activation result without reintroducing the unreturned-live-token race.\n````\n\n</details>\n---\nREVIEWS SINCE 2026-08-23T10:35Z\n2026-08-23T10:47:40Z | chatgpt-codex-connector | COMMENTED | commit=d9b60c51a3517f5b7635b4a8d224ae62a9f914e1\n\n### 💡 Codex Review\n\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\n\n**Reviewed commit:** `d9b60c51a3`\n    \n\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\n<br/>\n\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\n- Open a pull request for review\n- Mark a draft as ready\n- Comment \"@codex review\".\n\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\n\n\n\n\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \"@codex address that feedback\".\n            \n</details>\n---\n2026-08-23T10:51:20Z | cubic-dev-ai | COMMENTED | commit=d9b60c51a3517f5b7635b4a8d224ae62a9f914e1\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:start -->\n**3 issues found across 11 files (changes from recent commits).**\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)</summary>\n\n```text\n\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\n\n\n<file name=\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:411\">\nP1: After the attachment intent is deleted, a non-404 failure from `compensateDeletedDomain()` is swallowed while the method rethrows only the original attach error. Retain a durable reconciliation intent or persist this compensation failure; otherwise an ambiguous provider attach can leave an orphaned domain with no record to retry.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts:184\">\nP2: When a cursor has a null or missing position, `position.offset` throws before the invalid-offset checks run, turning malformed client input into an internal error. Validate that `position` is a non-array object before reading `offset`.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts:186\">\nP2: When a scope-matching cursor decodes to `null` or omits `position`, `position.offset` throws before validation, so malformed cursors return an internal error instead of `invalid_argument`. Validate the decoded position is an object before reading `offset`.</violation>\n</file>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/116/ai_pr_review_1787481784858_be960607-bbfb-4127-b64a-0e8c2a8c97b3?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F116)</sub>\n\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787481784858_be960607-bbfb-4127-b64a-0e8c2a8c97b3:d9b60c51a3517f5b7635b4a8d224ae62a9f914e1:dda4da8d-6525-4c72-8e78-c026f961de0e -->\n---\n2026-08-23T10:51:59Z | pullfrog | COMMENTED | commit=d9b60c51a3517f5b7635b4a8d224ae62a9f914e1\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> The latest fix commit introduces three correctness gaps in cursor error handling, HostFn reconciliation, and confirmation issuance that should be addressed before merge.\n\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `2011d9c`:\n\n- **Bound administration cursors** — scoped ApiFn and BotFn offsets to the active installation context and collection query.\n- **Handled concurrent domain deletion** — added HostFn compensation when provider attachment completes after its pending domain was deleted.\n- **Tightened shared validation** — rejected non-JSON primitive leaves through open schemas and exposed non-destructive ID-targeted writes before records exist.\n- **Changed activation-failure recovery** — returned the audited confirmation receipt when neither cancellation nor revocation can fence a rejected activation.\n\n<!--\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against d9b60c5;\nif commits have landed on SFNS-2 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\n\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\n- Files reviewed: 1801\n- Comm