{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T11:48:10.214Z","ordinal":13024,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0d3207775ece027d016a8addecc97c87d0bb913a9a4a979d78","status":"completed","call_id":"call_jekOuYY73QnKd8l7KXpVXTjV","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/superconsole/src/lib/server/types.ts\\n@@\\n   prepareActivation(input: {\\n     token: string;\\n     auditId: string;\\n+    /** Bound failure audit whose existence permanently fences reconciliation. */\\n+    denialAuditId: string;\\n     operationId: string;\\n*** Update File: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\\n@@\\n     if (!confirmation) throw new SuperConsoleHttpError('Confirmation issuance is unavailable.', { status: 503, code: 'CONFIRMATION_UNAVAILABLE' });\\n     const successAuditId = `audit_${crypto.randomUUID()}`;\\n+    const denialAuditId = `audit_${crypto.randomUUID()}`;\\n     try {\\n       await confirmation.prepareActivation({\\n         token: receipt.token,\\n         auditId: successAuditId,\\n+        denialAuditId,\\n@@\\n-      const denialAuditId = `audit_${crypto.randomUUID()}`;\\n-      let cancellationDurable = false;\\n       try {\\n         await confirmation.cancelActivation({\\n@@\\n         });\\n-        cancellationDurable = true;\\n       } catch {\\n         // A durable revoke below is an equivalent cancellation fence.\\n@@\\n         });\\n-        cancellationDurable = true;\\n       } catch {\\n-        // The explicit cancellation record, when present, remains authoritative.\\n-      }\\n-      if (!cancellationDurable) {\\n-        // The succeeded audit remains authoritative when an ambiguous provider\\n-        // outcome cannot be fenced. Return the receipt so reconciliation may\\n-        // activate it without turning an unreturned credential live after 503.\\n-        return receipt;\\n+        // The bound denial audit below remains an independent reconciliation fence.\\n       }\\n*** Update File: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/superconsole/README.md\\n@@\\n Confirmation services must return an unusable staged token from `issue` and\\n-durably bind it to the supplied terminal audit ID in `prepareActivation`.\\n+durably bind it to the supplied success and denial audit IDs in `prepareActivation`.\\n Super Console then writes that exact succeeded audit and activates the token.\\n Providers must reconcile prepared records after interruption: activate when the\\n-bound success audit exists unless a durable `cancelActivation` record exists;\\n-cancellation always wins. Otherwise providers revoke or expire the staged token.\\n+bound success audit exists unless the bound denial audit or a durable\\n+`cancelActivation` record exists; denial and cancellation always win. Otherwise\\n+providers revoke or expire the staged token.\\n Activation failures are durably cancelled before their denied event is written\\n and trigger an idempotent `revoke`; audit failures therefore cannot leave a live\\n unaudited token, while a post-audit interruption remains identifiable and\\n-recoverable without reactivating a denied confirmation. If neither cancellation\\n-nor revocation can durably fence an ambiguous activation result, Super Console\\n-returns the already-audited receipt instead of returning a 503 that could discard\\n-a token which reconciliation may later activate.\\n+recoverable without reactivating a denied confirmation. The pre-bound denial\\n+audit remains a reconciliation fence even when cancellation and revocation both\\n+fail, so rejected activation never returns an unusable credential as success.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02e6e-3560-7e22-a95e-b95a3d227c08","create_time":1787485674.742509}}}
