{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T11:48:35.561Z","ordinal":13036,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0d3207775ece027d016a8ade0fce7c87d08d95c77170e25930","status":"completed","call_id":"call_Qektu7byIuoLgKksmpeD4t55","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/superconsole/README.md\\n@@\\n-Activation failures are durably cancelled before their denied event is written\\n-and trigger an idempotent `revoke`; audit failures therefore cannot leave a live\\n-unaudited token, while a post-audit interruption remains identifiable and\\n-recoverable without reactivating a denied confirmation. The pre-bound denial\\n-audit remains a reconciliation fence even when cancellation and revocation both\\n-fail, so rejected activation never returns an unusable credential as success.\\n+Activation failures attempt durable cancellation and an idempotent `revoke`\\n+before writing their pre-bound denied event; audit failures therefore cannot\\n+leave a live unaudited token, while a post-audit interruption remains identifiable\\n+and recoverable without reactivating a denied confirmation. The bound denial audit\\n+remains a reconciliation fence even when cancellation and revocation both fail,\\n+so rejected activation never returns an unusable credential as success.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02e6e-3560-7e22-a95e-b95a3d227c08","create_time":1787485708.599003}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T11:48:35.574Z","ordinal":13037,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a024c5-b91b-72b3-ad56-490032d022a1","turn_id":"01a02e6e-3560-7e22-a95e-b95a3d227c08","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-935eb1a0-0ccc-46d8-a52d-ee5a7d916015","changes":{"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/superconsole/README.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -61,8 +61,8 @@\n providers revoke or expire the staged token.\n-Activation failures are durably cancelled before their denied event is written\n-and trigger an idempotent `revoke`; audit failures therefore cannot leave a live\n-unaudited token, while a post-audit interruption remains identifiable and\n-recoverable without reactivating a denied confirmation. The pre-bound denial\n-audit remains a reconciliation fence even when cancellation and revocation both\n-fail, so rejected activation never returns an unusable credential as success.\n+Activation failures attempt durable cancellation and an idempotent `revoke`\n+before writing their pre-bound denied event; audit failures therefore cannot\n+leave a live unaudited token, while a post-audit interruption remains identifiable\n+and recoverable without reactivating a denied confirmation. The bound denial audit\n+remains a reconciliation fence even when cancellation and revocation both fail,\n+so rejected activation never returns an unusable credential as success.\n \n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/superconsole/README.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1787485715573,"completed_at_ms":1787485715574}}
