{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T12:56:47.488Z","ordinal":13196,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0d3207775ece027d016a8aee0a6e0c87d0adf3c8a4c1a305c0","status":"completed","call_id":"call_3nnUKrHbNbzSVxkp9kXkG4ge","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\n  cmd: `jq -s -r '\n[.[].data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[]]\n| map(select(.isResolved == false)\n  | . as $t\n  | [(.comments.nodes[] | select(.createdAt >= \"2026-08-23T11:50:56Z\"))] as $new\n  | select(($new|length)>0)\n  | \"THREAD\\\\t\\\\($t.id)\\\\t\\\\($t.path):\\\\($t.line // $t.originalLine // 0)\\\\n\"\n    + ($new | map(\"COMMENT\\\\t\\\\(.author.login)\\\\t\\\\(.createdAt)\\\\t\\\\(.outdated)\\\\t\\\\(.url)\\\\n\\\\(.body)\\\\n\") | join(\"\\\\n\"))\n) | .[]' /tmp/pr116-review-round.CWNdBu/threads.jsonl\njq -r '.reviews[] | select(.submittedAt >= \"2026-08-23T11:50:56Z\" and (.body|length)>0) | \"REVIEW\\\\t\\\\(.author.login)\\\\t\\\\(.submittedAt)\\\\t\\\\(.state)\\\\n\\\\(.body)\\\\n\"' /tmp/pr116-review-round.CWNdBu/pr.json`,\n  workdir: \"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev\",\n  yield_time_ms: 10000,\n  max_output_tokens: 20000\n});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02eb0-78a7-7a20-b243-beaa58cdcdc6","create_time":1787489798.482119}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T12:56:47.686Z","ordinal":13197,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a024c5-b91b-72b3-ad56-490032d022a1","turn_id":"01a02eb0-78a7-7a20-b243-beaa58cdcdc6","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-1064cb92-f180-4ae2-978f-615337a3f9dd","process_id":"89852","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","jq -s -r '\n[.[].data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[]]\n| map(select(.isResolved == false)\n  | . as $t\n  | [(.comments.nodes[] | select(.createdAt >= \"2026-08-23T11:50:56Z\"))] as $new\n  | select(($new|length)>0)\n  | \"THREAD\\t\\($t.id)\\t\\($t.path):\\($t.line // $t.originalLine // 0)\\n\"\n    + ($new | map(\"COMMENT\\t\\(.author.login)\\t\\(.createdAt)\\t\\(.outdated)\\t\\(.url)\\n\\(.body)\\n\") | join(\"\\n\"))\n) | .[]' /tmp/pr116-review-round.CWNdBu/threads.jsonl\njq -r '.reviews[] | select(.submittedAt >= \"2026-08-23T11:50:56Z\" and (.body|length)>0) | \"REVIEW\\t\\(.author.login)\\t\\(.submittedAt)\\t\\(.state)\\n\\(.body)\\n\"' /tmp/pr116-review-round.CWNdBu/pr.json"],"cwd":"file:///Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"jq -s -r '\n[.[].data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[]]\n| map(select(.isResolved == false)\n  | . as $t\n  | [(.comments.nodes[] | select(.createdAt >= \"2026-08-23T11:50:56Z\"))] as $new\n  | select(($new|length)>0)\n  | \"THREAD\\t\\($t.id)\\t\\($t.path):\\($t.line // $t.originalLine // 0)\\n\"\n    + ($new | map(\"COMMENT\\t\\(.author.login)\\t\\(.createdAt)\\t\\(.outdated)\\t\\(.url)\\n\\(.body)\\n\") | join(\"\\n\"))\n) | .[]' /tmp/pr116-review-round.CWNdBu/threads.jsonl\njq -r '.reviews[] | select(.submittedAt >= \"2026-08-23T11:50:56Z\" and (.body|length)>0) | \"REVIEW\\t\\(.author.login)\\t\\(.submittedAt)\\t\\(.state)\\n\\(.body)\\n\"' /tmp/pr116-review-round.CWNdBu/pr.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"THREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfEZL\tuifn/dom/src/live-region.ts:84\nCOMMENT\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2026-08-23T11:54:58Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838433455\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Continue publishing after skipping a cleared announcement**\n\nWhen announcement A is queued before B and `clear(A)` runs before A is rendered, A becomes stale but remains in `queue`; the scheduled publisher shifts A and returns here without scheduling another pass, leaving B permanently unannounced. The same stall occurs if A is cleared while its animation frame is pending, so clearing one message must still advance the queue.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfEZN\tuifn/core/src/algorithms/virtualization.ts:36\nCOMMENT\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2026-08-23T11:54:58Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838433456\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Include partially visible rows in the virtual window**\n\nWhen `scrollOffset` is not aligned to `estimateSize`, `visible` counts only the viewport's full-size quotient and ignores the partial row at the leading edge. For example, with size 10, viewport 10, offset 5, and `overscan: 0`, this returns only index 0 even though index 1 is also visible, producing a blank region while scrolling; calculate the end from the viewport's absolute trailing offset or add the partial leading item.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfEZO\tuifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts:35\nCOMMENT\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2026-08-23T11:54:58Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838433458\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve years below 100 in calendar arithmetic**\n\nWhen an accepted ISO date has a year from 0000 through 0099, `Date.UTC` applies JavaScript's 1900-year offset. Thus `compareUIFnDates` considers year 0001 equal to 1901, and `addUIFnDateDays` jumps a year-0001 date into 1901. Construct dates using `setUTCFullYear` or reject this range consistently instead of accepting values that calendar operations reinterpret.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfFBa\tsuperconsole/README.md:64\nCOMMENT\tcubic-dev-ai\t2026-08-23T11:57:01Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838437139\n<!-- cubic:v=c999b7a3-8847-44ee-a110-3f47d07d05ba -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=010a75f8-f3d2-4025-b362-ae67b75e4819 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP1: When activation fails and cancellation, revocation, and the denial-audit write all fail, reconciliation can later activate the prepared token from its existing success audit. This contradicts the guarantee that the failure path cannot leave a live token; retain a durable denial/cancellation fence before returning, or document and handle this unresolved state explicitly.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/README.md, line 64:\n\n<comment>When activation fails and cancellation, revocation, and the denial-audit write all fail, reconciliation can later activate the prepared token from its existing success audit. This contradicts the guarantee that the failure path cannot leave a live token; retain a durable denial/cancellation fence before returning, or document and handle this unresolved state explicitly.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -53,18 +53,18 @@ then append a terminal outcome. Audit and domain state remain separate systems,\n+providers revoke or expire the staged token.\n+Activation failures attempt durable cancellation and an idempotent `revoke`\n+before writing their pre-bound denied event; audit failures therefore cannot\n+leave a live unaudited token, while a post-audit interruption remains identifiable\n+and recoverable without reactivating a denied confirmation. The bound denial audit\n+remains a reconciliation fence even when cancellation and revocation both fail,\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\nTHREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfFBb\thostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:397\nCOMMENT\tcubic-dev-ai\t2026-08-23T11:57:01Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838437140\n<!-- cubic:v=326efe59-380f-4a3d-ab8f-d0b5e0ec0317 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=010a75f8-f3d2-4025-b362-ae67b75e4819 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP2: When a replacement attachment claims the same hostname after the original pending record is deleted, this unconditional write resurrects the stale domain ID alongside the replacement. Persist compensation failure with a hostname/claim-token compare-and-set, or reconcile the newer claim first, so stale workers cannot create duplicate domain intents and retries against the wrong lifecycle.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts, line 397:\n\n<comment>When a replacement attachment claims the same hostname after the original pending record is deleted, this unconditional write resurrects the stale domain ID alongside the replacement. Persist compensation failure with a hostname/claim-token compare-and-set, or reconcile the newer claim first, so stale workers cannot create duplicate domain intents and retries against the wrong lifecycle.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -391,7 +391,15 @@ export class HostFnOperatorService {\n+        if (providerReportedNotFound(error)) return;\n+        // Restore a durable, provider-idempotent intent so a transient\n+        // compensation failure remains visible and detach can be retried.\n+        await this.store.putDomain({\n+          ...domain,\n+          status: \"failed\",\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\nREVIEW\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2026-08-23T11:54:58Z\tCOMMENTED\n\n### 💡 Codex Review\n\nHere ar