 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Include partially visible rows in the virtual window**\n\nWhen `scrollOffset` is not aligned to `estimateSize`, `visible` counts only the viewport's full-size quotient and ignores the partial row at the leading edge. For example, with size 10, viewport 10, offset 5, and `overscan: 0`, this returns only index 0 even though index 1 is also visible, producing a blank region while scrolling; calculate the end from the viewport's absolute trailing offset or add the partial leading item.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfEZO\tuifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts:35\nCOMMENT\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2026-08-23T11:54:58Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838433458\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve years below 100 in calendar arithmetic**\n\nWhen an accepted ISO date has a year from 0000 through 0099, `Date.UTC` applies JavaScript's 1900-year offset. Thus `compareUIFnDates` considers year 0001 equal to 1901, and `addUIFnDateDays` jumps a year-0001 date into 1901. Construct dates using `setUTCFullYear` or reject this range consistently instead of accepting values that calendar operations reinterpret.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfFBa\tsuperconsole/README.md:64\nCOMMENT\tcubic-dev-ai\t2026-08-23T11:57:01Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838437139\n<!-- cubic:v=c999b7a3-8847-44ee-a110-3f47d07d05ba -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=010a75f8-f3d2-4025-b362-ae67b75e4819 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP1: When activation fails and cancellation, revocation, and the denial-audit write all fail, reconciliation can later activate the prepared token from its existing success audit. This contradicts the guarantee that the failure path cannot leave a live token; retain a durable denial/cancellation fence before returning, 