{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T12:56:47.701Z","ordinal":13198,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a02eb1-ed55-7690-bffc-5f27b9575526","call_id":"call_3nnUKrHbNbzSVxkp9kXkG4ge","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"THREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfEZL\tuifn/dom/src/live-region.ts:84\nCOMMENT\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2026-08-23T11:54:58Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838433455\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Continue publishing after skipping a cleared announcement**\n\nWhen announcement A is queued before B and `clear(A)` runs before A is rendered, A becomes stale but remains in `queue`; the scheduled publisher shifts A and returns here without scheduling another pass, leaving B permanently unannounced. The same stall occurs if A is cleared while its animation frame is pending, so clearing one message must still advance the queue.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfEZN\tuifn/core/src/algorithms/virtualization.ts:36\nCOMMENT\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2026-08-23T11:54:58Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838433456\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Include partially visible rows in the virtual window**\n\nWhen `scrollOffset` is not aligned to `estimateSize`, `visible` counts only the viewport's full-size quotient and ignores the partial row at the leading edge. For example, with size 10, viewport 10, offset 5, and `overscan: 0`, this returns only index 0 even though index 1 is also visible, producing a blank region while scrolling; calculate the end from the viewport's absolute trailing offset or add the partial leading item.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfEZO\tuifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts:35\nCOMMENT\tchatgpt-c