{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T13:01:20.402Z","ordinal":13278,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0d3207775ece027d016a8aef09d75487d08543a8b07e2612a5","status":"completed","call_id":"call_g1mB2xb42sRkPAWKlL8IiJZ1","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/superconsole/src/lib/server/types.ts\\n@@\\n-  /** Durably bind the staged token to the terminal audit ID before that audit is written. */\\n+  /**\\n+   * Durably bind the staged token to its terminal audit IDs while leaving it fail-closed.\\n+   * A prepared record must never become verifiable from audit observation alone.\\n+   */\\n@@\\n-  /** Atomically make an audited staged token verifiable; a rejected call must leave it unusable. */\\n+  /**\\n+   * The only transition that may make a staged token verifiable. This operation must be\\n+   * atomic and idempotent; rejection guarantees the token remains unusable and cannot\\n+   * become active later through reconciliation.\\n+   */\\n*** Update File: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\\n@@\\n       try {\\n         await confirmation.revoke({\\n@@\\n         });\\n       } catch {\\n-        // The bound denial audit below remains an independent reconciliation fence.\\n+        // activate() rejection is fail-closed; revocation is an additional cleanup attempt.\\n       }\\n*** Update File: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/superconsole/README.md\\n@@\\n Confirmation services must return an unusable staged token from `issue` and\\n-durably bind it to the supplied success and denial audit IDs in `prepareActivation`.\\n-Super Console then writes that exact succeeded audit and activates the token.\\n-Providers must reconcile prepared records after interruption: activate when the\\n-bound success audit exists unless the bound denial audit or a durable\\n-`cancelActivation` record exists; denial and cancellation always win. Otherwise\\n-providers revoke or expire the staged token.\\n+durably bind it to the supplied success and denial audit IDs in `prepareActivation`\\n+without making it verifiable. Super Console then writes that exact succeeded audit\\n+and explicitly calls `activate`. That call is the only allowed transition to a\\n+verifiable token and must be atomic and idempotent: a rejected call guarantees the\\n+token is still unusable. Providers must never infer activation from a success audit\\n+alone during reconciliation; prepared records without a completed activation are\\n+revoked or expired.\\n Activation failures attempt durable cancellation and an idempotent `revoke`\\n-before writing their pre-bound denied event; audit failures therefore cannot\\n-leave a live unaudited token, while a post-audit interruption remains identifiable\\n-and recoverable without reactivating a denied confirmation. The bound denial audit\\n-remains a reconciliation fence even when cancellation and revocation both fail,\\n-so rejected activation never returns an unusable credential as success.\\n+before writing their pre-bound denied event. Those steps provide cleanup and durable\\n+failure evidence, but safety does not depend on all three succeeding: the fail-closed\\n+activation contract and no-auto-activation reconciliation rule prevent a rejected\\n+activation from becoming live later.\\n*** Update File: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/superconsole/src/lib/server/README.md\\n@@\\n-Bound confirmation services stage unusable tokens in `issue`, atomically make\\n-them verifiable in `activate`, and support idempotent `revoke`. Super Console\\n-records activation failure as a denied terminal event and revokes tokens when\\n-activation or the succeeded audit cannot complete.\\n+Bound confirmation services stage unusable tokens in `issue`, keep prepared\\n+records fail-closed, atomically make them verifiable only in `activate`, and support\\n+idempotent `revoke`. A rejected activation must remain unusable, and reconciliation\\n+must revoke or expire prepared records rather than infer activation from a success\\n+audit alone. Super Console records activation failure as a denied terminal event\\n+and attempts cancellation and revocation when activation or the succeeded audit\\n+cannot complete.\\n*** Update File: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts\\n@@\\n-  it('uses the bound denial audit when rejected activation cannot be cancelled or revoked', async () => {\\n+  it('keeps rejected activation fail-closed when cancellation, revocation, and denial audit fail', async () => {\\n     const capability = manifest({ destructive: true });\\n     const outcomes: Array<{ id: string; outcome: string }> = [];\\n+    let active = false;\\n     const prepareActivation = vi.fn(async () => undefined);\\n     const cancelActivation = vi.fn(async () => { throw new Error('cancellation unavailable'); });\\n     const revoke = vi.fn(async () => { throw new Error('revocation unavailable'); });\\n@@\\n       audit: {\\n         idempotentById: true,\\n         write: async (event) => {\\n-          if (event.operationId === 'superconsole.confirmations.issue') outcomes.push({ id: event.id, outcome: event.outcome });\\n+          if (event.operationId !== 'superconsole.confirmations.issue') return;\\n+          if (event.outcome === 'denied') throw new Error('denial audit unavailable');\\n+          outcomes.push({ id: event.id, outcome: event.outcome });\\n         },\\n       },\\n@@\\n         prepareActivation,\\n         cancelActivation,\\n         activate: async () => { throw new Error('ambiguous activation outcome'); },\\n         revoke,\\n-        verify: async () => false,\\n+        verify: async () => active,\\n       },\\n@@\\n \\n     expect(response.status).toBe(503);\\n-    expect(await response.json()).toMatchObject({ error: { code: 'CONFIRMATION_ACTIVATION_FAILED' } });\\n-    const deniedAuditId = outcomes.find((event) => event.outcome === 'denied')?.id;\\n-    expect(deniedAuditId).toEqual(expect.any(String));\\n+    expect(await response.json()).toMatchObject({ error: { code: 'AUDIT_UNAVAILABLE' } });\\n+    expect(active).toBe(false);\\n     expect(prepareActivation).toHaveBeenCalledWith(expect.objectContaining({\\n       token: 'ambiguous-token',\\n-      denialAuditId: deniedAuditId,\\n+      denialAuditId: expect.any(String),\\n     }));\\n     expect(cancelActivation).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);\\n     expect(revoke).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);\\n-    expect(outcomes.map((event) => event.outcome)).toEqual(['attempted', 'succeeded', 'denied']);\\n+    expect(outcomes.map((event) => event.outcome)).toEqual(['attempted', 'succeeded']);\\n   });\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02eb0-78a7-7a20-b243-beaa58cdcdc6","create_time":1787490035.80994}}}
