ed event. Those steps provide cleanup and durable\n+failure evidence, but safety does not depend on all three succeeding: the fail-closed\n+activation contract and no-auto-activation reconciliation rule prevent a rejected\n+activation from becoming live later.\n \n","move_path":null},"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/superconsole/src/lib/server/types.ts":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -178,3 +178,6 @@\n   }): Promise<{ token: string; expiresAt: string }>;\n-  /** Durably bind the staged token to the terminal audit ID before that audit is written. */\n+  /**\n+   * Durably bind the staged token to its terminal audit IDs while leaving it fail-closed.\n+   * A prepared record must never become verifiable from audit observation alone.\n+   */\n   prepareActivation(input: {\n@@ -199,3 +202,7 @@\n   }): Promise<void>;\n-  /** Atomically make an audited staged token verifiable; a rejected call must leave it unusable. */\n+  /**\n+   * The only transition that may make a staged token verifiable. This operation must be\n+   * atomic and idempotent; rejection guarantees the token remains unusable and cannot\n+   * become active later through reconciliation.\n+   */\n   activate(input: {\n","move_path":null},"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -887,5 +887,6 @@\n \n-  it('uses the bound denial audit when rejected activation cannot be cancelled or revoked', async () => {\n+  it('keeps rejected activation fail-closed when cancellation, revocation, and denial audit fail', async () => {\n     const capability = manifest({ destructive: true });\n     const outcomes: Array<{ id: string; outcome: string }> = [];\n+    let active = false;\n     const prepareActivation = vi.fn(async () => undefined);\n@@ -903,3 +904,5 @@\n         write: async (event) => {\n-          if (event.operationId === 'superconsole.confirmations.issue') outcomes.push({ id: event.id, outcome: event.outcome });\n+          if (event.operationId !== 'superconsole.confirmations.issue') return;\n+          if (event.outcome === 'denied') throw new Error('denial audit unavailable');\n+          outcomes.push({ id: event.id, outcome: event.outcome });\n         },\n@@ -913,3 +916,3 @@\n         revoke,\n-        verify: async () => false,\n+        verify: async () => active,\n       },\n@@ -924,8 +927,7 @@\n     expect(response.status).toBe(503);\n-    expect(await response.json()).toMatchObject({ error: { code: 'CONFIRMATION_ACTIVATION_FAILED' } });\n-    const deniedAuditId = outcomes.find((event) => event.outcome === 'denied')?.id;\n-    expect(deniedAuditId).toEqual(expect.any(String));\n+    expect(await response.json()).toMatchObject({ error: { code: 'AUDIT_UNAVAILABLE' } });\n+    expect(active).toBe(false);\n     expect(prepareActivation).toHaveBeenCalledWith(expect.objectContaining({\n       token: 'ambiguous-token',\n-      denialAuditId: deniedAuditId,\n+      denialAuditId: expect.any(String),\n     }));\n@@ -933,3 +935,3 @@\n     expect(revoke).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);\n-    expect(outcomes.map((event) => event.outcome)).toEqual(['attempted', 'succeeded', 'denied']);\n+    expect(outcomes.map((event) => event.outcome)).toEqual(['attempted', 'succeeded']);\n   });\n","move_path":null},"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -1147,3 +1147,3 @@\n       } catch {\n-        // The bound denial audit below remains an independent reconciliation fence.\n+        // activate() rejection is fail-closed; revocation is an additional cleanup attempt.\n       }\n","move_path":null},"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/superconsole/src/lib/server/README.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -42,6 +42,9 @@\n \n-Bound confirmation services stage unusable tokens in `issue`, atomically make\n-them verifiable in `activate`, and support idempotent `revoke`. Super Co