{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T15:30:21.292Z","ordinal":13403,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a024c5-b91b-72b3-ad56-490032d022a1","turn_id":"01a02f3d-64b6-73d3-92e9-b2fb7d88f458","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3d79d747-7c7d-4e5c-9546-c10f07c9a491","process_id":"55706","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","jq -s -r '\n[.[].data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[]]\n| map(select(.isResolved == false)\n  | . as $t\n  | [(.comments.nodes[] | select(.createdAt >= \"2026-08-23T13:02:45Z\"))] as $new\n  | select(($new|length)>0)\n  | \"THREAD\\t\\($t.id)\\t\\($t.path):\\($t.line // $t.originalLine // 0)\\n\"\n    + ($new | map(\"COMMENT\\t\\(.author.login)\\t\\(.createdAt)\\t\\(.outdated)\\t\\(.url)\\n\\(.body)\\n\") | join(\"\\n\"))\n) | .[]' /tmp/pr116-review-round.49a1DY/threads.jsonl\njq -r '.reviews[] | select(.submittedAt >= \"2026-08-23T13:02:45Z\" and (.body|length)>0) | \"REVIEW\\t\\(.author.login)\\t\\(.submittedAt)\\t\\(.state)\\n\\(.body)\\n\"' /tmp/pr116-review-round.49a1DY/pr.json"],"cwd":"file:///Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"jq -s -r '\n[.[].data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[]]\n| map(select(.isResolved == false)\n  | . as $t\n  | [(.comments.nodes[] | select(.createdAt >= \"2026-08-23T13:02:45Z\"))] as $new\n  | select(($new|length)>0)\n  | \"THREAD\\t\\($t.id)\\t\\($t.path):\\($t.line // $t.originalLine // 0)\\n\"\n    + ($new | map(\"COMMENT\\t\\(.author.login)\\t\\(.createdAt)\\t\\(.outdated)\\t\\(.url)\\n\\(.body)\\n\") | join(\"\\n\"))\n) | .[]' /tmp/pr116-review-round.49a1DY/threads.jsonl\njq -r '.reviews[] | select(.submittedAt >= \"2026-08-23T13:02:45Z\" and (.body|length)>0) | \"REVIEW\\t\\(.author.login)\\t\\(.submittedAt)\\t\\(.state)\\n\\(.body)\\n\"' /tmp/pr116-review-round.49a1DY/pr.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"THREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfcBH\tuifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts:550\nCOMMENT\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2026-08-23T13:09:35Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838574205\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Apply updated overlay inputs beyond `open`**\n\nWhen a mounted Dialog, Drawer, Popover, or other overlay receives updated inputs such as `modal`, `trapFocus`, `scrollLock`, `placement`, or `forceMount`, the adapter calls `controller.update(...)`, but this implementation synchronizes only `open`. The controller state, rendered ARIA attributes, focus trapping, and background isolation therefore retain their initial configuration; update the common overlay state for every supported mutable input before notifying subscribers.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfcBI\tuifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts:30\nCOMMENT\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2026-08-23T13:09:35Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838574206\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject calendar years outside the Date-backed range**\n\nWhen `year` is outside JavaScript's representable `Date` range, such as the six-digit year accepted by `parseUIFnIsoDate('999999-02-31')`, `daysInMonth` returns `NaN`; because `day > NaN` is false, this validation accepts even impossible dates. Subsequent formatting and day arithmetic then operate on an invalid `Date` or fail unpredictably, so reject years for which the computed month length is not finite or implement range-independent Gregorian arithmetic.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfcBJ\tuifn/dom/src/focus-scope.ts:284\nCOMMENT\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2026-08-23T13:09:35Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838574207\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep the prior focus scope active for disabled registrations**\n\nWhen a scope is registered with `enabled: false`, this unconditionally pauses the previous active scope even though `top()` excludes the new disabled record. The manager consequently has no active scope and the prior focus trap stops containing focus until the disabled record is destroyed; only pause the previous scope when the new record can become active, and recompute this relationship when `enabled` changes.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfcuM\thostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:241\nCOMMENT\tpullfrog\t2026-08-23T13:11:48Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838578528\nIncluding `targetId` in this check lets a newer attachment of the same hostname on another target go unnoticed, so stale compensation restores a second failed domain alongside the active replacement. Treat the hostname lifecycle consistently across targets, or explicitly reject cross-target reuse and cover this race.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Cross-target replacement bypasses stale-compensation fencing\n\n## Affected sites\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:236-245` — excludes only same-target hostname claims before restoring the stale record.\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:196-221` — permits the same hostname to be claimed under another target.\n- `hostfn/cli/src/__tests__/operator.test.ts:354-394` — replaces the stale domain only on the same target.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Stale compensation must not recreate an old domain record when any newer lifecycle owns the hostname in the active scope.\n- Add a replacement-race regression where the hostname moves to a different target.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nTHREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfcuN\tuifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts:77\nCOMMENT\tpullfrog\t2026-08-23T13:11:48Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838578531\nThe model and new tests accept year `0000`, but `Intl.DateTimeFormat` renders this corrected `Date` as year `1`; with no era in the default options, `formatUIFnDate()` now produces the same visible year as `0001`. Preserve year-zero semantics in localized output and add formatting coverage for the supported low-year boundary.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Year zero is localized as year one\n\n## Affected sites\n- `uifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts:75-77` — formats astronomical year zero without a BCE era.\n- `uifn/core/src/__tests__/phase-10-gesture-date-feedback.test.ts:154-161` — covers comparison and arithmetic but not localized formatting.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Localized output must distinguish supported year `0000` from year `0001` and represent its Gregorian era correctly.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nREVIEW\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2026-08-23T13:09:34Z\tCOMMENTED\n\n### 💡 Codex Review\n\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\n\n**Reviewed commit:** `31dc06e6c5`\n    \n\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\n<br/>\n\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\n- Open a pull request for review\n- Mark a draft as ready\n- Comment \"@codex review\".\n\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\n\n\n\n\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \"@codex address that feedback\".\n            \n</details>\n\nREVIEW\tpullfrog\t2026-08-23T13:11:49Z\tCOMMENTED\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> The latest fixes close the confirmation threads, but leave two correctness gaps in HostFn lifecycle reconciliation and low-year date formatting.\n\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `7c7ca08`:\n\n- **Fenced confirmation activation** — made successful atomic activation the only transition to a verifiable token and prohibited audit-driven activation during reconciliation.\n- **Guarded HostFn compensation** — added an atomic store operation intended to prevent stale failed intents from overwriting newer hostname lifecycles.\n- **Corrected UIFn edge behavior** — preserved years below 100, fixed fractional virtual-window bounds, and continued live-region publication after stale announcements.\n\n<!--\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 31dc06e;\nif commits have landed on SFNS-2 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\n\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\n- Files reviewed: 13\n- Commits reviewed: 1\n- Base: dev (72aabce)\n- Head: SFNS-2 (31dc06e)\n- Reviewed commits:\n  - 31dc06e — fix: close current PR review findings\n- Prior pullfrog review: 7c7ca08 (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#pullrequestreview-5002327554)\n-->\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [Fix all ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/116?action=fix&review_id=5002452534) ｜ [Fix 👍s ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/116?action=fix-approved&review_id=5002452534) ｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32641169116/job/97198376362) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"THREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfcBH\tuifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts:550\nCOMMENT\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2026-08-23T13:09:35Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838574205\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Apply updated overlay inputs beyond `open`**\n\nWhen a mounted Dialog, Drawer, Popover, or other overlay receives updated inputs such as `modal`, `trapFocus`, `scrollLock`, `placement`, or `forceMount`, the adapter calls `controller.update(...)`, but this implementation synchronizes only `open`. The controller state, rendered ARIA attributes, focus trapping, and background isolation therefore retain their initial configuration; update the common overlay state for every supported mutable input before notifying subscribers.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfcBI\tuifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts:30\nCOMMENT\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2026-08-23T13:09:35Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838574206\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject calendar years outside the Date-backed range**\n\nWhen `year` is outside JavaScript's representable `Date` range, such as the six-digit year accepted by `parseUIFnIsoDate('999999-02-31')`, `daysInMonth` returns `NaN`; because `day > NaN` is false, this validation accepts even impossible dates. Subsequent formatting and day arithmetic then operate on an invalid `Date` or fail unpredictably, so reject years for which the computed month length is not finite or implement range-independent Gregorian arithmetic.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfcBJ\tuifn/dom/src/focus-scope.ts:284\nCOMMENT\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2026-08-23T13:09:35Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838574207\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep the prior focus scope active for disabled registrations**\n\nWhen a scope is registered with `enabled: false`, this unconditionally pauses the previous active scope even though `top()` excludes the new disabled record. The manager consequently has no active scope and the prior focus trap stops containing focus until the disabled record is destroyed; only pause the previous scope when the new record can become active, and recompute this relationship when `enabled` changes.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\nTHREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfcuM\thostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:241\nCOMMENT\tpullfrog\t2026-08-23T13:11:48Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838578528\nIncluding `targetId` in this check lets a newer attachment of the same hostname on another target go unnoticed, so stale compensation restores a second failed domain alongside the active replacement. Treat the hostname lifecycle consistently across targets, or explicitly reject cross-target reuse and cover this race.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Cross-target replacement bypasses stale-compensation fencing\n\n## Affected sites\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:236-245` — excludes only same-target hostname claims before restoring the stale record.\n- `hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:196-221` — permits the same hostname to be claimed under another target.\n- `hostfn/cli/src/__tests__/operator.test.ts:354-394` — replaces the stale domain only on the same target.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Stale compensation must not recreate an old domain record when any newer lifecycle owns the hostname in the active scope.\n- Add a replacement-race regression where the hostname moves to a different target.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nTHREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfcuN\tuifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts:77\nCOMMENT\tpullfrog\t2026-08-23T13:11:48Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838578531\nThe model and new tests accept year `0000`, but `Intl.DateTimeFormat` renders this corrected `Date` as year `1`; with no era in the default options, `formatUIFnDate()` now produces the same visible year as `0001`. Preserve year-zero semantics in localized output and add formatting coverage for the supported low-year boundary.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Year zero is localized as year one\n\n## Affected sites\n- `uifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts:75-77` — formats astronomical year zero without a BCE era.\n- `uifn/core/src/__tests__/phase-10-gesture-date-feedback.test.ts:154-161` — covers comparison and arithmetic but not localized formatting.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Localized output must distinguish supported year `0000` from year `0001` and represent its Gregorian era correctly.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nREVIEW\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2026-08-23T13:09:34Z\tCOMMENTED\n\n### 💡 Codex Review\n\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\n\n**Reviewed commit:** `31dc06e6c5`\n    \n\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\n<br/>\n\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\n- Open a pull request for review\n- Mark a draft as ready\n- Comment \"@codex review\".\n\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\n\n\n\n\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \"@codex address that feedback\".\n            \n</details>\n\nREVIEW\tpullfrog\t2026-08-23T13:11:49Z\tCOMMENTED\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> The latest fixes close the confirmation threads, but leave two correctness gaps in HostFn lifecycle reconciliation and low-year date formatting.\n\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `7c7ca08`:\n\n- **Fenced confirmation activation** — made successful atomic activation the only transition to a verifiable token and prohibited audit-driven activation during reconciliation.\n- **Guarded HostFn compensation** — added an atomic store operation intended to prevent stale failed intents from overwriting newer hostname lifecycles.\n- **Corrected UIFn edge behavior** — preserved years below 100, fixed fractional virtual-window bounds, and continued live-region publication after stale announcements.\n\n<!--\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 31dc06e;\nif commit