s scope, modal/scroll lock, and positioner therefore retain stale behavior until close/reopen.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Live overlay resources do not follow mutable inputs\n\n## Affected sites\n- `uifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts:558-568` — publishes mutable policy and placement state after mount.\n- `uifn/dom/src/overlay.ts:220-270` — captures placement, focus-trap, modal, and scroll-lock settings only when resources are created.\n- `uifn/dom/src/overlay.ts:292-305` — updates dismissal and presence, but neither updates nor recreates those resources while `open` remains true.\n\n## Required outcome\n- An already-open overlay must reconcile focus trapping, modal isolation, scroll locking, and positioning with the latest controller inputs without requiring close/reopen.\n- Add DOM-level coverage that changes these inputs while open and observes the resource behavior, not only controller state.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nTHREAD\tPRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgWj2\tuifn/dom/src/focus-scope.ts:341\nCOMMENT\tpullfrog\t2026-08-23T15:50:22Z\tfalse\thttps://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838923305\n`paused` also records automatic stack suspension, so a middle scope that was paused by a newer child can remain stuck after disable/re-enable; disabling or destroying the child can also clear an explicit parent pause. Preserve explicit pause state separately from nesting activation and cover three-level transitions.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Enabled transitions conflate explicit and automatic pauses\n\n## Affected sites\n- `uifn/dom/src/focus-scope.ts:324-348` — `pause()` and nesting transitions share one `paused` flag; re-enabling skips a record that retained automatic pause.\n- `uifn/dom/src/focus-scope.ts:357-365` — destroying a child unconditionally clears the newest enabled parent's pause, including an explicit one.\n- `uifn/dom/src/focus-scope.test.ts:21-46` — covers only two levels and no explicit pause/resume sequence.\n\n## Required outcome\n- The active scope must be the newest enabled scope that is not explicitly paused across register, enable, disable, pause, resume, and destroy transitions.\n- Add three-level regressions for re-enabling an automatically paused middle scope and for removing a child above an explicitly paused parent.\n````\n\n</details>\n\nREVIEW\tcubic-dev-ai\t2026-08-23T15:38:39Z\tCOMMENTED\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:start -->\n**4 issues found across 8 files (changes from recent commits).**\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)</summary>\n\n```text\n\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\n\n\n<file name=\"uifn/dom/src/focus-scope.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/dom/src/focus-scope.ts:341\">\nP2: When a scope is disabled while a newer scope is active, it can retain the newer-scope pause flag and never become active again after that newer scope is disabled. Track stack-induced pause separately from explicit pause, or reconcile the stale pause when re-enabling the scope.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts:550\">\nP2: When an untyped AlertDialog update contains an outside-dismiss flag, the assertion throws after `currentProps` is mutated and permanently poisons subsequent updates. Validate a merged candidate first, then assign it to `currentProps` only after validation succeeds.</violation>\n\n<violation number=\"2\" location=\"uifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts:563\">\nP2: After `dialog.update({ closeOnInteractOutside: false })`, the base stops outside dismissal while `dialog.state.closeOnOutsideInteraction` still reports `true`. Synchronize Dialog's derived outside-interaction behavior with mutable overlay inputs, or reject this input instead of updating only the base state.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts:30\">\nP2: At the upper supported `Date` range, this validation rejects valid dates in the final representable month because `daysInMonth` overflows while constructing the month end. Compute the Gregorian month length without constructing an out-of-range date, then let the `instant` check reject only dates whose actual instant is out of range.</violation>\n</file>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/116/ai_pr_review_1787499390757_af5f963c-0984-499d-97e6-fd49f50ed028?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F116)</sub>\n\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787499390757_af5f963c-0984-499d-97e6-fd49f50ed028:66ccad4aae4ce32c4bdc524ca7c36d91b8be34f5:dda8f212-5e9c-4ac9-9bbc-1a75257593ad -->\n\nREVIEW\tchatgpt-codex-connector\t2026-08-23T15:39:30Z\tCOMMENTED\n\n### 💡 Codex Review\n\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\n\n**Reviewed commit:** `66ccad4aae`\n    \n\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\n<br/>\n\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\n- Open a pull request for review\n- Mark a draft as ready\n- Comment \"@codex review\".\n\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\n\n\n\n\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \"@codex address that feedback\".\n            \n</details>\n\nREVIEW\tpullfrog\t2026-08-23T15:50:23Z\tCOMMENTED\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> The latest fixes close both prior threads, but mutable overlay resources and nested focus-scope activation still diverge from their updated controller state.\n\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `31dc06e`:\n\n- **Enforced hostname ownership** — rejected cross-target hostname reuse and fenced stale HostFn compensation against any replacement in the active scope.\n- **Corrected low-year dates** — validated expanded dates through JavaScript's representable range and distinguished astronomical year zero with a BCE era.\n- **Synchronized overlay inputs** — updated mutable overlay controller state and callbacks after mount.\n- **Adjusted focus activation** — kept disabled registrations from pausing active scopes and transferred activity when registrations are enabled or disabled.\n\n<!--\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 66ccad4;\nif commits have landed on SFNS-2 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\n\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\n- Files reviewed: 1803\n- Commits reviewed: 35\n- Base: dev (72aabce)\n- Head: SFNS-2 (66ccad4)\n- Reviewed commits:\n  - 66ccad4 — fix: address latest PR review findings\n  - 31dc06e — fix: close current PR review findings\n  - 7c7ca08 — fix: close latest PR review gaps\n  - d9b60c5 — fix: resolve current PR review feedback\n  - 2011d9c — fix: address latest PR review findings\n  - afb902d — fix: close current PR review gaps\n  - 16a31f1 — fix: address latest PR review findings\n  - db08968 — fix: close reconciliation review gaps\n  - 73485e8 — fix: reconcile pending admin side effects\n  - fbb3868 — fix: resolve single-pass PR review findings\n  - 9cf9e61 — fix: close single-pass review findings\n  - 966f314 — fix: resolve final admin review round\n  - b1157c7 — fix: resolve latest admin review findings\n  - 09ff931 — fix: close post-push admin review gaps\n  - e3e7054 — fix: harden final admin re