{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T17:33:32.440Z","ordinal":13961,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a024c5-b91b-72b3-ad56-490032d022a1","turn_id":"01a02fae-186f-7650-a011-b5cdec75b51c","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f81e7bb3-a5be-4765-812d-2ccd340e4984","process_id":"42719","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","git show -s --format='%H%n%cI' HEAD\njq -rs '[.[] | select(.isResolved|not) | {id,path,line,originalLine,isOutdated,latest:(.comments.nodes|max_by(.createdAt)|{id,author:.author.login,createdAt,outdated,url,body})}] | sort_by(.latest.createdAt) | reverse | .[:40]' /tmp/pr116-review-round.VLvEzi/threads.jsonl"],"cwd":"file:///Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show -s --format='%H%n%cI' HEAD\njq -rs '[.[] | select(.isResolved|not) | {id,path,line,originalLine,isOutdated,latest:(.comments.nodes|max_by(.createdAt)|{id,author:.author.login,createdAt,outdated,url,body})}] | sort_by(.latest.createdAt) | reverse | .[:40]' /tmp/pr116-review-round.VLvEzi/threads.jsonl"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"60d32b4058286bff8cfc8b48a347a4e0bff22230\n2026-08-23T22:00:19+05:30\n[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgpD6\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/presence.ts\",\n    \"line\": 58,\n    \"originalLine\": 58,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0vz1\",\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:41:28Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839032565\",\n      \"body\": \"CSS uses `transition-property` and `animation-name` as the master lists, so duration and delay list lengths can exceed the number of events the browser emits. After the real motion ends, Presence can therefore remain `entering` or `exiting` until the fallback timer fires.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Presence waits for nonexistent motion events\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `uifn/dom/src/presence.ts:41-63` — derives event counts only from duration and delay lists.\\n- `uifn/dom/src/presence.ts:101-127` — requires every derived event or waits for `duration + 50ms`.\\n- `uifn/dom/src/presence.test.ts:33-52` — manually emits two events without defining two transitioning properties.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Complete promptly after the element's actual relevant motions finish without requiring events that CSS cannot emit.\\n- Add coverage where one `transition-property` has excess duration entries and produces only one end event.\\n\\n## References\\n- https://drafts.csswg.org/css-transitions/#transitions\\n- https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/animation-name\\n````\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgpD5\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/browser/overlay-harness.ts\",\n    \"line\": 206,\n    \"originalLine\": 206,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0vzy\",\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:41:28Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839032562\",\n      \"body\": \"`Dialog` has `policy.position: 'none'`, so this binding never creates a positioner and `dataset.side` remains unset. This makes the Playwright overlay matrix fail without covering live placement reconciliation; exercise placement on a positioned primitive while retaining the Dialog modal assertions.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgpD2\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/primitives/dialog.ts\",\n    \"line\": 152,\n    \"originalLine\": 152,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0vzu\",\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:41:28Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839032558\",\n      \"body\": \"`outsideInteractionBehavior` is applied only to the derived `behavior` after the base update has already persisted its dismissal flag. `dialog.update({ outsideInteractionBehavior: 'ignore' })` consequently reports `ignore` while `actions.onOutsideInteraction()` still closes the open Dialog.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Dialog outside-interaction aliases diverge after update\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `uifn/core/src/primitives/dialog.ts:150-155` — updates the derived behavior without synchronizing the base flag.\\n- `uifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts:451-468` — dismissal actions read the unchanged base `closeOnInteractOutside` value.\\n- `uifn/core/src/primitives/dialog.test.ts:55-89` — updates all aliases together, masking single-property updates.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Every supported outside-interaction input must leave the public Dialog state and dismissal actions with one consistent behavior.\\n- Cover updating `outsideInteractionBehavior` by itself in both closing and non-closing directions.\\n````\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgnj9\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n    \"line\": 176,\n    \"originalLine\": 176,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tqG\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:37:04Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023750\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Count Unicode code points for schema string lengths**\\n\\nWhen a schema constrains text containing supplementary Unicode characters, `String.length` counts UTF-16 code units rather than the Unicode code points required by JSON Schema. For example, `\\\"😀\\\"` is incorrectly rejected by `maxLength: 1` and incorrectly accepted by `minLength: 2`, so valid international input can fail administration operations; compute the length with code-point semantics such as `Array.from(value).length`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgnj8\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts\",\n    \"line\": 51,\n    \"originalLine\": 51,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tqF\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:37:04Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023749\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Encode negative calendar years with an ISO sign**\\n\\nWhen a date input is decremented from year 0 to year -1, which `createUIFnCalendarDate` and the controller actions permit, this produces `00-1-01-01`. That value is neither accepted by `parseUIFnIsoDate` nor interpreted correctly by the date picker's hyphen-splitting cell parser, and it is also submitted through the hidden form input. Serialize BCE years using signed expanded ISO notation, or reject negative years consistently.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgnj7\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/core/src/diff.ts\",\n    \"line\": 272,\n    \"originalLine\": 272,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tqC\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:37:04Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023746\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve open input compatibility on property removal**\\n\\nWhen an optional input property is removed while the new schema leaves `additionalProperties` enabled or unspecified, payloads containing that property remain valid because it becomes an unconstrained additional property. This unconditional classification nevertheless marks the manifest incompatible, so CI consumers can reject a schema-compatible release; determine input severity from the new `additionalProperties` policy rather than always reporting `breaking`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgnj3\",\n    \"path\": \"authfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n    \"line\": 459,\n    \"originalLine\": 459,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tp9\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:37:04Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023741\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind AuthFn user cursors to scope and query**\\n\\nWhen a cursor is reused after changing the active region, email filter, or sort direction, this forwards it unchanged to `listAuthFnAdminUsers`; that implementation encodes only `createdAt` and `id` (`authfn/core/src/core/admin-users.ts:230-252`). The timestamp is then interpreted against the new result set or opposite ordering, causing users to be skipped or repeated. Include the region and query identity in the cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgndQ\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/overlay.ts\",\n    \"line\": 307,\n    \"originalLine\": 307,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tgt\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023149\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=71a9af0e-6f10-42c9-b955-ccf0c826c765 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: When a positioned overlay opens, this launches two concurrent position calculations because `start()` performs an initial auto-update while the explicit update is still pending. The positioner marks the first result stale and reports a recoverable error on every initial open; chain `start()` after the initial update so only one calculation runs.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/src/overlay.ts, line 296:\\n\\n<comment>When a positioned overlay opens, this launches two concurrent position calculations because `start()` performs an initial auto-update while the explicit update is still pending. The positioner marks the first result stale and reports a recoverable error on every initial open; chain `start()` after the initial update so only one calculation runs.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -268,7 +281,29 @@ export function createUIFnOverlayDomBinding<TState extends UIFnOverlayBaseState>\\n+      modal = null;\\n     }\\n+    ensurePositioner();\\n+    void positioner?.update({\\n+      reference: options.reference ?? trigger,\\n+      floating,\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    void positioner?.update({\\n      reference: options.reference ?? trigger,\\n      floating,\\n      arrow: options.arrow,\\n      placement: current.placement,\\n      strategy: options.strategy,\\n      sideOffset: options.sideOffset,\\n      alignOffset: options.alignOffset,\\n      collisionPadding: options.collisionPadding,\\n      autoUpdate: true,\\n    }).then(() => positioner?.start()).catch((error) => scope.environment.error(error));\\n```\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgndM\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/positioning-rebind.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": 15,\n    \"originalLine\": 15,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tgp\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023145\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=6411273e-5e87-4796-ae12-94a7c0d34b32 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} -->\\nP2: This test couples the public positioning suite to Floating UI's private `autoUpdate` API. A provider refactor could preserve the UIFn contract while unnecessarily breaking this test; verify rebinding through the public positioner contract and observable cleanup instead.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/src/positioning-rebind.test.ts, line 15:\\n\\n<comment>This test couples the public positioning suite to Floating UI's private `autoUpdate` API. A provider refactor could preserve the UIFn contract while unnecessarily breaking this test; verify rebinding through the public positioner contract and observable cleanup instead.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@\\n+  })),\\n+}));\\n+\\n+vi.mock('@floating-ui/dom', () => ({\\n+  arrow: vi.fn(() => ({ name: 'arrow' })),\\n+  autoUpdate: floatingMocks.autoUpdate,\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgndL\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/primitives/dialog.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": 64,\n    \"originalLine\": 64,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tgo\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023144\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=dd93596d-d7c7-421c-90db-ec7f06c29188 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: This adds new mutable outside-interaction inputs without verifying them, so a regression could leave the dialog dismissible outside while the test still passes. Assert `closeOnOutsideInteraction: false` and `outsideInteractionBehavior: 'ignore'` in the state matcher.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/core/src/primitives/dialog.test.ts, line 64:\\n\\n<comment>This adds new mutable outside-interaction inputs without verifying them, so a regression could leave the dialog dismissible outside while the test still passes. Assert `closeOnOutsideInteraction: false` and `outsideInteractionBehavior: 'ignore'` in the state matcher.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -61,6 +61,8 @@ describe('dialog primitive', () => {\\n       scrollLock: false,\\n       closeOnEscape: false,\\n       closeOnInteractOutside: false,\\n+      closeOnOutsideInteraction: false,\\n+      outsideInteractionBehavior: 'ignore',\\n       placement: 'top-start',\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgndI\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/presence.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": 31,\n    \"originalLine\": 31,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tgj\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023139\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=a716b615-e351-49ef-8ad5-da247f397c59 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} -->\\nP2: This test does not verify the timeout fallback or the longest-motion delay: a broken timeout implementation, or one scheduling the wrong delay, still passes. Capture the scheduled callback and delay, assert the expected delay, and invoke the callback in a separate no-event case.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/src/presence.test.ts, line 31:\\n\\n<comment>This test does not verify the timeout fallback or the longest-motion delay: a broken timeout implementation, or one scheduling the wrong delay, still passes. Capture the scheduled callback and delay, assert the expected delay, and invoke the callback in a separate no-event case.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@\\n+          cleanup();\\n+        };\\n+      },\\n+      setTimeout: vi.fn(() => () => undefined),\\n+      window: {\\n+        getComputedStyle: () => ({\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgndH\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/positioning.ts\",\n    \"line\": 240,\n    \"originalLine\": 240,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tgi\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023138\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=c33450cf-f0a0-4711-8922-3ac1eb138570 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP1: When a running positioner uses a resolver that creates a fresh virtual anchor, every automatic update enters this rebinding branch and recursively creates another `autoUpdate`; context-menu positioning can therefore overflow the stack. Rebind based on the actual observer target or resolver configuration, not virtual-anchor object identity, and add a regression test for a fresh virtual anchor resolver.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/src/positioning.ts, line 240:\\n\\n<comment>When a running positioner uses a resolver that creates a fresh virtual anchor, every automatic update enters this rebinding branch and recursively creates another `autoUpdate`; context-menu positioning can therefore overflow the stack. Rebind based on the actual observer target or resolver configuration, not virtual-anchor object identity, and add a regression test for a fresh virtual anchor resolver.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -229,6 +235,27 @@ export function createUIFnPositioner(\\n     }\\n+    const restartAutoUpdate = running && (\\n+      autoUpdateConfigChanged\\n+      || reference !== boundReference\\n+      || floating !== boundFloating\\n+    );\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgndE\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/presence.ts\",\n    \"line\": 49,\n    \"originalLine\": 49,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tgf\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023135\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=4adb0be6-bb0c-46ea-ab6f-33c5732e79d4 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP1: When a CSS motion-property list is longer than its duration list, CSS repeats durations, but `pairedMotion` counts only duration/delay entries. Short repeated events can therefore reach zero before the longest animation or transition ends; derive the expected event count from `animation-name`/`transition-property`, or retain timer-based completion instead of finishing from this count.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/src/presence.ts, line 49:\\n\\n<comment>When a CSS motion-property list is longer than its duration list, CSS repeats durations, but `pairedMotion` counts only duration/delay entries. Short repeated events can therefore reach zero before the longest animation or transition ends; derive the expected event count from `animation-name`/`transition-property`, or retain timer-based completion instead of finishing from this count.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -38,25 +38,29 @@ function parseTimeList(value: string): number[] {\\n+    const total = (durations[index % durations.length] ?? 0)\\n+      + (delays[index % delays.length] ?? 0);\\n+    maximum = Math.max(maximum, total);\\n+    if (total > 0) active += 1;\\n   }\\n-  return maximum;\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgnc_\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/browser/overlay-harness.ts\",\n    \"line\": 206,\n    \"originalLine\": 206,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tga\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023130\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=38ccd4c8-1bfa-42a3-914d-76b5718972c5 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} -->\\nP1: The Dialog policy does not support positioning, so this assertion always sees an unset `data-side` and makes `runOverlayVectors` fail during the Dialog iteration. Assert `controller.state.placement` instead, or move this DOM-placement check to a positioned primitive such as Popover.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/browser/overlay-harness.ts, line 206:\\n\\n<comment>The Dialog policy does not support positioning, so this assertion always sees an unset `data-side` and makes `runOverlayVectors` fail during the Dialog iteration. Assert `controller.state.placement` instead, or move this DOM-placement check to a positioned primitive such as Popover.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -198,6 +199,16 @@ async function exerciseOpenPrimitive(\\n+    controller.update({ modal: false, trapFocus: false, scrollLock: false, placement: 'top-start' });\\n+    await wait(20);\\n+    invariant(platform.modals.size === 0, 'Dialog retained modal resources after an open update');\\n+    invariant(fixture.positioner.dataset.side === 'top', 'Dialog did not apply an open placement update');\\n+    controller.update({ modal: true, trapFocus: true, scrollLock: true });\\n+    await wait(20);\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    invariant(controller.state.placement === 'top-start', 'Dialog did not apply an open placement update');\\n```\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgWj0\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts\",\n    \"line\": 559,\n    \"originalLine\": 558,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0VIh\",\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T15:50:22Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838923297\",\n      \"body\": \"`update()` now changes `modal`, `trapFocus`, `scrollLock`, and `placement` while an overlay is open, but the DOM binding only acquires the corresponding resources on the closed-to-open transition. The existing focus scope, modal/scroll lock, and positioner therefore retain stale behavior until close/reopen.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Live overlay resources do not follow mutable inputs\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `uifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts:558-568` — publishes mutable policy and placement state after mount.\\n- `uifn/dom/src/overlay.ts:220-270` — captures placement, focus-trap, modal, and scroll-lock settings only when resources are created.\\n- `uifn/dom/src/overlay.ts:292-305` — updates dismissal and presence, but neither updates nor recreates those resources while `open` remains true.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- An already-open overlay must reconcile focus trapping, modal isolation, scroll locking, and positioning with the latest controller inputs without requiring close/reopen.\\n- Add DOM-level coverage that changes these inputs while open and observes the resource behavior, not only controller state.\\n````\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgSkC\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/positioning.ts\",\n    \"line\": 224,\n    \"originalLine\": 218,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0PWN\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T15:39:31Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838899597\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Rebind auto-update when positioning targets change**\\n\\nWhen `update()` replaces `reference` or `floating` on a running positioner, this computes one result using the new targets but leaves Floating UI's `autoUpdate` subscription attached to the old elements from `start()`. Subsequent resize or movement of the new anchor does not trigger repositioning, so the floating element becomes stale; restart the subscription when target or auto-update-related options change.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgSkA\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/presence.ts\",\n    \"line\": 116,\n    \"originalLine\": 106,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0PWL\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T15:39:31Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838899595\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Wait for the longest CSS motion before unmounting**\\n\\nWhen an element transitions multiple properties with different durations, or runs an animation and transition together, the first `transitionend` or `animationend` on the element calls `finish()` even though `motionDuration` deliberately calculated the longest completion time. Exit content is therefore marked unmounted and can disappear as soon as the shortest motion ends; completion needs to wait for all relevant motions or the computed maximum-duration fallback.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgSj_\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/scope.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 296,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0PWK\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T15:39:30Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838899594\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Retire released cleanups from the scope registry**\\n\\nWhen a long-lived DOM scope repeatedly opens and closes overlays, completes presence transitions, or restarts positioners, every released resource remains in `cleanups` until the entire scope is destroyed. Because `once` also retains its callback after release, these entries can retain observers, elements, and other captured objects, causing memory usage to grow with total historical resource acquisitions rather than active resources; remove each entry when its release function runs.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgSRT\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts\",\n    \"line\": 564,\n    \"originalLine\": 563,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0O6p\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T15:38:39Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838897833\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=f6be4088-2627-4d4e-931c-1a0283f2709d -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=dda8f212-5e9c-4ac9-9bbc-1a75257593ad -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: After `dialog.update({ closeOnInteractOutside: false })`, the base stops outside dismissal while `dialog.state.closeOnOutsideInteraction` still reports `true`. Synchronize Dialog's derived outside-interaction behavior with mutable overlay inputs, or reject this input instead of updating only the base state.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts, line 563:\\n\\n<comment>After `dialog.update({ closeOnInteractOutside: false })`, the base stops outside dismissal while `dialog.state.closeOnOutsideInteraction` still reports `true`. Synchronize Dialog's derived outside-interaction behavior with mutable overlay inputs, or reject this input instead of updating only the base state.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -546,6 +547,31 @@ export function createUIFnOverlayBase<TProps extends UIFnOverlayCommonProps>(\\n+            trapFocus: currentProps.trapFocus ?? (nextModal && policyValue.trapFocus),\\n+            scrollLock: currentProps.scrollLock ?? (nextModal && policyValue.scrollLock),\\n+            closeOnEscape: currentProps.closeOnEscape ?? policyValue.closeOnEscape,\\n+            closeOnInteractOutside: nextOutside,\\n+            placement: currentProps.placement ?? options.defaultPlacement ?? 'bottom',\\n+            forceMount: currentProps.forceMount ?? false,\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfcBJ\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/focus-scope.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 284,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7ky_5_\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T13:09:35Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838574207\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep the prior focus scope active for disabled registrations**\\n\\nWhen a scope is registered with `enabled: false`, this unconditionally pauses the previous active scope even though `top()` excludes the new disabled record. The manager consequently has no active scope and the prior focus trap stops containing focus until the disabled record is destroyed; only pause the previous scope when the new record can become active, and recompute this relationship when `enabled` changes.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfcBI\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts\",\n    \"line\": 39,\n    \"originalLine\": 30,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7ky_5-\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T13:09:35Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838574206\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject calendar years outside the Date-backed range**\\n\\nWhen `year` is outside JavaScript's representable `Date` range, such as the six-digit year accepted by `parseUIFnIsoDate('999999-02-31')`, `daysInMonth` returns `NaN`; because `day > NaN` is false, this validation accepts even impossible dates. Subsequent formatting and day arithmetic then operate on an invalid `Date` or fail unpredictably, so reject years for which the computed month length is not finite or implement range-independent Gregorian arithmetic.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfcBH\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts\",\n    \"line\": 577,\n    \"originalLine\": 550,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7ky_59\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T13:09:35Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838574205\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Apply updated overlay inputs beyond `open`**\\n\\nWhen a mounted Dialog, Drawer, Popover, or other overlay receives updated inputs such as `modal`, `trapFocus`, `scrollLock`, `placement`, or `forceMount`, the adapter calls `controller.update(...)`, but this implementation synchronizes only `open`. The controller state, rendered ARIA attributes, focus trapping, and background isolation therefore retain their initial configuration; update the common overlay state for every supported mutable input before notifying subscribers.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfEZO\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts\",\n    \"line\": 62,\n    \"originalLine\": 35,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kydiy\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T11:54:58Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838433458\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve years below 100 in calendar arithmetic**\\n\\nWhen an accepted ISO date has a year from 0000 through 0099, `Date.UTC` applies JavaScript's 1900-year offset. Thus `compareUIFnDates` considers year 0001 equal to 1901, and `addUIFnDateDays` jumps a year-0001 date into 1901. Construct dates using `setUTCFullYear` or reject this range consistently instead of accepting values that calendar operations reinterpret.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfEZN\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/algorithms/virtualization.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 36,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kydiw\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T11:54:58Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838433456\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Include partially visible rows in the virtual window**\\n\\nWhen `scrollOffset` is not aligned to `estimateSize`, `visible` counts only the viewport's full-size quotient and ignores the partial row at the leading edge. For example, with size 10, viewport 10, offset 5, and `overscan: 0`, this returns only index 0 even though index 1 is also visible, producing a blank region while scrolling; calculate the end from the viewport's absolute trailing offset or add the partial leading item.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfEZL\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/live-region.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 84,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kydiv\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T11:54:58Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838433455\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Continue publishing after skipping a cleared announcement**\\n\\nWhen announcement A is queued before B and `clear(A)` runs before A is rendered, A becomes stale but remains in `queue`; the scheduled publisher shifts A and returns here without scheduling another pass, leaving B permanently unannounced. The same stall occurs if A is cleared while its animation frame is pending, so clearing one message must still advance the queue.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bevtk\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/theme/src/mount.ts\",\n    \"line\": 88,\n    \"originalLine\": 87,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kx_hm\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T10:47:40Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838310502\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Resolve token references before emitting CSS variables**\\n\\nWhen a valid runtime theme uses a typed reference such as `{color.surface.canvas}` with the required fallback metadata, validation resolves it only for checking, but this code flattens the original theme and emits the brace expression literally. The resulting custom property is unusable when consumed as a color or dimension, so mounted referenced tokens do not apply; emit values from `resolveTokenReferences(theme).theme` (or translate references to valid CSS `var()` expressions).\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bevtj\",\n    \"path\": \"datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 64,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kx_hl\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T10:47:40Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838310501\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind DataFn metadata cursors to their collection**\\n\\nWhen a schema has more than one page of metadata, a cursor returned by `datafn.resources.list` can be reused with `datafn.relations.list`, `datafn.indices.list`, or `datafn.capabilities.list` in the same scope, because the cursor carries only an offset. The unrelated collection is then sliced from that offset, silently skipping its initial entries; include the operation or collection identity in these cursors and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIT\",\n    \"path\": \"apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 160,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kxaU2\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158134\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind ApiFn cursors to their resource and scope**\\n\\nWhen the offset returned by `listSpecs` is supplied to `listEnvironments`, or reused after switching to another authorized scope, this parser accepts it unchanged and skips that many unrelated records. Because the helper emits only a decimal offset for both collections, clients cannot distinguish these invalid cursor uses; include the operation and active scope in an opaque cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIS\",\n    \"path\": \"botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 154,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kxaU1\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158133\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind BotFn cursors to their collection query**\\n\\nWhen a channels cursor issued for `botId=A` is reused with `botId=B`, or a cursor from the bots list is supplied to the channels list, this shared parser accepts the raw offset and slices the unrelated result set from that position. The same cursor can also be reused in another authorized scope, yielding skipped or empty pages there; encode the operation, scope, and channel filter identity into the cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIQ\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n    \"line\": 134,\n    \"originalLine\": 131,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kxaUz\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158131\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject non-JSON primitive leaves in open schemas**\\n\\nWhen an adapter returns a `bigint` under a type-less or `additionalProperties: true` child schema, validation accepts it because only object prototypes and non-finite numbers are rejected. Fresh evidence after the plain-object fix is that the new guards still omit `bigint`, `symbol`, `function`, and `undefined`; the open entity schemas used by DataFn, BillFn, and SearchFn therefore allow values that cannot be represented by the REST/MCP envelopes, with a `bigint` causing the subsequent `JSON.stringify` to throw instead of producing the validated result. Reject every primitive type outside the JSON value set even when the schema omits `type`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIN\",\n    \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\n    \"line\": 395,\n    \"originalLine\": 395,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kxaUw\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158128\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Expose create and upsert operations before a record exists**\\n\\nWhen an ID-targeted operation can create a new record, this classifies it exclusively as a detail-page action, while module-level actions accept only collection targets or resources with no list/detail route. Consequently operations such as `botfn.bots.upsert`, `botfn.channels.connect`, `apifn.specs.register`, and `apifn.environments.upsert` are only reachable after navigating to an existing record whose ID is then prebound; an empty collection has no console path for creating its first record. Project these creation/upsert operations as collection actions while leaving their ID fields editable.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_n\",\n    \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n    \"line\": 494,\n    \"originalLine\": 444,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwxiJ\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991049\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile variables when metadata persistence fails**\\n\\nWhen `executor.setVariable` succeeds for a new variable but this store write rejects, the provider retains the live secret while the operator returns an error and has no record through which to list or delete it. A retry is not guaranteed safe because `setVariable` has no idempotency contract; persist a durable intent before the provider call or compensate/reconcile the provider variable if final persistence fails.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_l\",\n    \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 105,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwxiH\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991047\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Compare action enum objects structurally**\\n\\nWhen an action field declares an object or array in `enum` or `const`, the form parses the operator's JSON into a new object and these `Object.is` checks always reject it by reference, even when it is structurally identical to the declared value. The administration validator permits these JSON-valued members, so such operations pass manifest validation but cannot be submitted through the generic action UI; use the same structural JSON equality semantics as the runtime validator.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_i\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n    \"line\": 271,\n    \"originalLine\": 262,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwxiE\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991044\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject non-plain objects as JSON values**\\n\\nWhen an in-process dispatcher caller supplies a `Date`, `Map`, or other class instance under `type: \\\"object\\\"`, this branch accepts it as a valid JSON object because it never checks the prototype. The immutable snapshot preserves such instances, and output redaction converts them through `Object.entries`—for example, a valid-looking `Date` response becomes `{}`—so adapters can receive or return values that change shape at transport time; require arrays or plain/null-prototype objects throughout JSON validation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdoWJ\",\n    \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 414,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwYRk\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T06:40:38Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837887588\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile variable records after provider deletion**\\n\\nWhen the provider deletion succeeds but `store.deleteVariable` rejects, the stale variable record remains while this request returns an error. Retrying with the same idempotency key replays that error, and retrying with a new key can still never remove the record when the provider reports that the already-deleted variable is not found, because this path does not tolerate provider-not-found as `detachDomain` does. Treat an already-absent provider variable as success or persist a deletion intent so the store record can be reconciled.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdgrE\",\n    \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 40,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwNOB\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T06:10:24Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837842305\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Resolve composed schemas before deciding an action has no fields**\\n\\nWhen a valid operation input schema declares its named properties through `allOf`, this returns no editable fields because only top-level `properties` is inspected. The generic action then either submits `{}` immediately or shows a dialog without the required controls, so operations using a schema composition accepted by the manifest validator cannot be invoked from Super Console; merge compatible `allOf` object properties and requirements before constructing the fields.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdgrD\",\n    \"path\": \"filefn/server/src/index.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 334,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwNOA\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T06:10:24Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837842304\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restrict the public processing service to authorized methods**\\n\\nWhen an application exposes this newly public service through an in-process integration, callers can invoke `processing.listArtifacts(fileId, ctx)` directly even though that method explicitly ignores `ctx` and queries all artifacts for the file; only `listArtifactsForFile` calls `requireReadableFile`. Publishing the full `ProcessingService` therefore bypasses the authorization enforced by both the HTTP routes and the admin adapter, so expose an authorization-safe facade or keep the worker-level methods private.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdRKH\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 86,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kv2vJ\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T05:06:53Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837750217\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Compare object-valued enum members structurally**\\n\\nWhen an operation schema declares an object or array in `enum`, JSON-decoded input that is structurally identical is rejected because `Object.is` compares those values by reference. `AdminJsonSchema` permits arbitrary enum values and manifest validation does not restrict them to scalars, so such a valid schema becomes unusable through REST or MCP; compare enum members using JSON structural equality instead.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bc5vf\",\n    \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 1062,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kvVRa\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T03:26:35Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837613146\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Make confirmation issuance recoverable after audit failures**\\n\\nWhen `performConfirmOperation` successfully creates a valid confirmation token but this terminal audit write fails, the endpoint returns an error and discards the only receipt while the token remains live and the audit trail contains only the attempted event. Retrying issues another token, so a transient sink failure accumulates valid, unreturned credentials without a successful issuance record; make issuance replay-safe or revoke/reconcile the issued token before returning the failure.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bc5vd\",\n    \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 299,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kvVRY\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T03:26:35Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837613144\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile attached domains when persistence fails**\\n\\nWhen the provider successfully attaches the domain but `putDomain` rejects, this operation returns an error while leaving a live domain with no corresponding store record. The failed idempotent invocation is then fenced as an error, and retrying with a new key can attach a duplicate; meanwhile the console cannot discover or detach the original domain. Persist a durable pending intent before calling the executor, or compensate the provider attachment when the final write fails.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  }\n]\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"60d32b4058286bff8cfc8b48a347a4e0bff22230\n2026-08-23T22:00:19+05:30\n[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgpD6\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/presence.ts\",\n    \"line\": 58,\n    \"originalLine\": 58,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0vz1\",\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:41:28Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839032565\",\n      \"body\": \"CSS uses `transition-property` and `animation-name` as the master lists, so duration and delay list lengths can exceed the number of events the browser emits. After the real motion ends, Presence can therefore remain `entering` or `exiting` until the fallback timer fires.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Presence waits for nonexistent motion events\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `uifn/dom/src/presence.ts:41-63` — derives event counts only from duration and delay lists.\\n- `uifn/dom/src/presence.ts:101-127` — requires every derived event or waits for `duration + 50ms`.\\n- `uifn/dom/src/presence.test.ts:33-52` — manually emits two events without defining two transitioning properties.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Complete promptly after the element's actual relevant motions finish without requiring events that CSS cannot emit.\\n- Add coverage where one `transition-property` has excess duration entries and produces only one end event.\\n\\n## References\\n- https://drafts.csswg.org/css-transitions/#transitions\\n- https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/animation-name\\n````\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgpD5\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/browser/overlay-harness.ts\",\n    \"line\": 206,\n    \"originalLine\": 206,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0vzy\",\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:41:28Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839032562\",\n      \"body\": \"`Dialog` has `policy.position: 'none'`, so this binding never creates a positioner and `dataset.side` remains unset. This makes the Playwright overlay matrix fail without covering live placement reconciliation; exercise placement on a positioned primitive while retaining the Dialog modal assertions.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgpD2\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/primitives/dialog.ts\",\n    \"line\": 152,\n    \"originalLine\": 152,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0vzu\",\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:41:28Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839032558\",\n      \"body\": \"`outsideInteractionBehavior` is applied only to the derived `behavior` after the base update has already persisted its dismissal flag. `dialog.update({ outsideInteractionBehavior: 'ignore' })` consequently reports `ignore` while `actions.onOutsideInteraction()` still closes the open Dialog.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Dialog outside-interaction aliases diverge after update\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `uifn/core/src/primitives/dialog.ts:150-155` — updates the derived behavior without synchronizing the base flag.\\n- `uifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts:451-468` — dismissal actions read the unchanged base `closeOnInteractOutside` value.\\n- `uifn/core/src/primitives/dialog.test.ts:55-89` — updates all aliases together, masking single-property updates.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Every supported outside-interaction input must leave the public Dialog state and dismissal actions with one consistent behavior.\\n- Cover updating `outsideInteractionBehavior` by itself in both closing and non-closing directions.\\n````\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgnj9\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n    \"line\": 176,\n    \"originalLine\": 176,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tqG\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:37:04Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023750\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Count Unicode code points for schema string lengths**\\n\\nWhen a schema constrains text containing supplementary Unicode characters, `String.length` counts UTF-16 code units rather than the Unicode code points required by JSON Schema. For example, `\\\"😀\\\"` is incorrectly rejected by `maxLength: 1` and incorrectly accepted by `minLength: 2`, so valid international input can fail administration operations; compute the length with code-point semantics such as `Array.from(value).length`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgnj8\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts\",\n    \"line\": 51,\n    \"originalLine\": 51,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tqF\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:37:04Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023749\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Encode negative calendar years with an ISO sign**\\n\\nWhen a date input is decremented from year 0 to year -1, which `createUIFnCalendarDate` and the controller actions permit, this produces `00-1-01-01`. That value is neither accepted by `parseUIFnIsoDate` nor interpreted correctly by the date picker's hyphen-splitting cell parser, and it is also submitted through the hidden form input. Serialize BCE years using signed expanded ISO notation, or reject negative years consistently.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgnj7\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/core/src/diff.ts\",\n    \"line\": 272,\n    \"originalLine\": 272,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tqC\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:37:04Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023746\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve open input compatibility on property removal**\\n\\nWhen an optional input property is removed while the new schema leaves `additionalProperties` enabled or unspecified, payloads containing that property remain valid because it becomes an unconstrained additional property. This unconditional classification nevertheless marks the manifest incompatible, so CI consumers can reject a schema-compatible release; determine input severity from the new `additionalProperties` policy rather than always reporting `breaking`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgnj3\",\n    \"path\": \"authfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n    \"line\": 459,\n    \"originalLine\": 459,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tp9\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:37:04Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023741\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind AuthFn user cursors to scope and query**\\n\\nWhen a cursor is reused after changing the active region, email filter, or sort direction, this forwards it unchanged to `listAuthFnAdminUsers`; that implementation encodes only `createdAt` and `id` (`authfn/core/src/core/admin-users.ts:230-252`). The timestamp is then interpreted against the new result set or opposite ordering, causing users to be skipped or repeated. Include the region and query identity in the cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgndQ\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/overlay.ts\",\n    \"line\": 307,\n    \"originalLine\": 307,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tgt\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023149\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=71a9af0e-6f10-42c9-b955-ccf0c826c765 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: When a positioned overlay opens, this launches two concurrent position calculations because `start()` performs an initial auto-update while the explicit update is still pending. The positioner marks the first result stale and reports a recoverable error on every initial open; chain `start()` after the initial update so only one calculation runs.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/src/overlay.ts, line 296:\\n\\n<comment>When a positioned overlay opens, this launches two concurrent position calculations because `start()` performs an initial auto-update while the explicit update is still pending. The positioner marks the first result stale and reports a recoverable error on every initial open; chain `start()` after the initial update so only one calculation runs.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -268,7 +281,29 @@ export function createUIFnOverlayDomBinding<TState extends UIFnOverlayBaseState>\\n+      modal = null;\\n     }\\n+    ensurePositioner();\\n+    void positioner?.update({\\n+      reference: options.reference ?? trigger,\\n+      floating,\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    void positioner?.update({\\n      reference: options.reference ?? trigger,\\n      floating,\\n      arrow: options.arrow,\\n      placement: current.placement,\\n      strategy: options.strategy,\\n      sideOffset: options.sideOffset,\\n      alignOffset: options.alignOffset,\\n      collisionPadding: options.collisionPadding,\\n      autoUpdate: true,\\n    }).then(() => positioner?.start()).catch((error) => scope.environment.error(error));\\n```\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgndM\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/positioning-rebind.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": 15,\n    \"originalLine\": 15,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tgp\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023145\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=6411273e-5e87-4796-ae12-94a7c0d34b32 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} -->\\nP2: This test couples the public positioning suite to Floating UI's private `autoUpdate` API. A provider refactor could preserve the UIFn contract while unnecessarily breaking this test; verify rebinding through the public positioner contract and observable cleanup instead.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/src/positioning-rebind.test.ts, line 15:\\n\\n<comment>This test couples the public positioning suite to Floating UI's private `autoUpdate` API. A provider refactor could preserve the UIFn contract while unnecessarily breaking this test; verify rebinding through the public positioner contract and observable cleanup instead.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@\\n+  })),\\n+}));\\n+\\n+vi.mock('@floating-ui/dom', () => ({\\n+  arrow: vi.fn(() => ({ name: 'arrow' })),\\n+  autoUpdate: floatingMocks.autoUpdate,\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgndL\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/primitives/dialog.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": 64,\n    \"originalLine\": 64,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tgo\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023144\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=dd93596d-d7c7-421c-90db-ec7f06c29188 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: This adds new mutable outside-interaction inputs without verifying them, so a regression could leave the dialog dismissible outside while the test still passes. Assert `closeOnOutsideInteraction: false` and `outsideInteractionBehavior: 'ignore'` in the state matcher.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/core/src/primitives/dialog.test.ts, line 64:\\n\\n<comment>This adds new mutable outside-interaction inputs without verifying them, so a regression could leave the dialog dismissible outside while the test still passes. Assert `closeOnOutsideInteraction: false` and `outsideInteractionBehavior: 'ignore'` in the state matcher.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -61,6 +61,8 @@ describe('dialog primitive', () => {\\n       scrollLock: false,\\n       closeOnEscape: false,\\n       closeOnInteractOutside: false,\\n+      closeOnOutsideInteraction: false,\\n+      outsideInteractionBehavior: 'ignore',\\n       placement: 'top-start',\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgndI\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/presence.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": 31,\n    \"originalLine\": 31,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tgj\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023139\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=a716b615-e351-49ef-8ad5-da247f397c59 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} -->\\nP2: This test does not verify the timeout fallback or the longest-motion delay: a broken timeout implementation, or one scheduling the wrong delay, still passes. Capture the scheduled callback and delay, assert the expected delay, and invoke the callback in a separate no-event case.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/src/presence.test.ts, line 31:\\n\\n<comment>This test does not verify the timeout fallback or the longest-motion delay: a broken timeout implementation, or one scheduling the wrong delay, still passes. Capture the scheduled callback and delay, assert the expected delay, and invoke the callback in a separate no-event case.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@\\n+          cleanup();\\n+        };\\n+      },\\n+      setTimeout: vi.fn(() => () => undefined),\\n+      window: {\\n+        getComputedStyle: () => ({\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgndH\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/positioning.ts\",\n    \"line\": 240,\n    \"originalLine\": 240,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tgi\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023138\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=c33450cf-f0a0-4711-8922-3ac1eb138570 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP1: When a running positioner uses a resolver that creates a fresh virtual anchor, every automatic update enters this rebinding branch and recursively creates another `autoUpdate`; context-menu positioning can therefore overflow the stack. Rebind based on the actual observer target or resolver configuration, not virtual-anchor object identity, and add a regression test for a fresh virtual anchor resolver.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/src/positioning.ts, line 240:\\n\\n<comment>When a running positioner uses a resolver that creates a fresh virtual anchor, every automatic update enters this rebinding branch and recursively creates another `autoUpdate`; context-menu positioning can therefore overflow the stack. Rebind based on the actual observer target or resolver configuration, not virtual-anchor object identity, and add a regression test for a fresh virtual anchor resolver.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -229,6 +235,27 @@ export function createUIFnPositioner(\\n     }\\n+    const restartAutoUpdate = running && (\\n+      autoUpdateConfigChanged\\n+      || reference !== boundReference\\n+      || floating !== boundFloating\\n+    );\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgndE\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/presence.ts\",\n    \"line\": 49,\n    \"originalLine\": 49,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tgf\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023135\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=4adb0be6-bb0c-46ea-ab6f-33c5732e79d4 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP1: When a CSS motion-property list is longer than its duration list, CSS repeats durations, but `pairedMotion` counts only duration/delay entries. Short repeated events can therefore reach zero before the longest animation or transition ends; derive the expected event count from `animation-name`/`transition-property`, or retain timer-based completion instead of finishing from this count.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/src/presence.ts, line 49:\\n\\n<comment>When a CSS motion-property list is longer than its duration list, CSS repeats durations, but `pairedMotion` counts only duration/delay entries. Short repeated events can therefore reach zero before the longest animation or transition ends; derive the expected event count from `animation-name`/`transition-property`, or retain timer-based completion instead of finishing from this count.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -38,25 +38,29 @@ function parseTimeList(value: string): number[] {\\n+    const total = (durations[index % durations.length] ?? 0)\\n+      + (delays[index % delays.length] ?? 0);\\n+    maximum = Math.max(maximum, total);\\n+    if (total > 0) active += 1;\\n   }\\n-  return maximum;\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgnc_\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/browser/overlay-harness.ts\",\n    \"line\": 206,\n    \"originalLine\": 206,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tga\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023130\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=38ccd4c8-1bfa-42a3-914d-76b5718972c5 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} -->\\nP1: The Dialog policy does not support positioning, so this assertion always sees an unset `data-side` and makes `runOverlayVectors` fail during the Dialog iteration. Assert `controller.state.placement` instead, or move this DOM-placement check to a positioned primitive such as Popover.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/browser/overlay-harness.ts, line 206:\\n\\n<comment>The Dialog policy does not support positioning, so this assertion always sees an unset `data-side` and makes `runOverlayVectors` fail during the Dialog iteration. Assert `controller.state.placement` instead, or move this DOM-placement check to a positioned primitive such as Popover.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -198,6 +199,16 @@ async function exerciseOpenPrimitive(\\n+    controller.update({ modal: false, trapFocus: false, scrollLock: false, placement: 'top-start' });\\n+    await wait(20);\\n+    invariant(platform.modals.size === 0, 'Dialog retained modal resources after an open update');\\n+    invariant(fixture.positioner.dataset.side === 'top', 'Dialog did not apply an open placement update');\\n+    controller.update({ modal: true, trapFocus: true, scrollLock: true });\\n+    await wait(20);\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    invariant(controller.state.placement === 'top-start', 'Dialog did not apply an open placement update');\\n```\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgWj0\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts\",\n    \"line\": 559,\n    \"originalLine\": 558,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0VIh\",\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T15:50:22Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838923297\",\n      \"body\": \"`update()` now changes `modal`, `trapFocus`, `scrollLock`, and `placement` while an overlay is open, but the DOM binding only acquires the corresponding resources on the closed-to-open transition. The existing focus scope, modal/scroll lock, and positioner therefore retain stale behavior until close/reopen.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Live overlay resources do not follow mutable inputs\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `uifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts:558-568` — publishes mutable policy and placement state after mount.\\n- `uifn/dom/src/overlay.ts:220-270` — captures placement, focus-trap, modal, and scroll-lock settings only when resources are created.\\n- `uifn/dom/src/overlay.ts:292-305` — updates dismissal and presence, but neither updates nor recreates those resources while `open` remains true.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- An already-open overlay must reconcile focus trapping, modal isolation, scroll locking, and positioning with the latest controller inputs without requiring close/reopen.\\n- Add DOM-level coverage that changes these inputs while open and observes the resource behavior, not only controller state.\\n````\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgSkC\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/positioning.ts\",\n    \"line\": 224,\n    \"originalLine\": 218,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0PWN\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T15:39:31Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838899597\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Rebind auto-update when positioning targets change**\\n\\nWhen `update()` replaces `reference` or `floating` on a running positioner, this computes one result using the new targets but leaves Floating UI's `autoUpdate` subscription attached to the old elements from `start()`. Subsequent resize or movement of the new anchor does not trigger repositioning, so the floating element becomes stale; restart the subscription when target or auto-update-related options change.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgSkA\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/presence.ts\",\n    \"line\": 116,\n    \"originalLine\": 106,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0PWL\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T15:39:31Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838899595\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Wait for the longest CSS motion before unmounting**\\n\\nWhen an element transitions multiple properties with different durations, or runs an animation and transition together, the first `transitionend` or `animationend` on the element calls `finish()` even though `motionDuration` deliberately calculated the longest completion time. Exit content is therefore marked unmounted and can disappear as soon as the shortest motion ends; completion needs to wait for all relevant motions or the computed maximum-duration fallback.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgSj_\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/scope.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 296,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0PWK\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T15:39:30Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838899594\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Retire released cleanups from the scope registry**\\n\\nWhen a long-lived DOM scope repeatedly opens and closes overlays, completes presence transitions, or restarts positioners, every released resource remains in `cleanups` until the entire scope is destroyed. Because `once` also retains its callback after release, these entries can retain observers, elements, and other captured objects, causing memory usage to grow with total historical resource acquisitions rather than active resources; remove each entry when its release function runs.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgSRT\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts\",\n    \"line\": 564,\n    \"originalLine\": 563,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0O6p\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T15:38:39Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838897833\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=f6be4088-2627-4d4e-931c-1a0283f2709d -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=dda8f212-5e9c-4ac9-9bbc-1a75257593ad -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: After `dialog.update({ closeOnInteractOutside: false })`, the base stops outside dismissal while `dialog.state.closeOnOutsideInteraction` still reports `true`. Synchronize Dialog's derived outside-interaction behavior with mutable overlay inputs, or reject this input instead of updating only the base state.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts, line 563:\\n\\n<comment>After `dialog.update({ closeOnInteractOutside: false })`, the base stops outside dismissal while `dialog.state.closeOnOutsideInteraction` still reports `true`. Synchronize Dialog's derived outside-interaction behavior with mutable overlay inputs, or reject this input instead of updating only the base state.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -546,6 +547,31 @@ export function createUIFnOverlayBase<TProps extends UIFnOverlayCommonProps>(\\n+            trapFocus: currentProps.trapFocus ?? (nextModal && policyValue.trapFocus),\\n+            scrollLock: currentProps.scrollLock ?? (nextModal && policyValue.scrollLock),\\n+            closeOnEscape: currentProps.closeOnEscape ?? policyValue.closeOnEscape,\\n+            closeOnInteractOutside: nextOutside,\\n+            placement: currentProps.placement ?? options.defaultPlacement ?? 'bottom',\\n+            forceMount: currentProps.forceMount ?? false,\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfcBJ\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/focus-scope.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 284,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7ky_5_\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T13:09:35Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838574207\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep the prior focus scope active for disabled registrations**\\n\\nWhen a scope is registered with `enabled: false`, this unconditionally pauses the previous active scope even though `top()` excludes the new disabled record. The manager consequently has no active scope and the prior focus trap stops containing focus until the disabled record is destroyed; only pause the previous scope when the new record can become active, and recompute this relationship when `enabled` changes.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfcBI\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts\",\n    \"line\": 39,\n    \"originalLine\": 30,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7ky_5-\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T13:09:35Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838574206\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject calendar years outside the Date-backed range**\\n\\nWhen `year` is outside JavaScript's representable `Date` range, such as the six-digit year accepted by `parseUIFnIsoDate('999999-02-31')`, `daysInMonth` returns `NaN`; because `day > NaN` is false, this validation accepts even impossible dates. Subsequent formatting and day arithmetic then operate on an invalid `Date` or fail unpredictably, so reject years for which the computed month length is not finite or implement range-independent Gregorian arithmetic.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfcBH\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts\",\n    \"line\": 577,\n    \"originalLine\": 550,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7ky_59\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T13:09:35Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838574205\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Apply updated overlay inputs beyond `open`**\\n\\nWhen a mounted Dialog, Drawer, Popover, or other overlay receives updated inputs such as `modal`, `trapFocus`, `scrollLock`, `placement`, or `forceMount`, the adapter calls `controller.update(...)`, but this implementation synchronizes only `open`. The controller state, rendered ARIA attributes, focus trapping, and background isolation therefore retain their initial configuration; update the common overlay state for every supported mutable input before notifying subscribers.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfEZO\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts\",\n    \"line\": 62,\n    \"originalLine\": 35,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kydiy\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T11:54:58Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838433458\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve years below 100 in calendar arithmetic**\\n\\nWhen an accepted ISO date has a year from 0000 through 0099, `Date.UTC` applies JavaScript's 1900-year offset. Thus `compareUIFnDates` considers year 0001 equal to 1901, and `addUIFnDateDays` jumps a year-0001 date into 1901. Construct dates using `setUTCFullYear` or reject this range consistently instead of accepting values that calendar operations reinterpret.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfEZN\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/algorithms/virtualization.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 36,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kydiw\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T11:54:58Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838433456\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Include partially visible rows in the virtual window**\\n\\nWhen `scrollOffset` is not aligned to `estimateSize`, `visible` counts only the viewport's full-size quotient and ignores the partial row at the leading edge. For example, with size 10, viewport 10, offset 5, and `overscan: 0`, this returns only index 0 even though index 1 is also visible, producing a blank region while scrolling; calculate the end from the viewport's absolute trailing offset or add the partial leading item.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfEZL\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/live-region.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 84,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kydiv\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T11:54:58Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838433455\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Continue publishing after skipping a cleared announcement**\\n\\nWhen announcement A is queued before B and `clear(A)` runs before A is rendered, A becomes stale but remains in `queue`; the scheduled publisher shifts A and returns here without scheduling another pass, leaving B permanently unannounced. The same stall occurs if A is cleared while its animation frame is pending, so clearing one message must still advance the queue.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bevtk\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/theme/src/mount.ts\",\n    \"line\": 88,\n    \"originalLine\": 87,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kx_hm\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T10:47:40Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838310502\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Resolve token references before emitting CSS variables**\\n\\nWhen a valid runtime theme uses a typed reference such as `{color.surface.canvas}` with the required fallback metadata, validation resolves it only for checking, but this code flattens the original theme and emits the brace expression literally. The resulting custom property is unusable when consumed as a color or dimension, so mounted referenced tokens do not apply; emit values from `resolveTokenReferences(theme).theme` (or translate references to valid CSS `var()` expressions).\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bevtj\",\n    \"path\": \"datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 64,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kx_hl\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T10:47:40Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838310501\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind DataFn metadata cursors to their collection**\\n\\nWhen a schema has more than one page of metadata, a cursor returned by `datafn.resources.list` can be reused with `datafn.relations.list`, `datafn.indices.list`, or `datafn.capabilities.list` in the same scope, because the cursor carries only an offset. The unrelated collection is then sliced from that offset, silently skipping its initial entries; include the operation or collection identity in these cursors and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIT\",\n    \"path\": \"apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 160,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kxaU2\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158134\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind ApiFn cursors to their resource and scope**\\n\\nWhen the offset returned by `listSpecs` is supplied to `listEnvironments`, or reused after switching to another authorized scope, this parser accepts it unchanged and skips that many unrelated records. Because the helper emits only a decimal offset for both collections, clients cannot distinguish these invalid cursor uses; include the operation and active scope in an opaque cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIS\",\n    \"path\": \"botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 154,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kxaU1\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158133\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind BotFn cursors to their collection query**\\n\\nWhen a channels cursor issued for `botId=A` is reused with `botId=B`, or a cursor from the bots list is supplied to the channels list, this shared parser accepts the raw offset and slices the unrelated result set from that position. The same cursor can also be reused in another authorized scope, yielding skipped or empty pages there; encode the operation, scope, and channel filter identity into the cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIQ\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n    \"line\": 134,\n    \"originalLine\": 131,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kxaUz\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158131\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject non-JSON primitive leaves in open schemas**\\n\\nWhen an adapter returns a `bigint` under a type-less or `additionalProperties: true` child schema, validation accepts it because only object prototypes and non-finite numbers are rejected. Fresh evidence after the plain-object fix is that the new guards still omit `bigint`, `symbol`, `function`, and `undefined`; the open entity schemas used by DataFn, BillFn, and SearchFn therefore allow values that cannot be represented by the REST/MCP envelopes, with a `bigint` causing the subsequent `JSON.stringify` to throw instead of producing the validated result. Reject every primitive type outside the JSON value set even when the schema omits `type`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIN\",\n    \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\n    \"line\": 395,\n    \"originalLine\": 395,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kxaUw\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158128\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Expose create and upsert operations before a record exists**\\n\\nWhen an ID-targeted operation can create a new record, this classifies it exclusively as a detail-page action, while module-level actions accept only collection targets or resources with no list/detail route. Consequently operations such as `botfn.bots.upsert`, `botfn.channels.connect`, `apifn.specs.register`, and `apifn.environments.upsert` are only reachable after navigating to an existing record whose ID is then prebound; an empty collection has no console path for creating its first record. Project these creation/upsert operations as collection actions while leaving their ID fields editable.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_n\",\n    \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n    \"line\": 494,\n    \"originalLine\": 444,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwxiJ\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991049\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile variables when metadata persistence fails**\\n\\nWhen `executor.setVariable` succeeds for a new variable but this store write rejects, the provider retains the live secret while the operator returns an error and has no record through which to list or delete it. A retry is not guaranteed safe because `setVariable` has no idempotency contract; persist a durable intent before the provider call or compensate/reconcile the provider variable if final persistence fails.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_l\",\n    \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 105,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwxiH\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991047\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Compare action enum objects structurally**\\n\\nWhen an action field declares an object or array in `enum` or `const`, the form parses the operator's JSON into a new object and these `Object.is` checks always reject it by reference, even when it is structurally identical to the declared value. The administration validator permits these JSON-valued members, so such operations pass manifest validation but cannot be submitted through the generic action UI; use the same structural JSON equality semantics as the runtime validator.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_i\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n    \"line\": 271,\n    \"originalLine\": 262,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwxiE\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991044\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject non-plain objects as JSON values**\\n\\nWhen an in-process dispatcher caller supplies a `Date`, `Map`, or other class instance under `type: \\\"object\\\"`, this branch accepts it as a valid JSON object because it never checks the prototype. The immutable snapshot preserves such instances, and output redaction converts them through `Object.entries`—for example, a valid-looking `Date` response becomes `{}`—so adapters can receive or return values that change shape at transport time; require arrays or plain/null-prototype objects throughout JSON validation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdoWJ\",\n    \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 414,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwYRk\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T06:40:38Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837887588\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile variable records after provider deletion**\\n\\nWhen the provider deletion succeeds but `store.deleteVariable` rejects, the stale variable record remains while this request returns an error. Retrying with the same idempotency key replays that error, and retrying with a new key can still never remove the record when the provider reports that the already-deleted variable is not found, because this path does not tolerate provider-not-found as `detachDomain` does. Treat an already-absent provider variable as success or persist a deletion intent so the store record can be reconciled.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdgrE\",\n    \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 40,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwNOB\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T06:10:24Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837842305\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Resolve composed schemas before deciding an action has no fields**\\n\\nWhen a valid operation input schema declares its named properties through `allOf`, this returns no editable fields because only top-level `properties` is inspected. The generic action then either submits `{}` immediately or shows a dialog without the required controls, so operations using a schema composition accepted by the manifest validator cannot be invoked from Super Console; merge compatible `allOf` object properties and requirements before constructing the fields.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdgrD\",\n    \"path\": \"filefn/server/src/index.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 334,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwNOA\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T06:10:24Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837842304\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restrict the public processing service to authorized methods**\\n\\nWhen an application exposes this newly public service through an in-process integration, callers can invoke `processing.listArtifacts(fileId, ctx)` directly even though that method explicitly ignores `ctx` and queries all artifacts for the file; only `listArtifactsForFile` calls `requireReadableFile`. Publishing the full `ProcessingService` therefore bypasses the authorization enforced by both the HTTP routes and the admin adapter, so expose an authorization-safe facade or keep the worker-level methods private.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdRKH\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 86,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kv2vJ\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T05:06:53Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837750217\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Compare object-valued enum members structurally**\\n\\nWhen an operation schema declares an object or array in `enum`, JSON-decoded input that is structurally identical is rejected because `Object.is` compares those values by reference. `AdminJsonSchema` permits arbitrary enum values and manifest validation does not restrict them to scalars, so such a valid schema becomes unusable through REST or MCP; compare enum members using JSON structural equality instead.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bc5vf\",\n    \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 1062,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kvVRa\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T03:26:35Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837613146\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Make confirmation issuance recoverable after audit failures**\\n\\nWhen `performConfirmOperation` successfully creates a valid confirmation token but this terminal audit write fails, the endpoint returns an error and discards the only receipt while the token remains live and the audit trail contains only the attempted event. Retrying issues another token, so a transient sink failure accumulates valid, unreturned credentials without a successful issuance record; make issuance replay-safe or revoke/reconcile the issued token before returning the failure.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bc5vd\",\n    \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 299,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kvVRY\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T03:26:35Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837613144\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile attached domains when persistence fails**\\n\\nWhen the provider successfully attaches the domain but `putDomain` rejects, this operation returns an error while leaving a live domain with no corresponding store record. The failed idempotent invocation is then fenced as an error, and retrying with a new key can attach a duplicate; meanwhile the console cannot discover or detach the original domain. Persist a durable pending intent before calling the executor, or compensate the provider attachment when the final write fails.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":8208},"formatted_output":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 12645)\nTotal output lines: 604\n\n60d32b4058286bff8cfc8b48a347a4e0bff22230\n2026-08-23T22:00:19+05:30\n[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgpD6\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/presence.ts\",\n    \"line\": 58,\n    \"originalLine\": 58,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0vz1\",\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:41:28Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839032565\",\n      \"body\": \"CSS uses `transition-property` and `animation-name` as the master lists, so duration and delay list lengths can exceed the number of events the browser emits. After the real motion ends, Presence can therefore remain `entering` or `exiting` until the fallback timer fires.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Presence waits for nonexistent motion events\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `uifn/dom/src/presence.ts:41-63` — derives event counts only from duration and delay lists.\\n- `uifn/dom/src/presence.ts:101-127` — requires every derived event or waits for `duration + 50ms`.\\n- `uifn/dom/src/presence.test.ts:33-52` — manually emits two events without defining two transitioning properties.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Complete promptly after the element's actual relevant motions finish without requiring events that CSS cannot emit.\\n- Add coverage where one `transition-property` has excess duration entries and produces only one end event.\\n\\n## References\\n- https://drafts.csswg.org/css-transitions/#transitions\\n- https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/animation-name\\n````\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgpD5\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/browser/overlay-harness.ts\",\n    \"line\": 206,\n    \"originalLine\": 206,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0vzy\",\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:41:28Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839032562\",\n      \"body\": \"`Dialog` has `policy.position: 'none'`, so this binding never creates a positioner and `dataset.side` remains unset. This makes the Playwright overlay matrix fail without covering live placement reconciliation; exercise placement on a positioned primitive while retaining the Dialog modal assertions.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgpD2\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/primitives/dialog.ts\",\n    \"line\": 152,\n    \"originalLine\": 152,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0vzu\",\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:41:28Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839032558\",\n      \"body\": \"`outsideInteractionBehavior` is applied only to the derived `behavior` after the base update has already persisted its dismissal flag. `dialog.update({ outsideInteractionBehavior: 'ignore' })` consequently reports `ignore` while `actions.onOutsideInteraction()` still closes the open Dialog.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Dialog outside-interaction aliases diverge after update\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `uifn/core/src/primitives/dialog.ts:150-155` — updates the derived behavior without synchronizing the base flag.\\n- `uifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts:451-468` — dismissal actions read the unchanged base `closeOnInteractOutside` value.\\n- `uifn/core/src/primitives/dialog.test.ts:55-89` — updates all aliases together, masking single-property updates.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Every supported outside-interaction input must leave the public Dialog state and dismissal actions with one consistent behavior.\\n- Cover updating `outsideInteractionBehavior` by itself in both closing and non-closing directions.\\n````\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgnj9\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n    \"line\": 176,\n    \"originalLine\": 176,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tqG\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:37:04Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023750\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Count Unicode code points for schema string lengths**\\n\\nWhen a schema constrains text containing supplementary Unicode characters, `String.length` counts UTF-16 code units rather than the Unicode code points required by JSON Schema. For example, `\\\"😀\\\"` is incorrectly rejected by `maxLength: 1` and incorrectly accepted by `minLength: 2`, so valid international input can fail administration operations; compute the length with code-point semantics such as `Array.from(value).length`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgnj8\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts\",\n    \"line\": 51,\n    \"originalLine\": 51,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tqF\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:37:04Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023749\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Encode negative calendar years with an ISO sign**\\n\\nWhen a date input is decremented from year 0 to year -1, which `createUIFnCalendarDate` and the controller actions permit, this produces `00-1-01-01`. That value is neither accepted by `parseUIFnIsoDate` nor interpreted correctly by the date picker's hyphen-splitting cell parser, and it is also submitted through the hidden form input. Serialize BCE years using signed expanded ISO notation, or reject negative years consistently.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgnj7\",\n    \"path\": \"mcpfn/core/src/diff.ts\",\n    \"line\": 272,\n    \"originalLine\": 272,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tqC\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:37:04Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023746\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve open input compatibility on property removal**\\n\\nWhen an optional input property is removed while the new schema leaves `additionalProperties` enabled or unspecified, payloads containing that property remain valid because it becomes an unconstrained additional property. This unconditional classification nevertheless marks the manifest incompatible, so CI consumers can reject a schema-compatible release; determine input severity from the new `additionalProperties` policy rather than always reporting `breaking`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgnj3\",\n    \"path\": \"authfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n    \"line\": 459,\n    \"originalLine\": 459,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tp9\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:37:04Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023741\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind AuthFn user cursors to scope and query**\\n\\nWhen a cursor is reused after changing the active region, email filter, or sort direction, this forwards it unchanged to `listAuthFnAdminUsers`; that implementation encodes only `createdAt` and `id` (`authfn/core/src/core/admin-users.ts:230-252`). The timestamp is then interpreted against the new result set or opposite ordering, causing users to be skipped or repeated. Include the region and query identity in the cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgndQ\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/overlay.ts\",\n    \"line\": 307,\n    \"originalLine\": 307,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tgt\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023149\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=71a9af0e-6f10-42c9-b955-ccf0c826c765 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: When a positioned overlay opens, this launches two concurrent position calculations because `start()` performs an initial auto-update while the explicit update is still pending. The positioner marks the first result stale and reports a recoverable error on every initial open; chain `start()` after the initial update so only one calculation runs.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/src/overlay.ts, line 296:\\n\\n<comment>When a positioned overlay opens, this launches two concurrent position calculations because `start()` performs an initial auto-update while the explicit update is still pending. The positioner marks the first result stale and reports a recoverable error on every initial open; chain `start()` after the initial update so only one calculation runs.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -268,7 +281,29 @@ export function createUIFnOverlayDomBinding<TState extends UIFnOverlayBaseState>\\n+      modal = null;\\n     }\\n+    ensurePositioner();\\n+    void positioner?.update({\\n+      reference: options.reference ?? trigger,\\n+      floating,\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n```suggestion\\n    void positioner?.update({\\n      reference: options.reference ?? trigger,\\n      floating,\\n      arrow: options.arrow,\\n      placement: current.placement,\\n      strategy: options.strategy,\\n      sideOffset: options.sideOffset,\\n      alignOffset: options.alignOffset,\\n      collisionPadding: options.collisionPadding,\\n      autoUpdate: true,\\n    }).then(() => positioner?.start()).catch((error) => scope.environment.error(error));\\n```\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgndM\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/positioning-rebind.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": 15,\n    \"originalLine\": 15,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tgp\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023145\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=6411273e-5e87-4796-ae12-94a7c0d34b32 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} -->\\nP2: This test couples the public positioning suite to Floating UI's private `autoUpdate` API. A provider refactor could preserve the UIFn contract while unnecessarily breaking this test; verify rebinding through the public positioner contract and observable cleanup instead.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/src/positioning-rebind.test.ts, line 15:\\n\\n<comment>This test couples the public positioning suite to Floating UI's private `autoUpdate` API. A provider refactor could preserve the UIFn contract while unnecessarily breaking this test; verify rebinding through the public positioner contract and observable cleanup instead.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@\\n+  })),\\n+}));\\n+\\n+vi.mock('@floating-ui/dom', () => ({\\n+  arrow: vi.fn(() => ({ name: 'arrow' })),\\n+  autoUpdate: floatingMocks.autoUpdate,\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgndL\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/primitives/dialog.test.ts\",\n    \"line\": 64,\n    \"originalLine\": 64,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tgo\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023144\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=d