restartAutoUpdate = running && (\\n+      autoUpdateConfigChanged\\n+      || reference !== boundReference\\n+      || floating !== boundFloating\\n+    );\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgndE\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/presence.ts\",\n    \"line\": 49,\n    \"originalLine\": 49,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tgf\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023135\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=4adb0be6-bb0c-46ea-ab6f-33c5732e79d4 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP1: When a CSS motion-property list is longer than its duration list, CSS repeats durations, but `pairedMotion` counts only duration/delay entries. Short repeated events can therefore reach zero before the longest animation or transition ends; derive the expected event count from `animation-name`/`transition-property`, or retain timer-based completion instead of finishing from this count.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/src/presence.ts, line 49:\\n\\n<comment>When a CSS motion-property list is longer than its duration list, CSS repeats durations, but `pairedMotion` counts only duration/delay entries. Short repeated events can therefore reach zero before the longest animation or transition ends; derive the expected event count from `animation-name`/`transition-property`, or retain timer-based completion instead of finishing from this count.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -38,25 +38,29 @@ function parseTimeList(value: string): number[] {\\n+    const total = (durations[index % durations.length] ?? 0)\\n+      + (delays[index % delays.length] ?? 0);\\n+    maximum = Math.max(maximum, total);\\n+    if (total > 0) active += 1;\\n   }\\n-  return maximum;\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgnc_\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/browser/overlay-harness.ts\",\n    \"line\": 206,\n    \"originalLine\": 206,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tga\",\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:36:46Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023130\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=38ccd4c8-1bfa-42a3-914d-76b5718972c5 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":10} -->\\nP1: The Dialog policy does not support positioning, so this assertion always sees an unset `data-side` and makes `runOverlayVectors` fail during the Dialog iteration. Assert `controller.state.placement` instead, or move this DOM-placement check to a positioned primitive such as Popover.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/browser/overlay-harness.ts, line 206:\\n\\n<comment>The Dialog policy does not support positioning,…2645 tokens truncated…`placement`, or `forceMount`, the adapter calls `controller.update(...)`, but this implementation synchronizes only `open`. The controller state, rendered ARIA attributes, focus trapping, and background isolation therefore retain their initial configuration; update the common overlay state for every supported mutable input before notifying subscribers.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfEZO\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts\",\n    \"line\": 62,\n    \"originalLine\": 35,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kydiy\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T11:54:58Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838433458\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve years below 100 in calendar arithmetic**\\n\\nWhen an accepted ISO date has a year from 0000 through 0099, `Date.UTC` applies JavaScript's 1900-year offset. Thus `compareUIFnDates` considers year 0001 equal to 1901, and `addUIFnDateDays` jumps a year-0001 date into 1901. Construct dates using `setUTCFullYear` or reject this range consistently instead of accepting values that calendar operations reinterpret.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfEZN\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/core/src/algorithms/virtualization.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 36,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kydiw\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T11:54:58Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838433456\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Include partially visible rows in the virtual window**\\n\\nWhen `scrollOffset` is not aligned to `estimateSize`, `visible` counts only the viewport's full-size quotient and ignores the partial row at the leading edge. For example, with size 10, viewport 10, offset 5, and `overscan: 0`, this returns only index 0 even though index 1 is also visible, producing a blank region while scrolling; calculate the end from the viewport's absolute trailing offset or add the partial leading item.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bfEZL\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/dom/src/live-region.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 84,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kydiv\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T11:54:58Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838433455\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Continue publishing after skipping a cleared announcement**\\n\\nWhen announcement A is queued before B and `clear(A)` runs before A is rendered, A becomes stale but remains in `queue`; the scheduled publisher shifts A and returns here without scheduling another pass, leaving B permanently unannounced. The same stall occurs if A is cleared while its animation frame is pending, so clearing one message must still advance the queue.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bevtk\",\n    \"path\": \"uifn/theme/src/mount.ts\",\n    \"line\": 88,\n    \"originalLine\": 87,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kx_hm\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T10:47:40Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838310502\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Resolve token references before emitting CSS variables**\\n\\nWhen a valid runtime theme uses a typed reference such as `{color.surface.canvas}` with the required fallback metadata, validation resolves it only for checking, but this code flattens the original theme and emits the brace expression literally. The resulting custom property is unusable when consumed as a color or dimension, so mounted referenced tokens do not apply; emit values from `resolveTokenReferences(theme).theme` (or translate references to valid CSS `var()` expressions).\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bevtj\",\n    \"path\": \"datafn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 64,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kx_hl\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T10:47:40Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838310501\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind DataFn metadata cursors to their collection**\\n\\nWhen a schema has more than one page of metadata, a cursor returned by `datafn.resources.list` can be reused with `datafn.relations.list`, `datafn.indices.list`, or `datafn.capabilities.list` in the same scope, because the cursor carries only an offset. The unrelated collection is then sliced from that offset, silently skipping its initial entries; include the operation or collection identity in these cursors and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIT\",\n    \"path\": \"apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 160,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kxaU2\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158134\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind ApiFn cursors to their resource and scope**\\n\\nWhen the offset returned by `listSpecs` is supplied to `listEnvironments`, or reused after switching to another authorized scope, this parser accepts it unchanged and skips that many unrelated records. Because the helper emits only a decimal offset for both collections, clients cannot distinguish these invalid cursor uses; include the operation and active scope in an opaque cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIS\",\n    \"path\": \"botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 154,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kxaU1\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158133\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind BotFn cursors to their collection query**\\n\\nWhen a channels cursor issued for `botId=A` is reused with `botId=B`, or a cursor from the bots list is supplied to the channels list, this shared parser accepts the raw offset and slices the unrelated result set from that position. The same cursor can also be reused in another authorized scope, yielding skipped or empty pages there; encode the operation, scope, and channel filter identity into the cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIQ\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n    \"line\": 134,\n    \"originalLine\": 131,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kxaUz\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158131\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject non-JSON primitive leaves in open schemas**\\n\\nWhen an adapter returns a `bigint` under a type-less or `additionalProperties: true` child schema, validation accepts it because only object prototypes and non-finite numbers are rejected. Fresh evidence after the plain-object fix is that the new guards still omit `bigint`, `symbol`, `function`, and `undefined`; the open entity schemas used by DataFn, BillFn, and SearchFn therefore allow values that cannot be represented by the REST/MCP envelopes, with a `bigint` causing the subsequent `JSON.stringify` to throw instead of producing the validated result. Reject every primitive type outside the JSON value set even when the schema omits `type`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIN\",\n    \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\n    \"line\": 395,\n    \"originalLine\": 395,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kxaUw\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158128\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Expose create and upsert operations before a record exists**\\n\\nWhen an ID-targeted operation can create a new record, this classifies it exclusively as a detail-page action, while module-level actions accept only collection targets or resources with no list/detail route. Consequently operations such as `botfn.bots.upsert`, `botfn.channels.connect`, `apifn.specs.register`, and `apifn.environments.upsert` are only reachable after navigating to an existing record whose ID is then prebound; an empty collection has no console path for creating its first record. Project these creation/upsert operations as collection actions while leaving their ID fields editable.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_n\",\n    \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n    \"line\": 494,\n    \"originalLine\": 444,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwxiJ\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991049\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile variables when metadata persistence fails**\\n\\nWhen `executor.setVariable` succeeds for a new variable but this store write rejects, the provider retains the live secret while the operator returns an error and has no record through which to list or delete it. A retry is not guaranteed safe because `setVariable` has no idempotency contract; persist a durable intent before the provider call or compensate/reconcile the provider variable if final persistence fails.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_l\",\n    \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 105,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwxiH\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991047\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Compare action enum objects structurally**\\n\\nWhen an action field declares an object or array in `enum` or `const`, the form parses the operator's JSON into a new object and these `Object.is` checks always reject it by reference, even when it is structurally identical to the declared value. The administration validator permits these JSON-valued members, so such operations pass manifest validation but cannot be submitted through the generic action UI; use the same structural JSON equality semantics as the runtime validator.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_i\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n    \"line\": 271,\n    \"originalLine\": 262,\n    \"isOutdated\": false,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwxiE\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n      \"outdated\": false,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991044\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject non-plain objects as JSON values**\\n\\nWhen an in-process dispatcher caller supplies a `Date`, `Map`, or other class instance under `type: \\\"object\\\"`, this branch accepts it as a valid JSON object because it never checks the prototype. The immutable snapshot preserves such instances, and output redaction converts them through `Object.entries`—for example, a valid-looking `Date` response becomes `{}`—so adapters can receive or return values that change shape at transport time; require arrays or plain/null-prototype objects throughout JSON validation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdoWJ\",\n    \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 414,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwYRk\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T06:40:38Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837887588\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile variable records after provider deletion**\\n\\nWhen the provider deletion succeeds but `store.deleteVariable` rejects, the stale variable record remains while this request returns an error. Retrying with the same idempotency key replays that error, and retrying with a new key can still never remove the record when the provider reports that the already-deleted variable is not found, because this path does not tolerate provider-not-found as `detachDomain` does. Treat an already-absent provider variable as success or persist a deletion intent so the store record can be reconciled.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdgrE\",\n    \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/components/action-form.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 40,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwNOB\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T06:10:24Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837842305\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Resolve composed schemas before deciding an action has no fields**\\n\\nWhen a valid operation input schema declares its named properties through `allOf`, this returns no editable fields because only top-level `properties` is inspected. The generic action then either submits `{}` immediately or shows a dialog without the required controls, so operations using a schema composition accepted by the manifest validator cannot be invoked from Super Console; merge compatible `allOf` object properties and requirements before constructing the fields.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdgrD\",\n    \"path\": \"filefn/server/src/index.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 334,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwNOA\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T06:10:24Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837842304\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Restrict the public processing service to authorized methods**\\n\\nWhen an application exposes this newly public service through an in-process integration, callers can invoke `processing.listArtifacts(fileId, ctx)` directly even though that method explicitly ignores `ctx` and queries all artifacts for the file; only `listArtifactsForFile` calls `requireReadableFile`. Publishing the full `ProcessingService` therefore bypasses the authorization enforced by both the HTTP routes and the admin adapter, so expose an authorization-safe facade or keep the worker-level methods private.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bdRKH\",\n    \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 86,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kv2vJ\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T05:06:53Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837750217\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Compare object-valued enum members structurally**\\n\\nWhen an operation schema declares an object or array in `enum`, JSON-decoded input that is structurally identical is rejected because `Object.is` compares those values by reference. `AdminJsonSchema` permits arbitrary enum values and manifest validation does not restrict them to scalars, so such a valid schema becomes unusable through REST or MCP; compare enum members using JSON structural equality instead.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bc5vf\",\n    \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 1062,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kvVRa\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T03:26:35Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837613146\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Make confirmation issuance recoverable after audit failures**\\n\\nWhen `performConfirmOperation` successfully creates a valid confirmation token but this terminal audit write fails, the endpoint returns an error and discards the only receipt while the token remains live and the audit trail contains only the attempted event. Retrying issues another token, so a transient sink failure accumulates valid, unreturned credentials without a successful issuance record; make issuance replay-safe or revoke/reconcile the issued token before returning the failure.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bc5vd\",\n    \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n    \"line\": null,\n    \"originalLine\": 299,\n    \"isOutdated\": true,\n    \"latest\": {\n      \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kvVRY\",\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T03:26:35Z\",\n      \"outdated\": true,\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837613144\",\n      \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile attached domains when persistence fails**\\n\\nWhen the provider successfully attaches the domain but `putDomain` rejects, this operation returns an error while leaving a live domain with no corresponding store record. The failed idempotent invocation is then fenced as an error, and retrying with a new key can attach a duplicate; meanwhile the console cannot discover or detach the original domain. Persist a durable pending intent before calling the executor, or compensate the provider attachment when the final write fails.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n    }\n  }\n]\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02fae-186f-7650-a011-b5cdec75b51c","create_time":1787506412.447728}}}
