cit update is still pending. The positioner marks the first result stale and reports a recoverable error on every initial open; chain `start()` after the initial update so only one calculation runs.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/src/overlay.ts, line 296:\n\n<comment>When a positioned overlay opens, this launches two concurrent position calculations because `start()` performs an initial auto-update while the explicit update is still pending. The positioner marks the first result stale and reports a recoverable error on every initial open; chain `start()` after the initial update so only one calculation runs.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -268,7 +281,29 @@ export function createUIFnOverlayDomBinding<TState extends UIFnOverlayBaseState>\n+      modal = null;\n     }\n+    ensurePositioner();\n+    void positioner?.update({\n+      reference: options.reference ?? trigger,\n+      floating,\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\n    void positioner?.update({\n      reference: options.reference ?? trigger,\n      floating,\n      arrow: options.arrow,\n      placement: current.placement,\n      strategy: options.strategy,\n      sideOffset: options.sideOffset,\n      alignOffset: options.alignOffset,\n      collisionPadding: options.collisionPadding,\n      autoUpdate: true,\n    }).then(() => positioner?.start()).catch((error) => scope.environment.error(error));\n```\n\n### authfn/admin/src/index.ts:459\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind AuthFn user cursors to scope and query**\n\nWhen a cursor is reused after changing the active region, email filter, or sort direction, this forwards it unchanged to `listAuthFnAdminUsers`; that implementation encodes only `createdAt` and `id` (`authfn/core/src/core/admin-users.ts:230-252`). The timestamp is then interpreted against the new result set or opposite ordering, causing users to be skipped or repeated. Include the region and query identity in the cursor and reject mismatches.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n### mcpfn/core/src/diff.ts:272\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve open input compatibility on property removal**\n\nWhen an optional input property is removed while the new schema leaves `additionalProperties` enabled or unspecified, payloads containing that property remain valid because it becomes an unconstrained additional property. This unconditional classification nevertheless marks the manifest incompatible, so CI consumers can reject a schema-compatible release; determine input severity from the new `additionalProperties` policy rather than always reporting `breaking`.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n### uifn/core/src/algorithms/date-time.ts:51\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Encode negative calendar years with an ISO sign**\n\nWhen a date input is decremented from year 0 to year -1, which `createUIFnCalendarDate` and the controller actions permit, this produces `00-1-01-01`. That value is neither accepted by `parseUIFnIsoDate` nor interpreted correctly by the date picker's hyphen-splitting cell parser, and it is also submitted through the hidden form input. Serialize BCE years using signed expanded ISO notation, or reject negative years consistently.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n### packages/admin/src/validator.ts:176\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Count Unicode code points for schema string lengths**\n\nWhen a schema constrains text containing supplementary Unicode characters, `String.length` counts UTF-16 code units rather than the Unicode code points required by JSON Schema. For example, `\"😀\"` is incorrectly rejected by `maxLength: 1` and incorrectly accepted by `minLength: 2`, so valid international input can fail administration operations; compute the length with code-point semantics such as `Array.from(value).length`.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n### uifn/core/src/primitives/dialog.ts:152\n`outsideInteractionBehavior` is applied only to the derived `behavior` after the base update has already persisted its dismissal flag. `dialog.update({ outsideInteractionBehavior: 'ignore' })` consequently reports `ignore` while `actions.onOutsideInteraction()` still closes the open Dialog.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Dialog outside-interaction aliases diverge after update\n\n## Affected sites\n- `uifn/core/src/primitives/dialog.ts:150-155` — updates the derived behavior without synchronizing the base flag.\n- `uifn/core/src/primitives/overlay.ts:451-468` — dismissal actions read the unchanged base `closeOnInteractOutside` value.\n- `uifn/core/src/primitives/dialog.test.ts:55-89` — updates all aliases together, masking single-property updates.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Every supported outside-interaction input must leave the public Dialog state and dismissal actions with one consistent behavior.\n- Cover updating `outsideInteractionBehavior` by itself in both closing and non-closing directions.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n### uifn/dom/browser/overlay-harness.ts:206\n`Dialog` has `policy.position: 'none'`, so this binding never creates a positioner and `dataset.side` remains unset. This makes the Playwright overlay matrix fail without covering live placement reconciliation; exercise placement on a positioned primitive while retaining the Dialog modal assertions.\n\n### uifn/dom/src/presence.ts:58\nCSS uses `transition-property` and `animation-name` as the master lists, so duration and delay list lengths can exceed the number of events the browser emits. After the real motion ends, Presence can therefore remain `entering` or `exiting` until the fallback timer fires.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Presence waits for nonexistent motion events\n\n## Affected sites\n- `uifn/dom/src/presence.ts:41-63` — derives event counts only from duration and delay lists.\n- `uifn/dom/src/presence.ts:101-127` — requires every derived event or waits for `duration + 50ms`.\n- `uifn/dom/src/presence.test.ts:33-52` — manually emits two events without defining two transitioning properties.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Complete promptly after the element's actual relevant motions finish without requiring events that CSS cannot emit.\n- Add coverage where one `transition-property` has excess duration entries and produces only one end event.\n\n## References\n- https://drafts.csswg.org/css-transitions/#transitions\n- https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/animation-name\n````\n\n</details>\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10292},"formatted_output":"\n### uifn/dom/browser/overlay-harness.ts:206\n<!-- cubic:v=38ccd4c8-1bfa-42a3-914d-76b5718972c5 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":10} -->\nP1: The Dialog policy does not support positioning, so this assertion always sees an unset `data-side` and makes `runOverlayVectors` fail during the Dialog iteration. Assert `controller.state.placement` instead, or move this DOM-placement check to a positioned primitive such as Popover.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/browser/overlay-harness.ts, line 206:\n\n<comment>The Dialog policy does not support positioning, so this assertion always sees an unset `data-side` and makes `runOverlayVectors` fail during the Dialog iteration. Assert `controller.state.placement` instead, or move this DOM-placement check to a positioned primitive such as Popover.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -198,6 +199,16 @@ async function exerciseOpenPrimitive(\n+    controller.update({ modal: false, trapFocus: false, scrollLock: false, placement: 'top-start' });\n+    await wait(20);\n+    invariant(platform.modals.size === 0, 'Dialog retained modal resources after an open update');\n+    invariant(fixture.positioner.dataset.side === 'top', 'Dialog did not apply an open placement update');\n+    controller.update({ modal: true, trapFocus: true, scrollLock: true });\n+    await wait(20);\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\n    invariant(controller.state.placement === 'top-start', 'Dialog did not apply an open placement update');\n```\n\n### uifn/dom/src/presence.ts:49\n<!-- cubic:v=4adb0be6-bb0c-46ea-ab6f-33c5732e79d4 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP1: When a CSS motion-property list is longer than its duration list, CSS repeats durations, but `pairedMotion` counts only duration/delay entries. Short repeated events can therefore reach zero before the longest animation or transition ends; derive the expected event count from `animation-name`/`transition-property`, or retain timer-based completion instead of finishing from this count.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/src/presence.ts, line 49:\n\n<comment>When a CSS motion-property list is longer than its duration list, CSS repeats durations, but `pairedMotion` counts only duration/delay entries. Short repeated events can therefore reach zero before the longest animation or transition ends; derive the expected event count from `animation-name`/`transition-property`, or retain timer-based completion instead of finishing from this count.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -38,25 +38,29 @@ function parseTimeList(value: string): number[] {\n+    const total = (durations[index % durations.length] ?? 0)\n+      + (delays[index % delays.length] ?? 0);\n+    maximum = Math.max(maximum, total);\n+    if (total > 0) active += 1;\n   }\n-  return maximum;\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n### uifn/dom/src/positioning.ts:240\n<!-- cubic:v=c33450cf-f0a0-4711-8922-3ac1eb138570 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP1: When a running positioner uses a resolver that creates a fresh virtual anchor, every automatic update enters this rebinding branch and recursively creates another `autoUpdate`; context-menu positioning can therefore overflow the stack. Rebind based on the actual observer target or resolver configuration, not virtual-anchor object identity, and add a regression test for a fresh virtual anchor resolver.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At uifn/dom/src/positioning.ts, line 240:\n\n<comment>When a running positioner uses a resolver that creates a fresh virtual anchor, every automatic update enters this rebinding branch and recursively creates another `autoUpdate`; context-menu positioning can therefore overflow the stack. Rebind based on the actual observer target or resolver configuration, not virtual-anchor object identity, and add a regression test for a fresh virtual anchor resolver.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -229,6 +235,27 @@ export function createUIFnPositioner(\n     }\n+    const restartAutoUpdate = running && (\n+      autoUpdateConfigChanged\n+      || reference !== boundReference\n+      || floating !== boundFloating\n+    );\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n### uifn/dom/src/presence.test.ts:31\n<!-- cubic:v=a716b615-e351-49ef-8ad5-da247f397c59 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":10} -->\nP2: This test does not verify the timeout fallback or the longest-motion delay: a broken timeout implementation, or one scheduling the wrong delay, still passes. Capture the scheduled callback and delay, assert the expected delay, and invoke the callback