alog dismissible outside while the test still passes. Assert `closeOnOutsideInteraction: false` and `outsideInteractionBehavior: 'ignore'` in the state matcher.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/dom/browser/overlay-harness.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/dom/browser/overlay-harness.ts:206\">\nP1: The Dialog policy does not support positioning, so this assertion always sees an unset `data-side` and makes `runOverlayVectors` fail during the Dialog iteration. Assert `controller.state.placement` instead, or move this DOM-placement check to a positioned primitive such as Popover.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/dom/src/positioning-rebind.test.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/dom/src/positioning-rebind.test.ts:15\">\nP2: This test couples the public positioning suite to Floating UI's private `autoUpdate` API. A provider refactor could preserve the UIFn contract while unnecessarily breaking this test; verify rebinding through the public positioner contract and observable cleanup instead.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/dom/src/presence.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/dom/src/presence.ts:49\">\nP1: When a CSS motion-property list is longer than its duration list, CSS repeats durations, but `pairedMotion` counts only duration/delay entries. Short repeated events can therefore reach zero before the longest animation or transition ends; derive the expected event count from `animation-name`/`transition-property`, or retain timer-based completion instead of finishing from this count.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/dom/src/positioning.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/dom/src/positioning.ts:240\">\nP1: When a running positioner uses a resolver that creates a fresh virtual anchor, every automatic update enters this rebinding branch and recursively creates another `autoUpdate`; context-menu positioning can therefore overflow the stack. Rebind based on the actual observer target or resolver configuration, not virtual-anchor object identity, and add a regression test for a fresh virtual anchor resolver.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/dom/src/overlay.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/dom/src/overlay.ts:296\">\nP2: When a positioned overlay opens, this launches two concurrent position calculations because `start()` performs an initial auto-update while the explicit update is still pending. The positioner marks the first result stale and reports a recoverable error on every initial open; chain `start()` after the initial update so only one calculation runs.</violation>\n</file>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>**Requires human review**: Auto-approval blocked because this review re-detected 1 unresolved issue already reported by Cubic.<br />**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/116/ai_pr_review_1787502642736_abdf3638-644b-459a-9052-1ad5c22a880c?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F116)</sub>\n\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787502642736_abdf3638-644b-459a-9052-1ad5c22a880c:60d32b4058286bff8cfc8b48a347a4e0bff22230:e53b106d-bab5-4e6b-8fe4-3a0602dfd798 -->\n\n### chatgpt-codex-connector[bot] 2026-08-23T16:37:04Z\n\n### 💡 Codex Review\n\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\n\n**Reviewed commit:** `60d32b4058`\n    \n\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\n<br/>\n\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\n- Open a pull request for review\n- Mark a draft as ready\n- Comment \"@codex review\".\n\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\n\n\n\n\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. 