{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T03:41:38.945Z","ordinal":14324,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a024c5-b91b-72b3-ad56-490032d022a1","turn_id":"01a031db-b58e-77c0-8e9b-da6a53ad6063","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0d3207775ece027d016a8bbd6f960087d09ede4a05d6b34a6c","content":[{"type":"Text","text":":codex-annotation{index=\"1\"} Because `packages/admin/src/mcp.ts` projects admin operations into MCP tool definitions. It imports `McpFnObjectSchema` and `McpFnToolDefinition` from `@mcpfn/core` for type compatibility.\n\nIt is only a type-level dependency; the runtime accepts a structurally compatible registry. Therefore, copying the entire local `mcpfn` function into this PR was unnecessary—the types could be local or sourced from the published package."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1787542895704,"completed_at_ms":1787542898945}}
