{"timestamp":"2026-08-26T10:53:02.796Z","ordinal":14342,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a03db3-b5cc-7ba3-9365-c098104fcbcc","call_id":"call_x1BldRZ6Ze3Wys9tTsbiuCyE","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"67:applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev; reuse_rule=worktree/allowlist/gate procedure is reusable; PR heads, mergeability, and review state require live revalidation.\n86:- Move UiFn generated `.conduct` verifier output outside the PR worktree before staging. A green release gate does not prove mergeability: PR #118 was `UNSTABLE` and PR #119 remained `DIRTY` from a pre-existing base conflict at handoff. [Task 1]\n269:applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane; reuse_rule=workflow mechanics are reusable; PR heads, checks, mergeability, architecture state, and deployment evidence require live revalidation.\n399:# Task Group: August 23 Superfunctions PR #116 bounded remediation and scope diagnosis\n403:## Task 1: Refetch/fix PR #116 and diagnose imported MCPFn/UIFn scope, success\n411:- PR #116, SFNS-2, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, reviewThreads, nodeType, undefined versus null, authfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt, MCPFn, UIFn, d27cceb2\n421:- A review-fix pass is not a scope audit. Before dev-port remediation, compare the whole PR against the exact `origin/dev` inventory: SFNS-2’s MCPFn/UIFn expansion came from copying next-only workspace dependency trees, not from the intended dev-relevant admin scope. [Task 1]\n651:- SFN-22, splane, Super Console, manifest-driven, GH_CONFIG_DIR, PR #48, sf-next/next, git merge-tree, --match-head-commit, 523c66ae\n666:- A passing local suite does not clear external CI: remote CI was still running and Vercel account-plan checks were known failing at merge time. Keep that separate from mergeability/review state. The CiFn signed-download test was pre-existing adapter evidence, not an SFN-22 regression. [Task 1]\n697:applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane; reuse_rule=all worktree/PR counts, checks, and mergeability are snapshots; rerun live commands before action.\n726:- Use `git worktree list --porcelain`, `git branch -vv`, `gh pr list --state all ... headRefOid`, then `gh pr view` for mergeability/checks. Match PR head SHA to checked-out branch HEAD, but distinguish a dirty worktree whose committed SHA matches a PR from a worktree actually on that head branch. [Task 1]\n979:- when the user said “dont push yet” and requested consultation for non-straightforward conflicts -> preflight with `git merge-tree --write-tree`, preserve local commits, and stop for ambiguity. [Task 1]\n1809:- PR #38, `8ab8bb12`, `66a5fff2`, `12580dd2`, `GH_CONFIG_DIR`, `sf-next/next`, `package-lock.json`, `release-packages.json`, `git merge-tree --write-tree`\n1831:- Use `git merge-tree --write-tree` to expose shared-file conflicts before a real merge; do not call merge success proof that all hosted checks were green when checks are pending or unrelated Vercel failures remain. [Task 2]\n2574:- Symptom: a conflict appears again after a successful resolution push. Cause: `next` advanced. Fix: fetch `sf-next/next` and re-check mergeability immediately before `gh pr merge`. A detached stable-gate/browser child can mutate checked-in traces after the parent exits; use a persistent session, wait for children, then restore generated evidence and remove temporary Playwright artifacts. Keep Vercel/private-org, guardrails, and unavailable registry-signing failures separate from merge correctness. [Task 6]\n4011:## Task 8: Review and locally fix SRO-631 reshape mergeability without disturbing staged work, success\n4019:- btnextjs, SRO-631, reshape, mergeability, ackBlocked, normalizeMergeability, staged, unstaged, Node 22, Vitest, ESLint\n4056:- btnextjs, PR #748, SRO-704, git merge-tree --write-tree, git merge --no-commit --no-ff, MERGE_HEAD, ReshapeReviewModal, groupKeyForSource, ThemeProvider, Node 22, 1814 tests\n4082:- Preview the real conflict scope with `git merge-tree --write-tree HEAD origin/staging` before merging. For PR #748, one conflict in `ReshapeReviewModal.tsx` required keeping staging's `groupKeyForSource` grouping and SRO-704 semantic `bg-surface`; the isolated `DescopeSigninFlow` test also needed its real light `ThemeProvider`. [Task 15]\n4099:- Symptom: a UI acknowledgement guard is bypassable or mergeability display disagrees with its score. Cause: only one Create path was guarded and LLM fields were trusted independently. Fix: gate the shared callback and reconcile verdict/score before rendering or committing. [Task 8]\n{\"baseRefName\":\"dev\",\"baseRefOid\":\"72aabce915426325450663feffd7a53089ef4489\",\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-21T15:55:31Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"samalaaravind02@gmail.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"name\":\"Aravind Samala\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-21T15:55:31Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"SFNS-2 port Super Console admin surfaces to dev\",\"oid\":\"d27cceb2b786bcb08c2be5445ece12146c1123c4\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-22T02:50:32Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"samalaaravind02@gmail.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"name\":\"Aravind Samala\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-22T02:50:32Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix: address PR review feedback\",\"oid\":\"8d16f12d9a673cbed04f6c20cc9a06b0e770389e\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-22T04:15:40Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"samalaaravind02@gmail.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDU3NTcx\",\"login\":\"thyaravind\",\"name\":\"Aravind Samala\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-22T04:15:40Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix: address latest PR review feedback\",\"oid\":\"8ad9b668d13ae8354920ab8d6e4ef6f1b01eeaec\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-22T06:00:32Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\