meric document searchable. Alias every finite number whose canonical string matches the target, or reject unsupported numeric IDs during indexing.</violation>\\n</file>\\n\\n<file name=\\\"billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts:68\\\">\\nP2: When the manifest advertises catalog fields absent from the records, this generic filter drops every record for a non-`undefined` value and the sorter falls back to `id`. Align the manifest with the record shape or map those fields before applying the controls.</violation>\\n</file>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/116/ai_pr_review_1787372161972_6a3d7534-32a0-44ed-b613-0338ea4f04cd?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F116)</sub>\\n\\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787372161972_6a3d7534-32a0-44ed-b613-0338ea4f04cd:8ad9b668d13ae8354920ab8d6e4ef6f1b01eeaec:e132b4ff-cab0-498f-ac59-f8230337c676 -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T06:05:22Z\",\n      \"body\": \"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `e1f368ac35`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting 