<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:26:13Z\",\n      \"body\": \"> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> The new deterministic scheduler can execute an interval after it has already been canceled by an earlier callback in the same flush.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `616f549`:\\n\\n- **Nested context-bound resources** — made AuthFn sessions and DataFn records reachable from their parent detail pages without exposing invalid standalone lists.\\n- **Canonicalized administration scopes** — normalized organization-root aliases for Super Console requests and HostFn cursor binding.\\n- **Corrected the CSRF projection** — included provider CSRF metadata for safe-method mutations as well as unsafe HTTP methods.\\n- **Expanded grapheme fallback matching** — grouped common modifier, regional-indicator, combining-mark, and ZWJ sequences when `Intl.Segmenter` is unavailable.\\n- **Tightened Phase 14 tracing** — added interval advancement, numeric timer ordering, and exact setter-state matching to the parity harness.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 0daaba2;\\nif commits have landed on SFNS-2 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\\n\\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\\n- Files reviewed: 1797\\n- Commits reviewed: 1