ev (72aabce)\\n- Head: SFNS-2 (09ff931)\\n- Reviewed commits:\\n  - 09ff931 — fix: close post-push admin review gaps\\n- Prior pullfrog review: e3e7054 (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#pullrequestreview-5000285051)\\n-->\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [Fix all ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/116?action=fix&review_id=5000305659) ｜ [Fix 👍s ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/116?action=fix-approved&review_id=5000305659) ｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32576627004/job/97039815460) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:13:41Z\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:review-summary:start -->\\n**2 issues found** across 15 files (changes from recent commits).\\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:end -->\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)</summary>\\n\\n```text\\n\\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\\n\\n\\n<file name=\\\"filefn/admin/src/index.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"filefn/admin/src/index.ts:367\\\">\\nP2: When a FileFn service returns `accepted: true` without `item.token`, this callback throws after the share was created and leaves the share active without durable cleanup. Require `item.token` for the create-share contract and provide a durable reconciliation path for responses that still omit it.</violation>\\n</file>\\n\\n<file name=\\\"superconsole/tests/ui/admin-api.test.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"superconsole/tests/ui/admin-api.test.ts:192\\\">\\nP2: Per the HTML spec and current Chrome/Firefox/Safari, `window.open(url, '_blank', 'noopener')` returns null because the `noopener` feature is set. The mock makes it return `{ opener: window }`, so it asserts the opposite of the real browser contract: in production `popup` is always null, `openSafeAdminDownload` returns false, `openSafeAdminDownloadReceipt` resolves false, and ActionButton.svelte throws 'The download receipt did not contain a trusted URL.' after every successful download. Model the real contract (mock `window.open` to return null) and change the implementation so a null result from a noopener open is not treated as failure; the `popup.opener = null` branch is dead code in real browsers.</violation>\\n</file>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/116/ai_pr_review_1787407692009_42964375-ef58-4926-b9f5-913ba40a5cc1?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F116)</sub>\\n\\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787407692009_42964375-ef58-4926-b9f5-913ba40a5cc1:b1157c7823c35cf2d060ab21d9e1ddc93d2aa943:de51d2b7-51be-4233-98de-40e1e764bc05 -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\n      \"body\": \"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `b1157c7823`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](http