le>\\n\\n<file name=\\\"uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"uifn/svelte/lib/internal/compound.ts:570\\\">\\nP2: Re-selecting the currently selected file hangs the picker. After the first selection, `input.files` keeps the chosen file, so picking the same file again fires no `change` event; `capability.pick()`'s promise never settles and the FileUpload controller stays in status `picking`, silently dropping the selection. Clear the input before reopening the dialog: in `createUIFnNativeFilePickerCapability.pick()` do `input.value = ''` right before `input.click()`, so a repeat selection of the same file regenerates the `change` event (and add a browser test for pick → pick same file).</violation>\\n</file>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/116/ai_pr_review_1787541452815_f2c5f9f1-9798-4b9f-9dcc-fe919289bd1f?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F116)</sub>\\n\\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787541452815_f2c5f9f1-9798-4b9f-9dcc-fe919289bd1f:c281437b9693a8f80afbcd502bb3e4de6615ccb8:ea86a593-4a84-44d3-8795-bd65d84a692b -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-24T04:14:48Z\",\n      \"body\": \"> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> The synchronous observer-installation guard still permits a live positioner to remain subscribed to the wrong virtual anchor.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `1551ef7`, I reviewed the corrective commit through `c281437`:\\n\\n- **Corrected MCP schema variance** — classified removal of a previously required property from an open input schema as additive while retaining breaking classification for newly required removals.\\n\\n- **Preserved nullable action inputs** — routed nullable unions through JSON editing, retained JSON `null` defaults, and rejected empty union combinators.\\n\\n- **Hardened UIFn runtime boundaries** — represented pre-year-zero calendar cells explicitly, terminated unavailable lower-bound navigation, and guarded synchronous position-observer installation.\\n\\n- **Connected native FileUpload ownership** — reconciled declared file collections and wired Svelte trigger, native input, bound state, and form reset behavior through the DOM bridge.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against c281437;\\nif commits have landed on SFNS-2 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\\n\\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\\n- Files reviewed: 1809\\n- Commits reviewed: 39\\n- Base: dev (72aabce)\\n- Head: SFNS-2 (c281437)\\n- Reviewed commits:\\n  - c281437b — fix: address refreshed PR review findings\\n  - 1551ef79 — fix: address current PR review findings\\n  - 4d2b29c9 — fix: address latest PR review findings\\n  - 60d32b40 — fix(uifn): address latest overlay review findings\\n  - 66ccad4a — fix: address latest PR review findings\\n  - 31dc06e6 — fix: close current PR review findings\\n  - 7c7ca088 — fix: close latest PR review gaps\\n  - d9b60c51 — fix: resolve current PR review feedback\\n  - 2011d9c6 — fix: address latest PR review findings\\n  - afb902da — fix: close current PR review gaps\\n  - 16a31f15 — fix: address latest PR review findings\\n  - db08968e — fix: close reconciliation review gaps\\n  - 73485e82 — fix: reconcile pending admin side effects\\n  - fbb3868f — fix: resolve single-pass PR review findings\\n  - 9cf9e611 — fix: close single-pass review findings\\n  - 966f3141 — fix: resolve final admin review round\\n  - b1157c78 — fix: resolve latest admin review findings\\n  - 09ff9316 — fix: close post-push admin review gaps\\n  -