in registry.ts line 234 and `route()` in openapi.ts line 71, both `trim().split(/\\\\s+/, 1)[0]`). Four places now derive `method`/`path` from a string route with three distinct implementations that must stay in sync; a future change to one (e.g. method normalization or path handling) can silently diverge the registry route, validation, matching, and OpenAPI generation. Extract the split-and-validate logic into a single shared helper in this package and use it from `routeOf`, `operationRoutePath`, `routeMatches`, and `route`.</violation>\\n</file>\\n\\n<file name=\\\"uifn/core/scripts/build.mjs\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"uifn/core/scripts/build.mjs:13\\\">\\nP2: The generated wildcard primitive entries now reintroduce removed `createX` APIs, contradicting the package’s breaking-no-shims contract. Remove these aliases, or update the migration manifest and compatibility contract to document their incompatible legacy behavior.</violation>\\n</file>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>Reply with feedback, questions, or to request a fix.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/116/ai_pr_review_1787367056771_267b63b5-9188-46fd-83de-8b2d5628a52a?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F116)</sub>\\n\\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787367056771_267b63b5-9188-46fd-83de-8b2d5628a52a:8d16f12d9a673cbed04f6c20cc9a06b0e770389e:e23e6324-2c6c-4e6a-843e-4e4bd3612e24 -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T04:20:36Z\",\n      \"body\": \"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `8ad9b668d1`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T04:26:09Z\",\n      \"body\": \"> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> The latest fix commit introduces three correctness and resource-control regressions that should be addressed before merge.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `8d16f12`:\\n\\n- **Implemented domain list controls** — added BillFn filtering, search, sorting, and cursor pagination, and extended PlugFn sync-job pagination beyond the first hundred rows.\\n- **Centralized admin route handling** — extracted shared route parsing and rejected reserved prototype segments in presentation input paths.\\n- **Corrected transport edge cases** — aligned MCP `toJSON` canonicalization and removed both string and numeric forms of numeric-looking SearchFn document IDs.\\n- **Hardened runtime behavior** — fixed the prior Svelte scanner and range endpoint findings, registration cleanup races, reentrant async cancellation, locale-search performance, and legacy avatar subscriptions.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 8ad9b66;\\nif commits have landed on SFNS-2 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\\n\\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\\n- Files reviewed: 1783\\n- Commits reviewed: 3\\n- Base: dev (72aabce)\\n- Head: SFNS-2 (8ad9b66)\\n- Reviewed commits:\\n  - 8ad9b66 — fix: address latest PR review feedback\\n  - 8d16f12 — fix: address PR review feedback\\n  - d27cceb — SFNS-2 port Super Console admin surfaces to dev\\n- Prior pul