lugFn paging and tenant-isolation fixes still need a database rollout and deterministic page ordering before merge.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `8ad9b66`, covering fix commit `e1f368a`:\\n\\n- **Aligned BillFn controls** — matched catalog presentation fields to real product, plan, and price records and added numeric sorting and cursor validation.\\n- **Moved PlugFn paging into storage** — added tenant-scoped sync-job persistence, storage offsets, and tenant filtering for installation and sync-job lists.\\n- **Made SearchFn IDs explicit** — separated string and numeric document targets so deleting one representation preserves the other.\\n- **Reworked UIFn edge handling** — added collator-based grapheme matching and corrected floating-point range endpoint alignment.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against e1f368a;\\nif commits have landed on SFNS-2 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\\n\\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\\n- Files reviewed: 1790\\n- Commits reviewed: 4\\n- Base: dev (72aabce)\\n- Head: SFNS-2 (e1f368a)\\n- Reviewed commits:\\n  - d27cceb — SFNS-2 port Super Console admin surfaces to dev\\n  - 8d16f12 — fix: address PR review feedback\\n  - 8ad9b66 — fix: address latest PR review feedback\\n  - e1f368a — fix: address refreshed admin review findings\\n- Prior pullfrog review: 8ad9b66 (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#pullrequestreview-4998938669)\\n-->\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [Fix all ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/116?action=fix&review_id=4999281739) ｜ [Fix 👍s ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/116?action=fix-approved&review_id=4999281739) ｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32555839931/job/96989690073) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T06:09:39Z\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:review-summary:start -->\\n**1 issue found** across 19 files (changes from recent commits).\\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:end -->\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)</summary>\\n\\n```text\\n\\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\\n\\n\\n<file name=\\\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts:56\\\">\\nP2: For values with no exact normalized substring match, the new collation fallback segments the whole value and, for each starting grapheme, tries up to queryLength±8 slice lengths with an array slice+join+`collator.compare` per attempt. This is an O(n) segmentation plus O(n·span) comparison scan per call — a regression from the previous single regex pass. I measured ~48–93ms to reject a single 50k-char non-matching value. Consider bounding the scan (e.g. limit value segments examined or bail out after a cap) so filtering large lists stays within the old single-pass cost when there is no match.</violation>\\n</file>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/116/ai_pr_re