- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:26:13Z\",\n      \"body\": \"> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> The new deterministic scheduler can execute an interval after it has already been canceled by an earlier callback in the same flush.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `616f549`:\\n\\n- **Nested context-bound resources** — made AuthFn sessions and DataFn records reachable from their parent detail pages without exposing invalid standalone lists.\\n- **Canonicalized administration scopes** — normalized organization-root aliases for Super Console requests and HostFn cursor binding.\\n- **Corrected the CSRF projection** — included provider CSRF metadata for safe-method mutations as well as unsafe HTTP methods.\\n- **Expanded grapheme fallback matching** — grouped common modifier, regional-indicator, combining-mark, and ZWJ sequences when `Intl.Segmenter` is unavailable.\\n- **Tightened Phase 14 tracing** — added interval advancement, numeric timer ordering, and exact setter-state matching to the parity harness.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 0daaba2;\\nif commits have landed on SFNS-2 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\\n\\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\\n- Files reviewed: 1797\\n- Commits reviewed: 11\\n- Base: dev (72aabce)\\n- Head: SFNS-2 (0daaba2)\\n- Reviewed commits:\\n  - d27cceb — SFNS-2 port Super Console admin surfaces to dev\\n  - 8d16f12 — fix: address PR review feedback\\n  - 8ad9b66 — fix: address latest PR review feedback\\n  - e1f368a — fix: address refreshed admin review findings\\n  - 9307965 — fix: address post-push review feedback\\n  - e3800be — fix: track SuperConsole app error types\\n  - 21fbc39 — fix: address latest PR review findings\\n  - e1062e1 — test: allow Svelte catalog render in CI\\n  - 94c8cc3 — fix: keep webhook metadata lint-clean\\n  - 616f549 — fix: resolve refreshed PR review findings\\n  - 0daaba2 — fix: address post-push review feedback\\n- Prior pullfrog review: 616f549 (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#pullrequestreview-4999793245)\\n-->\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [Fix all ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/116?action=fix&review_id=4999847009) ｜ [Fix 👍s ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/116?action=fix-approved&review_id=4999847009) ｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32564177298/job/97010256347) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:31:22Z\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:review-summary:start -->\\n**1 issue found** across 10 files (changes from recent commits).\\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:end -->\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)</summary>\\n\\n```text\\n\\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\\n\\n\\n<file name=\\\"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts:709\\\">\\nP2: When a user continues pagination with a cursor issued by the previous HostFn version, this check rejects it because the old position contains only `offset`. Version the cursor format and provide a compatibility path for in-flight cursors so rolling deployments do not strand paginated admin pages.</violation>\\n</file>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/116/ai_pr_review_1787390912160_0d49e94d-0e2b-4502-80bd-9d95ac9c20be?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F116)</sub>\\n\\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787390912160_0d49e94d-0e2b-4502-80bd-9d95ac9c20be:239ba000b3f97ca2dbc9e5c0207f41da2a4b44ba:c399a9ed-1c7a-49dd-b678-501e2107db35 -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:34:27Z\",\n      \"body\": \"> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> The strengthened trace validator still accepts malformed optional evidence and normalizes it lossily.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `0daaba2`, covering fix commit `239ba00`:\\n\\n- **Preserved BotFn relationships** — added atomic store operations and race coverage for bot deletion and channel connection.\\n- **Bound HostFn cursors** — tied cursor offsets to each list operation and its active filter or parent identity.\\n- **Strengthened UIFn trace validation** — validated required nested evidence, environment fields, result values, and cleanup counters.\\n- **Corrected UIFn runtime edges** — suppressed canceled same-deadline intervals and limited fallback ZWJ grouping to pictographic sequences.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 239ba00;\\nif commits have landed on SFNS-2 s