uestions or update the PR. Try commenting \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T10:51:55Z\",\n      \"body\": \"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `a422e0fa93`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T10:53:17Z\",\n      \"body\": \"> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> UIFn normalization still corrupts a valid trace after the validator accepts it.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `239ba00`, covering fix commit `a422e0f`:\\n\\n- **Canonicalized MCP templates** — rejected equivalent non-query resource-template patterns that differ only by variable names.\\n\\n- **Bound PlugFn cursors** — tied list cursors to their operation and active filter identity.\\n\\n- **Preserved encoded identifiers** — decoded encoded SearchFn resource names and allowed single-encoded slashes in Super Console route parameters without weakening traversal checks.\\n\\n- **Strengthened trace validation** — validated optional step, transaction, and part evidence and distinguished shared acyclic JSON objects from cycles.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against a422e0f;\\nif commits have landed on SFNS-2 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\\n\\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\\n- Files reviewed: 1797\\n- Commits reviewed: 13\\n- Base: dev (72aabce)\\n- Head: SFNS-2 (a422e0f)\\n- Reviewed commits:\\n  - a422e0f — fix: address final PR review wave\\n  - 239ba00 — fix: close remaining review edge cases\\n  - 0daaba2 — fix: address post-push review feedback\\n  - 616f549 — fix: resolve refreshed PR review findings\\n  - 94c8cc3 — fix: keep webhook metadata lint-clean\\n  - e1062e1 — test: allow Svelte catalog render in CI\\n  - 21fbc39 — fix: address latest PR review findings\\n  - e3800be — fix: track SuperConsole app error types\\n  - 9307965 — fix: address post-push review feedback\\n  - e1f368a — fix: address refreshed admin review findings\\n  - 8ad9b66 — fix: address latest PR review feedback\\n  - 8d16f12 — fix: address PR review feedback\\n  - d27cceb — SFNS-2 port Super Console admin surfaces to dev\\n- Prior pullfrog review: 239ba00 (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#pullrequestreview-4999860190)\\n-->\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [Fix all ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/116?action=fix&review_id=4999971401) ｜ [Fix 👍s ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/116?action=fix-approved&review_id=4999971401) ｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32568555254/job/97020640348) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T10:54:51Z\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:review-summary:start -->\\n**All reported issues were addressed** across 11 files (changes from recent commits).\\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:end -->\\n\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/116/ai_pr_review_1787395673321_4e3efeb4-590b-4d76-8204-12fc68a1a494?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F116)</sub>\\n\\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787395673321_4e3efeb4-590b-4d76-8204-12fc68a1a494:a422e0fa933ac6b328293a76c4b6167bb50e95c3:851c703b-f91e-40a3-9120-49bce4958eb2 -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:32Z\",\n      \"body\": \"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `593b81f203`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:10:39Z\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:review-summary:start -->\\n**6 issues found across 16 files (changes from recent commits).**\\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:end -->\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)</summary>\\n\\n```text\\n\\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\\n\\n\\n<file name=\\\"billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts:90\\\">\\nP2: When `search` is empty or whitespace-only, filtering treats it as no search but the cursor identity treats it differently, so an equivalent next-page request is rejected. Normalize empty searches to `undefined` before computing the identity.</violation>\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"2\\\" location=\\\"billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts:92\\\">\\nP2: When callers omit a sort direction or send a descriptor without a field, the comparator uses the same effective ordering but the cursor identity changes. Build the identity from normalized effective sort descriptors so equivalent page requests can continue.</violation>\\n</file>\\n\\n<file name=\\\"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts:85\\\">\\nP2: During a rolling deployment, a page cursor issued by the previous server contains only `offset`, so this check rejects the next-page request. Version the cursor schema and retain a compatibility path while old cursors drain, or explicitly handle restart semantics instead of invalidating `version: 1` tokens silently.</violation>\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"2\\\" location=\\\"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts:186\\\">\\nP3: `listAdapters` uses an operation identity that is not declared or registered. Use `searchfn.adapters-backends.list` so operation-bound cursor validation remains consistent.</violation>\\n</file>\\n\\n<file name=\\\"superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"superconsole/tests/server/super-console.test.ts:382\\\">\\nP3: 'does not route an encoded separator embedded in a literal segment' passes even if the server treated %2f as a real route separator: decoded or not, records%2fother matches no registered route, so the 404/OPERATION_NOT_ENABLED assertions cannot detect a routing regression. Use a path whose over-decoded form would hit a real route, e.g. /api/admin/v1/modules/examplefn/resources%2frecords (would dispatch the records handler if %2f were split), and keep asserting 404 and handler not called.</violation>\\n</file>\\n\\n<file name=\\\"packages/admin/src/pagination.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"packages/admin/src/pagination.ts:47\\\">\\nP3: The cursor identity is produced by `stableSerialize`, which sorts object keys with `localeCompare`. That ordering depends on the process locale and ICU version, so a cursor identity computed by one server process (or before a redeploy) can fail strict equality against the same query recomputed by another process, rejecting valid cursors with \\\"does not belong to this collection query.\\\" Sort keys by UTF-16 code units (`.sort()` default or `(a,b) => a < b ? -1 : a > b ? 1 : 0`) so identities are reproducible across processes.</violation>\\n</file>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/116/ai_pr_review_1787396698854_760c5555-5a8c-4949-aee6-5e8d0b1c408b?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F116)</sub>\\n\\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787396698854_760c5555-5a8c-4949-aee6-5e8d0b1c408b:593b81f203083e025edfe71463b14b5139ea236a:5a311de1-61b7-4d68-8481-4dcf664e4fbd -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:16:37Z\",\n      \"body\": \"> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> The new semicolon-template exception makes MCP resource dispatch registration-order dependent under the pinned SDK and must be fixed before merge.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `a422e0f`, covering fix commit `593b81f`:\\n\\n- **Bound collection cursors** — tied BillFn and SearchFn offsets to their operation and active query, and tied owner-scoped PlugFn offsets to the mapped identity.\\n\\n- **Preserved composite identifiers** — percent-encoded colon-bearing DataFn resource names and verified SearchFn deletion under encoded resources.\\n\\n- **Tightened route decoding** — distinguished encoded separators in route parameters from encoded separators embedded in literal Super Console segments.\\n\\n- **Corrected semantic normalization** — preserved reused acyclic trace objects while retaining cycle detection.\\n\\n- **Refined MCP template identity** — distinguished semicolon path-parameter expressions from canonicalized non-query templates.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 593b81f;\\nif commits have landed on SFNS-2 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\\n\\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\\n- Files reviewed: 16\\n- Commits reviewed: 1\\n- Base: dev (72aabce)\\n- Head: SFNS-2 (593b81f)\\n- Reviewed commits:\\n  - 593b81f — fix: close post-refetch review issues\\n- Prior pullfrog review: a422e0f (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#pullrequestreview-4999971401)\\n-->\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [Fix all ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/116?action=fix&review_id=5000002240) ｜ [Fix 👍s ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/116?action=fix-approved&review_id=5000002240) ｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32569323032/job/97022407951) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:19:40Z\",\n      \"body\": \"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `5e968d7056`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:40:41Z\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:review-summary:start -->\\n**3 issues found** across 8 files (changes from recent commits).\\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:end -->\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)</summary>\\n\\n```text\\n\\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\\n\\n\\n<file name=\\\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts:122\\\">\\nP3: scoped() now deep-clones every element before listDeployments/listDomains/listVariables apply their targetId filter, so entries that get discarded are cloned wastefully (and listVariables transiently clones the stored secret value before stripping it). Filter by targetId first, then clone only what is returned.</violation>\\n</file>\\n\\n<file name=\\\"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts:727\\\">\\nP2: When a record’s `updatedAt` changes between page requests, this offset cursor no longer identifies the same page boundary, so records can be skipped or repeated. Sort by an immutable key such as `id`, or switch this cursor to a keyset containing the sort key.</violation>\\n</file>\\n\\n<file name=\\\"mcpfn/core/tests/protocol.test.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"mcpfn/core/tests/protocol.test.ts:64\\\">\\nP2: This new assertion codifies a false-positive duplicate: `docs://users/{;name}` is rejected as a duplicate of `docs://users/{id}` only because `resourceTemplatePattern`'s operator set `[+#./?&]` omits `;`, so `{;name}` normalizes to `{v0}` like `{id}`. `;` is a valid RFC 6570 operator; sections prefixed this way match `docs://users/;name=...`, distinct from plain-segment matches. Valid template forms using `{;...}` are now rejected with a misleading \\\"Duplicate ... URI\\\" error. Add `;` to the operator set in registry.ts so `{;v0}` is kept and genuinely overlapping matrix templates still collide; if `;` templates are instead intentionally unsupported, reject them with an explicit message and code rather than a duplicate error.</violation>\\n</file>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/116/ai_pr_review_1787398521169_fd62b8a1-18ae-4089-b82f-628a564f36b9?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F116)</sub>\\n\\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787398521169_fd62b8a1-18ae-4089-b82f-628a564f36b9:b2718e4ed53dd5ee5e04dac45c917bba478d3a1c:565efb3e-1cfe-4884-a6da-1f223d760f97 -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:41:37Z\",\n      \"body\": \"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `b2718e4ed5`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T11:49:44Z\",\n      \"body\": \"> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> HostFn pagination remains nondeterministic for some valid IDs and can repeat or skip records across pages.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** in `b2718e4` since the prior Pullfrog review:\\n\\n- **Stabilized HostFn reads** — sorted complete HostFn result sets before applying offset cursors and strengthened the pagination regression.\\n- **Isolated memory-store records** — returned defensive clones from HostFn list and get operations and added focused coverage.\\n- **Closed MCP template ambiguity** — rejected semicolon templates that overlap ordinary variables under the pinned SDK matcher.\\n- **Forwarded Svelte root attributes** — routed undeclared root props to native elements while retaining declared controller inputs.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written aga