n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:05:26Z\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:review-summary:start -->\\n**All reported issues were addressed** across 2 files (changes from recent commits).\\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:end -->\\n\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/116/ai_pr_review_1787399740042_cfffbf2e-faf4-4791-9c0b-3ebf79abc3c1?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F116)</sub>\\n\\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787399740042_cfffbf2e-faf4-4791-9c0b-3ebf79abc3c1:c6aea5c7b1c3b023d51510b821e61b7a7f17b32f:22be5463-3f8c-4e83-93ac-026ff63a485e -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:22:43Z\",\n      \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:review-summary:start -->\\n**1 issue found** across 8 files (changes from recent commits).\\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:end -->\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)</summary>\\n\\n```text\\n\\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\\n\\n\\n<file name=\\\"mcpfn/core/src/server.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"mcpfn/core/src/server.ts:124\\\">\\nP3: This changes the public cursor shape, but `mcpfn/core/README.md` still documents `mcpfn:<offset>` cursors. Update the package documentation to describe the opaque, operation/collection-bound cursor and its expiry behavior.</violation>\\n</file>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/116/ai_pr_review_1787401157506_96f4234c-c2b5-4686-801a-30c7d1327b4c?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F116)</sub>\\n\\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787401157506_96f4234c-c2b5-4686-801a-30c7d1327b4c:358c4d2bec007a1e6c8a738302df38e03a6281e4:8add03eb-2e54-4224-a134-d62e7a9b9b83 -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:31:55Z\",\n      \"body\": \"> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> The deterministic Svelte root-prop fix regresses valid typed native properties and should be corrected before merging.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** since the prior Pullfrog review at `c6aea5c`:\\n\\n- **Bound MCP pagination**: tied cursors to both the list operation and a hash of the currently visible collection.\\n- **Expanded resource actions**: exposed targeted read operations other than the selected list and detail operations.\\n- **Made root-prop routing deterministic**: replaced browser-only discovery with static native-property classification and normalized `aria`, `data`, and `on` bags.\\n- **Hardened token validation**: rejected partial token leaves and cyclic token-group objects before recursive flattening.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 358c4d2;\\nif commits have landed on SFNS-2 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\\n\\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\\n- Files reviewed: 1799\\n- Commits reviewed: 18\\n- Base: dev (72aabce)\\n- Head: SFNS-2 (358c4d2)\\n- Reviewed commits:\\n  - 358c4d2 — fix: close final PR review gaps\\n  - c6aea5c — fix: preserve Svelte controller prop routing\\n  - b2718e4 — fix: address final refetched review findings\\n  - 5e968d7 — refactor: keep cursor identity package-local\\n  - 593b81f — fix: close post-refetch review issues\\n  - a422e0f — fix: address final PR review wave\\n  - 239ba00 — fix: close remaining review edge cases\\n  - 0daaba2 — fix: address post-push review feedback\\n  - 616f549 — fix: resolve refreshed PR review findings\\n  - 94c8cc3 — fix: keep webhook metadata lint-clean\\n  - e1062e1 — test: allow Svelte catalog render in CI\\n  - 21fbc39 — fix: address latest PR review findings\\n  - e3800be — fix: track SuperConsole app error types\\n  - 9307965 — fix: address post-push review feedback\\n  - e1f368a — fix: address refreshed admin review findings\\n  - 8ad9b66 — fix: address latest PR review feedback\\n  - 8d16f12 — fix: address PR review feedback\\n  - d27cceb — SFNS-2 port Super Console admin surfaces to dev\\n- Prior pullfrog review: c6aea5c (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#pullrequestreview-5000145552)\\n-->\\n\\n### ℹ️ Cursor documentation no longer matches the runtime\\n\\n`mcpfn/core/README.md` still describes list cursors as `mcpfn:<offset>`, but this commit changes the public format and semantics to bind the operation and visible collection. Consumers reading the package documentation will implement or troubleshoot against a contract the server no longer emits.\\n\\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\\n\\n````markdown\\n# Document the bound MCP cursor contract\\n\\n## Affected sites\\n- `mcpfn/core/README.md:92` — promises the old offset-only cursor format.\\n- `mcpfn/core/src/server.ts:95-126` — emits and validates operation- and collection-bound cursors.\\n\\n## Required outcome\\n- Describe the current opaque cursor format and its invalidation behavior when the operation or visible collection changes.\\n````\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-gr