 as outside the configured API. Constrain this option for the SvelteKit transport or mount/delegate routes using the configured base path.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At superconsole/src/lib/server/transport.ts, line 25:\\n\\n<comment>When an installation sets `apiBasePath` to anything other than `/api/admin/v1`, the mounted transport cannot serve it: custom-path requests do not match these routes, while requests at the fixed path are rejected as outside the configured API. Constrain this option for the SvelteKit transport or mount/delegate routes using the configured base path.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@\\n+      headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json; charset=utf-8', 'cache-control': 'no-store' },\\n+    });\\n+  }\\n+  return console.handle(request);\\n+}\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bV47B\",\n      \"path\": \"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"line\": 79,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7klGdY\",\n        \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T03:11:11Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3834931032\",\n        \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=53368711-c4f6-4ddd-a894-4fa095bceaac -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e23e6324-2c6c-4e6a-843e-4e4bd3612e24 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":5} -->\\nP3: This service issues and accepts plain offset cursors that are not signed or authenticated; `decodeAdminCursor`'s own contract requires production providers to issue opaque, signed cursor positions. Any operator in scope can forge or alter an offset. This is only a data-exposure/page-skip risk (scope is still validated), but it diverges from the documented guidance to use signed cursors for production admin surfaces.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 71:\\n\\n<comment>This service issues and accepts plain offset cursors that are not signed or authenticated; `decodeAdminCursor`'s own contract requires production providers to issue opaque, signed cursor positions. Any operator in scope can forge or alter an offset. This is only a data-exposure/page-skip risk (scope is still validated), but it diverges from the documented guidance to use signed cursors for production admin surfaces.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -39,21 +43,63 @@ function item(value: object): AdminOperationResult<SearchFnItemOutput> {\\n+    }\\n+    return String(left.id ?? \\\"\\\").localeCompare(String(right.id ?? \\\"\\\"));\\n+  });\\n+  const decoded = input.cursor\\n+    ? decodeAdminCursor<{ offset?: unknown }>(input.cursor, context.scope)\\n+    : { offset: 0 };\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bWSjP\",\n      \"path\": \"billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"line\": 82,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kls7Z\",\n        \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T04:32:38Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835088601\",\n        \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=d37f08b0-fdf9-47e7-a2ba-9175b691b67a -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=e132b4ff-cab0-498f-ac59-f8230337c676 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: When the manifest advertises catalog fields absent from the records, this generic filter drops every record for a non-`undefined` value and the sorter falls back to `id`. Align the manifest with the record shape or map those fields before applying the controls.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At billfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts, line 68:\\n\\n<comment>When the manifest advertises catalog fields absent from the records, this generic filter drops every record for a non-`undefined` value and the sorter falls back to `id`. Align the manifest with the record shape or map those fields before applying the controls.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -51,8 +54,35 @@ function asJson(value: object): JsonRecord {\\n+    records = records.filter((value) => JSON.stringify(value).toLowerCase().includes(query));\\n+  }\\n+  if (input.filter) {\\n+    records = records.filter((value) => Object.entries(input.filter!).every(([key, expected]) => Object.is(value[key], expected)));\\n+  }\\n+  const sorts = input.sort ?? [];\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXaG9\",\n      \"path\": \"datafn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"line\": 502,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7knZEt\",\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T07:39:29Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835531565\",\n        \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Supply a resource selector before exposing Records**\\n\\nWhen an operator opens the DataFn Records card in Super Console, the generated list request contains no `filter`, because this resource declares neither presentation filters nor a parent binding. Requiring `filter` here therefore makes the default Records route fail validation on every visit, leaving record browsing unusable unless the operator manually constructs a JSON query parameter; add a control/binding for `filter.resource` or stop advertising this as a standalone list.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bXfQa\",\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"line\": 738,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kngc-\",\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T07:57:05Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835561790\",\n        \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Encode cursor payloads as UTF-8**\\n\\nWhen any active scope identifier contains a non-Latin-1 character and a HostFn list has another page, `btoa(JSON.stringify(...))` throws `InvalidCharacterError` while constructing `nextCursor`, causing an otherwise successful list request to fail. Admin scope validation permits arbitrary nonblank Unicode strings, so encode the JSON as UTF-8 bytes before base64 encoding and reverse that transformation when decoding.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bX1GN\",\n      \"path\": \"botfn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\n      \"line\": 292,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7koAB3\",\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:14:07Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835691127\",\n        \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Make bot deletion and channel connection atomic**\\n\\nWhen `connectChannel` and `deleteBot` run concurrently, the connect path can observe the bot here, then the delete path can observe no channels and delete it, after which the connect path persists a channel for the now-missing bot. Because the store contract exposes only these separate reads and writes, even the supplied memory implementation permits an orphaned active external binding; enforce the bot-exists/channel-empty invariant atomically in the persistence layer.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bX52F\",\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"line\": 709,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7koG58\",\n        \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T09:31:22Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835719292\",\n        \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=44d0df05-0c14-4598-be82-2f7f6eb7f22a -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=c399a9ed-1c7a-49dd-b678-501e2107db35 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP2: When a user continues pagination with a cursor issued by the previous HostFn version, this check rejects it because the old position contains only `offset`. Version the cursor format and provide a compatibility path for in-flight cursors so rolling deployments do not strand paginated admin pages.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it…4587 tokens truncated…ds.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Expose read-classified resource actions**\\n\\nWhen a resource has a non-list/get read operation, this filter removes it from the only detail-page action projection. In the inspected manifests this makes `filefn.files.download`, `filefn.artifacts.download`, and `apifn.specs.compare` unreachable from the generic Super Console UI even though their capabilities are enabled; distinguish read actions from canonical list/detail reads rather than dropping every read-classified operation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bYwNo\",\n      \"path\": \"apifn/admin/src/operator-service.ts\",\n      \"line\": 301,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kpWDb\",\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T12:34:49Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836043483\",\n        \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject credentials embedded in environment URLs**\\n\\nWhen `baseUrl` is an HTTP(S) URL such as `REDACTED`, this validation accepts it and persists `parsed.toString()`. Environment records are explicitly presented as non-secret endpoints and return `baseUrl` without redaction, so the embedded credential is exposed through list/get responses and the generic console; reject URLs with a nonempty `username` or `REDACTED` before storing them.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bY_MU\",\n      \"path\": \"searchfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"line\": 594,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kprf8\",\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T13:27:17Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836131324\",\n        \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Expose document actions as collection actions**\\n\\nWhen SearchFn is operated through the generic Super Console, `documents` has no list or get operation (`domainReadResourceIds` excludes it), but `index` and `remove-document` are projected here as ID-bound resource actions. The module page only renders collection actions, while the non-listable documents resource has no reachable detail page, so both operations are unavailable in the UI; project these action-only operations as collection actions so their `id` inputs can be entered in the action form.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bZFMh\",\n      \"path\": \"filefn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"line\": 199,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kp0NX\",\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T13:48:01Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836166999\",\n        \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Make share-link creation replay-safe after audit failures**\\n\\nWhen `shares.createShareLink` succeeds but the required terminal audit write fails, `AdminDispatcher` returns a dependency error after the live share and its one-time plaintext token have already been created. Because this operation explicitly disables idempotency, a retry creates another share instead of recovering the first result; the first link remains active while its token is lost, and it cannot be revoked through this admin API because revocation requires that original token. Preserve the result behind an idempotency key or otherwise reconcile/revoke the created share on post-execution failure.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bZNZ3\",\n      \"path\": \"filefn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"line\": 367,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kqAJq\",\n        \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:13:41Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836215914\",\n        \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=ae4eaeb5-91cc-4b8f-94ea-7038ebd9faab -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=de51d2b7-51be-4233-98de-40e1e764bc05 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":8} -->\\nP2: When a FileFn service returns `accepted: true` without `item.token`, this callback throws after the share was created and leaves the share active without durable cleanup. Require `item.token` for the create-share contract and provide a durable reconciliation path for responses that still omit it.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At filefn/admin/src/index.ts, line 367:\\n\\n<comment>When a FileFn service returns `accepted: true` without `item.token`, this callback throws after the share was created and leaves the share active without durable cleanup. Require `item.token` for the create-share contract and provide a durable reconciliation path for responses that still omit it.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -355,6 +355,19 @@ export function createFileFnAdminAdapter(service: FileFnAdminService): AdminCapa\\n+        const shareInput = input as CreateShareAdminInput;\\n+        const shareResult = result as AdminOperationResult<FileFnAdminOperationOutputMap[\\\"filefn.share-links.create-share\\\"]>;\\n+        const token = shareResult.data.item?.token;\\n+        if (!token) throw new Error(\\\"The created FileFn share token is unavailable for compensation.\\\");\\n+        await service.revokeShareLink({ fileId: shareInput.fileId, token }, context);\\n+      },\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bZNjY\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n      \"line\": 97,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kqAXR\",\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836216785\",\n        \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject non-finite JSON numbers**\\n\\nWhen a direct dispatcher caller supplies, or an adapter returns, `NaN` or either infinity under a schema declaring `type: \\\"number\\\"`, `valueType` classifies it as a valid number. The dispatcher consequently accepts the value, while JSON serialization changes it to `null`, so clients receive data that no longer satisfies the declared output schema; non-finite numbers should fail validation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bZNjZ\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n      \"line\": 276,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kqAXU\",\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T14:14:10Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836216788\",\n        \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Require schema properties to be owned by the input**\\n\\nWhen an input has a custom prototype containing a required field, this `in` check accepts the inherited value even though the subsequent `Object.entries` traversal never validates it. This is reachable through the module HTTP transport because assigning a parsed `{\\\"__proto__\\\": {...}}` body changes the accumulator's prototype; the dispatcher then clones away that prototype and invokes the adapter with the required field missing instead of rejecting the request. Check required fields with `Object.hasOwn`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6baJcm\",\n      \"path\": \"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"line\": 357,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7krWwa\",\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T17:16:45Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836570650\",\n        \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Filter connection lists by exact tenant identity**\\n\\nWhen the identity mapper returns a tenantless identity (`tenantId` is undefined), this passes an owner with an undefined tenant to `connections.list`; PlugFn's `ConnectionStorage.listByOwner` omits the tenant predicate when that value is absent, so connections for the same user or organization in every tenant are returned and mapped without an `assertConnectionOwner` check. This leaks cross-tenant connection names, scopes, and status through the list operation even though the corresponding detail operation rejects those records; post-filter the results using the exact tenant/owner checks or make the storage query distinguish tenantless records.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6baKc5\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/idempotency.ts\",\n      \"line\": 25,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7krYN9\",\n        \"author\": \"cubic-dev-ai\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-22T17:19:51Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3836576637\",\n        \"body\": \"<!-- cubic:v=e4d0a90a-8a2e-48b8-9fa7-873371ab35cd -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=5275fc5a-473b-448f-902e-ead0ba012162 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: When a required-audit idempotent mutation loses its terminal sink acknowledgement, replay redelivers the stable event ID without the original policy metadata. Persist the metadata in the pending audit marker before `writeAudit` so reconciliation reproduces the terminal event shape.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At packages/admin/src/idempotency.ts, line 25:\\n\\n<comment>When a required-audit idempotent mutation loses its terminal sink acknowledgement, replay redelivers the stable event ID without the original policy metadata. Persist the metadata in the pending audit marker before `writeAudit` so reconciliation reproduces the terminal event shape.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -19,6 +19,10 @@ export interface AdminIdempotencyRecord<T = unknown> {\\n+    /** Terminal event shape to redeliver when a sink acknowledgement is lost. */\\n+    outcome?: \\\"succeeded\\\" | \\\"failed\\\";\\n+    errorCode?: string;\\n+    metadata?: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>>;\\n     updatedAt: string;\\n   };\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_i\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n      \"line\": 272,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwxiE\",\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991044\",\n        \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject non-plain objects as JSON values**\\n\\nWhen an in-process dispatcher caller supplies a `Date`, `Map`, or other class instance under `type: \\\"object\\\"`, this branch accepts it as a valid JSON object because it never checks the prototype. The immutable snapshot preserves such instances, and output redaction converts them through `Object.entries`—for example, a valid-looking `Date` response becomes `{}`—so adapters can receive or return values that change shape at transport time; require arrays or plain/null-prototype objects throughout JSON validation.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bd5_n\",\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n      \"line\": 494,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kwxiJ\",\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T07:44:38Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3837991049\",\n        \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reconcile variables when metadata persistence fails**\\n\\nWhen `executor.setVariable` succeeds for a new variable but this store write rejects, the provider retains the live secret while the operator returns an error and has no record through which to list or delete it. A retry is not guaranteed safe because `setVariable` has no idempotency contract; persist a durable intent before the provider call or compensate/reconcile the provider variable if final persistence fails.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIN\",\n      \"path\": \"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts\",\n      \"line\": 395,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kxaUw\",\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158128\",\n        \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Expose create and upsert operations before a record exists**\\n\\nWhen an ID-targeted operation can create a new record, this classifies it exclusively as a detail-page action, while module-level actions accept only collection targets or resources with no list/detail route. Consequently operations such as `botfn.bots.upsert`, `botfn.channels.connect`, `apifn.specs.register`, and `apifn.environments.upsert` are only reachable after navigating to an existing record whose ID is then prebound; an empty collection has no console path for creating its first record. Project these creation/upsert operations as collection actions while leaving their ID fields editable.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6beWIQ\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n      \"line\": 134,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kxaUz\",\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T09:18:13Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3838158131\",\n        \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject non-JSON primitive leaves in open schemas**\\n\\nWhen an adapter returns a `bigint` under a type-less or `additionalProperties: true` child schema, validation accepts it because only object prototypes and non-finite numbers are rejected. Fresh evidence after the plain-object fix is that the new guards still omit `bigint`, `symbol`, `function`, and `undefined`; the open entity schemas used by DataFn, BillFn, and SearchFn therefore allow values that cannot be represented by the REST/MCP envelopes, with a `bigint` causing the subsequent `JSON.stringify` to throw instead of producing the validated result. Reject every primitive type outside the JSON value set even when the schema omits `type`.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bgnj3\",\n      \"path\": \"authfn/admin/src/index.ts\",\n      \"line\": 459,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7k0tp9\",\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-23T16:37:04Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3839023741\",\n        \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Bind AuthFn user cursors to scope and query**\\n\\nWhen a cursor is reused after changing the active region, email filter, or sort direction, this forwards it unchanged to `listAuthFnAdminUsers`; that implementation encodes only `createdAt` and `id` (`authfn/core/src/core/admin-users.ts:230-252`). The timestamp is then interpreted against the new result set or opposite ordering, causing users to be skipped or repeated. Include the region and query identity in the cursor and reject mismatches.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6cblvM\",\n      \"path\": \"hostfn/cli/src/operator.ts\",\n      \"line\": 379,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7mMrQS\",\n        \"author\": \"github-code-quality\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-26T11:01:38Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3862082578\",\n        \"body\": \"## Missing await\\n\\n<p>Missing await. The value 'promise' is always a promise.</p>\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6cblvb\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\n      \"line\": 480,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7mMrQn\",\n        \"author\": \"github-code-quality\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-26T11:01:38Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3862082599\",\n        \"body\": \"## Useless conditional\\n\\n<p>This use of variable 'compensationAuditMetadata' always evaluates to true.</p>\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6cblvj\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts\",\n      \"line\": 570,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7mMrQx\",\n        \"author\": \"github-code-quality\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-26T11:01:38Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3862082609\",\n        \"body\": \"## Useless conditional\\n\\n<p>This use of variable 'compensationAuditMetadata' always evaluates to true.</p>\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6cblvx\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/admin/src/validator.ts\",\n      \"line\": 480,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7mMrRE\",\n        \"author\": \"github-code-quality\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-26T11:01:38Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3862082628\",\n        \"body\": \"## Useless conditional\\n\\n<p>This negation always evaluates to false.</p>\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6cblv7\",\n      \"path\": \"filefn/server/src/index.ts\",\n      \"line\": 12,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7mMrRP\",\n        \"author\": \"github-code-quality\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-26T11:01:38Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3862082639\",\n        \"body\": \"## Unused variable, import, function or class\\n\\n<p>Unused import createNucleusPolicies.</p>\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6cbp3H\",\n      \"path\": \"filefn/admin/src/domain-service.ts\",\n      \"line\": 242,\n      \"latest\": {\n        \"id\": \"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7mMxVq\",\n        \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-26T11:05:29Z\",\n        \"outdated\": false,\n        \"url\": \"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3862107498\",\n        \"body\": \"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Expose an authorized processing entry point**\\n\\nWhen `filefn.artifacts.process-file` is invoked for a readable file, `processing` is the public service facade constructed in `filefn/server/src/index.ts`, and that facade deliberately exposes only five read-oriented methods—no `triggerProcessing`. This call therefore attempts to invoke `undefined` and every otherwise-valid process-file action fails instead of running configured processors; expose an authorization-safe processing method on the facade and call that method here.\\n\\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"staleCount\": 128\n}\n"},"started_at_ms":1787743371092,"completed_at_ms":1787743376381}}
