e of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\\n\\n\\n<file name=\\\"filefn/server/src/index.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"filefn/server/src/index.ts:354\\\">\\nP1: When a custom `authorizer` grants or denies access beyond visibility and grants, this new processing facade ignores that decision. Route processing through the configured authorizer before enqueueing, or inject the authorizer into `ProcessingService`.</violation>\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"2\\\" location=\\\"filefn/server/src/index.ts:362\\\">\\nP2: When a tenant-scoped caller processes a file with no stored tenant, this drops the caller tenant from the processor job. Preserve the route behavior by falling back to `ctx.tenantId`.</violation>\\n</file>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/116/ai_pr_review_1787743702623_f9063092-f745-442b-942b-6d4e888f5912?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F116)</sub>\\n\\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787743702623_f9063092-f745-442b-942b-6d4e888f5912:f39e43cd6ae4bf2382c674bdd145a1f7349ebf2b:516cd530-752b-45d6-908e-920badfaaba4 -->\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"chatgpt-codex-connector\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-26T11:33:56Z\",\n      \"body\": \"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `f39e43cd6a`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"pullfrog\",\n      \"state\": \"COMMENTED\",\n      \"submittedAt\": \"2026-08-26T11:35:18Z\",\n      \"body\": \"> ℹ️ No new issues found in this corrective delta; existing review threads outside this delta remain unchanged.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** I reviewed the corrective commit added after `bbd23d7`:\\n\\n- **Hardened FileFn processing authorization** — routed admin processing through a file-authorized facade that binds the requested version to its stored file and derives the processor payload from stored metadata.\\n\\n- **Tightened HostFn in-flight cleanup** — compared the complete attachment registration before deleting its map entry so cleanup cannot remove a replacement entry.\\n\\n- **Normalized shared admin records** — retained compensation metadata consistently in pending and failed durable records and preserved open-schema presentation compatibility.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against f39e43c;\\nif commits have landed on SFNS-2 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\\n\\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\\n- Files reviewed: 7\\n- Commits reviewed: 1\\n- Base: dev (f45c75f)\\n- Head: SFNS-2 (f39e43c)\\n- Reviewed commits:\\n  - f39e43c — fix: address post-merge review findings\\n- Prior pullfrog review: c281437 (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#pullrequestreview-5004489129)\\n-->\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=