nerated `.conduct` verifier output outside the PR worktree before staging. A green release gate does not prove mergeability: PR #118 was `UNSTABLE` and PR #119 remained `DIRTY` from a pre-existing base conflict at handoff. [Task 1]\n113:- Vitest does not accept Jest's `--runInBand`; rerun the workspace test without it. For schema-valued `additionalProperties`, recursively compare compatibility and cast to `McpFnJsonSchema` when needed for behavior and typecheck. [Task 1]\n422:# Task Group: August 23 Superfunctions PR #116 bounded remediation and scope diagnosis\n426:## Task 1: Refetch/fix PR #116 and diagnose imported MCPFn/UIFn scope, success\n434:- PR #116, SFNS-2, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, reviewThreads, nodeType, undefined versus null, authfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt, MCPFn, UIFn, d27cceb2\n444:- A review-fix pass is not a scope audit. Before dev-port remediation, compare the whole PR against the exact `origin/dev` inventory: SFNS-2’s MCPFn/UIFn expansion came from copying next-only workspace dependency trees, not from the intended dev-relevant admin scope. [Task 1]\n453:applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev; reuse_rule=worktree, approval, and exact-head procedures are reusable, but code, PR, CI, and deployment evidence are snapshot-specific.\n459:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T23-21-55-01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-25T16:25:10+00:00, thread_id=01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af, DATA-1 and AUTH-1 implemented, merged, and cleaned up)\n469:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T23-21-55-01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-25T16:25:10+00:00, thread_id=01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af, all 14 unresolved threads were stale or already