for similar architecture-opinion or provenance questions in this checkout, but keep claims scoped to the inspected files rather than the entire package tree.\n5471:- authfn/core, services/account/src/auth.ts, social-oauth.ts, oauth-support.ts, package barrel, source provenance, Just answer, superfunctions-dev/authfn/core\n5482:- did you read actual source code, where is the source code, services/account/node_modules/@authfn/core, file:../../../superfunctions-dev/authfn/core, symlink target, epistemic honesty\n5492:- In this workspace, `services/account/node_modules/@authfn/core` resolves to the linked local checkout `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/authfn/core`, so package reads can and should be source-based. [Task 2]\n5503:applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/nucleus with sibling source in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions and /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev; reuse_rule=safe for similar migration-audit work here, but treat exact risk lists, downgraded findings, and attached documents as checkout-specific.\n5619:- when the user asks to \"explain the merge conflicts\" before a fix -> start with a grounded conflict explanation and resolution plan before editing. [Task 28]\n5674:- Symptom: a merge conflict in Drizzle metadata is treated like a broad code conflict. Cause: the journal collision is not isolated from the feature changes. Fix: inspect `drizzle/meta/_journal.json`, renumber the migration cleanly, and validate with `drizzle-kit check`. [Task 5]\n"},"started_at_ms":1787746674862,"completed_at_ms":1787746674864}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-26T12:17:54.891Z","ordinal":15033,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a03e01-68cb-7e31-861f-6837867a04c4","call_id":"call_tpmXrcWQK8zC6OiK1QKsoY4i","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"89:scope: Use for independently replaying, reviewing, and delivering McpFn and UiFn changes from `sf-next/next` to `origin/dev` without disturbing a dirty checkout.\n90:applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev; reuse_rule=worktree/allowlist/gate procedure is reusable; PR heads, mergeability, and review state require live revalidation.\n92:## Task 1: Create and remediate separate McpFn and UiFn PRs, success\n96:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T23-23-22-01a02fc1-72e9-7123-bc9e-a52e926f9b99.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-25T03:34:26+00:00, thread_id=01a02fc1-72e9-7123-bc9e-a52e926f9b99, PR #118 and #119 pushed with exact-head verification; #118 was UNSTABLE and #119 DIRTY at handoff)\n108:- For `origin/dev` PRs, exclude `.conduct` and stage an explicit path allowlist. McpFn's authoritative broad gate is `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH npm run gate:mcpfn-release`; UiFn's is `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:$PATH node scripts/verify-uifn-stable.mjs`, which can be quiet for minutes. [Task 1]\n109:- Move UiFn generated `.conduct` verifier output outside the PR worktree before staging. A green release gate does not prove mergeability: PR #118 was `UNSTABLE` and PR #119 remained `DIRTY` from a pre-existing base conflict at handoff. [Task 1]\n113:- Vitest does not accept Jest's `--runInBand`; rerun the workspace test without it. For schema-valued `additionalProperties`, recursively compare compatibility and cast to `McpFnJsonSchema` when needed for behavior and typecheck. [Task 1]\n422:# Task Group: August 23 Superfunctions PR #116 bounded remediation and scope diagnosis\n426:## Task 1: Refetch/fix PR #116 and diagnose imported MCPFn/UIFn scope, success\n434:- PR #116, SFNS-2, 21n/pr-refetch-fix@1.0.1, reviewThreads, nodeType, undefined versus null, authfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt, MCPFn, UIFn, d27cceb2\n444:- A review-fix pass is not a scope audit. Before dev-port remediation, compare the whole PR against the exact `origin/dev` inventory: SFNS-2’s MCPFn/UIFn expansion came from copying next-only workspace dependency trees, not from the intended dev-relevant admin scope. [Task 1]\n453:applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev; reuse_rule=worktree, approval, and exact-head procedures are reusable, but code, PR, CI, and deployment evidence are snapshot-specific.\n459:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T23-21-55-01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-25T16:25:10+00:00, thread_id=01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af, DATA-1 and AUTH-1 implemented, merged, and cleaned up)\n469:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T23-21-55-01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-25T16:25:10+00:00, thread_id=01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af, all 14 unresolved threads were stale or already fixed)\n479:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T23-21-55-01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-25T16:25:10+00:00, thread_id=01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af, exact-head merges completed and final origin/dev verified)\n489:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T23-21-55-01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-25T16:25:10+00:00, thread_id=01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af, dedicated worktrees removed without touching others)\n685:- Safely synchronize with `git fetch sf-next next`, ancestry check, `git switch next`, `git merge --ff-only sf-next/next`, local-branch deletion, upstream reset, and `git rev-list --left-right --count next...sf-next/next`; preserve the separate `superfunctions-dev` worktree. [Task 1]\n1563:applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/{superfunctions,superfunctions-dev,worktrees/superfunctions/*}; reuse_rule=verify current ref, account, and package state; counts/SHA/release status are time-specific.\n1575:## Task 2: Publish next-only npm packages and remediate McpFn PR #42, success\n1616:- McpFn release gate needs Node 24; a root install can mask standalone dependencies. In hosted McpFn CI, run `node scripts/ci-install-rollup-native.mjs` after `npm ci` before the gate because npm can omit `@rollup/rollup-linux-x64-gnu`. Validate post-push local/ref/PR SHA equality and merge with an exact-head guard. [Task 2]\n1623:- Do not dispatch all tag releases sharing one concurrency group. Remove sibling-source aliases and root-tool assumptions from package tests; do not attribute generic JavaScript, Python, Vercel, or dependency-cycle baseline failures to McpFn without the exact job logs. [Task 2]\n1711:applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/{superfunctions,superfunctions-dev,worktrees/superfunctions/*}; reuse_rule=use the review workflow across Superfunctions PRs, but inspect the exact PR SHA, authenticated account, and clean worktree before applying findings.\n1727:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-10T17-24-09-ah21-pr_112_refetch_review_fixes_and_push.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/archived_sessions/rollout-2026-08-10T22-54-09-019fecb4-0775-7c70-901b-b1c6f5df36e1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-10T19:22:22+00:00, thread_id=019fecb4-0775-7c70-901b-b1c6f5df36e1, 73 affected-package tests passed; CI billing lock remained external)\n1839:- PR #38 merged into `sf-next/next` at `12580dd2`. Base conflicts in `.conduct/logs.csv`, `README.md`, `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, and `release-packages.json` were resolved by retaining MailFn and McpFn registrations and regenerating the lockfile; GitHub operations used `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other`. [Task 2]\n1970:- At the inspected snapshot, nine entries included eight live worktrees and one stale/prunable `/private/tmp/sf-docsfn-core-pack-a2712232`. `superfunctions-dev` was a broad dirty integration stack (377 tracked + 95 untracked paths, 10 commits behind stored `origin/dev`); `SFN-15` held large generated `.conduct` evidence; `codex/mcpfn` had 103 modified + 80 untracked paths. Counts and divergence are snapshot-specific. [Task 1]\n2072:# Task Group: McpFn authentication regression testkit in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mcpfn\n2073:scope: Use when implementing or validating reusable API-key/OAuth regression coverage, OAuth metadata compatibility, or browser authorization flows for an McpFn consumer such as Skillplane.\n2084:- @mcpfn/testing/auth, runAuthRegressionSuite, assertAuthRegressionSuite, McpFnAuthProviderAdapter, resource_metadata, createOAuthClientMetadataVariants, assertAuthorizationCodeClientMetadata\n2094:- @mcpfn/testing/playwright, McpFnMockOAuthAuthorizationServer, PKCE S256, refresh rotation, revocation, auth-flow.spec.ts, gate:mcpfn-release, better-sqlite3\n2098:- when the user said “proceed and implement this” after discussing a reusable McpFn auth testkit -> implement the agreed testkit rather than returning design guidance alone. [Task 1]\n2102:- `@mcpfn/testing/auth` owns common protocol assertions for missing, invalid, valid, insufficient-scope, expired, wrong-resource, and revoked credentials; consumers supply only `McpFnAuthProviderAdapter.issue()`/`revoke()` plus a target request adapter. OAuth failures require a Bearer `WWW-Authenticate` challenge with `resource_metadata`; API-key tests intentionally do not. [Task 1]\n2104:- `McpFnMockOAuthAuthorizationServer` provides discovery, consent, callback capture, PKCE S256, one-time codes, refresh rotation, revocation, expiry, resource binding, and token verification. Public imports are `@mcpfn/testing/auth` and `@mcpfn/testing/playwright`; Playwright stays an optional peer/subpath. [Task 2]\n2138:- when the user said \"fix all merge conflicts\" and \"dont commit or push yet\" -> leave resolution local/uncommitted and do not cross the publication boundary. [Task 1]\n2349:# Task Group: Superfunctions current DataFn and AuthFn audits in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev\n2351:applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev; reuse_rule=re-audit dirty source, deployment preconditions, and current tests before acting on any finding.\n2357:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-08T03-26-04-CM7L-datafn_read_only_audit_linear_sf_px.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/08/rollout-2026-08-08T08-56-04-019fdf68-06a7-7801-a36b-191690fdedb1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-08T04:29:17+00:00, thread_id=019fdf68-06a7-7801-a36b-191690fdedb1, read-only audit and verified SF Px Linear publication)\n2367:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-08T03-27-01-wNdB-authfn_current_tree_audit_linear_sf_px.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/08/rollout-2026-08-08T08-57-01-019fdf68-e4b1-7150-a616-6d0649912f3f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-08T04:36:22+00:00, thread_id=019fdf68-e4b1-7150-a616-6d0649912f3f, full audit and Linear publication)\n2368:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/08/rollout-2026-08-08T08-57-24-019fdf69-3e4b-7470-9b1f-a9a74219509f.jso