ep` and `show`; worktree naming does not constrain the diff. [Task 2]\n5285:# Task Group: DataFn/FileFn transport auth comparison in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev\n5286:scope: Use for read-only source comparisons between Nucleus DataFn transport auth and FileFn client auth in `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev`, especially when the user asks whether FileFn can adopt the same shared HTTP/auth provider shape. Boundaries: this is grounded in current source, not a shipped FileFn API change; re-check the exact client types and request paths before reusing implementation claims.\n5287:applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev; reuse_rule=safe for similar source-grounded auth transport comparisons in this checkout, but distinguish current capability from proposed API shape every time.\n5293:- rollout_summaries/2026-06-24T06-32-02-7DtI-datafn_filefn_auth_transport_comparison.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/06/24/rollout-2026-06-24T12-02-03-019ef854-1ea0-7d31-90cb-fed7430b6a56.jsonl, updated_at=2026-06-24T06:37:57+00:00, thread_id=019ef854-1ea0-7d31-90cb-fed7430b6a56, exact call-site read separated AuthFn-backed DataFn transport auth from FileFn’s simpler `getAuthHeaders` demo)\n5303:- rollout_summaries/2026-06-24T06-32-02-7DtI-datafn_filefn_auth_transport_comparison.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/06/24/rollout-2026-06-24T12-02-03-019ef854-1ea0-7d31-90cb-fed7430b6a56.jsonl, updated_at=2026-06-24T06:37:57+00:00, thread_id=019ef854-1ea0-7d31-90cb-fed7430b6a56, verified that the shared `@superfunctions/http` auth provider already exists and FileFn could align to it with caveats)\n5363:applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/nucleus with sibling validation work in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev; reuse_rule=safe for similar Nucleus migration QA or browser-bridge diagnosis in these linked checkouts, but re-check the exact dev host, auth state, backend health, and current migration diff before reusing as proof of current correctness.\n5460:applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/nucleus with linked package source in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/authfn/core; reuse_rule=safe for similar architecture-opinion or provenance questions in this checkout, but keep claims scoped to the inspected files rather than the entire package tree.\n5471:- authfn/core, services/account/src/auth.ts, social-oauth.ts, oauth-support.ts, package barrel, source provenance, Just answer, superfunctions-dev/authfn/core\n5482:- did you read actual source code, where is the source code, services/account/node_modules/@authfn/core, file:../../../superfunctions-dev/authfn/core, symlink target, epistemic honesty\n5492:- In this workspace, `services/account/node_modules/@authfn/core` resolves to the linked local checkout `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/authfn/core`, so package reads can and should be source-based. [Task 2]\n5503:applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/nucleus with sibling source in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions and /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev; reuse_rule=safe for similar migration-audit work here, but treat exact risk lists, downgraded findings, and attached documents as checkout-specific.\n5619:- when the user asks to \"explain the merge conflicts\" before a fix -> start with a grounded conflict explanation and resolution plan before editing. [Task 28]\n5674:- Symptom: a merge conflict in Drizzle metadata is treated like a broad code conflict. Cause: the journal collision is not isolated from the feature changes. Fix: inspect `drizzle/meta/_journal.json`, renumber the migration cleanly, and validate with `drizzle-kit check`. [Task 5]\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a03e01-41e1-7f90-8d5d-2a7f7ce5cc2b","create_time":1787746674.891936}}}
